Mr. Thong Khon's recommendation was made during the monthly meeting of the party in Baray and Taing Kork districts of Kampong Thom province on the morning of October 4, 2020.
After listening to the reports of the two district party presidents regarding the local situation and the registration process, Mr. Thong Khon made some recommendations:
* Efforts must be made to facilitate and expedite the issuance of ID cards in accordance with legal procedures for citizens who have not yet obtained a Cambodian identity card and citizens who already have an identity card but have lost or misplaced the data in the existing ID card. .
* The working group must go to the village, commune to meet with the people to ask about the inspection of the voter list and to go to the new voter registration, if they have not fulfilled these obligations, explain how to coordinate with them. Ask them to check the voter list or to register a new voter for everyone.
* Regarding the review of the voter list and the new voter registration, Mr. Thong Khon also submitted a plan to the party chairmen of Baray and Taing Kork districts, as well as the chairmen of each commune party, as well as the working groups to help the two districts. This is given close attention to party members and party family members.
* Must continue to strengthen and expand more party members to get votes in the upcoming election.
Participate in strengthening security, order and controlling the minds of party members to grasp the general situation at the local level to avoid any negative incidents.
The meeting was determined to follow the recommendations of Mr. Thong Khon, especially to show the spirit of the work to encourage people to check the list and go to register to vote for new achievements for the Cambodian People's Party with Samdech Techo. Hun Sen is the chairman.
Please be informed that the NEC has announced that the process of reviewing the voter list and voter registration in 2020 will take only 19 days, and this process will start from October 1, 2020, which will be closed at By October 19, 2020.
Kathina Ceremony of the King of Thailand was donated to the monks waiting for the rain at the Indo-Cambodia pagoda, collecting more than 30,000 dollars
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Panyarak Phunsap, Thai Ambassador to Cambodia, this morning, October 4, 2020, presided over the Royal Kathina Ceremony of His Majesty the King of the Kingdom of Thailand. The Ministry of Foreign Affairs of Thailand brought to pay homage to the monks who waited for the rainy season for a quarter at the Buddha Seima, Wat Indo Kampuchea Thom Nirimit, Sangkat Prey Veng, Khan Dangkor, Phnom Penh.
The Thai Embassy in Cambodia held a ceremony to pay homage to Preah Ratanatray, Samathan Sil, invite monks to celebrate Preah Berit and give a traditional Khmer sermon on October 3, 2020 at the Thai Embassy in Cambodia.
In this Kathina ceremony, the royal gift from the King of Thailand was 16,508 US dollars and the Thai Buddhist festival in Cambodia and the Cambodian Buddhists, which the Thai Embassy in Cambodia received 13,010 US dollars and 12,583 US dollars. 900 Riel.
Please be informed that the Thai Ministry of Foreign Affairs always organizes the Royal Kathina Festival at many Buddhist pagodas in different countries every year. For Cambodia, it received its first royal Kathina in 1995 and celebrates almost every year, alternating between the pagodas of the Mahanikaya and the Dhammayutnikaya.
The 2020 Royal Kathina Parade at Indo Kampuchea Thom Nirimit Pagoda proceeded in an orderly manner and in accordance with the highest honor of the King of the Kingdom of Thailand.
Every Buddhist is grateful to His Majesty the Most Gracious, who has always had great merits in upholding Buddhism, which most Cambodians and Thais respect. Meanwhile, the ties between the two countries have also been strengthened, especially at the population level. Head of the Royal Government issues a sub-decree on the procedures and procedures for the implementation of the law on anti-financing for the proliferation of weapons of mass destruction
