NEC issues notification on what to do and what is prohibited in reviewing the 2020 voter list and registration
(Phnom Penh): The National Election Committee (NEC) on October 3, 2020, issued a notification to all stakeholders on the implementation and prohibitions in the census process. Names and registration for the 2020 election.
According to the announcement received by Fresh News, the process of reviewing the voter list and voter registration in 2020 will take place from October 1 to 19, 2020. This activity has been taking place in all 1,646 communes across the country in accordance with the NEC's work calendar, and to ensure the smooth running of the voter list and voter registration. Inform all stakeholders of the following necessary factors:
1. To be implemented: * Everyone present in the voter registration office and in the inner premises of those polling stations shall be under the control and guidance of the NEC or the NEC or the CPP. Pursuant to the provisions of the Law on the Election of Members of the National Assembly and the Law on the Amendment of this Law and the regulations and procedures for the annual review of the voter list and voter registration.
