APSARA Authority completes capacity building training for 155 travel agents in Angkor area
(Siem Reap): A one-month training course for travel agents on temple risk in Angkor resorts organized by the Angkor Tourism Development Department in collaboration with the Department of Temple Preservation in Angkor Park and Preventive Archeology and Angkor Training Center.
Mr. Lim Sru, Director of Angkor Travel Agency, said that the temple risk training course was attended by 155 travel agents at major temples such as Angkor Wat, Bayon, Ta Prohm, Transfiguration and Bakong. The project was completed on September 30, 2020.
Mr. Lim Srou said that this training course taught all participants about the role of travel agents, explaining to national and international experts about the general history of Angkor Park, the history of conservation and restoration of temples, site inspections of risk and protection measures. To save the temple.
Through these lessons, some basic travel agencies can participate in surveying, providing information and contributing information to tourists to know and prevent various risks at the temple.
Speaking at the closing ceremony of the travel agency training at Bakong Temple, Mr. Sok Sangvar, Deputy Director General in charge of Angkor Tourism Development Department, thanked all the trainers for sharing their knowledge and experience to the team.
The Deputy Director General of APSARA Authority expressed his hope that the trained team will use this knowledge and continue to share this new knowledge fruitfully in their daily work for good. Better in Angkor.
