17 Potato Removal Workers Victim of Lightning Strike in Memot District Thanking Samdech Kittipritthbandit for Giving Relief (Video inside) (Tbong Khmum) Tbong Khmum Province expressed its deepest gratitude to Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, a humanitarian mother who always thinks about the well-being of the victims immediately after receiving the news.
On Friday, October 2, 2020, Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, assigned his subordinates to visit their homes and bring humanitarian donations to the workers. Give to these 17 people who were injured by lightning on September 27, 2020 at Satum village, Choam Kravien commune, Memot district, Tbong Khmum province.
On that occasion, the Cambodian Red Cross delegation met with Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, who sent a message of condolences to all the victims, even though Samdech did not invite them directly. Emotions, compassion, love, thinking of well-being.
In particular, I wish all the victims a speedy recovery and a strong sense of normalcy to continue working to raise the standard of living and improve the living standards of families under the shadow of this peace.
At the same time, Ms. Men Neary Sopheak, First Deputy Secretary General of the Cambodian Red Cross, also brought a message of appeal from Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen to all people:
* Take good care of your health, stay clean and continue to live a normal life in a new way to stay safe and prevent Kovid-19 infection.
* Increase vigilance and prevent chickenpox, dengue fever and other infectious diseases in the community.
* Be careful when it is raining, wind, lightning, thunder or lightning, especially pay attention to the weather situation notification of the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology and other precautionary measures.
* Please respect the traffic law consistently and always be careful when driving for the safety of yourself and others.
On that occasion, Dr. Uy Sam Ath, Director of the Disaster Management Department of the Cambodian Red Cross, also disseminated information to the people about the phenomenon of thunder and lightning and what to do to protect themselves from various natural disasters that may eventually occur.
After the meeting, the delegation was divided into two groups and visited all the affected people to their homes under the slogan "Where there are difficulties, there is the Cambodian Red Cross."
