"Bakong Village, My Village" is a new tourism product on Siem Reap land! Minister Thong Khon Expresses Full Support and Asks Relevant Authorities for Additional Support to Communities
(Siem Reap): In line with the tourism policy and vision of the Royal Government, which wants Siem Reap to have new tourism products in addition to the World Heritage Site, now "Bakong community, my village" has developed beautifully in the territory of Bakong commune. Prasat Bakong district can serve almost all the needs of tourists in the country.
The Bakong Phum Khnom community has been serving local tourists for almost a month now and has received significant support from tourists, which is an important contribution to the promotion of tourism and promotion. Internal tourism movement at a time when the world as well as Cambodia is facing the Kovid-19 crisis.
The presence of this tourism community was fully supported by Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, and Mr. Ngov Sengkak, Director of the Siem Reap Provincial Department of Tourism, Ms. Chhay Sivlin, Director of the Cambodian Tourism Agency (CATA), Prasat Bakong District Administration and Bakong Commune Administration. Well.
The Minister advised the community leaders to focus on hospitality in the community and to provide quality tourism services, while the service staff must be friendly, friendly and friendly. .
He stressed that as long as the hospitality, service quality and hygiene work well, the community will be able to attract more tourists and participate in promoting Siem Reap tourist destinations better.
At the same time, Minister Thong Khon also requested the APSARA Authority, Siem Reap Provincial Administration and the Provincial Department of Tourism to continue to support the Bakong community in my village so that this good tourism product can grow and develop. By sustainability, innovation and high responsibility, that is, to walk in line with the concept of "development serves conservation, conservation serves development".
Mr. Thong Khon expressed the hope that this joint implementation will bring benefits to local people to have a more prosperous life and preserve the national heritage there.
Mr. Sot Sour, President of Bakong Phum I Community, said that the purpose of establishing this tourism community is to:
1: Promote tourism potential in the area of Bakong temple through communication, temple visits and rural landscapes to attract more tourists to visit.
2. Encourage local people to create local agricultural products, vegetables, fruits, livestock, meat and souvenirs to sell to tourists, increase direct income, improve community life, reduce poverty and migration.
3: Promote hygiene and clean environment in the community, participate in promoting and implementing the movement "clean city, clean resort, good service, good hospitality and warmth."
In addition, the community also organizes many entertainment programs during the festival season, such as performances of martial arts, chapei, chapei, yike dance, which is the cultural identity of the Khmer nation since ancient times. On October 2, 914 more vehicles were inspected and fined
According to the spokesperson of the General Commissioner, within 155 days of tightening the road traffic law by increasing the fine according to Sub-Decree No. 39, from May 1 to October 2, 2020, the traffic police nationwide inspected And fined a total of 182470 vehicles, including 135014 motorcycles and 40724 vehicles of all types.
Lt. Gen. Chhay Kimkhoeun continued that for the past 155 days, the implementation of the new sub-decree to fine the offending vehicles has been going well. He thanked and commended all the road users for their good obedience to the traffic law so far, especially the traffic police for their dedication and hard work. Tighten traffic with the highest sense of responsibility.
Please note that for October 2, 2020, traffic accidents across Cambodia also occurred 6 times, in which 4 people died, 5 people were injured (3 people were seriously injured). During the 155 days, there were 1,280 traffic accidents in Cambodia, in which 643 people were killed and 1994 injured (1,194 seriously injured).
