Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth Chairs an Inter-Ministerial Meeting to Review and Discuss the Outcome of the Cambodia-Korea Free Trade Agreement Negotiations
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Economy and Finance, and Chairman of the Economic and Financial Policy Committee (CSEC), chaired an inter-ministerial meeting to review and discuss the results of the talks. Cambodia-Korea FTA
The meeting was attended by Mr. and Mrs. Ministers and leaders of relevant ministries and institutions as well as members of the Cambodian Negotiation Working Group, which was held at the Ministry of Economy and Finance on the morning of October 2, 2020.
The free trade agreement was initiated by the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, during a recent state visit to Phnom Penh by the President of the Republic of Korea, Moon Jae-in.
In addition to the mechanisms being implemented, the agreement aims to improve the penetration of both parties' products into each other's markets by reducing tariff and non-tariff barriers and promoting Trade facilitation aims to increase bilateral trade volume, as well as to contribute to strengthening and expanding cooperation and deepening economic integration between the two countries.
The Cambodia-Korea Free Trade Agreement Negotiation Team has already held two rounds of video talks from August 31 to September 3, 2020.
The meeting noted the results of the two rounds of negotiations and praised the progress made by the negotiating team in each section, as well as provided some key guidance on specific tasks to the negotiating team as a basis. The next round of talks is aimed at concluding negotiations on the agreement by the end of 2020, as agreed between the two sides.
The negotiation of this agreement also shows the strong commitment of the Royal Government of Cambodia in its efforts to continue its economic integration into the region and the world, despite the current difficult situation to gain access to markets. Issued for Cambodian products that are richer and better, as well as contribute to creating more job opportunities for people.
Through this agreement, Cambodia will have a better opportunity to export its potential products to the Korean market, which Cambodia does not have in the current mechanism between Cambodia and Korea.
In addition to the reduction of tariff barriers, non-tariff measures and rules of origin as well as trade-related procedures and procedures have also been improved and simplified to facilitate trade between Both countries. The positive effects of this agreement will contribute to the development and sustainability of national economic growth by boosting trade volume between the two countries.
The Meeting also reaffirmed the Royal Government of Cambodia's commitment to support multilateralism and the rule of law, although some countries have been implementing protectionist and unilateral mechanisms, especially in Cambodia. In the context of the Kovid 19 crisis.
