Ministry of Interior Urges Capital-Provincial Governors to Strengthen the Implementation of the Roles and Duties of Sangkat Bee Clerks in the 2020 Voter List Review Process
According to the letter from the Ministry of Interior, according to the calendar of the examination of the voter list and voter registration in 2020 and the notification letter of the NEC, the examination of the voter list and voter registration in 2020 starts from 1st to October 19th, 2020.
In order for the process of reviewing the voter list and voter registration in 2020 to be successful according to the plan set by the Ministry of Interior, please request the Capital and Provincial Governors to inspect and strengthen the implementation of the duties and responsibilities of the commune / sangkat clerk as follows:
1: Each Commune / Sangkat Clerk shall take care to perform his / her duties and responsibilities related to the examination of the voter list and voter registration in 2020 in accordance with the laws, regulations and procedures for the examination of the voter list and voter registration. .
2. Each commune / sangkat clerk must be present on a regular basis to participate in the performance of his / her duties in reviewing the voter list and voter registration in 2020, except for the most urgent business or health problems that can not work.
In case the Commune / Sangkat Clerk is absent and unable to perform his / her duties, he / she shall report to the Commune / Sangkat Chief and shall request for leave in accordance with the prescribed principles, procedures and procedures.
Municipal, district and khan governors shall coordinate and assign one official of the municipal, district and khan administration to assist in the examination of the voter list and voter registration in 2020 to replace the commune / sangkat clerk who is absent or does not have a commune / sangkat clerk to ensure the continuity of this work. .
