(Phnom Penh): October 2, 2020 is the second day of the process of reviewing the voter list and voter registration 2020, organized by the National Election Committee (NEC).
In order to register to vote, Cambodian citizens of either sex born on or before January 1, 2003 must have an ID card. If you do not have an ID card, you must go to the Commune / Sangkat Hall to get the ID card for the election.
Voter registration is very important for citizens to have the right to participate in the 2022 Commune / Sangkat Council elections and the 2023 National Assembly elections.
If not registered on the voter list prepared by the NEC, Cambodians of both sexes will not be eligible to vote. The NEC calls on Cambodians of both sexes born before or before January 1, 2003 to go and register to vote and check the voter list.
