The European Union (EU) has contributed 400 million euros (about $ 469 million) to support the COVAX project, but the EU itself is unwilling to participate due to a lack of confidence in its member states. In the distribution of the above program. Instead, the EU has signed agreements to purchase more than 1 billion doses of the vaccine directly with vaccine developers.
As part of the COVAX project, WHO and GAVI have called on countries to prioritize front-line health workers, then the elderly, with the goal of vaccinating 20 percent of the world's population. Another challenge is that many vaccine candidates need to be kept at a cool temperature from the production site to the patient, so transportation will be a major obstacle.
Another hurdle is that most leading vaccine applicants require 2 doses per person, which can cause complications. In addition, fears of lawsuits in the event of a vaccine not being effective can also jeopardize the agreement, as vaccine developers may require clear assurances that they will not face any lawsuits. In case of death or adverse effects from their vaccine.
