(Phnom Penh): Monks and Buddhists at the foot of Phneat Simpaly pagoda in Sangkat Snor, Khan Kambol, Phnom Penh, were shocked and surprised after the pool in the pagoda was made of brick, cement and concrete. A large one dug into the ground to prepare for planting bricks up to 5 meters deep, suddenly emerged without knowing the reason and there was no landslide at all.
Preah Serey Kosal Som Sokha, Preah Vinay Thor, Phnom Penh Capital Hall, Preah Krou Anukon, Khan Kampol and Preah Chao Athikar of Wat Phneat Simpaly in Sangkat Snor, Khan Kampoul, Phnom Penh, has issued a decree to inform Fresh News on October 2, 2020 that the leaking pool This strange incident is 8 meters long and 5 meters wide.
Preah Serey Kosal Som Sokha described that the reservoir was dug to a depth of 5 meters, then planted a brick around and poured concrete at the bottom. In addition to being 5 meters underground, the reservoir also raised bricks 3 meters above the ground.
The chief abbot of Phneat pagoda insisted that after the construction team had completed the construction, which took several days, he had not yet poured water into it. Suddenly, from the first day of Ben 1, this pool began to emerge gradually until October 2, 2020, rising to a height of about 3 meters. And this emergence is very strange, the land around did not collapse at all, and the pagoda fence next to the reservoir did not shake or crack at all.
Both Preah Sereikosal Som Sokha and the construction team were very surprised, saying that if the land here collapsed, it would cause the pool to rise, there should be landslide marks around it and the fence next to it. There should also be some breakage. But no landslides or broken fences were seen.
Preah Serey Kosal Som Sokha insisted that what he said was not meant to inspire any miracle or miracle, only to wonder about this incident, while some builders also wondered about such an event.
Please be informed that Phneat Simpaly Pagoda is located in Sangkat Snor, Khan Kampol, Phnom Penh, which is the largest pagoda in Phnom Penh.
