France registers 25,000 volunteers to take part in its second and third Kovid-19 vaccine tests (Video inside) (Paris): French authorities on Thursday called for the recruitment of 25 young volunteers. Thousands to register for large-scale trials of their vaccine candidates to assess their safety and efficacy. This is according to the release by CNA on Thursday, October 1, 2020.
The French public research institute Inserm, which is in charge of the project, did not name the vaccine being tested, saying only that it was in talks with pharmaceutical companies to select the most successful vaccine candidates for the project. Test.
The second and third phases, which will begin this month, will be conducted at 24 hospitals across the country, with volunteers invited to register online.
There is currently no internationally approved vaccine to prevent COVID-19, which has killed more than 1 million people worldwide. According to the World Health Organization, more than 150 potential vaccines are being developed around the world, with 38 being tested in humans in the second and third phases.
