The following is a brief history of the founding of the People's Republic of China:
In addition, less than a year after the king abdicated, General Yeon Xikai, a figure appointed by Prince Puyi as prime minister, decided to establish a republic on February 12, 1912. . With the army in full force, Yeon Sikai appointed himself president of the new regime.
It was not until February 1912, after Prince Puyi decided to abdicate under the pressure of his former prime minister, Yean Xikai, that the monarchy, which had ruled China since 1644, collapsed. Completely demolished.
Because of his achievements in assisting the rebels in the revolution and his military power, the interim president, Sun Yat-sen, who ruled China for just over two months, handed over the presidency to Yen Sikai. Back.
Conflicts between the two major Chinese political parties after the election led to a second revolution by Sun Yat-sen, who had succeeded in overthrowing the monarchy, with the aim of overthrowing the government of Yen Sikai. Unfortunately, with so few troops, the revolution was completely defeated and Sun Yat-sen even fled to Japan.
On June 6, 1916, Yeon Sikai died of an illness. After his death, his former generals took his subordinates to serve them and lived like their respective warlords.
Back then, Sun Yat-sen's Kuomintang Nationalist Party shook hands with the Chinese Communist Party. Although the two groups have different positions. The communists wanted to establish a communist state and abolish the feudal class left over from the monarchy, but the Kuomintang focused on cracking down on warlords to unite the nation and lead the country to industrial growth.
The communist movement under President Mao Zedong, restructured in the style of Marxism-Leninism, has made remarkable progress. Mao Zedong was a powerful leader who learned the military leadership tactics of the ancient Chinese scholar Sun Su and loved to read the story of Sam Kok. He devised a powerful guerrilla strategy.
In 1948, Mao Zedong's forces seized Manchuria and captured more than 400,000 government soldiers. Mao Zedong soon besieged the area of more than 400,000 government troops, and at that time, fearing that Mao Zedong would take over the area, Zhang Kai-hek intended to use fighter jets to drop bombs and demolish the area, but his troops realized this. They laid down their arms and surrendered to Mao Zedong peacefully.
The whole of mainland China came under the control of Mao Zedong's Chinese Communist Party, and he reorganized China. In addition, on October 1, 1949, President Mao Zedong announced the establishment of the People's Republic of China, with Beijing as its capital ever since.
Every year on the founding day of the People's Republic of China, the Chinese government in Beijing as well as Chinese embassies abroad celebrate. But for 2020, due to concerns over the spread of Kovid 19, the Chinese government does not seem to be celebrating the event.
