(Kampong Chhnang): Phnom Kangri is a mountain that embodies the legend of Khmer history, "The story of Puthisen Neang Kangri", which is thousands of hectares in Trangel and Po communes, Kampong Leng district, Kampong Chhnang province and is about 7 miles away. Kilometers from the provincial town of Kampong Chhnang, having to travel across three rivers to reach this mountain.
Regarding the legend related to Phnom Neang Kangri, which is a historical mountain, Mr. Ta Ouk Huot, 67 years old, the chief abbot of Kampong Leng district and the first deputy chief of Ta Ngil commune, said that the ancient legend of Phnom Neang Kangri has a long history. So far, there are some places and names of places that are still called today, he can not remember all, just remember some by hearing from the ancestors only.
The story of the story of Phnom Neang Kangri, according to some research documents and the description of the elders in the village, there is a story that in the past there were two farmers, a couple with 12 children. Unable to raise the 12 children, the couple decided to abandon them in the forest. After thinking about it, the couple took their 12 children for a walk in the forest with a lot of food.
Knowing this, they were so frightened that they ran away until they met a king named Preah Bat Brahmadon, who reigned in the kingdom of Preah Si. After meeting the 12 women, the criminal king was very pleased and brought them to the kingdom and appointed them as his 12 wives.
Until adulthood, Rith Sen always asked his mother to find his father. Rith Sen's mother told the story to all the children and let them find a place to study. Rith Sen was also known by the commander as her 12 children and was sent to learn the alphabet. When Rith Sen grew up, the criminal king announced that he was looking for a brave man to be the commander. At that time, Rith Sen passed the exam and was also appointed as the commander.
When the giant knew the story of Rith Sen and did not hesitate, the giant used a trick to Rith Sen to bring his message to the kingdom of Santhob Borach to hand over to the princess Kanri, the queen of that kingdom. Princess Kangri is the adopted daughter of the giant giant, which the giant's teacher picked on the lotus flower and sent the giant giant to love like a child.
After reading the royal message, he ordered all the brigades in the palace to arrange the wedding immediately. After getting married, because she loves her husband so much, Kangri took Rithi Sen to visit his kingdom and took him to see the sacred objects in her kingdom without any concealment.
When he saw her 12 glasses, Rithi Sen made the girl drunk and took the leaves to pray for the giant to fall asleep, then Rith Sen stole the 12 glasses and used the leaves. The winged silk blows on the horse so that the winged horse can fly. Then Rithi Sen got on a horse and flew away.
As for Kangri, after getting drunk and cursing, she found out that Rithi Sen ran away from her. She tried to run after Rithi Sen. Run along, shouting Rithi Sen gradually.
Seeing this, Rithi Sen hurriedly took all 12 of her glasses to help her mother and uncle in the cave so that she could see as before and brought her mother and uncle to meet the criminal king. As for the criminal king, he also cursed the giant's dream. After the giantess found out about the dead girl, she immediately left the kingdom, and the criminal king came to receive the 12 of them and Rith Sen to the Royal Palace and lived in peace forever.
The legend of the history of Phnom Neang Kangri, which has been prepared as an article to share with the audience to listen and read above, is an excerpt from the story of our Khmer people, which is compiled as a novel and a fairy tale. The other part is quoted from the memories of the old people who told the news agency Fresh News in Kampong Chhnang province. According to history books, this is a long story.
