Spokesman for the General Commission: On October 1, another 721 vehicles were inspected and fined
According to the spokesperson of the General Commissioner, within 154 days of tightening the road traffic law by increasing the fine according to Sub-Decree No. 49, from May 1 to October 1, 2020, the traffic police throughout the country inspected And fined a total of 181,556 vehicles, including 134,316 motorcycles and 47,240 vehicles of all types.
Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun said that for the past 154 days, the implementation of the new sub-decree to fine vehicles for offenses has been going well. He thanked and commended all the road users for their good obedience to the traffic law so far, especially the traffic police for their dedication and hard work. Tighten traffic with the highest sense of responsibility.
Please note that for October 1, 2020, traffic accidents throughout the country also occurred 6 times, in which 2 people died, 13 people were injured (011 people were seriously injured).
Royal Government cuts over 12 million USD to build sewer system and wastewater treatment plant in Stung Sen city
(Kampong Thom): Mr. Sok Lou, Governor of Kampong Thom Province, confirmed that the Royal Government has dropped more than 12 million US dollars to build a sewer system and wastewater treatment plant in Stung Sen City.
Mr. Sok Lou confirmed this during the ceremony of Krong Pali to build a sewer system and wastewater treatment station in Throne Lech Village, Sangkat Damrey Choan Khla, Stung Sen City, Kampong Thom Province on October 1, 2020.
Mr. Sok Loo thanked Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, for providing a project to build a sewer system and wastewater treatment plant in Kampong Thom province. The project is a government project, a loan from the Asian Development Bank (ADB), with a total budget of more than $ 12 million, including more than 39 km of drainage and many other infrastructure.
The provincial governor requested the construction company to speed up the construction because without the drainage system, Stung Sen city would be flooded due to rain.
Mr. Sok Lou also warned the cadastral and construction officials to thoroughly inspect all the constructions that have been constructed, especially the landfill, the construction of houses, the construction of fences, etc. Make a blockage without a drainage system and so on.
Second, the construction of a landfill with a capacity of 48,000 cubic meters and the installation of garbage collection vehicles and waste storage.
He said that the project is in the process of preparing an IELA report to request a letter of approval from the Ministry of Environment and study the detailed plan, which achieved 63% and plans to put up for auction in the near future, and the construction project has a period of 3 years. Implemented from July 2020 to July 2023. NEC: The first day of the 2020 voter list and voter registration process went smoothly without any problems
According to the NEC, according to the work calendar, the examination of voter list and voter registration lasts for 19 days, divided into three stages:
For the first four days, from October 1 to 4, 2020, the voter registration offices will be open at the commune / sangkat halls.
For the next 10 days, from October 5 to 14, 2020, voter registration offices will be mobile in some villages in each commune. Separately, for October 8, 2020, Commune / Sangkat Councils must close the voter registration office for one day to open a meeting with the voter registration team to evaluate the work.
For the last 5 days, from October 15 to 19, 2020, the voter registration offices will be reopened at the commune / sangkat halls.
According to population and polling station statistics, the NEC plans to register 300,390 new voters and remove 123,251 names from the voter list, while 23,418 polling stations.
The review of the 2020 voter list and registration will take place from October 1 to 19, 2020, both Saturday and Sunday. Therefore, all Cambodians who have not yet registered to vote, please go and register to vote at the Commune / Sangkat Hall.
