Russia's new ambassador speaks Khmer fluently
(Phnom Penh): In the past, Cambodians used to admire the Japanese Ambassador to Cambodia, who was able to speak Khmer fluently while working in Cambodia. But now another Russian ambassador also speaks Khmer fluently.
Mr. Anatoly Borovik, the new Ambassador of the Russian Federation to Cambodia, paid a courtesy call on Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, at the Ministry of Foreign Affairs on the morning of October 1, 2020. Speak Khmer fluently.
Borovik's clear Khmer language caught the attention of Cambodian diplomats, especially Cambodian journalists. Foreign Ministry reporters similarly said that apart from the Japanese ambassador, they had never seen a Russian ambassador speak Khmer like this.
The fact that the Russian Ambassador can speak Khmer is because he has been working in Cambodia since the 1980s and has also studied Khmer literature.
