(Phnom Penh): Mr. Kong Vibol, the Royal Government delegate in charge of the Director General of the General Department of Taxation, on October 1, 2020, emphasized that the tax on capital gains is not created to oppress the people, but on the contrary. Will help poor people.
Mr. Kong Vibol made this emphasis in the program "Tax of Cambodia" on the tax on capital gains organized by the General Department of Taxation this morning, October 1, 2020.
According to the General Department of Taxation, the tax on capital gains is beneficial for the poor as well as for rural development, roads, wells and ponds.
In connection with the claim that the tax was created to suppress the people, Mr. Kong Vibol said that it is a misconception that all people who own real estate must be taxed, but not unless they can sell and make a profit. This tax.
In addition, Mr. Kong Vibol pointed out that the tax on capital gains, compared to other countries, Cambodia has the highest preference for this tax.
Mr. Kong Vibol said that the tax from capital gains, the Royal Government to help hundreds of thousands of workers in need and people living in poverty and to maintain some infrastructure.
At the same time, Mr. Kong Vibol also stated that on January 1, 2021, the General Department of Taxation will start to apply this capital gains tax, unless there is a change in any decision of the Royal Government through Ministry of Economy and Finance.
According to Van Puthipol, undersecretary of state at the Ministry of Economy and Finance, the top 90 percent of taxpayers are those in the real estate business, but not the general population. Sales of real estate are taxable only for profit. Cambodia-Singapore hold talks on draft warehousing development agreement in Phnom Penh
(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, this morning, October 1, 2020, led a delegation to a meeting between senior Cambodian and Singaporean officials via video to discuss a draft framework agreement. Khan for the development of Phnom Penh Logistics Center.
The meeting was also attended by senior leaders of relevant ministries and institutions of the two countries, including the leaders of YCH and IA, in order to discuss the draft framework agreement as well as gather additional input from all relevant institutions. This agreement has legal content and can be accepted by all parties, especially to serve the national interest as a whole in line with the long-term vision of the Royal Government.
The senior minister said that to push the project to run more smoothly and move forward. According to the plan, the ministry is looking for development partners and reports to the management for further guidance and guidance before the next meeting.
Please note that the logistics center is a warehouse for the distribution of goods in the country and continue to distribute to other countries and a place for the collection of goods from abroad to make it easier to distribute. Hold other countries as well.
