(Phnom Penh): Automated car ownership transfer system that allows car owners to apply for online ownership was announced on September 30, 2020.
The transfer of ownership of a car is seen as more complicated because of the transfer procedure. This difficulty has led to some car sales not having the transfer of ownership between the old car owners to the sub-owners. Buying and selling a car without transferring ownership also causes a lot of complications when the car has legal issues.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol stated that the automated vehicle ownership transfer system will facilitate the management of all types of vehicles in Cambodia, provide legal ownership to vehicle owners, and contribute to the collection of taxes, ensure security, order, social safety and prevention. Various imitations to be effective.
He added that through the reform of digital technology, people will be more comfortable and able to access public services with transparency, efficiency and accountability.
Minister Sun Chanthol emphasized that the automated vehicle ownership transfer system can help reduce the complexity for people who come to receive public services from the Ministry of Public Works and Transport and to provide timely services, reduce other official costs through automated systems. This has already set the price, just pay the price, the budget will go into the national budget, not elsewhere.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol urges people who have bought or sold registered vehicles but have not yet transferred their vehicle ownership to transfer their vehicle ownership in order to legally own their vehicles and be free from liability. Laws such as car accident or car crime.
Please note that after applying for car ownership online, vehicle owners can pick up the vehicle identification card or credit card at the service center at Chip Monoromol Mall along Norodom Blvd., Sangkat Tonle Bassac, Khan Chamkarmon or at Provide other services.
