(Phnom Penh): His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of Cambodia, has issued a Royal Decree appointing Em Chanmakara as Secretary of State for the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation in addition to his current position. This is according to the King's Royal Decree, which was received by Fresh News on October 1, 2020.
Starting as a simple member of the activities to serve the interests of Cambodian children from the age of 13, in 1997, Em Chanmakara developed himself by striving to fulfill the role of building many works for the people and the royal family. The Government of Cambodia until the following positions and positions:
He is currently the Secretary of State of the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation and the Secretary General of the General Secretariat of the Disability Action Council, with the rank of Senior Official, Level 3 of the Administrative Officer of the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation.
Medals and medals of the Kingdom of Cambodia that have been awarded:
Background:
Before becoming Secretary of State of the Ministry of Social Affairs, Em Chanmakara started social work at the age of 13 and was well known for advocating and promoting children's rights, making many people understand the value of children. Which is an important component of society. Based on this conscience, Em Chanmakara has been struggling to overcome all obstacles for the cause of children since 1997.
In 2011, Mr. Em Chanmakara had the opportunity to serve the state as Chief of the Cabinet of Ministers and Minister of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation.
Mr. Em Chanmakara received his high school diploma from Boeung Trabek High School in 202, received a bachelor's degree in law from the Royal University of Law and Economics in 2006 and a master's degree in 2014.
