Chbar Ampov District Governor Distributes Donations to 73 Families in Veal Sbov Community and Calls for Continuation of Kovid-19 Prevention
(Phnom Penh): Chbar Ampov District Governor Mr. Cheng Monira this morning, October 1, 2020, led a working group to visit and distribute gifts to 73 families in Veal Sbov community, Sangkat Kbal Koh, Chbar Ampov district.
On that occasion, Mr. Cheng Monira also received a message from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross to all the people who have always considered. And care for local people.
Especially for the poor, the poor, the disabled, the people living with HIV / AIDS, especially during the period of Kovid-19, etc., both princes instructed the authorities at all levels to consider the well-being and difficulties Of the people to solve in time.
In addition, the district governor emphasized that although there is currently no Kovid-19 infection in the community in Cambodia, we must all be careful and take care of the environment around us. Follow the guidelines of the Ministry of Health, such as washing your hands with soap or alcohol and wearing a mask.
At the same time, Mr. Cheng Monira also addressed the questions of the people and accepted the request to solve them continuously without leaving the people living in the Veal Sbov community in trouble.
