Citizens, please prepare documents! Authorities declare a systematic land registration jurisdiction in Sangkat Phleung Cheh Roret, Khan Kambol
(Phnom Penh): Phnom Penh Municipal Authority announces the area of systematic land registration (hard plan) in Sangkat Pleung Cheh Roteh, Khan Kambol for the people to occupy and use both residential and agricultural land legally. Reduce any disputes arising from land issues and announce to the people to prepare the relevant documents.
The launching ceremony was held on the morning of October 1, 2020 under the chairmanship of Mr. Ben Sochi, Deputy Director of the Department of Land Management, Urban Planning, Construction and Cadastral Affairs of Phnom Penh and Mr. Khim Sunsoda, Governor of Kampol District.
According to the report, there are a total of 4,500 plots of land in Phleung Cheh Roteh commune, including 4,400 residential plots and 100 agricultural plots. There are 53 plots of land with title deeds, while the land holdings of 1,500 local families and 3,500 non-local families.
Mr. Ben Sochi explained to all the people about the procedure of land registration in a systematic way or in simple language called solid planning to prepare enough relevant documents such as court verdict, inheritance, identity card, book Family, residence book, birth certificate, old card, agricultural receipt and card distributed by the team to show to the team who measured and made the plan.
On the other hand, in relation to land, there is a title, but there is no history. Define boundaries and have the consent of the owners of adjacent land. If the land is still unresolved, the team can not measure and issue a title deed.
At the same time, Mr. Khim Sunsoda pointed out that Kambol district has 7 communes, of which 5 communes have registered land systematically. In particular, in Sangkat Phleung Cheh Roteh, there are many land issues because the land has not been registered systematically.
He added that in the past, the district has resolved a lot of disputes between people and people, most of which are overlapping, and some lost documents, lost receipts, but asked the district to get a new card, and the district. Follow the procedure as follows.
