(Banteay Meanchey): Police in Serei Sophorn City, Banteay Meanchey Province arrested two youths in connection with drug distribution and use and confiscated some exhibits on September 30, 2020.
The arrest of the two suspects was led by Brigadier General Yan Sovann, Commander of the Serey Sophorn City Gendarmerie, who raided the location where the two young men were selling and smoking at the mouth of the Keab River in Keab Village, Sangkat Teuk Thla, Serey Sophorn City. Banteay Meanchey Province.
Mr. Yan Sovann continued that the two suspects were named Ly Vannak, male, 27 years old, false occupation and the second: Huon Kimhong, male, 29 years old, occupation worker. Both suspects live in Keab Village, Sangkat Teuk Thla, Serey Sophorn City, Banteay Meanchey Province.
The confiscated items include: 2 small bags of methamphetamine, ice 3.90 grams, 1 motorcycle, 2 mobile phones, 1 watch and some other items.
After questioning and testing the urine, it was found that one suspect was involved in a case of storage and the other was involved in a case of illegal use of drugs. The two suspects were sent to the Provincial Gendarmerie Headquarters to build a case to be sent to court for legal proceedings.
