(Kampong Chhnang): The President and staff of LOD Real Estate Company (LOD) Branch in Kampong Chhnang Province, a total of 4 people were arrested by the Gendarmerie on September 29, 2020 in connection with the case of intentional destruction of property in Kampong Chhnang village South rice field, Chulsa commune, Chulkiri district, Kampong Chhnang province.
The victim is Leang Kim Chheang, male, 20 years old, living in Kampong Basrov village, Chulsa commune, Chulkiri district, Kampong Chhnang province.
Lieutenant Colonel Hang Socheat, Deputy Commander of Kampong Chhnang Provincial Gendarmerie Command, confirmed that the four suspects were involved in breaking into the debtor's house to seize the motorcycle that the debtor had paid in installments with the company. The above is due to the debtor failing to pay interest for 3 months.
In the seizure of a motorcycle from a debtor, three employees of the company acted by breaking the chain lock, which the motorcycle owner locked to prevent theft. After unlocking the motorcycle chain, they took the debtor's motorcycle to the village chief's house.
According to the commander, the case where the organization staff went to cut the motorcycle chain from the debtor was on the order of the LOD boss in Kampong Chhnang province without the consent of the debtor and the commune authorities. In particular, there is no permission from the Prosecutor's Office of the Kampong Chhnang Provincial Court.
After the incident, the victim, who is a debtor, reported to the prosecutor of the provincial court and the authorities to intervene. The victim said the suspect broke into his home without permission and confiscated one of his motorcycles without his consent.
Meanwhile, after receiving reports from residents, Mr. Ith Sothea, Prosecutor of Kampong Chhnang Provincial Court, ordered the military police to go to the scene immediately and arrested three youths immediately and reached The arrest of the company president at the Kampong Chhnang branch.
The four suspects are currently being processed by the military and sent to the provincial prosecutor's office for further investigation. General Miech Sophanna presents five strategies to combat counterfeit and substandard medicines in Cambodia Europe
(Phnom Penh): General Miech Sophanna, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Interior and Chairman of the Anti-Counterfeiting Products Committee (CPPCC), led a number of senior officials to participate and serve as speakers at the Asia-Europe Forum on Fight against counterfeit and substandard medicines through a video system conducted from September 29 to 30, 2020 and organized by the Ministry of Health of Cambodia with the support of the Asia-Europe Foundation.
The leadership of the General to attend the Asia-Europe Forum of the General was made at the invitation of the Minister of Health, Mr. Mam Bunheng, and with the permission of Samdech Chakra Tbahom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior.
The Asia-Europe Forum features keynote speakers representing the 53 Asia-Europe Member States (30 in the EU and 21 in the ASEAN Community), as well as a number of development partners. In this forum, on the afternoon of September 30, 2020, General Miech Sophanna made a presentation on the strategy to implement the law to fight against counterfeit and substandard drugs in the Kingdom of Cambodia.
The senior official of the Ministry of Interior stated that the CPP has implemented five strategies to combat counterfeit and substandard medicines in Cambodia, including:
1: Raise the issue of counterfeit products on a global scale at the national, regional and international levels.
* National level: Raise awareness through media coverage, campaigns and seminars, etc. * Hold regional conferences on combating counterfeit drugs and products in Phnom Penh (November 5-6, 2018). At the same time, it also has the support of the United Nations.
