Representative of the British Embassy in Cambodia visits "Samdech Mey Library"
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Max Theary Phearaktheary, Representative of the British Embassy in Cambodia, on the afternoon of September 30, 2020, visited the Samdech Mey Library of the Documentation Institute of the Documentation Center of Cambodia.
Youk Chhang presented the guests of the Documentation Library, Audiovisual Library and Digital Archives of the Documentation Center of Cambodia with a detailed description of the design and background of the Institute of Manuscripts, the work of world-class architect Zaha Hadid. Of British descent, Iraqi.
In 2010 and 2011, her architectural work received the Sterling Award from the British Institute of Architects. UNESCO has named Zaha Hadid as "Artist for Peace". The French Republic honors Zaha Hadid with the Medal of Arts and Literature.
In 2012, Queen Elizabeth II presented the Queen with a Medal of Honor. In 2016, prior to her death, Zaha Hadid was the only female architect and the first in more than 160 years to receive a Royal Gold Medal from the British Royal Institution of Architecture.
Mr. Max Theary expressed his deep interest in the Samdech Mey Library, as well as the documentation work of the Documentation Center of Cambodia and the work related to the tribunal prosecuting the Khmer Rouge leaders, especially on the design of the Leaf Institute, the permanent location of the Documentation Center of Cambodia. He posed a number of important questions about the historical process.
