Pursat City Police Crack Down on Drug Offenses in 2 Different Locations, Arrested 6 Suspects
(Pursat): The intervention force and anti-drug crime force of the Municipal Police Inspectorate cooperated with the police force to crack down on drug offenses in 2 different locations, arrest 6 suspects and confiscate a large number of exhibits .
The above operation took place at 11:38 AM on September 29, 2020 at the point of Dey Krahorm Road in the village of Transit and at the point of carving in the village of O Thkov, Sangkat Roleap, Pursat City, Pursat Province.
Sources from the police said that in the first case, at Dey Krahorm Road in the village of Chhlang, Sangkat Roleap, Pursat City, the police cracked down on cases of illegal storage, trafficking and use of drugs, detaining 4 suspects, including :
First name: Rith Thursday, male, 23 years old, living in Roleap village, Sangkat Roleap, Pursat city, Pursat province, Second name: Moeun Samy, male, 20 years old, living in Tuol Krous village, Sangkat Chamroeun Phal, Pursat city, Pursat province, Third name: Sun Tak Male, 32 years old, living in Toul Krous Village, Sangkat Chamroeun Phal, Pursat City, Pursat Province, and 4th: Name: Thi Soeun, Male, 22 years old, living in O Thkov Village, Sangkat Roleap, Pursat City, Pursat Province.
Sources from the police said that the second case was at the point of sculpture in O Thkov village, Sangkat Roleap, Pursat city, the police have cracked down on cases of illegal use of drugs to detain 2 suspects, including:
First name: Seng Chantra, male, 25 years old, living in Phum Roleap, Sangkat Roleap, Pursat City, Pursat Province, and second name: Non Thanak, male, 30 years old, living in Koh Village, Sangkat Lolok Sor, Pursat City, Pursat Province.
Confiscated 1 set of drug smoking equipment, some smoked drug bags, 1 mobile phone and 1 recycled knife.
All six suspects, along with exhibits, are currently being held at the Pursat City Police Inspectorate for further proceedings.
Oddar Meanchey Provincial Governor Warns to Remove Any Officials Who Do Not Work and Have Irregular Problems
(Oddar Meanchey): Mr. Pen Kosal, Governor of Oddar Meanchey Province, said that all provincial governors, deputy governors, governors and deputy governors do not need to be removed or removed from office for a four-year term if there is no problem. Irregularities in the performance of duties within 3 to 6 months can be removed or removed from office.
Speaking at the inauguration ceremony of Banteay Ampil District Governor this morning, September 30, 2020, Mr. Pen Kosal added that the mandate is a number, if wrong, there is no internal solidarity with civil servants, the Armed Forces, the people. The leader has not progressed to the position, and if he waits, he will be removed from his position and will not have to reach the mandate.
Mr. Pen Kosal said that the change of officials now is not a mistake, because they have to change the mandate.
The provincial governor also instructed the district governor, who is to be announced to take office today, to do more good deeds, to find creative ideas to develop and build Banteay Ampil district to be more prosperous.
Please note that the new Banteay Ampil district governor to be announced at this time is Mr. Neou Sam Dararith, former governor of Trapeang Prasat district, Oddar Meanchey province. Representative of Director General of Prison Visits Preah Vihear Provincial Prison Officials
