The law was passed by a vote of 46 to 38, as part of a series of measures passed by parliament last Friday to strengthen austerity measures across the country. But debates in parliament over the measure came to an end when the government failed to attract support amid protests outside parliament on Tuesday.
The blockade went into effect on September 18, requiring the closure of most offices, markets, churches, schools and other cultural venues. In addition, it is forbidden to travel more than 1 km from home, but there are restrictions for important destinations such as shopping for food and medicine or receiving emergency medical treatment.
The new law will also give the government special powers to declare a state of emergency due to the coronavirus outbreak for a week. During that time, the 1km travel limit will apply to demonstrations and there will also be restrictions on the number of participants.
So far, the Israeli government has not used this power, but with more than 237,000 cases and 1,528 deaths in the more populous country. With 9 million people, Israel now has the highest per capita infection rate in the world.
Water well donated by Duke Prit Moha Upasika Thomman Vivathana Bun Seangly was handed over to people living in Svay Chrum district, Svay Rieng province
(Svay Rieng): Lieutenant Colonel Chheang Sovanratana led a team to hand over a water well donated by Duke Dean Vivathana Bun Seangly through Rev. Bun Samlen and her husband, children and grandchildren. People live in Krol commune, Svay Chrum district, Svay Rieng province.
Lieutenant Colonel Chheang Sovanratana said, "This well will help supply clean water and improve the well-being of students and people living in this community." In addition, our team has planted many trees near schools and wells to shade and enhance the beauty of the environment with a beautiful green nature, especially contributing to the preservation of the environment and inspire love. Naturally.
On that occasion, the Lieutenant Colonel also brought materials and study for students with some money. His team is committed to continuing to develop the villages, communes in this district to be even better, especially to improve the living standards of the people.
Please be informed that the clean water well, which was donated by the Duke of Priest Moha Vivathana Bun Seangly, will be handed over to the people living in Svay Chrum District, Svay Rieng Province for use on September 29, 2020 at a cost of about 4 million Riels.
Royal Message of the King of Cambodia to President Xi Jinping on the Occasion of the 71st Anniversary of the Establishment of the People's Republic of China
(Phnom Penh): His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of the Kingdom of Cambodia, sends a message to President Xi Jinping of the People's Republic of China on the special occasion of the 71st anniversary. Establishment of the People's Republic of China
In his message: "On behalf of the people of the whole Kingdom of Cambodia, I would like to take this opportunity to celebrate the 71st anniversary of the founding of the People's Republic of China and send my heartfelt congratulations to His Excellency, the Communist Party, the State Council, the Chinese People's Liberation Army, as well as the most courageous and great people of China.
China's success in eradicating poverty in rural areas and building a prosperous Chinese society is commendable.
The Kingdom of Cambodia has always stood shoulder to shoulder with the People's Republic of China and has always adhered to the one-China policy. We will continue to support His Excellency's Belt and Road Initiative, as well as the initiative to build a community with a shared future for humanity.
The Queen Mother and I would like to express our deep gratitude to His Excellency for welcoming us to check our health and rest in China at all times. We will always remember our first meeting, which was like a family reunion with His Excellency and His Excellency Peng Liyuan. We will continue to deepen this special friendship with you.
I wish you good health and success in all your endeavors to lead the People's Republic of China towards great peace, development and prosperity.
