(Phnom Penh): Officials from the Ministry of Tourism have identified four priority ecotourism community destinations that have great potential for tourism and are attracting a lot of tourists, but there is no further development assistance that requires assistance. Support from inter-ministerial-relevant institutions.
This was stated at the 5th meeting of the Inter-Ministerial Working Group on Management and Development of Community-Based Tourism and Ecotourism on September 30, 2020 at the Ministry of Tourism, chaired by Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, as the Chairman of the Inter-Ministerial Working Group. The Ministry will be joined by Mr. Say Sam Al, Minister of the Ministry of Environment and Permanent Deputy Chairman of the Inter-Ministerial Working Group.
On that occasion, the meeting mentioned 4 priority tourism community goals, including: Rolak Kang Cheung ecotourism community (Phnom Khnong Phsar) in Oral district, Kampong Speu province, Phat Sanday fishing community in Kampong Svay district, Kampong Thom province, Teuk Chob Khnar ecotourism community. Po is located in Sot Nikum district, Siem Reap province, and the Toul Porn Tali (Boeung Sneh) tourism community is located in Svay Anthor district, Prey Veng province.
The meeting continued that these four communities are newly established communities and have also just incorporated new tourism activities and services, which require additional development assistance to the community from the Ministry of Tourism and other relevant ministries and institutions.
The Ministry of Tourism will continue to research other priority tourism communities to help further develop in relation to the above cases.
Although the spread of Kovid-19 is a hindrance, it is also an opportunity to boost local tourism to tourism communities and ecotourism sites, which have contributed to mitigating the impact. From the Kovid disease. In the context of the Kovid-19 epidemic, tourist attitudes are turning to adventure tourism, community tourism and ecotourism rather than collective tourism destinations.
The Minister also made some recommendations to the meeting as well as some relevant inter-ministerial working groups, including:
* The Secretariat shall coordinate with the representatives of the relevant ministries and institutions to solve problems for the above communities.
* Agreed to organize the 2nd National Ecotourism Forum, but requested to organize in the spirit of the meeting and the actual situation in accordance with the tourism safety rules to prevent Kovid-19 disease.
* The Secretariat shall report the results of this meeting to the Royal Government for information and recommendations.
The working group must strive to hold the 6th working group meeting no later than 6 months to promote the resolution of community issues as we set out in this 5th meeting. UAE to build spacecraft to explore part of moon never-before-seen
