Dr. Mao Havannal and Duke Pung Kheav Se Inspect the Construction of the New Phnom Penh Airport and Accelerate the Construction
(Central): General Dr. Mao Ha Vannal, Minister in Charge of the Secretariat of Civil Aviation, and Duke Pung Kheav Se, President of the Cambodia Airport Construction Company (CAIC) this morning, September 30, 2020, led a delegation to inspect the construction of the International Airport. Phnom Penh Thmey, located in Kandal Province.
Oknha Pung Kheav Se, President of the Cambodian Airport Construction Company, which was awarded the right to build the new Phnom Penh Airport, stated that under the guidance of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, and the care of General Dr. Mao Havanal, he believed that Construction will go well according to plan.
Duke Pung Kheav Se said that the new Phnom Penh International Airport has received construction rights from the Royal Government and Civil Aviation is also the guardian of the airport.
Duke Pung Kheav Se emphasized that he would continue to inspect the construction of the airport at least once every six months to encourage the builders and speed up the construction according to plan.
General Dr. Mao Havanal stated that on behalf of the Secretariat of Civil Aviation, he and his team will do their best to support the activities of the new Phnom Penh Airport project to be successful, effective and supported by International community.
Dr. Mao Havanal said that what is being developed here is not in anyone's interest, but in the common interest to preserve the history of Khmer children. In particular, the new Phnom Penh Airport is a great achievement for the Royal Government during the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, a new history left for the Cambodian people for hundreds of years to come.
Construction of the 108-meter-high air control tower is scheduled for completion by the end of 2022.
Construction of more than 40 other buildings and facilities for the operation of the airport, including VIP passenger terminal, wastewater management facility, solid waste storage facility, vehicle repair facility, fuel storage facility and storage facility, fire station, etc.
Duke Pong Kheavse had previously stated that the construction work for the first phase was planned to cost 1,500 million US dollars, not including the value of the land, which could receive 13 million tourists a year. 2 will be completed by 2030 can receive 30 million tourists per year and the third phase will be completed in 2050 can receive 50 million tourists per year.
The Government Spokesperson's Unit Suspends the Press Conference on "Procedures for Implementing the Capital Profit Tax at the 20% Tax Rate" by Business Officials
(Phnom Penh): The Spokesperson of the Royal Government on September 30, 2020, issued a new announcement on the suspension of the press conference on "Procedures for the implementation of the tax on capital gains at the rate of 20%". Scheduled for October 1, 2020.
According to a press release from Fresh News, the reason why the Royal Government Spokesperson's Unit suspended the conference was because the professional officers of the General Department of Taxation had other duties and could not participate as honorary speakers.
The Royal Government Spokesperson added that all media outlets can contact the General Department of Taxation directly through the 1277 Call Center for information on the implementation of capital gains tax on GDT Facebook Live on Thursday. October 1, 2020 at 10:00 AM. Chip Mong Co., Ltd. provides location for Chip Mong No Rom Mall Shopping Center, providing registration, transfer of ownership and exchange of driver's license.
(Phnom Penh): In order to facilitate the provision of more convenient public services to the people, Chip Mong Company has provided the location of the third floor of the building "Chip Mong No Romol" on Norodom Blvd. in Tonle Bassac, Chamkarmon The Ministry of Public Works and Transport (MPWT) acts as a service center for vehicle registration, vehicle ownership transfer and driver's license exchange.
The opening ceremony of the center was held on Wednesday, September 30, 2020. Duke Leang Khun, CEO of Chip Mong, said at the ceremony that his company provided the Ministry of Public Works and Transport with a building location free of charge.
Duke Leang Khun stated that through its supermarket in the center of Phnom Penh, it will contribute to providing more convenient public services to people from all over. The CEO of a well-known company who has always been involved in development with the Royal Government considers the location of this shopping mall as a partnership with the Royal Government to bring better public services.
Duke Leang Khun emphasized that "the provision of free centers is a reflection of the position of Chip Mong, a local company in joining the Royal Government, to improve the provision of public services and to facilitate "People are using vehicles everywhere."
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, stated that the provision of public services easier and closer to people's homes is a strong desire of the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
The senior minister thanked Chip Mong for providing a location for car registration, car ownership transfer and driver's license exchange, which made it easier for the people. The senior minister stressed that this is a good collaboration between the private sector and the government.
Senior Minister Sun Chan, a prominent minister in the modernization of public services, emphasized that "this is a good cooperation between the Royal Government and the private sector, it is very important that the Royal Government can not do anything alone without the contribution of Private sector. This shows the close relationship between the private sector and our government.
Not only providing location, car registration service, car ownership transfer and driver's license exchange to the people, Chip Mong through its bank "Chip Mong Beng" also cooperates with the Ministry of Public Works and Transport to provide Citizens to pay for all public services and car registration services, transfer car ownership and easily change the driver's license.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol made the announcement at the inauguration of a car registration and transfer license center at Chip Mon Noromol Mall along Norodom Boulevard in Tonle Bassac commune, Chamkarmon district.
Mr. Sun Chanthol considered that the process of selling more personal license plates is a success in launching this service to meet the needs of car users and also raised funds to support the national economy.
This "personal special license plate" can be purchased for life by simply deleting the name when selling the car or they can sell the license plate when selling the car. The owner of the license plate can also keep this license plate for posterity, just by exchanging information about who will continue to control the license plate.
Notably, part of the proceeds from the sale of this special personal license plate was brought to Kantha Bopha Hospital by the Ministry.
