(World): In the world today, three major eras have been selected for use in daily life, including the Buddhist era, the Christian era and the Mahamat era, as these eras are associated with religious events. Large, closely related since ancient times.
Related to this point, there are also some questions asked how they count the years of each era and from when? On the other hand, how was the counting of the years before those eras? These questions are answered as follows: * About the era and the beginning of the year.
But the chronology of the Buddhist era in Siam is not the same as in other countries, because the Siamese set the chronology of the Buddhist era, one year after the Buddha's death, from the 15th day of the month of Pisak. One year after the Buddha's Nirvana. Currently, Cambodia, Myanmar, Laos and Sri Lanka have reached the Buddhist era in 2564, but Siam is still counting the Buddhist era to 2563.
Lt. Gen. Mao Sophan expresses his deepest gratitude to the retired and disabled soldiers who sacrificed their lives for the cause of national liberation
Lt. Gen. Mao Sophan made this statement on the morning of September 30, 2020, when he was invited to represent Lt. Gen. Hun Manet, Deputy Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces (RCAF). Awarded medals to retired and disabled soldiers with the participation of representatives of the 1st Office of the Army, Deputy Commanders, Officers, Deputy Officers and Soldiers in the 70th Brigade Headquarters.
The lieutenant general said that retired and disabled soldiers have contributed to maintaining peace, security, social order and contributing to the development of the country under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, which has made Cambodia a glorious success. Historically.
On that occasion, 26 retired and disabled soldiers also received an additional incentive of 1,200,000 Riels, of which 200,000 Riels was a precious gift from Lt. Gen. Hun Manet. And Mrs. Pech Chanmony and 1,000,000 Riels as a donation from the 70th Brigade Command and some other food items. The National Assembly will hold its 5th session of the 6th legislature on October 5 with 11 agendas
