Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit allow their husbands to see their children and take care of their pregnant wives
(Phnom Penh): A 29-year-old man named So Dara, who had a 5-year-old baby and his wife was about to give birth, was released from Kampong Speu Provincial Prison on May 9, 2020. He was released on bail after receiving the deepest condolences from Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen on September 25, 2020.
But later, due to the situation of his wife and young children in need of special care, Phan Sokuntheary, his wife and mother, was released on bail before her husband due to pregnancy and childbirth. Chronic back surgery recently.
Due to a chronic illness and close to the time of delivery, Phan Sokuntheary's sister suffered greatly due to the lack of a family support and had to take care of a 5-year-old child alone. Regularly unable to earn a living.
Due to the deadlock, Ms. Phan Sokuntheary applied for the mercy and mercy of Samdech Techo Prime Minister through Samdech's official page to help her husband get out of jail to take care of her. Chronic and near-term disease.
After reviewing the request and the report of the couple, Samdech Techo Prime Minister and Samdech Kittipritthbandit were very sympathetic and sent Mr. Duong Dara, Samdech's personal assistant, in cooperation with the Governor of Kampong Speu, General Commission of the National Police to study This case is thoroughly detailed.
Receiving the highest level of guidance from Samdech Techo, Mr. Duong Dara led the case study team to examine the facts and the law and prepared documents and letters of guarantee for Ms. Phan Sokuntheary to secure her husband So Dara. Bail in accordance with legal procedures.
Since So Dara was charged with misdemeanor and no serious harm, as well as the law, the Investigating Judge of Kampong Speu Provincial Court decided to release the accused on September 25, 2020.
Phan Sokuntheary and Sodara were overjoyed and expressed their deepest gratitude to the two Samdechs for their generosity in freeing and reuniting their beloved family. . This precious and precious merit makes people all over the country excited on behalf of the family of Phan Sokuntheary and wish both Samdechs good health to lead Cambodia forever.
Deputy Governor of Svay Rieng Province: Vocational training plays an important role in reducing poverty!
(Svay Rieng): Mr. Ros Pharith, Deputy Governor of Svay Rieng Province, said that the employment and vocational training sector has an important role to reduce the poverty of the people by providing employment opportunities to those who are looking for work by providing Technical and vocational education and training to increase human resources in order to improve living standards by increasing household income.
On that occasion, he also expressed his appreciation to the civil servants of Techo Sen Svay Rieng Polytechnic Institute for their hard work in fulfilling the mission for the nation and success.
He stated that in the context of the world being plagued by Kovid-19, he also reminded her, especially the young students to take care of themselves, take care of their health, try to create a social gap. To prevent the spread of this deadly disease. But Cambodia is very lucky that Samdech Techo's leadership has the right strategy and timely measures to prevent the disease from spreading to the community.
He added that Techo Sen Svay Rieng Polytechnic Institute is responsible for major tasks during the technological development phase, as well as the fourth generation Industrial Revolution (IR4.0) to improve the quality of training and productivity of workers in the region. Especially in Svay Rieng province.
He also requested you to cooperate with the Institute in determining the subject of study, curriculum development to be in line with the current labor market situation and to cooperate in providing a place for trainees to study as well as receive trainees. Students to work at the end of graduation.
He also called on all factories to deepen cooperation and sign MoUs to meet each other's needs in the framework of public-private cooperation in order to upgrade skills in line with technology. Current and productive work. Secretariat of the Disability Action Council Holds a Dissemination Workshop on the National Strategic Plan on Disability 2019-2023 in Svay Rieng Province
(Svay Rieng): The General Secretariat of the Council for Disability Action (ACD) in collaboration with Svay Rieng Provincial Administration this morning, September 30, 2020, organized a workshop to disseminate the National Strategic Plan on Disability 2019-2023 and Technical standards for physical infrastructure make it easier for people with disabilities to become members of the Disability Action Council in Svay Rieng province.
According to Ms. Prak Thav Pheary, the Royal Government of Cambodia has made the disability sector a priority in other key priority areas, as defined in the Rectangular Strategy on the Implementation of the Disability Policy through the Establishment of a National Social Protection Policy Framework. Strengthen the implementation of the Law on the Protection and Promotion of the Rights of Persons with Disabilities;
In particular, Cambodia has introduced a number of important laws, regulations and policies to ensure non-discrimination, equal opportunities and full participation of people with disabilities in society.
She informed the whole workshop that at present at the national level, there are 21 ministries and institutions that have established the Disability Action Working Group, while at the sub-national level, the Disability Action Council has also been established in 25 capitals and provinces.
