The Royal Government has decided to continue to support workers in the garment-tourism sector and to provide tax incentives to the tourism-aviation sector until the end of 2020
(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Cambodia on September 30, 2020 decided to continue to provide cash subsidies to workers in the garment and tourism sector and tax incentives for tourism and aviation until the end of December 2020. .
After the factories, enterprises and businesses in the garment, textile, footwear, travel products, bags and tourism sectors received a permit to suspend the employment contract and / or a permit to extend the suspension of the employment contract, the statement said. From the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, after meeting the criteria and conditions for the suspension of the employment contract, the Royal Government of Cambodia will:
* Continue to provide a stipend of US $ 40 per month to 1 worker working in the tourism sector, such as hotels, guesthouses, restaurants and travel agencies for an additional 3 months until the end of December 2020. Enterprises and businesses in the tourism sector must contribute on a voluntary and practical basis in addition to what the Royal Government has to offer.
* Continue to exempt all types of monthly taxes for hotels, guesthouses, restaurants and travel agencies registered with the General Department of Taxation and have business activities in Phnom Penh, Siem Reap, Sihanoukville, Kep, Kampot , Bavet and Poipet for an additional 3 months from October to December 2020.
* Continue to extend the payment of social security obligations on pensions until the end of December 2020. The delay will be based on the actual economic situation again before December 2020. If the economic situation returns to normal, pension payments will begin normally, in which the employer pays 2% and the employee pays 2%. In the event that the impact does not diminish, the Royal Government will consider alternatives to assist factories - enterprises and employees.
* Exemption from the payment of patent tax and nominal tax and postponing the full audit for 2020 by the General Department of Taxation to travel agencies and other tourism operators.
Separately, for further measures to help the aviation sector, the Royal Government has decided to extend the Minimum Tax exemption for an additional three months from October to December 2020 to airlines registered in Cambodia and to extend Payments for civil aviation fees for an additional two months until the end of December 2020 with the permission of the airlines to arrange for the payment of such debts in stages after this extension.
Spokesman for the General Commission: On September 30, another 658 vehicles were inspected and fined
According to the spokesperson of the General Commissioner, within 153 days of tightening the road traffic law by increasing the fine according to Sub-Decree No. 39, from May 1 to September 30, 2020, the traffic police nationwide inspected And fined a total of 180,835 vehicles, including 133,809 motorcycles and 47,026 vehicles of all types.
The most notable offenses for motorcycles are not wearing a helmet, not having a license plate, being drunk and using a mobile phone. In particular, the offenses for cars are mostly speeding, overcrowding, driving licenses, no seat belts, drunkenness and using mobile phones.
Lt. Gen. Chhay Kimkhoeun continued that for the past 153 days, the implementation of the new sub-decree to fine the offending vehicles has been going well. He thanked and commended all the road users for their good obedience to the traffic law so far, especially the traffic police for their dedication and hard work. Tighten traffic with the highest sense of responsibility.
Please note that for September 30, 2020, traffic accidents across Cambodia also occurred 9 times, in which 5 people died and 9 people were injured (05 people were seriously injured).
