(Preah Vihear): The authorities of Cheb district, Preah Vihear province of Cambodia and Khong district authority of Champasak province of Laos are jointly committed to further strengthen good relations and cooperation with each other to provide warmth to the people. Who live along the border.
This joint commitment of the authorities of the two border districts of Cambodia and Laos was made on September 29, 2020 on the occasion of the Cambodian side led by Mr. Sok Santara, Governor of Chhep District, Preah Vihear Province. Dithy Sak Khamphou, Governor of Khong District, Champasak Province, Laos, in the auditorium of Yor Kampong Sralao Secondary School in Kampong Sralao 1 Commune, Cheb District, Preah Vihear Province.
On that occasion, Mr. Sok Santara said that Chhep and Khong districts had stopped meeting for two or three months. In particular, the current meeting is focused on strengthening the relationship and good cooperation between Cheb district, Preah Vihear province and Khong district, Champasak province of Laos, as well as discussing the challenges that have arisen along the border of the two districts. Two.
Mr. Sok Santara said that in order for the people along the border of both districts to live in peace and harmony, which has always been considered as a brother for a long time, he also asked the Khong district to discuss some solutions. Born in the past to make sure that the problem does not become a protracted wound that affects the good relations of the districts along the Cambodia-Laos border.
Meanwhile, the governor of Chhep district said that today, people living along the border of the two districts have not yet implemented the law 100 percent related to the border from Cambodia to Laos, as well as from Laos to Cambodia. This is because the two sides have not yet opened a joint international port.
Mr. Sok Santara emphasized that when the two sides open the international border, we will guide the people to change their habits by turning to the law, which leads to the convenience of the people of the two countries. In crossing the border legally. However, the governor of Chhep district also requested the people of the two countries to maintain good unity forever because it is the intention of the heads of government of the two countries.
The governor of Chhep district also said that Cambodia has a BLO border liaison office and the Lao side also has a border police, so any problems at the border must be resolved immediately so that no problem becomes a wound. .
In addition, Mr. Sok Santara also set out two principles for the two district authorities to implement, including: Organizing meetings of the BLO Cambodia and the BLO of Laos every month and second: the relationship between Chhep and Khong districts must be based on resolving various issues, with the two district administrations resolving the issue and committing to crack down on cross-border crime effectively and jointly maintain sanitation to prevent Kovid-19 disease.
In response, Ms. Dittisak Khamphou said she was pleased to attend a meeting with the Cambodian side to jointly resolve past issues.
"Even though a small number of people are still breaking the law, she, on behalf of the Khong District Authority, will continue to advise them to respect the laws of each country in order to maintain peace and live in peace," she said. Stung Treng Provincial Governor and US Ambassador Visit Borey O'Svay Sen Chey District to Discover the Potential of the Area
