Samdech Techo Hun Sen Highlights 5 Points in the Meeting of the Heads of Government on "Financing the Sustainable Development Agenda 2030 in the Context of Kovid 19 and the Future" (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): In the Meeting of the Heads of Government on Agenda for Sustainable Development 2030 in the context of Kovid 19 and the future "On September 29, 2020, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, highlighted five key points.
According to a speech received by Fresh News, Samdech Techo Hun Sen said: “I would like to highlight some of the priority work related to financing issues, which is an important way to serve the efforts of developing countries in Achieve the 2030 Agenda as follows:
1. Turning the threat of Kovid 19 into an opportunity for reform in each country to strengthen economic competitiveness, create a favorable environment for doing business and strengthen state revenue collection. At the same time, we must prioritize the nationalization of the national budget by focusing on relevant sectors with the goal of sustainable development 2030, such as education, health, social protection, agriculture and infrastructure.
2. Promoting trade policies and trade facilitation, as well as giving preferential treatment to developing countries to ensure that the benefits of globalization are distributed equitably and effectively. In this spirit, the world needs to continue to promote and support the principle of globalization through the opening up of international trade and the strengthening of multilateralism.
3: Continuing to strengthen the stability and diversification of the financial sector, innovation and improving the role and livelihood of the private sector to meet the financial needs to serve the goals of the 2030 Agenda through the introduction of incentives and investment promotion; Private capital inflows into developing countries, especially the promotion of foreign direct investment and the promotion of public-private partnership mechanisms.
4. Continuing to ensure the sustainability of international aid, especially financial assistance to developing countries, to continue to drive the reform process to serve the 2030 Agenda.
5. Continuing to strengthen the ownership of developing countries by building partnerships between all development actors, including bilateral, multilateral development partners, the private sector and other development actors.
According to Samdech Techo Hun Sen's speech, in addition, we must also ensure a harmonious, transparent and accountable relationship between the policies of development partners, both bilateral and multilateral, with policy priorities. Nation in the context of Kovid 19 and beyond for the purpose of sustainable development.
