(Banteay Meanchey): Mr. Oum Rath, Governor of Banteay Meanchey Province and Chairman of the Provincial Unity Command, led a combined force of more than 200 people to push down the rotten and congested bar in Stung Phneat in Phneat Sangkat, Serey Sophorn City, Banteay Meanchey Province. The beauty of the river will make it easier for the fish and the biodiversity of the river to survive.
The provincial governor emphasized during the visit to the bar on September 29, 2020 that Stung Phneat is a place for fish conservation and also a source of water for the people. This scavenger bar cleans the environment, makes the water clean for the fish to live on, and also draws clean water for the people to use.
Brigadier General Born Bin, Commander of the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Gendarmerie, who led about 55 provincial police forces in the operation, said that in addition to the core work of maintaining security and order, social work is also a task. Of the Gendarmerie as well. The Commander of the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Gendarmerie considers this visit to be a contribution to social work.
Brigadier General Born Bin also called on the people to keep clean and clean the environment to avoid the dumping of waste that can damage the environment in the river after the bar is ready.
Lt. Gen. Ey Sok Khy calls on private security company owners to continue sending their agents for training from the National Police
(Phnom Penh): Lt. Gen. E Sok Khi, Deputy Commissioner General of the National Police, on the evening of September 29, 2020, called on private security service providers to continue sending their security agents to receive private security training from the National Police. To strengthen the capacity to participate in maintaining security and social order.
On the occasion of presiding over the representative of General Dr. Neth Savoeun, General Commissioner of the National Police, at the closing ceremony of the 28th Private Security Agency Training Course and handed over the certificates to the trainees as private security agents, Lt. Gen. E Sok Khi highlighted the reasons for the training. This skill is to strengthen the capacity and to keep up with what is the progress of today's society.
At the same time, Lt. Gen. Ey Sok Khi also expressed his appreciation and sent a message to the private security agencies who have just received this training as follows:
* Ask all participants to take the knowledge from this study to expand and disseminate to their colleagues to apply in their work in companies and institutions.
* Contribute to the maintenance of security and social order, especially to jointly implement the policy of the Royal Government, which has issued the policy of safe villages and communes, and contribute to the prevention of crimes that occur at the local level.
* Must strive to further strengthen the professional capacity, respect the qualifications as a private security agent, the trust of customers, increase trust and enhance the dignity of the functions they perform.
* Increase cooperation with the authorities and local authorities by being good citizens, good masses, an important support force to the competent authorities to report crimes that have occurred immediately to the authorities and good cooperation to respond. Time.
In addition, Lt. Gen. E Sok Khi also requested the Department of Private Security Management to continue to pay attention to encourage the continuation of the training course, and in this situation must also consider the safety and prevention of Kovid-19.
