(Ratanakkiri): Senior Minister Ly Thuch, First Deputy Chairman of the Mines Authority and Chairman of the Mines Authority, said that Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, as a builder and peace lover, wanted to see Cambodia no longer threatened by cluster munitions.
The Senior Minister informed the meeting that after receiving permission from Samdech Techo Prime Minister, the Senior Minister selected the territory of Ratanakkiri Province, which was the most affected by the cluster munitions for the visit between W. Patrick Murphy. US Ambassador to Cambodia and Mines Authority leaders on September 30, 2020, whose visit will focus on cluster munitions clearance in Cambodia.
The Senior Minister also thanked donors and other outstanding friends, including Australia, the United Kingdom, Japan, Germany, Switzerland, China, Norway, South Korea, Canada, New Zealand, Ireland, UNDP and UNICEF, as well as civil society funds and philanthropists.
Minister Veng Sakhon welcomed and congratulated her on being supported by the World Food Program and appointed as the new Program Director for Cambodia.
On this occasion, Minister Veng Sakhon also thanked the World Food Program for providing humanitarian cooperation to reduce and eradicate hunger and promote nutrition worldwide, including in Cambodia. Also.
Minister Veng Sakhon added that under the leadership of the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, there was complete peace and political stability, and this remarkable achievement pushed Cambodia from a food insecure country for its people to a country with a food surplus. Export agricultural products to many countries as well.
Regarding agricultural support programs, Minister Veng Sakhon also praised the efforts of the World Food Program (WFP) to support the development of market information systems.
Meanwhile, Minister Veng Sakhon added that in terms of nutrition in Cambodia is progressing well, now Cambodia has a dairy farm and produce milk with high nutrients for the people. Especially for children.
She added that in the agricultural sector, the goal of World Food Program (WFP) support is to encourage smallholder farmers to increase local agricultural production to create jobs and increase household incomes.
In addition, create a food system that can reduce post-harvest losses and disasters, climate change, increase farmers' capacity and help farmers fill value-added production chains. All of this, she said, will help develop and protect society, ensure food security and access to food, especially contributing to the national economy.
Therefore, she hopes and believes that the cooperation between the World Food Program and the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries will continue to be effective and sustainable.
Minister Veng Sakhon welcomed the new goal of the World Food Program (WFP) in supporting agriculture, which he said was in line with the ministry's vision, focusing on training farmers to be creative in planting and promoting agriculture. Use modern technology to enable them to increase income, improve living standards and family nutrition.
Minister Veng Sakhon and his colleagues are pleased and welcome to cooperate with the World Food Program to jointly develop Cambodia's agricultural sector to grow to another level. Thailand prepares to reopen tourism with first flight from China
BANGKOK: Thailand will welcome foreign tourists for the first time when flights from China arrive next week, marking a resumption, a senior Thai official said on Tuesday. Gradually, tourism in this ASEAN country has also been severely affected by the closure measures. This was released by Reuters on Tuesday evening, September 28, 2020.
