Mr. Sok Touch urges young people not to drop out of school and to be determined to build knowledge and capacity to participate in social development
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Sok Touch, President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, sent a message to all young Cambodians that young people must not drop out of school, but must strive to build knowledge and capacity to participate in the development of society and the nation. All together.
Such a message by Dr. Sok Touch held a roundtable discussion on "The importance of choosing a major in higher education and post-graduate" on September 29, 2020. At the same time, he said that learning is not to be rich, but to be able to stand taller and look farther, and those who are strong choose their profession according to their talents.
Dr. also recommended to the whole forum, "Those who are strong choose the profession according to their talents, not according to the needs of the labor market, because the market is our creator, no one is our creator. " This is a message to students who are considering in deciding to choose a major in higher education, especially students who will be graduating from high school in the coming months.
(Phnom Penh): The Honorable Dr. Men Sam An, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Assembly-Senate Relations and Inspection, presided over the welcoming ceremony for the Lunar New Year and the celebration of the National Independence Day of the People's Republic of China, organized by the China Business Association. In Cambodia (Love Tiffany Restaurant) on the night of September 29, 2020.
Deputy Prime Minister Men Sam An said that under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Cambodia has achieved good political stability and development in all areas, especially investment, trade and tourism. The Royal Government also strives to protect investors based on the principle of good political stability to promote business and production in the circumstances of the garment sector is facing difficulties, the Royal Government has resolved the budget for workers.
The Royal Government of Cambodia has also set out a number of policies to develop the economy and society, in which the policy of national and religious harmony has created conditions for all races and ethnic groups living in Cambodia to live with. Together in harmony and together develop our motherland together.
Taking this opportunity, Deputy Prime Minister Men Sam An would like to join in the celebration of the 71st anniversary of the National Independence Day of the People's Republic of China and the celebration of the Chinese Lunar New Year. To the Water Festival, Ok Ambok and worship the moon of the Khmer people.
(Phnom Penh): A suspect posing as a National Police Officer of 5 has been arrested by the Phnom Penh Municipal Police and sent to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court to follow the procedure.
One of the suspects, Pang Kaktika, alias Chhang, a 21-year-old Sambath Sakda, was arrested by special forces at the corner of Kampuchea Krom Street and Street 253, Sangkat Teuk Laak 2, Khan Toul Kork, and the case file was sent to court on the morning of the 30th. September 2020 to continue to follow legal procedures.
According to the investigation of the Information and Quick Reaction Team of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police, the suspect found that he had set up a fake Facebook account called the Phnom Penh Municipal Police. After conducting a search, the team found that this person not only hacked the fake Facebook page of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police, but also disguised himself as a national police officer.
After the Information and Quick Reaction Team searched for sufficient information, the team cooperated to provide information to the Office of Minor Crimes of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police by conducting a search and arresting the suspect.
(Phnom Penh): According to the report of the General Commission of the National Police, on September 29, 2020, there were 9 traffic accidents across the country, resulting in 5 deaths and 6 minor injuries.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen addresses a meeting of the Heads of Government on "Financing the Sustainable Development Agenda 2030 in the context of Kovid 19 and the future" (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia On September 29, 2020, attended the meeting of the Head of Government on "Financing the 2030 Agenda for Sustainable Development in the context of Kovid 19 and beyond".
During the meeting, Samdech Techo delivered a keynote address highlighting some of the priority work related to financing, which is an important way to serve the efforts of developing countries to achieve the 2030 Agenda.
5. Continuing to strengthen the ownership of developing countries by building partnerships between all development actors, including bilateral, multilateral development partners, the private sector and other development actors.
Mr. Mao Thunin outlines some solutions related to the impact of the implementation of the Stung Pursat 1 hydropower project
(Pursat): The Governor of Pursat Province, Mr. Mao Thunin, on September 29, 2020, chaired a meeting to discuss the decision on the establishment of a working group, sub-working group and provincial secretariat to implement compensation for resettlement to the people and Public infrastructure affected by the Stung Pursat 1 hydropower project is located in Bramoy commune, Veal Veng district.
During the meeting, there was also an agenda to disseminate the notification of Pursat Provincial Administration on the acceptance of the people who actually occupied and enjoyed the land, forest cover and natural resource protection area within the jurisdiction of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries. Fisheries and the Ministry of Environment as well.
On that occasion, Mr. Mao Thunin expressed his full support for the Stung Pursat 1 hydropower project, which the Royal Government under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen decided to build more for use in Pursat province and can be distributed throughout Other countries to ensure domestic energy security, reduce imports.
The provincial governor said that the most important step is to address the impact, so ask the district authorities to actually check and keep 347 families to receive compensation, equivalent to 1,436 people.
He added that the new location for the residents must be re-studied by the company as well as stakeholders to make sure that the land in that area is suitable for agricultural crops or not? He added that houses built for people should build a model house for the committee to monitor and evaluate.
At the same time, the provincial governor instructed the representatives of investment companies in all construction work to have good cooperation with the working group, sub-working group and provincial secretariat or local authority to expedite and avoid the risk of implementation of the above project.
On the same day, after the meeting, Mr. Mao Thunin continued to coordinate and solve some challenges for the people and also provided food to more than 300 poor people and families in need of food at Pursat Provincial Hall. Also.
So far, Cambodia has seven hydropower plants, six of which are located in the southwestern part of the country: Atai Russey, Chrum Kamchay, Kirirom 1, Kirirom 3 and Tatai. The other is the Lower Sesan 2 hydropower plant in Stung Treng province, northeast of Cambodia.
During 2019, the Royal Government decided to build new power plants, including: Stung Pursat 1 Hydropower Plant in Pramoy Commune, Veal Veng District, Pursat Province, which can generate 80 megawatts of electricity and a solar power station. Located along National Road 5 in Krakor district, Pursat province, which can generate 60 megawatts of power.
APSARA Authority: The French side is committed to continue better cooperation in renovating the western Mebon temple
(Siem Reap): The French Embassy has expressed its commitment to make the renovation of the Western Mebon Temple, which it is a financier, run smoothly and transparently, and is committed to further cooperating with Apsara Authority as well.
This is the first visit by a French co-chair as he has just replaced the outgoing former co-chair.
Mr. Christopher Shigado appreciated and expressed his pleasure to visit the site of the Western Mebon Temple. He said that this first visit was to find out more about the work and to improve the cooperation between the French side and the Apsara Authority.
The representative of the French Embassy pledged that he would make every effort to ensure that the renovation work on the Western Mebon Temple, funded by the French, went smoothly and transparently.
Mr. Hang Pov expressed his appreciation for the cooperation between Cambodia and France, and he also hoped that the new Co-President of the French Embassy will continue to cooperate at the site of the renovation of the Western Mebon better and smoother. According to the plans of both parties. Six Chief Inspectors of Rolea Bier District, Kampong Chhnang Province Receive the Title of "Teacher" from Samdech Preah Pothivong Amlim Heng
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Preah Pothivong Amlim Heng, Samdech Preah Sang, First Deputy Director and President of the Permanent Assembly of Buddhism in the Kingdom of Cambodia, on Tuesday morning This September 2020, he presided over the presentation of the Certificate of Appointment as a Teacher to 6 Chief Inspectors in Rolea Bier District, Kampong Chhnang Province at Wat Monisovann (called Wat Champouk K'aek), Phnom Penh.
The ceremony was also attended and invited by His Excellency Sathavong Kosal, Honorary King, Advisor to Samdech Preah Akka Moha Sangkha, Reverend Dr. Tep Vong, Samdech Preah Moha Sangkha Reach of the Kingdom of Cambodia and Preah Kru Thommanuvat Santikosal Pen Kongkea, Honorary Councilor, Advisor to Samdech Preah Akka Moha Sangkha Reach and Mr. Sor Leang, Director of Kampong Chhnang Provincial Department of Cult and Religion.
According to the Royal Certificate of Samdech Preah Moha Somenathibodi, the Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia has been appointed:
First, Bhikkhu Ouch Sophal, named Chhaya Sachthanno, Preah Samuh, Deputy Sub-Governor of Rolea Bier District, Preah Chao Athikar of Wat Chiv Rainsy (Wat Damnak Key), Cheung Kreav Commune, Rolea Bier District, Kampong Chhnang Province, was appointed as a teacher of the Great Council.
Second: Bhikkhu Moch Sauly, named Chhaya Panhap Tibo, the chief abbot of Wat Samdech Non Nget Senchey Sattharam, also known as Wat Kralanh Chas, located in Srang Tear village, Prasnup commune, Rolea Bier district, Kampong Chhnang province, was appointed as Serey Mongkul Mony teacher of the Mahanikaya committee.
Third: Bhikkhu Neang Phirun Nam Chhaya Yontinno, Preah Chao Athikar Wat Banlang, Pong Ror Commune, Rolea Bier District, Kampong Chhnang Province, was appointed as a teacher of the Mahanikaya.
Fourth: Bhikkhu Seng Danam Chhaya Inpanho, Preah Chao Athikar Wat Thom Ratanasophea-Trea, Sre Thmei Commune, Rolea Bier District, Kampong Chhnang Province, was appointed as Preah Serey Thom Vongsa of Mahanikaya.
Fifth: Bhikkhu Soth Lang, named Chhaya Chanchhoto, Preah Chao Athikar of Wat Throne of Rainsy, Kraing Leav Commune, Rolea Bier District, Kampong Chhnang Province, was appointed as Preah Kru Sil Udom Vongsa of the Mahanikaya Committee.
