Thai black-clad soldiers arrest 7 Cambodian workers who smuggled across the border to find risky jobs
(Banteay Meanchey): Seven Cambodian male and female workers were detained by Thai black-clad soldiers at the Poipet border crossing as they crossed the border to seek work in Thailand at risk.
The seven Cambodian workers, two males, four females and a boy, were arrested by Thai soldiers of the 1205th Regiment in collaboration with relevant experts in Aranya district on September 28, 2020 at the border in Aranya district, Sa Kaeo province. .
According to a local Thai newspaper, the seven residents told Thai authorities that because of the Kovid-19 era, they were unemployed and their families were in need, so they were forced to cross the border. Illegal, ready to go to work at Rong Klue market.
After detaining the seven residents, they were taken to the 1205th Regiment barracks for further questioning. The border takes 2,000 baht from Thailand to Cambodia, and 2,000 baht from Cambodia.
Ministry of Land Management announces completion of distribution of social land concessions to 1,382 families in Chhlong district
(Kratie): The Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction has announced that it has completed the distribution of social land concessions to a total of 1,382 families living in Kampong Damrey commune, Chhlong district, Kratie province.
In a press release issued on September 29, 2020, the Ministry said that the Kratie Provincial Administration and the Kratie Provincial Land Use and Allocation Committee have distributed social land concessions to a total of 1,382 families in three groups. The first group consists of 998 families, the second group has 353 families and the third group has 31 families.
The allocation of social land concessions is in accordance with the procedures and legal documents in force and was completed on June 10, 2020.
In a statement, the ministry said that due to the absence of any further protests, the ministry had decided to close the division from today.
The Ministry stressed that in the event of a subsequent land claim, claiming to be one of the three groups, the Ministry and relevant institutions consider it a new land dispute that will not be resolved. Take it to solve and take strict legal action.
