(Phnom Penh): Speaking in a lecture to share his past experience as the personal assistant of the Prime Minister and the leader of youth institutions for more than 8 years, Mr. Hun Many said that "the management of a country requires consideration. The pair is a package on both the framework of the party, state and society.
This statement is a reflection of his personal views after studying and understanding the words of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, who once said to the public: "In the task of managing the country, we can not look at a tree, we must look The whole forest. ”
Starting from the presentation of the main roles and responsibilities of young people who take turns in thinking about the future of Cambodia, Mr. Hun Many said, "As young people who have an equal share in the responsibility for the fate of the country. "The task of each of us is to train and develop our abilities by applying the theory to a specific situation and to continue to expand our knowledge and skills through both learning and practice."
He also shared his personal experience in performing professional work, understanding the value of information and setting goals, priorities and positions of Cambodia.
At the same time, Mr. Hun Many emphasized the role of the younger generation, especially the youth in the field of diplomacy, which plays an important role in raising the national image on the international stage and as a defender of national interests.
"Considering the national interest and national honor is our priority," he said. In representing Cambodia in all our work on the international stage, we must take a strong stand on behalf of young Cambodians who are full of ability, knowledge and equal rights with other countries.
Please be informed that this lecture program was also attended by Dr. Chhem Keat Rithy, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, Mr. Tean Samnang, President of the National Institute of Diplomacy and International Relations and Mr. Dao Ansan, Executive Director of the Cambodia Development Center.
Health Minister: Improper management of counterfeit and substandard medicines leads to loss of confidence in the health system
(Phnom Penh): Professor Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health of Cambodia, said that the control of the spread of counterfeit and substandard drugs leads to a loss of confidence in the health system.
"Vaccines, medicines and medical equipment for Kovid-19 and other diseases require intervention, prevention, control and treatment with quality medical products, which should be a regional priority," said Mam Bunheng. And the world. "Improper control of the spread of counterfeit and substandard medicines will lead to loss of life and confidence in the country's health care providers' drugs and health care system."
The Prime Minister also called for the participation of the fight at the regional and global levels, especially should be discussed at the 13th Asia-Europe Summit because of the problem of low quality and counterfeit drugs. Significantly affects the quality of medical services and affects the lives of people.
Mr. Mam Bunheng stressed that "In addition to efforts to prevent the spread of Kovid-19 in our country, we are also working on other priority health-related issues, including counterfeit and substandard medicines." "The quality is endangering the health of the people due to the treatment of patients with counterfeit and substandard medicines and the increase in public health as the disease progresses."
According to the spokesperson of the General Commissioner, within 152 days of tightening the road traffic law by increasing the fine according to Sub-Decree No. 39, from May 1 to September 29, 2020, the traffic police throughout the country inspected And fined a total of 180,177 vehicles, including 133,309 motorcycles and 46,868 vehicles of all types.
Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun said that for the past 152 days, the implementation of the new sub-decree to fine the offending vehicles has been going well. He thanked and commended all the road users for their good obedience to the traffic law so far, especially the traffic police for their dedication and hard work. Tighten traffic with the highest sense of responsibility.
It should be noted that for September 29, 2020, there were 9 traffic accidents throughout Cambodia, in which 5 people were killed and 6 people were injured (05 people were seriously injured).
