Royal Academy of Cambodia Holds Roundtable Discussion on Importance of Higher Education and Postgraduate Selection
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of September 29, 2020, the Royal Academy of Cambodia organized a roundtable discussion on the importance of choosing a major in higher education and post-graduate education, as well as presenting important experiences and tips to students. Currently studying in higher education to do more research in addition to studying in school in order to increase the capacity, knowledge and practice in the labor market competition during the Industrial Revolution 4.0.
Because Cambodia is now open to the free market, the choice of students to study is not restricted. In today's study, most young people are embracing their skills to their liking, regardless of the future job market.
According to Dr. Sok Touch, President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, he shared his experience and tips: “Now there is a good opportunity to create a program for him to choose a subject, so those who have experience have shown that they have to choose. What subject? ”
On that occasion, Dr. Sok Touch said, "Even he himself is a person who failed the high school exam is only a backup. Therefore, he asked whether the choice of subjects of young people is to choose from relatives, choose from friends, regardless of the quality of education.
The President of the Royal Academy stated that the current job market, no matter what the subject, it is important to be sure to push the skills learned to create jobs. He expressed confidence that the profession plays an important role today because Cambodia is a country that sells services, so it needs human resources capable of all those services and so on.
Dr. Sok Touch emphasized that self-study is very important for the future of his job after higher education, but if students do more research, it will make it easier for them as well. .
Dr. Kin Phea, President of the Cambodian Institute of International Relations of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, said that the direction and skills of students in higher education and post-graduate education reflect the preparation of human resources to meet the needs of Cambodia and the market. Work on the universe.
Dr. Hor Peng, Rector of the National High School of Management, said that currently there are many job market opportunities for young people, but only depending on the knowledge, experience and efforts of young people. Especially if young people choose a subject that they study well, it is clear that young people will get a job as well as a salary like a shining diamond.
