Sambor Prei Kuk National Authority calls on the people of this heritage resort to respect the law for the national interest
(Kampong Thom): Mr. Heng Than, Deputy Director General of Sambor Prei Kuk National Authority, called on the people in the area of Sambor Prei Kuk to join the implementation of the law for the national interest.
He said this at a seminar to disseminate the law on the protection of heritage in the resort area of Sambor Prei Kuk, organized by the Department of Public Order of Sambor Prei Kuk National Authority on September 28, 2020 at Kampong Chheu Teal Institute of Technology, with the participation of district authorities, heritage police and people. More than 100 business people.
He said that the workshop was held to disseminate information to the people and local authorities living in the area to know the legal standards and understand the protection to participate in the preservation of cultural heritage, which is the heritage of the ancestors.
He said that the Sambor Prei Kuk National Authority has the duty to protect, preserve and preserve the traces of the structure of the ancient city, temples, customs, traditions, people's way of life and other forms of construction in the protected area of Sambor Prei Kuk. Protection and development in the protected area of Sambor Prei Kuk resort based on three main bases: people, cultural and natural heritage to be harmonious and balanced.
At the same time, Major General Sun Vuthy, Director of the Department of Public Order, requested all participants to disseminate to raise awareness of the heritage protection police force that stands guard at the resort and to inform the business people living in the three areas. Understand the law of heritage protection, law of heritage protection.
He also called on the affected traders in the area to join together, because if they do not participate, no matter how strong the protection forces are, it will not be possible.
It should be noted that Sambor Prei Kuk, a Cambodian temple, was inscribed on the World Heritage Committee's list of World Heritage Sites at the 41st Meeting in Krakow, Poland on July 8, 2017.
Sambor Prei Kuk Temple is located in Sambo Village, Sambo Commune, Prasat Sambo District, Kampong Thom Province, 25 km from Kampong Thom Provincial Town on National Road 62, turn right onto Kon Tnaot Road. »Which at that time was the center of a religion dedicated to Shiva.
