In the forum on the work of demarcation and demarcation of the Cambodia-Vietnam land border on the morning of September 29, 2020, Senior Minister Va Kimhong stressed that the work of the border post is not easy and requires a study on the map. Be clear with the actual situation.
According to Senior Minister Va Kimhong, the obstacles faced by the Cambodian-Vietnamese side in the construction of the border post include technical obstacles, legal obstacles, and even the Prime Ministers of the two countries asked the French President to send French experts to help in this work. On the work of converting the map from 1/100,000 to 1/50,000.
Senior Minister Var Kimhong said, "We will try to complete the remaining 16 percent of the border demarcation work as soon as possible, but there are many obstacles to overcome." "Technical legal barriers."
But what has been achieved so far is that 84% of the border posts have been erected, which the senior minister considers very proud of Cambodia because in its history.
The senior minister also claimed that Cambodia and Vietnam had held a protocol on the demarcation of the border between the two countries. He stressed that the protocol was made to describe the entire border line from Kantouy Neak to Kampot (post 314), which is more than 2,000 pages thick.
Related to the question of whether Cambodians can have a hard time understanding the border demarcation issues, which are all technical work? Senior Minister Var Kimhong responded and expressed his belief that it would not be difficult for the people to understand the border work if there were no politicians to inspire and exaggerate the truth about this work.
He said that the Royal Government of Cambodia is very willing to protect the territorial integrity by not allowing Cambodians to lose land as in the past, that is, keep what is present, and the point of disagreement 16 percent is required. Consensus between the two parties, because each party has clear evidence to protect its territorial integrity.
Please note that Cambodia and Vietnam share a land border with a length of about 1,270 kilometers. The two countries agreed to demarcate and demarcate the border, which reached 84 percent, and was signed by the Prime Minister of Cambodia and the Prime Minister of Vietnam Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the morning of October 5. 2019.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen has said that the demarcation of the border between Cambodia and Vietnam is very important, and if we do not try to end this border issue, Cambodia and Vietnam will continue to have border disputes for generations to come. This can easily become a political challenge, leading to the destruction of peace and development along the border.
