Please read the press release below: Soldiers of the 53rd Infantry Brigade helped dismantle and build houses for 27 people affected by the strong winds
(Battambang): Seeing the hardships of the people, the houses collapsed due to the strong winds on the evening of September 27, 2020, Brigadier General Keo Seng Lon, Commander of the 53rd Infantry Brigade, 5th Army Division, led the force. Of the division to help dismantle and rebuild houses for the people.
Relocation and construction of houses on September 28, 2020 by soldiers of the 53rd Infantry Brigade in cooperation with local authorities and Phnom Proek District Assistance Team. The strong wind caused damage to many crops and collapsed a total of 27 houses in Damnak Ksan village, Buor commune, Phnom Preuk district, Battambang province.
