Cambodia, China publish Xi Jinping's book on Chinese governance part 3
(Phnom Penh): With the support of the General Secretariat of the Senate of Cambodia and the Chinese Embassy in Cambodia, this morning, September 29, 2020, the Chinese Cultural Center in Cambodia and the Cambodia-China Progress Researchers Association organized a book dissemination program of Xi Jinping on China's Governance Part 3 in English
The event was held at the Cambodian Senate with about 200 participants from the General Secretariat of the Senate, the Secretariat of the National Assembly, representatives of ministries, institutions, organizations, civil society organizations, investment companies and students.
Oum Sarith, secretary-general of the General Secretariat of the Senate of Cambodia, said that Xi Jinping's book on Chinese governance is indeed a great treasure trove of wisdom on governing the country and also one of China's most precious treasures. . At the same time, China is willing to openly share its successful experience with other countries in the world.
Mr. Sarith said that compared to other countries, China is under a lot of pressure, facing the poverty of the people. Since 2012, China has reduced more than 300 million people in poverty since more than 40 years of reform.
