At the same time, in order to strengthen the national currency, the Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia called on the people to participate in promoting the use of the riel, which is the national currency, more widely.
He said that, in fact, the celebration of the re-introduction of the riel has been postponed since March due to the spread of Kovid 19, which the government has taken the most effective preventive measures.
After the liberation on January 7, 1979, the banking and monetary system began to recover from zero, and the economic situation was strained and removed from the international arena. Cambodia worked hard to establish a central bank, then known as the "National Bank of Cambodia", based on the few remaining human resources.
The sharp influx of the US dollar into smaller economies at a time when confidence in the national currency is already low has created a new problem for the national economy, the dollarization. So the problem of dollarization is not the result of government political decisions, but of market acceptance.
At the same time, the banking sector has continued to develop strongly and has expanded its services across the country. In the last two decades, banking assets have grown 93 times, credit has grown 178 times and deposits have increased 95 times. These growths reflect the confidence of investors and citizens in the Cambodian banking and monetary system.
He added that the best achievements so far have come from the efforts of all stakeholders. Peace has made it possible for all of us to unite and work hard to focus on sustainable development. The peace that Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, has achieved and continues to maintain is the foundation of all economic and social development in Cambodia and the sustainable use of the riel.
She considers that this is a big task that Cambodia has achieved while the Royal Government is trying to prevent the transmission of Kovid 19.
