In addition, the team cooperated to inspect 7,557 workers from Thailand through O'Smach, 1,009 to be relocated and 6,548 to be sent to the provinces to implement the program to provide cash to vulnerable families during Kovid-19 received 18,108 families with a total amount of 3,618 million riels. In particular, the rainy season cultivation throughout the province achieved 100 percent of the annual plan.
Commenting on the ceremony, Senior Minister Kun Kim emphasized that under the leadership of the Royal Government, with Samdech Techo Hun Sen as the Prime Minister of Cambodia, a series of great achievements have been made and the country has been saved from the epidemic. 19 and maintain peace throughout the country.
The Senior Minister praised the working groups at all levels for their solidarity and responsibility, went down to the grassroots to help the needy people in time and joined the Ben with the people at the local level. Province.
The Senior Minister and the Chairman of the Working Group also urged the working groups and parties at all levels to pay attention to the following tasks:
* First, pay attention to maintaining security and social order, continue to better implement the village-commune safety policy, jointly prevent the use of drug trafficking at the local level and prevent the suppression of all crimes.
* Third: Continue to open public forums in the backyard to solve their challenges and continue to find the poor and vulnerable by Kovid-19 Update 18,108 vulnerable families to take measures to help them
* Fourth: All localities must encourage people to be ready to check the list and register to vote for those who have reached the age of majority.
* Fifth: Prepare forces and means to help rescue people in the event of a disaster.
* Sixth: The provincial administration is assigned to end land issues in Anlong Veng district.
On behalf of the Royal Government of Cambodia, the Senior Minister expressed his deep gratitude to the Government and people of China for their continued contribution to development work with the Royal Government of Cambodia, including support for humanitarian mine action in Cambodia, both in terms of budget, technology and materials. By September 2020, the Chinese government will have provided tents, demining equipment, protective gear, drones, uniforms, shoes, belts and hats.
Regarding the mine sector in Cambodia, the Senior Minister stated that the Royal Government of Cambodia has set a clear vision and goal to end the mine threat that we know by 2025 and reduce the mine risk to a maximum. .
He called on China to continue to provide strong support to end the mine threat by 2025 and address the issue of post-2025 post-war explosive remnants.
The Senior Minister continued that the provision of assistance to the Chinese friends in the humanitarian demining work now and in the past is a contribution in response to and in line with Samdech Techo's long-term commitment and goals for the nation and people, including peace. Security, safety and development for all Cambodians.
On that occasion, the Senior Minister also thanked and praised China for its participation in the fight against the spread of Kovid-19 in Cambodia from the beginning.
At the same time, the Chinese Ambassador said that the Chinese government and people will continue to contribute to the development of Cambodia, including continuing to support the Royal Government of Cambodia's Mine Action Plan 2025, and the Ambassador considered the clearance work as a contribution. Provide happiness to the people of Cambodia as well.
