(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of September 28, 2020, at the office of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, the new business training center "Techo" and the Banking Association of Cambodia signed a memorandum of understanding on "Cooperation to improve technology. Finance in the Kingdom of Cambodia "with Dr. Kong Mary as a representative of the new business center" Techo "and Dr. In Channy as a representative of the Banking Association in Cambodia.
The signing ceremony was attended by representatives of relevant units under the auspices of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and many other private institutions. The MoU aims to contribute to boosting the financial environment and expanding the scope of work in the new business and financial technology sectors to support the digital economy in Cambodia.
The constant advancement of digital technology and telecommunications has led to the digitalization and integration of the digital chain that is happening in all sectors, including the financial sector. The potential of this new technology will serve as a new lever for socio-economic development that will emerge as a new form of economy called the digital economy.
(Phnom Penh): The Minister of Health, Prof. Mam Bunheng, instructed a total of 31 scholarship winners from the Government of Japan, Australia and New Zealand to study hard, research, strengthen their skills and be disciplined in order to be successful in their studies.
Minister Mam Bunheng encouraged all students to study and draw on good experiences from the development of their country to serve the country and show the progress of Cambodia under the leadership of the head of government.
