(Phnom Penh): Mr. Plang Sophal, Deputy Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, is continuing to open an investigation into the case of Mr. Thlang Phinra in connection with the insulting and threatening to shoot the owner of Angkor Chum and his wife at noon. September 20, 2020 ago. This is according to Mr. Kuch Kimlong, spokesman for the Phnom Penh Municipal Prosecutor's Office, told Fresh News on September 28, 2020.
The owner of Angkor Chum Noodle Shop, Phnom Penh's Toul Kork branch, has filed a lawsuit against Interior Ministry counter-terrorism director Thlang Phinra after the police officer pulled out a gun and threatened to shoot him and his wife. The above incident happened at 12 noon on September 20, 2020.
General Neth Savoeun, the National Police Commissioner General, decided to enforce the discipline of the forces and suspend the director of the Anti-Terrorism Bureau, who removed the guns of two Angkor Chum noodle shop owners and a couple in a drinking circle. This is according to Lt. Gen. E Sok Khi, Deputy Commissioner of the National Police, speaking to Fresh News on the morning of September 25, 2020.
Lt. Gen. Ey Sok Khi confirmed that "So far, His Excellency Lt. Gen. Dr. Neth Savoeun, General Commissioner of the National Police, has applied the discipline of Lt. Col. Thlang Phinra and decided to hand over the perpetrator, Thlang Phinra, to the court for further proceedings. "
It should be informed that, seeing the mistakes of the forces, General Neth Savoeun instructed Lt. Gen. E Sok Khi and Lt. Gen. Thou Saroeun, Director of the Counter-Terrorism Department of the General Commission of the National Police to visit and apologize to the victims. That its forces were wrong in this incident.
Victim name: Chuy Sokheng, male, 53 years old, present address: 91, Street 592, Sangkat Boeung Kak II, Khan Toul Kork, Phnom Penh, owner of Angkor Chum Noodle Shop, Toul Kork Branch, complained to Mr. Thlang Phinra to 3 institutions:
* First: Complaint to Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Interior * Second: Complaint to the Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court * Third: Complaint to the Bar Association of the Kingdom of Cambodia
The complaint came after the police officer insulted and threatened to shoot the victim and his wife by pulling out a gun from the waist and targeting the victim and his wife, who were having lunch in Ha. Noodles Angkor Chum, Tuol Kork branch directly.
