The inspector confirmed that before the incident, the two girls went to bathe in a pond in Bos Thom village, Ta Kong commune, when the water was flooding. While the two girls were bathing happily, the two girls were swept away by a tornado into a pond, causing the two siblings to drown.
The colonel said that because there were no people there and the deep water pit caused the two children to drown without help.
The bodies of the two girls, after being examined by the joint authorities, were handed over to their parents for a traditional ceremony. Troops of the 51st Infantry Brigade help harvest rice from the flood for the people
(Banteay Meanchey): Under the guidance of Lt. Gen. Hun Manet, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Commander of the Army, Major General Chhun Mao, Deputy Commander of the 5th Army Division and Commander of the First Direction, led the military force in the brigade headquarters. About 500 pedestrians from the 51st Infantry Division went down to help harvest their farmers affected by the floods that flooded their rice fields a few days this weekend in Mongkul Borei district.
The raid to harvest rice from this water took place on the morning of September 26, 2020 at Kramol village, Rohat Teuk commune, Mongkul Borei district, Banteay Meanchey province.
Ms. Kong Sopheap, Rohat Teuk commune chief, said that the people in this commune have done a lot for this year. Prolonged drought at the beginning of the season causes almost all of the rice farmers to die. The few remaining rice fields were inundated by heavy rains after the rice was almost ripe for harvest.
She said that on the 25th and 26th, more than 20 hectares of paddy fields of local farmers were flooded, making it difficult to harvest, but they thanked the military forces of the brigade headquarters. The 51st Infantry, with a force of about 500 people, helped harvest in time to seize a large amount of rice from the floods.
Major General Chhun Mao, Deputy Commander of the 5th Army Division, Commander of the 1st Direction, Banteay Meanchey, said that the 51st Infantry Brigade had deployed about 500 troops to help harvest farmers affected by the floods.
He said that according to the report of the commune authorities, the affected rice fields are more than 20 hectares, so the military must work together to harvest rice from the water in time and ready.
Although the harvest is not complete, at least we can get 70 to 80 percent of the rice from the flood, because harvesting rice in water is not easy, we can not see the plants and face In fact, on the first day of the harvest, a soldier who went down to harvest water in the middle of the field was bitten on the head, causing great pain. This is according to Mr. Chhun Mao.
Major General Chhun Mao said that many other parts of the district were still suffering, so he had to lead the intervention force until the water receded.
The General stated that the military forces of the 51st Infantry Brigade Command, in addition to their core work, always participated in all social activities to help the people affected by the strong winds, to repair the houses of the victims and, in fact, to help harvest and harvest during the floods. Almost every year.
At the same time, the Major General issued a message calling on people with small children to be extremely careful not to play in the water or climb trees to avoid drowning or biting.
