At the same time, the Ministry of Health also informed about measures to prevent the disease, including:
* Measure 1: Parents, guardians, all children, including local authorities, must actively participate in getting rid of water worms in places where water is left unused, such as car tires, motorcycles, bottle caps, cans, coconuts, rice bowls, soup, coffee cans, buried or burned. Or demolish or store in a way to prevent waterlogging.
* Step 3: In case of high fever symptoms, immediately take the patient to the state examination and treatment (public service) such as health centers and public hospitals nearest to you, do not try to treat patients. Immediate high fever on its own or delayed medical treatment in a private service that does not have the ability to treat typhoid fever or dengue fever at all.
Samdech Heng Samrin's remarks were made at the General Assembly of Hope of the Global Peace Federation to be held in the Republic of Korea on the morning of September 27, 2020. The General Assembly of the Global Peace Federation of Hope in 2020 is organized under the theme: "Towards building and improving the whole society after the Kovid-19 crisis: independence, prosperity and global values."
Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin stated that Kovid 19 has had a serious impact on the society and the global economy as a whole, but the response to this crisis varies from country to country, which has not yet resulted. Completely satisfied. Samdech continued that the response to the problem of Kovid 19 seems to show that the world is against the enemy, but the solution is not the same.
Samdech stressed that solving the problem of Kovid 19 requires working together to increase international cooperation and solidarity is an important and indispensable factor. At the same time, the President of the National Assembly shared his experience that Cambodia has effectively managed the situation of Kovid 19 through the implementation of a culture of sharing and solidarity to the General Assembly.
Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin said that the fight against Kovid 19 requires a lot of money, equipment and manpower. Cambodia has jointly donated and shared resources to the fullest extent possible, including public, private, development partners and non-governmental organizations to the people. The Royal Government has set out development strategies focusing on agriculture, agro-industry, digital transformation and domestic tourism, which are also priority sectors.
In order to rehabilitate and build the society now and after the end of the Kovid 19 crisis, the National Assembly President said that a specific rehabilitation plan should be drawn up, setting out the necessary scenarios for the gradual implementation of the Transit and trade operations, as well as the rehabilitation of areas most severely affected by the crisis, will be essential and necessary to maintain peace in the region and the world.
Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin further stated that in this context, the National Assembly must pay attention in passing laws and policies related to this technology in order to ensure the benefits for all countries in the region and the world, especially countries Develop capacity and infrastructure.
