The Senior Minister also said that the Royal Government of Cambodia has a master plan for national logistics, which requires a lot of investment from other countries to develop the logistics sector in Cambodia to grow, and now the Ministry has been considering the development of the center. Phnom Penh Logistics in collaboration with a private company in Singapore.
The Senior Minister also mentioned the reform of the transportation sector by using information technology mechanisms to provide public services to the people, including: automation system, vehicle registration, vehicle technical inspection and driver's license examination with payment. Services through partner banks and road maintenance programs (ROAD CARE Mobile App) that allow people to report broken roads to the Ministry of Public Works and Transport.
Mr. Alexander C. Feldman, US-ASEAN Business Council, expressed his deep appreciation for the Royal Government of Cambodia's efforts to prevent and control the spread of Kovid-19, especially some measures to prevent the effects of Kovid. -19 And even though Cambodia is affected by this disease, Cambodia is still highly committed and responsible to continue to promote infrastructure development.
The companies also expressed interest in investing in Cambodia and promised to spread the word to other partner companies to seek investment opportunities in Cambodia, especially investment in transport infrastructure and logistics.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol also encouraged Visa to cooperate with the Ministry in providing online payment services and urged Ford to study its feasibility of providing additional vehicle technical inspection services to its existing service centers in Cambodia. Turn the service closer to the people, as there are currently only two companies inspecting the technical characteristics of vehicles operating in Cambodia.
