The Minister of Agriculture ordered the Kandal Provincial Fisheries to reduce or stop the import of fish from abroad to give people a chance to raise fish with hope!
(Kandal): The Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, Mr. Veng Sakhon, ordered the Kandal Provincial Fisheries Administration to review the principle of importing all kinds of fish, that is, reduce the maximum or stop imports at once so as not to affect local fish production. Stop importing is a golden opportunity for people hoping to trade in the market easily.
The Minister ordered this during the ceremony and distribution of plastic tents, baby fish, catfish, frogs and food for aquaculture activities during the outbreak of Kovid-19 to 52 families in the commune. Preah Prosop, Khsach Kandal District, Kandal Province, on September 26, 2020, with the participation of Dr. Kong Sophoan, Governor of Kandal Province.
He added that Khsach Kandal district is one of the 11 districts in Kandal province that has the potential to produce vegetables to supply Phnom Penh, so farmers should take advantage of this golden opportunity through efforts to increase Productivity, vegetable production, animal husbandry, fish farming and mixed cropping to ensure sustainable supply, market and food security.
The Minister also instructed the Department of Fisheries Administration and local authorities to come and help promote fish farming, vegetable growing and animal husbandry in order to expand and strengthen the breeding capacity in all forms. It is necessary to monitor all the activities of the irrigators who will adopt the young fish today so that the rearing can be successful.
The Minister further stated that professional officers of Fisheries Administration must continue to provide additional training on breeding techniques, breeding, hatching, feed mixing methods, maintenance and economic efficiency, organize breeding production clusters to ensure supply, prepare clear breeding plans and implement contract agricultural production. .
