Mr. Thong Khon thanked Japanese investors in the tourism sector, including hotel owners, restaurants and supermarkets, who have always shown confidence and investment opportunities through investing heavily in Cambodia.
"Cambodia is always ready to welcome and provide good hospitality to Japanese investors and tourists," he said.
The Minister also called on relevant ministries and institutions, local authorities, businesses, tour operators and the people to continue to support and pay attention to contribute to the development of Cambodia's tourism sector.
Myanmar authorities on Sunday said that in just one week, a total of more than 500 people were arrested for violating COVID-19 prevention measures as the situation spread in an ASEAN country. This continues to be alarming. This was released by the Xinhua news agency on Sunday, September 27, 2020.
Between September 19 and 25, a total of 525 people were arrested in connection with violations of COVID-19 measures across Myanmar, of which 350 were arrested for not wearing masks in public places, 149 of them. Arrested for violating the curfew, and 26 were arrested for violating other points.
In the past, Myanmar authorities have decided to impose night curfews in some regions and states, including Rangoon, to control the spread of COVID-19. Currently, some cities in Rangoon, Mandalay, Baghdad and Iowa, as well as the state of Mon are under house arrest orders as they see a sharp increase in the number of cases.
