Chinese Foreign Minister: "China is always ready to help developing countries towards success"
BEIJING (Reuters) - As a good brother, a good friend and a good partner of all developing countries, China will always be ready to help them move forward, Chinese Foreign Minister Wang Yi said on Saturday. Success. This is according to a quote from the Xinhua news agency on Sunday, September 27, 2020.
Under the framework of South-South cooperation, China has provided more than 58 billion US dollars in foreign aid and set up projects, he said. In the wake of the COVID-19 crisis, China has sent medical teams to 32 countries and provided anti-epidemic equipment to 150 countries and four international organizations.
Wang Yi also pointed out that some of the COVID-19 vaccines developed by China are currently being tested in the third phase. According to Wang, once they are officially available, these vaccines will become a global commodity, giving developing countries a top priority.
