Ministry of Water Resources: From today to September 29, the rain will be scattered and increase gradually throughout most of the country, especially in the northwestern part of Thailand and the coastal provinces.
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology has issued an additional notification on the weather situation in Cambodia, stating that according to continuous monitoring, the weather situation is changing rapidly due to the low pressure system moving over Northern Thailand, Laos and central Vietnam. In the following days, the low pressure system will move down through the northern part of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
This will make the weather in the Kingdom of Cambodia on September 27-29 the following situation:
Scattered showers and thundershowers are expected throughout the country, especially in northwestern Thailand and coastal provinces, where heavy rain, strong winds, thunderstorms and high waves are expected.
The Ministry of Water Resources has called on people living in low-lying areas near mountainous waterways and fishermen to be aware of the dangers posed by the weather.
