Authorities find the body of a woman who drowned while swimming across the border from Thailand to Cambodia in Sala Krao district, Pailin province
(Pailin): The body of a woman who drowned while swimming across the Cambodian-Thai border on September 19, 2020 was found on the afternoon of September 26, 2020 at an orange plantation. In Ochheukrom village, Stung Karch commune, Sala Krao district, Pailin province, on the other side of Stung Dey Thai river.
Fresh News Agency in Pailin Province reported that after receiving this information, the competent force and local authorities went to the place where the body was found and conducted an autopsy and handed it over to the family for a traditional ceremony.
A Cambodian woman drowned in a stream along the Cambodian-Thai border in Pailin province as she and other Cambodian workers smuggled across the border from Thailand to Cambodia through a corridor. The floodwaters were suddenly swept away, causing drowning.
Mr. Seng Sokun, Pailin Provincial Police Commissioner, said that this incident happened at 5:50 pm on September 19, 2020 at Ochheukrom, Stung Karch Commune, Sala Krao District, Pailin Province, opposite Po Nam Ron District, Chan Borei Province. Thailand.
Mr. Seng Sokun said that there were three migrant workers, they were mothers, fathers and children, who smuggled across the border from Thailand into Cambodia through a stream along the border, but the mother could not swim across the stream. Also died from drowning in that stream.
After this incident, Mr. Phan Chanthul, Governor of Pailin Province, ordered the Pailin Provincial Police, Provincial Armed Forces and Provincial Armed Forces to arrive at the scene to search for the body of the victim.
According to Mr. Seng Sokun, the dead woman was named Seng Srey Mao, 41 years old, living in Svay Meas village, Kandor Chrum commune, Ponhea Krek district, Tbong Khmum province. The husband is named Chow Chheng, 41, and the daughter is named Chheng Daneth, 15 years old.
Cambodian Medical Association launches forum for more than 400 pediatricians
(Siem Reap): The Cambodian Medical Association on September 26, 2020 organized the 5th Conference on Pediatrics Update with the aim of providing a forum for pediatricians both at home and abroad to share and exchange information. Experience each other as well as help provide new knowledge this program at Sokha Hotel Siem Reap.
The program, chaired by Prof. Thea Kruy, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health, was also attended by more than 100 members of the Cambodian Pediatric Association and more than 300 members of the Cambodian Pediatric Association online, as well as speakers. Cambodia's expert doctors and speakers from Europe will also give online presentations.
The representative of the conference stated that the theme of this conference is:
* Treatment of severe pneumonia at Jayavarman VII Hospital.
* Chronic bronchitis cases and viral training experience to diagnose bacterial diseases at Angkor Hospital for Children.
* Cases of iron deficiency anemia in children caused by improper diet or malnutrition at the National Children's Hospital.
* Experience of detoxification in children in case of children with acute renal failure at Kantha Bopha Hospital.
* Understand the importance of the immune system and the health of the child's stomach, focusing on the microbial damage of children presented by speakers from Europe.
In addition, Professor Yit Sunnara instructed the members of the conference, all pediatricians from hospitals from provinces and cities to bring the latest knowledge to participate in the provision of medical services to our children. Efficiency, quality and safety.
He asked the members and the medical team to pay attention to adhere to the medical professional ethics and urge all participants to promote to other cooperatives to improve the provision of health services to the people. We are in line with the wise policy of the Royal Government under the wise leadership of Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen.
The Cambodian Housing Developers Association asks the Royal Government to postpone the implementation of the tax on capital gains from the sale of real estate
(Phnom Penh): As the capital gains tax for the sale of real estate will be officially implemented in January 2021, the Association of Housing Developers of Cambodia has expressed concern over the implementation of the new tax, each member claims. It will increase the cost for the people, especially the business people in this business, while the Kovid problem is not over yet.
Mr. Chrek Soknim said that under these circumstances, the state should delay the implementation of this round of income tax by waiting for an appropriate time. The state should delay until the economy recovers. Association members point out that if the state decides to tax at a time of global crisis, real estate activity could slow down, especially affecting consumer decisions.
According to the official of the General Department of Taxation, the tax on capital gains is not a new tax, it is determined by the law on finance for management. 2007 (new Article 7) will be amended to the new Article 7 (a) by the Law on Finance for the year 2019 and so far for about 13 years.
The Cambodian Association of Housing Developers has expressed its commitment to continue to support the Royal Government's tax collection policy and softness, which has always cared for and supported investors under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Kampuchea Krom. The slogan "Thank you for peace". Check out a collection of key images from the international events of September 26, 2020! (Photo inside)
