SHANGHAI: China will suspend imports of seafood from two Russian vessels for four weeks after experts found the coronavirus on the outer packaging. This is according to the release by CNA on Saturday afternoon, September 26, 2020.
Recently, China has continued to restrict seafood imports from some countries due to the COVID-19 pandemic on packaging. In fact, on Friday, Chinese customs officials announced that China would suspend seafood imports from a Brazilian company for a week.
Last week, China also suspended seafood imports from Indonesia after officials discovered frozen fish contained coronavirus. Authorities in the northeastern province of Jilin even found coronavirus on a package of squid imported from Russia.
