(Phnom Penh): At the invitation of Deputy Prime Minister Pham Binh Minh, Minister of Foreign Affairs of Vietnam, Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia will attend the 10th Mekong-Republic of Korea Foreign Ministers' Meeting to be held on September 28, 2020 via video system.
The statement said that the ministers will review the progress of Mekong-ROK cooperation and determine the future direction of this cooperation.
The Ministers will also exchange views on ways to strengthen partnerships and solidarity in addressing regional and global issues for sustainable growth, development and prosperity in the Mekong region and the Republic of Korea. The ministers will also discuss preparations for the second Mekong-ROK summit.
Koh Kong Provincial Health Department Launches Abattoir Campaign to Prevent Dengue Fever, Chicken Fever and Other Infectious Diseases
(Koh Kong): The Koh Kong Provincial Health Department has launched a campaign to spray and install abattoirs to control mosquito breeding grounds to prevent dengue fever, chickenpox and other infectious diseases for the health of the people.
The spraying and abattoir operation took place on September 26, 2020, around the area of Dang Tong Market, Village 4, Sangkat Dang Tong, Khemarak Phoumin City and Pak Klang Commune, Mondul Seima District, Koh Kong Province.
The operation was attended by Mr. Tou Savuth, Deputy Governor of Koh Kong Province, Dr. Toa Moeng, Director of Koh Kong Provincial Health Department, Mr. Chhuon Sovannda, Executive Director of the Cambodian Red Cross Branch and also attended by Red Cross students and youth.
According to Dr. Toa Moeng, in accordance with the guidelines of the Royal Government and the Ministry of Health to protect the health of the people, dengue fever and chickenpox caused by Mos Khla, the Ministry of Health, the working group has carried out spraying and abattoir operations to Eliminate mosquito breeding grounds to protect people from the effects of bird flu and dengue fever and other infectious diseases.
