(Banteay Meanchey): A group of Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen's volunteer lawyers has been granted the right to defend themselves in a criminal case of two couples who were detained by the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Court on charges of aggravated theft. Committed in 2017.
Members of the Samdech Techo Sen Volunteer Lawyers Group in Banteay Meanchey and Battambang Provinces, Sun Sary, Nherithy and Song Mao, were granted the right to defend Chhorn Chheak and Sok Srey Neang in Criminal Case No. 79 on March 3. August 2020 by the Battambang Provincial Court of Appeal, where the couple was detained by the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Court.
Two couples were detained by the provincial court on charges of aggravated theft at Phsar Kandal village, Phsar Kandal commune, Poipet city, Banteay Meanchey province on June 15, 2017, in accordance with the provisions of articles 353 and 357 of the Penal Code.
Mr. Ky Tech, Chairman of Samdech Techo Sen Volunteer Lawyers Group, told Fresh News that in the defense of the Battambang Court of Appeal, as a result, the Trial Chamber of the Battambang Court of Appeal decided to reject the decision of the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Court and Decided to release the couple on the afternoon of September 25, 2020.
The couple thanked Samdech Techo Prime Minister and Samdech Kittipritthbandit for setting up a group of Samdech Techo Sen volunteer lawyers to help vulnerable women with legal disputes and thanked the Trial Chamber. Appeal Battambang and Mr. Ky Tech, who sent Samdech Techo Sen's volunteer lawyer to help defend until justice for both of them.
After being detained and until September 25, 2020, for more than four months, they were considered victims and decided to appeal to Battambang until the second court dismissed the charges and Released on September 25, 2020. Kratie Police Detain Two Suspects After Driving to Destroy People's Homes in Prek Prosop District
(Kratie): Police in Prek Prosop district, Kratie province, under the command of Major General Lon Sophat, Provincial Police Commissioner, arrested two of the three suspects who drove a Highlander car through the wall of a house and stole property. Two houses in Ra village, Sop commune, Prek Prosop district, Kratie province, on September 26, 2020.
Colonel Chan Sophalla, Prek Prosop District Police Inspector, said this morning, September 26, 2020, that the victim, Seang Bora, male, 30 years old, current residence, Ra village, Sop commune, Prek Prosop district, Kratie province, was robbed. Take some items including: 2 mobile phones, more than one thousand dollars, more than 20 million riels, 2 cases of carabao drink.
The inspector confirmed that after receiving the news that there was a case of crime, the police force immediately raided the wall but did not chase after them and also contacted the inspection force outside to intercept in Prek Prang village, commune. Prey Prosop, Prek Prosop district, Kratie province.
The first suspect is Hiep Chaihap, male, 36 years old, ethnic Khmer, living in Kranhong village, Veal Mlou commune, Ponhea Krek district, Tbong Khmum province, and the second suspect is Seng Thavy, male, 25 years old, in Sre Ta Nguon village, Cha Son Moul commune, Memot district, Tbong Khmum province. Currently in Kapao commune, Kamchay Mea district, Prey Veng province.
After questioning the suspects, the two suspects confessed that on the night of the incident, the two of them actually broke into the house and stole another house. But Pov, male, 41 years old, was born in Prek Romdeng, Pong Ror Commune, Koh Sotin District, Kampong Cham Province. He is currently working on a farm and selling goods at the scene.
The two suspects, along with a white Highlander car with license plate Phnom Penh 2AB-0357, are currently being held at the Kratie Provincial Police Office for further investigation.
Minister of Agriculture and Governor of Kandal Province Distribute Fish Seedlings to Farmers in Khsach Kandal District
(Kandal): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries and Mr. Kong Sophoan, Governor of Kandal Province, this morning, September 26, 2020, visited and brought some catfish and other breeding materials. Distributed to 52 families in Preah Prosop village, Preah Prosop commune, Khsach Kandal district, Kandal province.
On that occasion, Minister Veng Sakhon held a get-together with a message from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister, to the people throughout Kandal Province and wished all the families to meet the four blessings. Do not be shy.
Minister Veng Sakhon added that Khsach Kandal district is one of the 11 districts in Kandal province that has the potential to produce vegetables to supply Phnom Penh, and therefore advised farmers to take advantage of this golden opportunity. Efforts to increase productivity, vegetable production, animal husbandry, fish farming and mixed cropping to ensure sustainable supply of markets and food security.
Regarding fish farming, Minister Veng Sakhon instructed the Department of Fisheries Administration and local authorities to come and help promote fish farming, vegetable growing and animal husbandry in order to expand and strengthen the breeding capacity in all forms. It is necessary to monitor all the activities of the irrigators who will adopt the young fish today so that the rearing can be successful.
The Fisheries Administration must review the policy of importing all kinds of fish in order to reduce the quantity or stop the import, which will affect the local fish production. For today, 52 farmers, each family received 700 catfish, 4 sacks of food and 1 plastic tent for raising fish.
On this occasion, Minister Veng Sakhon also donated 1,000 liters of oil to help pump water to save rice.
In the same Khsach Kandal district, from the fish distribution program, Minister Veng Sakhon, the provincial governor and his colleagues continued to inspect the production of vegetable crops (cucumbers, cucumbers, nong chroung, noung moul, tralach and tomatoes) of farmers in Boeung Krachap village, Prek Tamak commune.
The owner of the plantation, male and female, described to the Minister the officials about planting, harvesting, marketing, income, employment, supplementation, safety and other issues.
After inspecting the vegetable farm, Minister Veng Sakhon congratulated and supported the efforts to grow vegetables as a source of income for the family.
