Mr. Say Sam Al: Peace is a sacred opportunity to restore the nation's economy, prestige and even greater prosperity
(Preah Sihanouk): Say Sam Al, Chairman of the Working Group of the Cambodian People's Party in Preah Sihanouk Province confirmed that for the Cambodian People's Party
Building a bridge of peace is important and indispensable. Peace is a sacred opportunity to restore the country's economy, prestige and prestige to greater prosperity.
Mr. Say Sam Al made this statement on September 26, 2020, when he chaired a meeting to disseminate information on the procedures for reviewing the voter list, voter registration and the process of organizing the election. Commune / Sangkat Council 2022 and National Assembly Election 2023, with the participation of members of the Sihanoukville Provincial Working Group and CPP members at all levels of Sihanoukville.
"For the CPP, building a bridge of peace is important and indispensable," he said. "This peace is a sacred opportunity to restore the country's economy, prestige and prestige to greater prosperity."
Mr. Say Sam Al emphasized that reconciliation, national unification, the end of the war, the building of complete peace have led to the development of all areas for the motherland and a key factor of the policy of the Cambodian People's Party under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo. Hun Sen, head of the Royal Government. At present, the fruits of peace have been making the people benefit and rejoice greatly for the Royal Government.
Mr. Say Sam Al said that the general principles for reviewing the registration and review of the annual voter list and the election, the sharing of experiences related to the election work and the work direction for the upcoming election were presented by the speakers. Important from ministries, professional institutions and the Election Committee (NEC).
On that occasion, Mr. Say Sam Al considered that the forum organized now is very important for members in Sihanoukville to understand more about the procedures of voter registration, voter registration and the election process. .
At the same time, Mr. Say Sam Al emphasized that the election confirms the people's support for political parties. In 2022, there will be Commune / Sangkat Council elections, and in 2023, there will be elections for the 7th legislature of the National Assembly. Spokesman for the General Commission: On September 26, another 872 vehicles were inspected and fined
According to the spokesperson of the General Commissioner, within 149 days of tightening the road traffic law by increasing the fine according to Sub-Decree No. 39, from May 1 to September 26, 2020, the traffic police nationwide inspected And fined a total of 178,180 vehicles, including 13,911 motorcycles and 46,269 vehicles of all types.
Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun said that for the past 149 days, the implementation of the new sub-decree to fine vehicles for offenses has been going well. He thanked and commended all the road users for their good obedience to the traffic law so far, especially the traffic police for their dedication and hard work. Tighten traffic with the highest sense of responsibility.
Please note that for September 26, 2020, traffic accidents throughout Cambodia also occurred 7 times, in which 4 people died, 4 people were injured (4 people were seriously injured). During the 149 days, there were 1,236 traffic accidents in Cambodia, in which 619 people were killed and 1935 injured (1,154 seriously injured).
