(Phnom Penh): While many countries are celebrating "World Cleanup Day" on September 26, 2020, Cambodia is also celebrating this International Day, focusing on disseminating laws related to garbage and educating people. Take care of proper garbage disposal.
Mr. Huot Hay, Deputy Governor of Phnom Penh, said that in order for Phnom Penh to have no garbage, there are three factors:
* First, people must dispose of garbage properly within the set time, and when the garbage is stored, the garbage must be packed properly. * Second: Garbage collection companies must collect garbage properly on time and Clean each litter bin thoroughly. * Third: Public institutions must also have a standard landfill.
He said that when these three things are in harmony, then the whole city is a city without garbage, beautiful and attractive to tourists.
Mr. Huot Hay called on the people of Phnom Penh to dispose of garbage properly on time and when garbage is stored properly, so that workers can easily collect garbage in garbage trucks. And cause beauty in the capital as well.
Mr. Sok Penh Vuth, Daun Penh District Governor, said that the purpose of the cleaning and sanitation campaign now is to show the people who come to visit the riverside park to love the environment, know how to properly dispose of garbage and not. Trash should be dumped in public places or outside the bins and must contribute to improving the beauty, hygiene and environment around us.
Mr. Hout Rithy, Director of the Department of Clean City Support and Competition Promotion of the Ministry of Tourism, said that in 2019, the world celebrated this day for the first time, with 157 countries and 21 million people participating. A total of 100,000 tons of garbage was collected, of which about 800,000 people in Cambodia celebrated the day.
Mr. Hout Rithy said that in 2020, the world will celebrate this day for the second time, with 158 countries around the world participating.
The director of the international organization also suggested that the Royal Government of Cambodia should tighten the implementation of laws related to waste management. Anyone who litters must be fined or punished for their actions.
Also present were Mr. Ou Chheang, Governor of Kien Svay District, District Councilors, Commune Councilors, Youth and a total of 245 farmers.
During the ceremony, Mr. Kao Thach also informed the farmers and young people about 6 important points:
1. Disseminate the current political situation and highlight the achievements of the Royal Government of Cambodia, headed by Samdech Techo Hun Sen. At the same time, Mr. Kao Thach continues to encourage and nurture the youth and farmers to continue to love and support the Cambodian People's Party and to help spread the good deeds and achievements of the party.
2: About economic news abroad and in Cambodia.
3. About the role of the Rural Development Bank and Agriculture.
4. Credit policy and procedures for obtaining credit in the special financing project of the Royal Government of 50 million US dollars.
5: Share information about the agricultural sector in Cambodia and give some practical examples as input about planning for cultivation, raising, which makes a profit in terms of budget, time and especially to ensure adequate supply to the market. .
At the same time, Mr. Kao Thach will organize trainers to participate in training on animal husbandry and vegetable growing, business plan for you to have an entrepreneurial idea.
Khmer King Presents Diplomas to Buddhist Students at Sihamoni Raja University (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of the Kingdom of Cambodia On the morning of Saturday, September 26, 2020, His Majesty the King was pleased to present diplomas to a total of 815 Buddhist students of Sihamoni Raja University.
The Royal Graduation Ceremony was also attended by Samdech Preah Abhisiri Sokunthea, High Priest, Honorary Doctor, Dr. Bour Kri, High Priest of the Dhamma Judiciary of the Kingdom of Cambodia and Rector of Sihamoni Raja Buddhist University and leaders. Many priests. The ceremony was also attended by Mr. Chhit Sokhon, Minister of Cult and Religion and other senior officials of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
Fellows - Students who graduated under the high presidency of the King of Cambodia today include: Bachelor's and Master's degrees. The Royal Graduation Ceremony for the students has been held twice before. The first and second royal ceremonies were held in the Royal Palace due to the small number of students.
Separately, the third Royal Graduation Ceremony was held at the Koh Pich Theater due to the large number of students. The Royal Ceremony of Graduation Ceremony was held in a solemn and orderly manner.
The winning students, both men and women, were highlighted in traditional Khmer costumes, requiring them to wear embroidered shirts, tunics with stilettos, and color-coded according to their degree level.
The King of Cambodia said that under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the society has achieved peace and prosperity in all fields, including Buddhism from primary school to higher education.
The King of Cambodia commended all the leaders of Sihamoni Raja Buddhist University for their hard work and dedication to lead and manage the Buddhist University and provide knowledge to the students and students.
Sihamoni Raja Buddhist University is a public higher education institution that contributes to the education of monks and the children of the Cambodian people free of charge. The Buddhist University has played an important role in imparting knowledge and cultivating human resources in Cambodia.
Samdech Preah Moha Sangkha Reach Bour Kri said that the Buddhist University of Sihamoni Raja trained in 6 majors, including: science of education, general management, philosophy of Buddhism, law, computer science and English.
Samdech Preah Moha Sangkha Reach Bour Kri also said that from the academic year 2004 to 2019, Preah Sihamoni Raja Buddhist University has successfully trained 3 undergraduate and graduate students. 982 students and are training a total of 1,675 students in the 2020 school year.
In addition, in order to meet the actual needs and quality of education of Buddhist students, the University of Buddhism has set the priority goal that "quality education is the main cause of promoting national prestige on the international stage and as a child. The key to solving economic and social problems.
