The "Honorary Doctor of Economic Security" Awarding Ceremony to Honorary General Dr. Hing Bun Heang was presided over by Dr. Kao Kim Hourn, Founder, Chairman and Rector of the University of Cambodia at the Bodyguard Headquarters in Tuol Krasang, Takhmao City, Kandal Province. With the participation of government officials and some distinguished guests as well.
According to a press release from the University of Cambodia, this is the 55th time since the establishment of the University of Cambodia in 2003 that the university has awarded degrees to students and dignitaries. The first diploma was awarded in 2004 to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
The reason why the University of Cambodia decided to award the "Honorary Doctor of Economics" degree to General Hing Bun Heang is because:
* Factor 1: He served as the Commander of the Bodyguard Command, in which he served and protected the leaders and institutions of Cambodia as well as the leaders of other countries during their visits and participation. Meeting in Cambodia.
* Factor 2: He has been actively involved in maintaining peace, security, and political stability, which are important for Cambodia's economic growth and sustainable development.
* Factor 3: He actively supported the development and promotion of civil-military relations by assisting with work related to natural disasters and community development.
