Spokesman for the General Commission: On September 25, another 1,066 vehicles were inspected and fined
According to the spokesperson of the General Commissioner, within 148 days of tightening the road traffic law by increasing the fine according to Sub-Decree No. 39, from May 1 to September 25, 2020, the traffic police nationwide inspected And fined a total of 177,308 vehicles, including 131,302 motorcycles and 46,006 vehicles of all types.
Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun said that for the past 148 days, the implementation of the new sub-decree to fine vehicles for offenses has been going well. He thanked and commended all the road users for their good obedience to the traffic law so far, especially the traffic police for their dedication and hard work. Tighten traffic with the highest sense of responsibility.
It should be noted that for September 25, 2020, there were 9 traffic accidents throughout Cambodia, in which 7 people were killed and 8 people were injured (06 people were seriously injured). During the 148 days, there were 1229 traffic accidents in Cambodia, in which 615 people were killed and 1931 injured (1,150 seriously injured).
