Cambodia-Australia Agricultural Value Chain Program Provides Additional Financial Assistance to Agricultural Enterprises through the Second Cambodian Entrepreneurship Assistance Package
In response to the impact of Kovid 19 disease that Cambodian entrepreneurs are facing, the Ministry of Economy and Finance, through Cambodian Entrepreneurs, has developed this Cambodian Entrepreneurship Assistance Package.
This program is a sharp strategic solution designed to respond to the challenges facing start-ups and small and medium enterprises in Cambodia. The program is also one of the main ways to stabilize the supply and demand in the market, especially to help start-ups and small and medium-sized enterprises to resume business during the post-19 crisis period.
In a mission to promote agricultural processing to replace imports, Cambodian entrepreneurs have established partnership agreements with CAVAC. In addition, in the process of implementing the Cambodian Entrepreneur Assistance Package, CAVAC participated as an evaluation committee in the third phase. Through this arrangement, CAVAC is fully equipped to provide additional financial assistance to any qualifying entrepreneur who meets the CAVAC program objectives.
Cambodian Entrepreneurs believes that the financial assistance provided through the Cambodian Green Assistance Package can be an effective solution for start-ups and small and medium enterprises to resume business in the meantime. Cambodian Entrepreneurs also hopes that many other partners can initiate various activities to support start-ups and small and medium enterprises, as well as to promote the development of the entrepreneurial ecosystem in Cambodia.
