The Ministry of Economy issued a press release on the results of the second meeting of the Policy Action Committee for the Promotion of Small and Medium Enterprises.
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Economy and Finance has issued a press release on the outcome of the second meeting of the Policy Action Committee for the Promotion of Small and Medium Enterprises.
"The Second Meeting of the Policy Action Committee for the Promotion of Small and Medium Enterprises" was held on the afternoon of September 23, 2020, at the Ministry of Economy and Finance under the chairmanship of Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister. Ministry of Economy and Finance and Chairman of the Policy Action Committee for the Promotion of Small and Medium Enterprises (OSME).
The meeting was attended by the leaders of relevant ministries and institutions who are members of the committee. To promote small and medium enterprises, this second meeting, the Committee discussed the following agenda:
1: Progress of the implementation of the measures approved at the first meeting: After reviewing the progress report of the implementation of the measures for the past two months, the meeting highly appreciated the results achieved and urged the Ministry - Institutions Involve, continue to cooperate and promote the implementation of each measure more effectively.
2: Measures for requesting review and decision: a: Redefining small and medium enterprises (SMEs):
In order to be consistent between the relevant ministries and institutions for the implementation of targeted and effective SME development policies, once again, the meeting discussed the definition of small and medium enterprises, which was determined based on the conditions. The two numbers are: 1. Number of staff and 2. Annual turnover or assets divided into three sectors: - Agriculture, - Industry, and - Services and trade.
B: Elimination and modification of duplicate licenses or certificates:
The meeting also urged the relevant ministries and institutions to explore the possibility of facilitating and expediting administrative procedures and linking the issuance of licenses or other relevant certificates to the CamDX online nursery, which the Royal Government has recently launched.
C: Adjust the overlapping inspection functions between ministries and institutions:
3: Proposal for additional measures:
The meeting also requested the inspection team to adhere to the inspection procedures and to clarify the rights of the business owners to the owners of small and medium enterprises during the inspection.
Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister and Chairman of the Meeting, emphasized that enhancing the effectiveness of the implementation of the approved measures and promoting further work to promote small and medium enterprises requires inter-ministerial coordination and inter-sectoral cooperation in Monitoring and implementation.
