Samdech Techo Hun Sen Celebrates the 27th Anniversary of the Promulgation of the Cambodian Constitution (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): On September 24, 2020, this is the 27th anniversary of the official promulgation of the Constitution of Cambodia. The Kingdom of Cambodia after the end of the conflict and after the 1993 elections. The Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, congratulated the promulgation of the Constitution, the supreme law of Cambodia.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen recalled that on September 24, 1993, in the Great Temple of Deva Vinich in the Royal Palace, His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk, the former King Father, he signed the Royal Decree announcing Officially use the Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia. September 24 is the birthday of the 1993 Constitution, and by 2020, the Cambodian Constitution will be 27 years old.
Samdech Techo, Head of the Royal Government, emphasized that the Constitution is the supreme law of the Kingdom of Cambodia. All laws and decisions of state institutions must be in strict accordance with the Constitution. Some of the most important points clearly stated in the Constitution are that Cambodia must strictly adhere to the constitutional monarchy, liberal democracy and pluralism.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen added that the Cambodian Constitution stipulates the principle of separation of powers: the legislature, the executive and the judiciary, and also approves the fundamental rights of the people and the rule of law.
