This statement was made on the occasion of Mr. Patrick Murphy's meeting with Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Economy and Finance. The meeting took place on the morning of September 23, 2020 at the Ministry of Economy.
During the meeting, Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth expressed his deep gratitude to the Government and people of the United States for their generous contributions to Cambodia's development, especially in the areas of health, education, agriculture, environment and governance.
Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth said that the United States, like other development partners, has actively contributed to the Royal Government of Cambodia in the fight against Kovid-19.
In fact, on May 21, 2020, the United States announced a grant of US $ 7.5 million for the recovery of the Cambodian economy after being affected by Kovid-19 and for the fight against epidemics. This.
At the same time, Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth also informed Ambassador Patrick Murphy that the Royal Government of Cambodia is currently implementing intervention measures to maintain economic and social stability and promote economic growth.
At the same time, the Royal Government of Cambodia will turn the challenges of the Kovid-19 crisis into an opportunity for reform and preparation for economic recovery.
In particular, trade and investment cooperation between the two countries, Cambodia and the United States, went smoothly and with remarkable progress.
In a bid to help revive the Cambodian economy, the United States International Development Finance Corporation (DFC) will provide low-interest financing to the private sector in Cambodia, especially for small and medium-sized enterprises, to alleviate difficulties. Is facing the crisis of Kovid-19 disease.
Therefore, the Ambassador will encourage more American investors to invest in Cambodia to expand bilateral trade between the two countries and contribute to the livelihood of the Cambodian people.
On that occasion, Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth once again thanked the American government and people for their invaluable contributions to Cambodia's economic and social development.
Senior Ministry of Health official tells US businesses investing in Cambodia not to worry as government slows reforms
Secretary of State O Vandin said that despite the global crisis caused by Kovid-19, which has slowed the global economy, US businessmen investing in Cambodia should not be alarmed. Cambodia does not slow down the pace of reforms and new incentives in social development.
She said that although the Kovid-19 epidemic has been causing many difficulties to the social and economic work process, the Ministry of Health has not slowed down the work of reform, construction and improvement of infrastructure and improving the quality of health services. .
She also thanked the US government as well as some of the companies that have cooperated well with the Department of Health to help the health sector in the past, especially in the context where we have been fighting the disease. Covid-19.
The Secretary of State informed the meeting that as of September 23, 2020, Cambodia had 275 cases of 19 Kovid infections and only one case was being treated at the Khmer-Soviet Friendship Hospital and there were no fatalities due to Kovid-19 disease.
The Ministry of Health has not yet seen a transmission of the deadly virus into the community. The proud and effective management and response to Kovid-19 is due in large part to the wise leadership of the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, who has led and put in place measures. Timely and active participation of sub-national authorities and people across the country.
In addition, Ms. O Vandin encouraged all American investors to conduct their business in accordance with the laws in force in Cambodia to provide Cambodians with quality health products and services and to participate in the fight against counterfeit drugs and Poor quality with the Ministry of Health, which is one of the many priorities under the guidance of Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
She also asked company representatives to continue to promote the Royal Government's efforts to enhance Cambodia's competitiveness and to attract more American investors to invest in the health sector in Cambodia, especially in the capacity building of the department. Doctors, training and digital health technology modernization.
