(Phnom Penh): Mr. Vong Soth, Minister of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, claims that more than 10,000 families have had their poor cards revoked after their lives have been lifted out of poverty.
Mr. Vong Soth confirmed this at the press conference to present the results of the implementation of the cash support program for the poor affected by Kovid 19 on September 23, 2020.
Mr. Vong Soth said that while searching for the poor and affected people during the 19 epidemic of Kovid, the ministry team also found people living out of poverty.
"To say that those who cross the poverty line means that they no longer meet these poor conditions," he said. When we find out that he is no longer eligible, we withdraw the card. "Here, we continue to practice, both recognizing the new and withdrawing the old card, generally speaking, those who meet all the conditions, we keep if you pass the conditions and we withdraw the card back."
Mr. Theng Panhathorn, the Royal Government delegate in charge of the Director General of Planning of the Ministry of Planning, stated in an interview with Fresh News that the people who received the equity card and were considered poor were examined and evaluated according to three main conditions: : Housing situation, appliances and daily living conditions. These citizens are interviewed and inspected by the officials where they live.
