Drug addiction is a treatable brain disease! Nationwide drug crackdown for September 23: 24 cases cracked, 63 arrested
(Phnom Penh): The nationwide campaign against illegal drugs for September 23, 2020 showed that law enforcement forces cracked down on 24 cases, including 11 cases of use, 13 cases of trafficking and arrested 63 suspects.
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Health on September 23, 2020 confirmed that breast milk is the perfect food for babies and children in all circumstances. No product, including formula milk, is better than breast milk.
Once again, the Ministry of Health would like to reassure the public that "scientific evidence makes it clear that breast milk is the perfect food for babies and children in all circumstances." No product, including formula milk, is better than breast milk. "Breast milk contains all the nutrients a baby needs without adding food, water or drink during the first six months of life."
According to the Ministry of Health, the main nutrients in breast milk include: Protein, which is an important building block for the development of children's physical growth. Stabilizing a child's body temperature, as well as helping the child's body to store energy and water, which are essential needs of children on a regular basis.
In addition, breast milk is rich in nutrients and minerals such as asbestos, iron, potassium, calcium, etc., which are important agents for protecting children from diseases.
Strong scientific evidence confirms that breastfeeding immediately during the first hour after birth can prevent 20% of infant deaths in children who are exclusively breastfed during the first six months Reduced diarrhea by 11 times and pneumonia by 15 times compared to children who were not breastfed.
The Ministry of Health states that not breastfeeding seriously affects the brain and cognitive development of children. Children who were not fully breastfed had smaller brain size than children who were fully breastfed. Not only that, they lose their intelligence compared to children who are fully breastfed.
Breastfeeding, including formula, can pose many risks to children, such as diarrhea, pneumonia, asthma, poor intelligence, diabetes, high blood pressure, heart disease, and overweight. Obesity and so on.
The Ministry of Health calls on all stakeholders working in maternal and child health to:
1. Strengthen cooperation to ensure good nutrition for mothers and children, in which breastfeeding is the best investment to reduce child malnutrition.
2. Increase awareness campaigns on the importance of breastfeeding and the risks of formula feeding at both the national and sub-national levels, including public and private health facilities.
3: Public and private media, social media must continue to disseminate and actively develop programs related to breastfeeding with meaning and content, higher education and
4: Continuing to strengthen the strict implementation of Sub-Decree No. 133 dated 18 November 2005 on the Promotion of Products for Baby and Child and Joint Inter-Ministerial Prakas No. 061 dated 16 August 2007 On the implementation of Sub-Decree No. 133 on the promotion of products for raising infants and children.
The second round of Kovid 19 subsidy ends in September, while the third round is under consideration
(Phnom Penh): Cash support to the poor during the four-month period of the 19-year epidemic in the first and second rounds will end in September 2020, and the implementation of the round-the-clock cash program 3 The following month is under consideration and development of Kovid's disease 19.
In June, Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen decided to release a national budget package to support the poor level 1 and level 2 to help alleviate the hardships of life when they lost their income due to the epidemic of Kovid 19. .
Mr. Vong Soth, Minister of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, said in a press conference on September 23, 2020 that the cash support program has run well under the care of Ministry officials and Local authorities.
Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Economy and Finance, has stated that since the launch of the cash assistance program for poor and vulnerable families during the fight against Kovid 19 from 25 May. June As of September 08, 2020, the Royal Government has already provided more than $ 78 million to poor and vulnerable families.
With the closing of the second round of cash subsidies in September, it is not yet known whether the Royal Government will continue to implement this cash subsidy program for the third round in October and November.
Mr. Vong Soth said in the press conference that for the third round is not clear yet, it depends on the decision of Samdech Techo Prime Minister. However, the minister hopes that the cash program will continue as Kovid 19 has not yet ended.
John Narith, Undersecretary of State at the Ministry of Economy and Finance and Secretary-General of the National Council for Social Protection, also did not dare to confirm whether the program will be implemented or not? He told Fresh News by telephone that the government was monitoring the situation of Kovid 19.
According to Mr. John Narith, if the situation of Kovid 19 continues to spread and have a serious impact on society, the Royal Government may continue to implement this program.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen has announced that the Royal Government has prepared up to 125 million US dollars for 5 months to help the poor. The Prime Minister also announced that as long as Kovid 19 disease is still endemic and affects society, the Royal Government will continue to provide cash to the poor.
Please be informed that on June 24, 2020, the Royal Government announced the implementation of the program to provide cash to people living in poverty and vulnerable to Kovid 19 disease.
The sponsorship lasts for two months for the first round, June and July, and the second round applies for August and September.
To receive this allowance, poor and vulnerable families must have a valid equity card based on poverty level: poor level 1 (poor) or poor level 2 (poor) and go to verify the list of cash aid programs. Poor families during the fight against Kovid 19 at a commune hall.
