Leaders of the Board of Priests of Cambodia inspire Cambodians to replant seedlings because it is very useful
(Siem Reap): Preah Moha Vimal Thom Sereysovano Pin Sem, Royal High Court and Supreme Advisor to the Board of Priests of the Kingdom of Cambodia and Preah Chao Athikar Wat Reachbo, led about 60 monks to plant seedlings in the northern part of Angkor Wat. And inspired Cambodians everywhere to replant the seedlings, because this plant is very useful, we just do not know.
He said that the palm tree has great benefits that the Cambodian people must know and participate in replanting so as not to lose, especially the palm tree is a high plant in Brahmanism and used as a medicine.
The main purpose of Venerable Pin Sem seeking to plant seedlings now is because he understands its enormous value, which he describes as saying that according to ancient rules, seedlings can be used as a medicine for healing. Age helps the human body a lot, helps to have strong skin and so on.
The bud is also a plant that is revered in Brahmanism, it is often said to be a plant of Shiva (Iso), because its leaves have three leaves in each stalk, like the spear of the three-headed Shiva, and it is like the eye. Preah Iso is like that.
The bud is also a plant used in royal ceremonies, as its leaves are used in coronation and royal ceremonies.
Understanding the value of the overgrown saplings, the Venerable Pin Sem initiated the idea of replanting the Angkor area and was able to attract tourists as its flowers were fragrant all the time. One month.
In addition, he also wants all Cambodians to start replanting valuable plants such as Sdao, Krasang and tamarind, which he understands that it serves the daily lives of Cambodians, but people turn Do not understand its value and do not replant.
Mr. Hang Pov, Director General of APSARA Authority, said that APSARA Authority is happy to cooperate and provide a location for planting this seedlings. The Apsara Authority has prepared a plot of land north of Angkor Thom to be used for plantations and planting various varieties of seedlings for the benefit of the future, as well as for the Cambodian people to know about this plant.
He added that in the Angkor resort, there are up to 183 species of trees, and the principle of the APSARA Authority is to maintain the area is still rich in natural resources, such as forever.
Pursat Provincial Governor Tells Authorities and Road Construction Company to Inspected and Resolve the Water Source to Release Floods from Pursat City
(Pursat): Mr. Mao Thunin, Governor of Pursat Province, told the Pursat Municipal Authority and the construction company of Vieng Krong Road to inspect the location to open the water to do to relieve the flooding that is flooding quickly. At the same time, it is necessary to immediately report the actual situation to the provincial administration for review, response and timely resolution.
The provincial governor said this on September 23, 2020 at the forum of Pursat provincial hall on the occasion of chairing an emergency meeting to solve the flooding in Pursat city with the participation of the deputy governor. Relevant skills: Intercity road construction companies and water treatment plant construction companies, as well as many other relevant officials.
Mr. Mao Thunin said that after being affected by two consecutive days of rainstorms, Pursat province was experiencing floods and flash floods along the Pursat River, which flows through four cities and districts. (There are 18 communes / sangkats) causing damage to housing, rice and some infrastructure.
The 11-kilometer-long, 60-meter-wide bypass and flyover across the Pursat River is a new economic route that facilitates transportation and travel to avoid congestion when entering the city, the provincial governor said. He added that for the sake of aesthetics and to raise the profile of the province, the provincial administration requires 10 meters on each side of the road and 2 meters on the chest to plant flowers or plants that prove the identity of Pursat province.
Mr. Mao Thunin said, "We have already resolved the impact on the people, but there are still two families who refuse to accept compensation, so we ask the municipal authorities to take legal action so as not to obstruct the implementation of the project." Above this.
At the same time, he also asked Silsong Shinkovan, a company that builds roads between cities, to speed up the construction of the flyover as soon as possible after the floods have eased and to deal with the opening of the water to release water. That is flooding Pursat quickly.
On that occasion, Mr. Mao Thunin also handed over a letter of thanks to the philanthropists who donated rice, materials and funds to the provincial administration to help solve the problem in the face of the situation in Pursat province is facing floods.
