The Royal Government allows spectators to watch the Samdech Techo Hun Sen Football Tournament and the Metfone Cambodian League Trophy again, but limited to 10% of the total number of seats!
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Health on September 23, 2020, issued a press release on allowing spectators to watch the Samdech Techo Hun Sen Football Tournament and the Metfone Cambodian League 2020, but limited the number of people. Only 10% of the total number of seats.
According to the press release of Samdech Techo Prime Minister dated 23 September 2020 on the letter No. 202 SCOL dated 22 September 2020 of the Ministry of Health to allow spectators to watch the competition. Samdech Techo Hun Sen Football Trophy and Metfone Cambodian League 2020, allowing for 10% of the total number of seats in each stadium, but the following measures must be observed:
* Continue to broadcast live sports matches on Facebook TV. * Establish a committee to monitor club sports competitions in the context of Kovi-19 disease. * Visitors must pre-register online by setting a clear seat location and address, as well as a telephone number. * Each club must adhere to the health rules that have been implemented, such as:
1: There must be an automatic thermometer equipped with a camera and a disinfectant alcohol spray at the entrance of the stadium 2: All spectators must always wear a mask during the game 3: Each club must have enough alcohol or hand washing for Visitors 4: Keep personal safety distance 5: Each stadium must have adequate toilets (one toilet for 25 to 50 people if possible).
6: Do not allow spectators with colds to watch the game.
7. Sports clubs that do not follow the rules of the Ministry of Health do not allow spectators.
8. If any audience is found to have Kovid-19, the Inter-Ministerial Commission for the Fight against Kovid-19 will temporarily suspend the audience until a new decision is made by the Prime Minister.
Therefore, for the safety and well-being of the Cambodian people as well as the whole of Cambodia, the Inter-Ministerial Commission for the Fight against Kovid-19 calls on all citizens to continue to take the necessary precautionary measures to prevent the spread of Kovid virus. -19 From person to person and not to be transmitted into our community.
