Thirteen houses collapsed and their roofs were completely opened due to rain and strong winds in Svay Rieng province
(Svay Rieng): At least 13 houses collapsed and their roofs were completely opened in Svay Chrum, Svay Rieng and Romduol districts due to heavy rain mixed with strong winds. The above natural disaster, which occurred at 9:30 pm on September 22, 2020, did not cause any danger to people.
According to the authorities, in Romduol district, there was rain mixed with strong winds, causing damage to 3 houses, including:
1. Name: Neth Sam An, male, living in Prey Srokum village, Pong Teuk commune, Romduol district, house made of galvanized iron, size 5 x 8, roof completely damaged. Houses made of wood, walls and corrugated iron roofs caused complete collapse. Name: San French, male, living in Leak Reachea village, Kampong Chak commune, a house made of 6 x 7 cypress wood, causing 9 cypress roofs to open.
The source added that in Svay Rieng city, there are 2 people, including:
1. Name: Neou Saran, male, 39 years old, in Svay Toeur village, Sangkat Svay Toeur, causing damage to a house, size 6x7, zinc roof (damaged 10 sheets of zinc, fallen trees). 2. Name: Preap Saren, male, 54 years old, in Prey Chhlak village. Sangkat Prey Chhlak, house size 5 x 7, zinc roof, causing the roof to be completely open.
