According to the guidelines, the Ministry of Health recently observed that some mothers complained about their children's health problems after formula feeding.
Some of the mothers confirmed that their children had anemia after being fed formula, and the results of the hospital examination confirmed that their children had iron deficiency. .
Once again, the Ministry of Health would like to assure the public that scientific evidence makes it clear that breast milk is the perfect food for babies and children in all circumstances.
No product, including formula milk, is better than breast milk. Breast milk contains all the nutrients a baby needs without the need for additional food, water or beverages during the first six months of life.
The main nutrients in breast milk include protein, which is an important building block for the development of the child's body. Balances as well as helping the child's body to store energy and fluids, which are the basic needs of children on a regular basis.
