(Stung Treng): 1,917 hectares of social land concessions of Stung Treng were cleared by the troops of the Provincial Military Operations Command to be distributed to the families of the retired youths of the three forces.
In the case of clearing the social land concession of Stung Treng province, which has 1,917 hectares of land to be distributed to the families of retired veterans, about 70 families in Kham Phan village, Samaki commune, Stung Treng city protested. Asked the commune chief to intervene at the national level to cut down their land that has been occupied and cultivated for a long time.
In applying for a settlement from the local authorities to the national level, the above-mentioned people accused the provincial military operations force of clearing land to sell to Chinese companies.
On the afternoon of September 22, 2020, Major General Svay Nhon, Deputy Commander of Stung Treng Provincial Military Operations Command, denied the allegations made by the people and confirmed to the public and the people in Kham Phan village on the afternoon of September 22, 2020 that There is no sale of land to any Chinese group, please do not believe the incitement from the outside world.
He said that the first step in clearing land is to clear about four roads to divide the lot to be distributed to the families of retired veterans, not to clear half a hectare of land for sale. 1 A is no sale.
Mr. Chan Sok Khom, Deputy Commander of Stung Treng Provincial Military Operations Command, said that the social land area of this province is 1,917 hectares for distribution to 1,188 families of retired veterans and 1 family received 30 plots of land in Kbal Dey village. Meters and 40 meters long and 2 hectares of agricultural land.
Separately, the village chief Kham Phan confirmed that the clearing was clearing, but asked to skip the land that the people have already enjoyed.
