(Pailin): On September 23, 2020, Mr. Phan Chanthul, Governor of Pailin Province, accompanied by Mr. Cheng Nhan, Mr. Khlok Nouy, Deputy Governor, Mr. Sun Yi, Governor of Pailin City and local authorities and the working group invited to talk. Visit and listen to the requests of traders who sell in Pahi Market (Lower Market) in Pahi Cheung Village, Sangkat Pailin, Pailin City, Pailin Province, after the situation of Kovid-19 disease in Cambodia seems to have improved.
During the visit, Mr. Phan Chanthul observed that the number of vendors and traders has increased, the stalls are not yet suitable, the road conditions in the market are narrow, causing traffic jams every day. There is regular watering, especially when it rains, because there is no drainage system to release water, and this is a concern and request of traders.
The provincial governor stated that the authority has the role of solving all the worries and concerns of the people in the market area and in the countryside in order to facilitate the people's livelihood in order to improve the family economy and contribute to the implementation of the reduction policy. Poverty under the right and skillful leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
On that occasion, Mr. Phan Chanthul requested all traders in the market to participate in improving hygiene and public aesthetics by placing goods in an orderly manner instead of displaying on the street, causing traffic jams, especially the owners. Market tax must cooperate with local authorities to maintain good order and security of the market.
Please be informed that: On that occasion, Mr. Phan Chanthul, Governor of Pailin Province, accepted the requests and concerns of traders on the road in the market and the drainage system. Learn to solve these problems as soon as possible. Kampot Provincial Governor Presides Over a Meeting to Discuss Public Infrastructure Improvement Project in Two Communes, Teuk Chhou District
(Kampot): Mr. Chiao Tay, Provincial Governor, chaired a meeting to discuss public infrastructure improvement projects in two communes, Trapeang Thom and Prek Thnout communes in Teuk Chhou district, which was held at Kampot Provincial Hall on September 23, 2020. Involve the leaders of departments, units and relevant authorities.
The purpose of the meeting is to discuss and study the impact to achieve rehabilitation and build to achieve successful results.
According to the presentation by the Provincial Department of Land Management, Urban Planning, Construction and Cadastral Affairs, the first project is the rehabilitation of a 2,000-meter-long canal in Trapeang Chrey village, Trapeang Thom commune, Teuk Chhou district, and the second project is the construction of a 12-meter-long concrete road with a length of 1842 meters in Prek Thnout village, commune. Prek Tnaot, Teuk Chhou district.
Mr. Chiao Tai agreed on the two projects and requested the officials of the relevant departments and authorities in the meeting to discuss and make suggestions for the process of restoration and construction of canals and concrete roads in both projects. The above two to achieve better results.
Saang District Police Arrested for Drinking Alcohol and Finding Villagers
(Kandal): After receiving a series of complaints in the case of a man who was drunk, he found out that the villagers were chasing him to the house of Saang district police on September 22, 2020.
Saang district authorities said that the incident of beating a villager in the house and pulling a knife to chase them happened on September 21, 2020 in Prek Snong village, Prek Koy commune, Saang district, Kandal province.
The victim, Sok Yonn, 26, a laborer, resided in Prek Snong village, Prek Koy commune, Saang district, Kandal province, while the suspect, Chan Nith, 27, a laborer, resided in Prek Snong village, Prek Koy commune.
Immediately after receiving the complaint from the victim, the police arrived at the scene and the suspect escaped, but on the morning of September 22, 2020, the police brought the suspect for questioning. In front of the police, the suspect confessed that he had beaten the victim and threatened to cut him with a knife.
The suspect is currently being sent to the Saang District Police Inspectorate to build a case file.
