Announcing the transfer of duties and appointments to senior police officers of the Department of Private Security Management
(Phnom Penh): The Senior Police Chief of the Private Security Management Department was announced to transfer his duties, appointments and ranks this morning, September 23, 2020, under the chairmanship of Lt. Gen. Ey Sok Khi, Deputy Commissioner General of the National Police, representing General Santi Dr. Neth Savoeun, National Police Commissioner.
On that occasion, Lt. Gen. Ey Sok Khi praised all the police officers of the Private Security Management Department who worked hard to get the position and promotion. He stated that what he got today was from what he had worked hard for in the past.
Lt. Gen. Ey Sok Khi claimed that the announcement of the role and promotion was due to the high attention of the leaders of the Royal Government, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Interior and General Sandibandit. Neth Savoeun, National Police Commissioner General, to encourage police officers to work hard.
According to Lt. Gen. E Sok Khi, all police officers who have been promoted and promoted must think that this is a new burden for themselves, that is, take what the leadership gives them to use for the purpose and according to what is The leadership should not be used to oppress the people.
In addition, Lt. Gen. Ey Sok Khi also reminded and introduced some work, including:
* Be grateful and have absolute loyalty to the King, the Head of the Royal Government, the Ministry of Interior and the General Commission of the National Police, no matter what the circumstances.
* Always be vigilant against the enemy's tactics that expand the dirty plan to overthrow the government.
* Must strengthen the internal unity of the unit and continue the tradition of internal unity well.
* Must respect traffic laws, especially vehicles equipped with unit number plates.
At the same time, Lt. Gen. Lim Sokharasmey, Director of the Department of Private Security Management, also reported on what the Department has achieved, especially in relation to the training of private security agents.
