General knowledge: In the history of the world, there are a total of 174 empires, but only 5 of the strongest
In 476 CE, the Western Roman Empire was completely overthrown by the German Empire. The Eastern Roman Empire was renamed the Byzantine Empire and lasted until the 15th century. By 1453, the Byzantine Empire was completely overthrown by the Ottoman Empire.
Before its complete collapse, this vast empire had been divided into four parts. Until 1368 CE, the entire empire collapsed.
