(Kampong Thom): Major General Som Sun, Commander of Kampong Thom Military Operation Area and President of Kampong Thom Provincial Veterans Association and his associates, accompanied by Sandan District Veterans Association and local authorities, handed over a new house as a gift to Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen through Senior Minister Kun Kim, Secretary General of the Cambodian Veterans Association.
The President of the Cambodian Veterans Association of Kampong Thom Province also donated food and money from Lt. Gen. Hun Manet to four other poor families, both of which took place on Wednesday morning, September 23, 2020.
Lt. Gen. Som Sun confirmed that 63-year-old Neay Chamnang Noly joined the army in 1988 at the 3rd Battalion of the Kampong Thom Provincial Army and was wounded in 1992 at the battle of Ny Pech Commune, Kampong Svay District, Kampong Thom Province. . Nou Ly is survived by his wife, leaving four children in his care, and currently lives in Samreth village, Chheu Teal commune, Sandan district, Kampong Thom province.
The new house, which was built and handed over to him, is now made of wood, with a galvanized roof, walls and floorboards, 4 meters by 6 meters. On this occasion, Major General Som Sun brought a message from Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit, who always consider the well-being and lives of our veterans and people at all times.
"The two princes called on our people to continue to be vigilant in preventing the spread of the 19-virus virus, which currently has millions of people infected and nearly a million dead." This is according to Mr. Som Sun.
During the handover ceremony, the team brought a gift from Lt. Gen. Dr. Hun Manet to support him: 50 kg of rice, 2 boxes of noodles, 2 kinds of fish sauce, 1 soy sauce, 1 mosquito net, 1 medicine and some money. Four other poor families who participated in the event received 25 kg of rice, a box of noodles, 2 bags of fish sauce, soy sauce, mosquito nets, some medicine and some money.
It should be noted that the new house that was handed over now is the 170th house that Samdech Techo handed over to the Kampong Thom Veterans Association.
