WASHINGTON (Reuters) - The US House of Representatives has approved a bill to keep the government running until Dec. 11 after two parties in Congress and White House officials signed an agreement to provide assistance to farmers and aid. Food for low-income families. This was released by Bloomberg on Wednesday, September 23, 2020.
The bill passed this Tuesday by a vote of 359 to 57, and the bill was sent to the Senate for a vote before the closure of government spending on September 30. Prevent a federal government shutdown before the November 3 US presidential election.
In addition to the budget for government agencies, the agreement will also allocate $ 30 billion to the Department of Agriculture, which the Trump administration and lawmakers expect. Democrats received about $ 8 billion for a child feeding program, up from the $ 2 billion first submitted last Friday.
Democrats have accused US President Donald Trump of using the draft budget for political gain. In fact, last Thursday, he announced that $ 13 billion from the CCC was to help rural areas in an election campaign in Wisconsin, a key battlefield state in the upcoming presidential election.
Mr. M. Chhun Lim: Differences in understanding of issues and solutions lead to ambiguity in the implementation of the Constitution in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): The Constitutional Council of the Kingdom of Cambodia on Wednesday morning, September 23, 2020, organized a conference to celebrate the 27th anniversary of the promulgation of the Constitution of Cambodia (September 24, 1993-September 24). 2020). The ceremony was presided over by His Excellency Dr. M. Chhun Lim, President of the Constitutional Council of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
"In order to measure the process of implementing the Cambodian Constitution to be fair and equitable for Cambodian society, it is necessary to weigh the Western ideology and also to consider the traditional characteristics of Cambodia in order to be optimistic and fair. Generous in evaluating the implementation of the Constitution in Cambodia. This is an additional emphasis of Dr. M. Chhun Lim, the Honorary Legal Officer.
The President of the Constitutional Council stated that the discussion in today's conference will surely lead to the development of the values of "Khmer-style modern constitutionalism", which is moving forward gently, vigorously and firmly, gradually adapting. In line with the modern concept of constitutionalism, it is necessary to maintain peace, stability, as well as to preserve the beautiful traditional culture of the nation.
