Constitutional Council Holds Conference to Celebrate 27th Anniversary of the Promulgation of the Constitution
(Phnom Penh): The Constitutional Council on September 23, 2020, organized a conference to celebrate the 27th anniversary of the promulgation of the Cambodian Constitution after the 1993 election.
The conference is also attended by Cambodian intellectuals, most of whom have a master's degree and a doctoral dissertation from major universities in Cambodia and other countries, and are all involved in public service or internal affairs. Professional and know the difficulties and eases of the national process.
Please note that the Constitution is the supreme law for a democratic Cambodia. The Constitution governs the sovereignty, role and status of the King, the fundamental rights of the Cambodian people, the economy, education, culture and social affairs, the functioning of the National Assembly, the Senate, the Congress and the Royal Government, the functioning of the judiciary, the Constitutional Council, the administration and the National Assembly.
Cambodia first drafted its constitution in 1947. The current Constitution of Cambodia, the Sixth Constitution, was approved by the Constituent Assembly on September 21, 1993, and was officially promulgated by the King of Cambodia, His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk. By Royal Kram, dated September 24, 1993. This constitution has 16 chapters and 158 articles.
