National Council of Cambodia for Children Holds Workshop on Child Protection from Exploitation
(Siem Reap): The General Secretariat of the Cambodian National Council for Children, in collaboration with the Dutch Territory (TDH), APLE and CPU, organized a workshop on promoting the protection of children from sexual exploitation and abuse in the criminal justice process. At Khemara Angkor Hotel.
The workshop was held for two days from September 22-23, 2020 under the chairmanship of Ms. Nheb Sopheap, Secretary General of the General Secretariat of the National Council for Children for Cambodia.
This workshop was held for three purposes:
* First, to raise awareness and use of existing national and international legal standards to protect children from sexual abuse and exploitation.
* Second: Study the shortcomings of the law and the implementation of challenges that hinder the effectiveness of implementation.
* Third: Identify strategic solutions and opportunities for cooperation between relevant institutions to promote response and intervention.
