The suspect was detained by the authorities to prepare a case for legal action. Cambodian Aquaculture Association officially inaugurated, Minister of Agriculture instructs the association to continue to promote and promote the development of freshwater and marine aquaculture
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, presided over the inauguration ceremony of the Cambodian Aquaculture Association and was attended by the Secretary of State, Undersecretary of State, representatives of the US Embassy, aquaculture, and many national and international guests. Himawari Hotel on September 22, 2020.
More importantly, it is timely and practical to implement the Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen's instruction on July 14 that hydropower farmers should form associations to form or unite as a force to protest the price. Technical training, dissemination of laws and regulations, and low-interest financing.
In connection with the current ceremony, Minister Veng Sakhon reminded the ceremony that so far, the Fisheries Administration has facilitated the establishment of 516 fishing communities (475 freshwater and 41 sea). Establish a total of 677 fisheries conservation areas, establish 895 community fish ponds, establish 309 fish hatcheries, 269 of which are owned by farmers.
Minister Veng Sakhon pointed out that there are currently a total of 46,000 aquaculture farmers, including 41,939 aquaculture families in ponds and 4,061 aquaculture families.
Minister Veng Sakhon clarified that due to the growing demand for freshwater and marine fish, it is necessary for stakeholders, especially aquaculture associations, to increase the capacity of breeding, breeding, production, care, protection and conservation. The height of the production chain, processing, increase value added and household income.
In response to this need, Minister Veng Sakhon advised the Association to continue to promote and promote the development of freshwater and marine aquaculture in accordance with the "Strategic Plan for Aquaculture Development 2016-2030":
Please be informed that the Fisheries Association of Cambodia was approved and recognized by the Royal Government of the Ministry of Interior on June 16, 2020.
The Cambodian Aquaculture Association aims to develop sustainable production, marketing, aquaculture and related products by strengthening technology, increasing the voice, market information and related services to the association members with transparency, equity and ethics.
The Cambodian Aquaculture Association is supported by the Aquaculture Development Project for Sustainable Trade in Cambodia (KAS), funded by the US Department of Agriculture, to promote freshwater fish production and develop aquaculture for long-term market and aquaculture needs. Long.
The KAS project has a number of development partners and organizations, such as the American Soybean Association, World Vision Cambodia, Sensei, Kansas University, Arbans University, and a number of development partners.
The Cambodian Fishermen's Association will cooperate with the government and local authorities, as well as national and international organizations, local and foreign investors, which aim to contribute to the economic development of Cambodia.
