(Pursat): After being affected by a series of rainstorms for two consecutive days, the geography of Pursat province experienced flooding and flooding along the Pursat River, which flows through four cities and districts (including There are 18 communes) affecting housing, rice fields and some infrastructure.
Pursat Provincial Administration issued a notification on the evening of September 22, 2020 about the impact as follows:
1: Veal Veng district, affected 4 communes, including Pramoy commune, Anlong Reap commune, Krapeu Pi commune and O'Som commune, a total of 20 villages, flooded 8 villages, 2 families, of which 2 families lost 24 boards, but did not cause accidents Anything will affect 318.5 hectares of crops, damage to 3 bridges, 1 road, Stung Krapeu point and 1 bridge collapse.
2: Pursat City affected 6 communes with 1,427 families, including flooded 828 hectares of rice fields, flooded 15 roads, including 1 dirt road, 11 red dirt roads, 2 rubber roads and 1 concrete road. Wire.
3: Kandeang district, affected 7 communes, a total of 27 villages, including 8,550 meters of flooded rubber roads, 1,685 meters of red dirt roads, affected 283 hectares of light rice and 2 banks collapsed.
4: Phnom Kravanh district affected 2 communes, in which Samrong commune evacuated 180 families, damaged 1,017 meters of roads and broke a bridge.
The spokesman further stated that the disaster management committees of the provinces, municipalities, districts, communes, sangkats and relevant institutions at all levels inspected the intervention 24 hours a day.
The US Embassy thanks Cambodia for facilitating the return of its diplomats during Kovid 19
The statement was made by the US Ambassador to Cambodia during a courtesy call on Prof. Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health, on the afternoon of September 22, 2020. This is the office of the Ministry of Health.
The US Ambassador expressed his deep gratitude and appreciation to the Royal Government of Cambodia for its excellent control of the 19 cases of Kovid. The status of the Kovid 19 pandemic has been successful to date. This was confirmed by the spokesperson and Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health, Ms. O Vandin.
In response, the Minister of Health also thanked the US Embassy in Cambodia and the United States Government, as well as officials for their good cooperation with the health sector in Cambodia, which has helped in the past, especially in the field of health. During the 199 Kovid Outbreak, the United States provided some funding to its partners to help improve health.
At the same time, the Minister said that while Cambodia is fighting against Kovid 19, the Ministry will also expand more laboratories in some provinces besides Siem Reap and Battambang to bring this service closer to the people, so hope to have partners Development continues to help more.
Please be informed that as of 07:00 AM on September 22, 2020, Cambodia has identified a total of 275 people with 19 cases of Kovid (54 females and 221 males), of which the total number of cured patients nationwide is 274 people (54 females and 220 males) and 1 patient is being treated at the Khmer-Soviet Friendship Hospital in Phnom Penh. The European Union is still testing 38 coronavirus vaccines, which are still being tested for efficacy and safety.
The World Health Organization (WHO) says 38 vaccine candidates are being tested, including those developed in China and Russia, while another 149 are still being evaluated.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, made seven recommendations to the World Economic Forum to recover the economies of developing countries from the Kovid 19 crisis (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on the afternoon of September 22, 2020. Join the World Economic Forum 2020 Summit via video.
At the same time, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also made seven recommendations to contribute to help developing countries can continue to build a sustainable future in the crisis caused by Kovid 19 disease. These seven recommendations include:
Second, the philosophy of the Royal Government of Cambodia is to turn the threat of Kovid-19 into an opportunity for reform in each country. On this basis. The Royal Government of Cambodia has not slowed down its reform work in all areas. Instead, our goal is to increase Cambodia's competitiveness by facilitating and creating a conducive environment for doing business and investing in the country.
Third, Kovid's disease has had an impact on public finances, especially state revenues. Loss of revenue requires the government to introduce new mechanisms to mobilize financial resources that can be used for future development. To achieve this, the partnership between the public and private sectors is seen as an indispensable core mechanism that will help solve the financial difficulties of developing countries both during and after the crisis.
Fifth, we must continue to work to strengthen globalization, which in the past has contributed significantly to economic growth and created unprecedented conditions for poverty reduction and improving the living standards of people at all levels. Caste.
In this context, we must ensure that our cooperation mechanisms remain open and supportive of the multilateral trading system, especially the acceleration of our social and economic connectivity, to advance the agenda. Of each country's sustainable development and environment.
Sixth, without delay, we must strategically consider the work to restore and promote the recovery of economic growth, after the end of the Code-19 crisis, by accelerating the implementation of plans and mechanisms. Existing and designed to add quickly and efficiently.
Seventh, at the global level, we must continue to ensure the sustainability of international aid, especially financial assistance to developing countries, to continue to drive the sustainable reform movement, which is the 2030 Agenda for the Development Goals. Sustainable.
In addition to these recommendations, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also thanked all development partners for their proactive cooperation and financial and technical assistance that helped Cambodia to control the spread. Of Kovid 19 disease very well.
Spokesman for the General Commission: On September 22, another 1,262 vehicles were inspected and fined
According to the spokesperson of the General Commissioner, within 145 days of tightening the road traffic law by increasing the fine according to Sub-Decree No. 39, from May 1 to September 22, 2020, the traffic police nationwide inspected And fined a total of 173,912 vehicles, including 128,869 motorcycles and 45,043 vehicles of all types.
Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun said that for the past 145 days, the implementation of the new sub-decree to fine vehicles for offenses has been going well. He thanked and commended all the road users for their good obedience to the traffic law so far, especially the traffic police for their dedication and hard work. Tighten traffic with the highest sense of responsibility.
Please note that for September 22, 2020, traffic accidents throughout Cambodia also occurred 5 times, in which 3 people died and 2 people were injured (2 people were seriously injured).
APSARA Authority collects water to prevent flooding of Angkor resort during heavy rains
(Siem Reap): Cambodia was affected by Typhoon Nol from September 18-20, 2020, which caused some areas to receive continuous rain and some areas were flooded, including Siem Reap province. The effects of this storm by getting a lot of rain.
Therefore, in order to cope with this situation, the water management team of APSARA Authority has made efforts to manage those waters in order to avoid flooding the Angkor resort area as well as Siem Reap city due to the effects of Typhoon Nol.
On the other hand, this year's rainy season, with slow rains and small amounts, makes it difficult to collect water into the reservoir and is also a major concern for the dry season water supply to the conservation of temples, clean water and agricultural irrigation. Of the people.
In this regard, the water experts of the Water Management Department of APSARA Authority, taking advantage of this heavy rainfall, managed and collected the rainwater through the traditional waterway system to be sent to be stored in the northern baray, Lalay Sindhu, Angkor Wat, Kasinthu Krong. Angkor Thom, West Baray, Kasindhu, Chao Srey Vibol and other reservoirs. Keynote Speech by Samdech Techo Hun Sen at the World Economic Forum Summit 2020
