(Phnom Penh): Mr. Soeur Lundy, Deputy Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, on the afternoon of September 22, 2020, completed the investigation and decided to charge the accused Pa Sovannarith with violence under Article 217 of the Code. Criminal.
Please be reminded that the Criminal Police of Khan Sen Sok, Phnom Penh, on the morning of September 21, 2020, sent the suspect, Pa Sovannarith, to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court to hand over to the Prosecutor's Office to continue the relevant procedure in the case of beating a girlfriend. Full face in Sangkat Phnom Penh Thmey.
Sen Sok District Police Inspector Mr. Hour Meng Wang confirmed that this incident happened in the rented room No. 401, 4th floor, Road 1976, Poung Peay Village, Sangkat Phnom Penh Thmey, Khan Sen Sok at 1:30 AM on September 20, 2020. .
Suspect's name is Pa Sovannarith, 20 years old, living at house No. 563, Lum Road, Prey Chisak Village, Sangkat Choam Chao 1, Khan Por Sen Chey. The victim was her boyfriend Nuon Kim Lang, 25 years old, staying in the room above. In the first half of 2020, Kampong Cham provincial justice police officers cracked down on nearly 200 drug crimes
(Kampong Cham): Mr. Un Chanda, Governor of Kampong Cham Province and Chairman of the Provincial Anti-Drug Committee, said that the judicial police officers of the Kampong Cham Provincial Police Commission have strengthened measures and cracked down on nearly 200 drug crimes in the first half of 2020. This is an increase over the last half of last year.
Mr. Un Chanda said this morning, September 22, 2020, at the conference hall of Kampong Cham Provincial Hall on the occasion of the meeting to disseminate the report on the results of drug control in the first half and the direction of work in the second half of 2020. With the participation of the heads of departments, units around the provinces - governors of the 10 districts - cities and the three armed forces as well.
The provincial governor said that in the past, the Kampong Cham Provincial Administrative Unity Command has regularly instructed the local authorities as well as the competent officials to carry out their duties and responsibilities at the local level.
The provincial governor confirmed that in the first half of 2020, the police have made efforts to carry out their work responsibly on their profession, in which the police have cracked down on drug offenses, along with some measures such as education measures. Disseminate administrative measures, legal measures, rehabilitation and integration measures, and national and international cooperation measures.
At the same time, the provincial administration has implemented new measures, such as meeting with the owners of resorts, hotel owners or guesthouses, etc. to educate and make contracts in order for them to cooperate with the authorities to help prevent drug crimes.
He added that as a result of these efforts, the authorities have cracked down on 199 drug crimes and arrested 703 offenders by the first half of 2020, an increase of 99. Compared to the first half of 2019, 100 cases were cracked and more than 200 perpetrators were arrested.
The provincial governor said that although Kampong Cham province is not a place of production, but the drug is circulating and will be used by criminals as a place for trafficking and distribution, which affects the people in the community. The authorities must increase their capacity to make effective efforts to implement prevention, control and suppression measures effectively.
On that occasion, General Meas Virith, Secretary General of the General Secretariat for Combating Drugs, praised the Chairman of the Kampong Cham Provincial Anti-Drug Committee as well as the Judicial Police Force for their joint efforts in preventing and cracking down on crime. Drugs get good results in the first half of 2020.
He also instructed the competent authorities to continue their efforts to increase information collection, increase investigations and lead to more successful crackdowns.
