National Assembly Expert Committee and Representatives of the Royal Government Discuss Some Important Draft Laws
(Phnom Penh): In the morning of September 22, 2020, the National Assembly Expert Committee met with representatives of the Royal Government to discuss three important draft laws before putting them on the agenda of the National Assembly Plenary Session. The meeting took place at the National Assembly.
Meeting between the Second Committee, the Fourth Committee, the Committees of the National Assembly and the National Audit Authority with representatives of the Royal Government to review three draft laws under the chairmanship of Mr. Kittisetha Dr. Cheam Yeap, Chairman of the Second Committee.
The agenda of today's meeting includes:
Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Economy and Finance, emphasized the importance of the agreement on the elimination of double taxation on income tax and the prevention of tax evasion and tax avoidance between the Royal Government of Malaysia and Korea. Encourage investors to come and invest in Cambodia.
He added that the meeting was to show the spirit of the draft law and the purpose of the law to be included in the upcoming plenary session of the National Assembly to discuss and approve in order to encourage investors to come to Cambodia and get Trust the Royal Government.
Mr. Cheam Yeap said that the National Assembly always invites the representatives of the Royal Government to defend the last three draft laws before the National Assembly discusses and approves them and sends them to the Senate for further approval. According to National Assembly officials, the National Assembly will convene a plenary session in early October 2020 to discuss and approve these draft laws.
On behalf of the Royal Government and the Ministry, Minister Veng Sakhon, through her, thanked the Government and people of Japan through JICA for helping to build and develop Cambodia to date, including the important infrastructure that supports The national economy.
