He added that this is a project that the Ministry wants to improve the quality and safety of agricultural products, increase production and ensure the quality of pure seeds and preserve the forest.
Minister Veng Sakhon instructed the working group of the General Department of Agriculture, Forestry Administration and relevant units to work together to implement the above project to achieve good results as expected.
(Phnom Penh): The National Training Committee (NTB) on September 22, 2020, approved the approval of six training standards and legal documents developed in the field of technical and vocational education (TVET).
The review and approval of this national support document was presided over by Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training and Chairman of the National Training Committee, accompanied by a ceremony to update the composition and duties of the new National Training Committee. In the morning of September 22, 2020 at the Phnom Penh Hotel.
The standard training package in 6 sectors has 33 occupations from level 1 to level 5 of the Cambodian National Qualifications Framework (CQF), including construction, 8 occupations, mechanics (automotive sub-sector), 7 occupations, electricity and energy. 5 Occupations in Business and Information Technology 4 Occupations in Manufacturing 7 Occupations in Air Conditioning and Heating 2 Occupations and Standard Package 1 level competency assessor training.
This work is to support the implementation of the Cambodian National Qualifications Framework (CQF) linked to the ASEAN Reference Qualifications Framework (AQRF), as well as to support the Capacity and Qualification Assessment System for Cambodia (CBACS) to promote and Promote the development of technical and vocational education and training to meet the needs of the current Cambodian socio-economic society.
