(Phnom Penh): General Kwan Seam, Deputy Commander-in-Chief of the Engineering Command of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, confirmed that the Royal Government led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen has paid constant attention to retired soldiers through Increase salaries, benefits, and unforgettable merits of veterans who have made significant contributions to the cause of the nation, the motherland and the people.
This confirmation was made by General Kwan Seam on September 22, 2020 at the ceremony to equip 120 retired soldiers of the Engineering Command with the participation of the Deputy Commander of the Engineering Command. Deputy Director of some engineering command offices at Chom Chao Engineering Command, Phnom Penh.
At a ceremony to pay tribute to retired soldiers in 2020 at that time, General Quan Sam said that retired soldiers are now a great contributor to the liberation of the country, overthrowing the genocidal regime. The Pol Pot race will actively participate in the national unity movement through win-win politics, bring peace, complete national unity, and build and develop the nation to this day.
"The policy of the Royal Government is to pay attention to the soldiers at all times by raising their salaries and other benefits, whether on duty, when they retire or after they retire," said General Quan Sam. "It is impossible to forget the merits of the veterans who have made great contributions to the cause of the nation, the motherland and the people."
General Kwan Seam also gave the following six recommendations to retired soldiers:
First, strive to complete the task successfully so that all retired soldiers do not despair of us.
Second: Together, think together, build together to build the national defense unconditionally, according to Samdech Techo Hun Sen: "The engineering force is the backbone of the Royal Government must not lose the beautiful culture of the force. Our engineering. ”
Third: Absolutely oppose the terrorists who want to destroy peace, destroy Cambodia.
Fourth, strive to learn, train tirelessly, strive to transfer knowledge to the next generation, build capacity and build human resources.
Fifth, strive to pay attention and support as much as possible to retired soldiers.
And 6: Retired soldiers must maintain dignity, love and be friendly with the village, commune and local authorities where they live, participate in the implementation of the principle of 9 points of safe villages and communes, as well as participate in disseminating the policies of the Royal Government, including 3 programs. Politics, as well as preventing and counteracting the psychological warfare of the opposition, must strive to build a new life with a prosperous and exemplary family.
At the same time, the General confirmed that the current rank of retired soldiers is the policy equity of the Royal Government, where retired soldiers are promoted one more level.
