Four Ministries and USID Launch Campaign to Protect Prey Lang through Behavior Change
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Environment, the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, the Ministry of Information and the Ministry of Tourism, in collaboration with the United States Agency for International Development (USAID), have launched an environmental-oriented social change campaign to protect Cambodia's forests and wildlife.
The inauguration ceremony was held this morning, September 22, 2020, under the chairmanship of Mr. Sao Sopheap, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment, Mr. Say Sam Al, Representative of the relevant Ministries, and Ms. Dina Reddy, Director of Mission, USAID, and civil society organizations. Some at the Ministry of Environment.
The launch of the Prey Lang Protection Campaign recognizes the importance of forests in the area, the rich biodiversity of the forest and the benefits of forest sustainability, and therefore the United States Agency for International Development (USAID) and key Cambodian ministries have agreed to work together. Promote public participation in the protection of forests and wildlife.
"Today's launch demonstrates USAID's long-standing partnership in the field of environmental assistance in Cambodia, as well as our continued commitment to biodiversity conservation," said Dina Reddy. Important for Cambodia. We hope that this awareness campaign will encourage more Cambodians to participate in protecting their natural heritage. ”
"Cambodia is a country rich in forests, plants and wildlife," she said. Cambodia's forests are an important resource for economic growth and sustainable living, as well as for the preservation of culture, nutrition, and for various natural remedies that have provided many benefits to local communities.
Mr. Sao Sopheap said, "Cambodians, young and old, have an obligation to participate in the conservation and protection of our precious natural resources." The purpose of this campaign is in line with the Royal Government of Cambodia's action plan and environmental protection strategy, which aims to strengthen the effectiveness of environmental protection, natural resource management, biodiversity conservation and sustainable development.
The Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment continued that under the leadership of the Royal Government of Cambodia, headed by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, it is firmly committed to the sustainable management of the environment and natural resources.
This event demonstrates the US Government's commitment to promoting environmental protection, sustainable use of natural resources, and positive public action on the environment and nature.
