General knowledge: The secret behind the phenomenon "Sunrise at the top of the central tower of Angkor Wat" that occurs twice a year regularly
(Phnom Penh): In the early morning between September 22-23, 2020, the phenomenon of the sun rising on the top of the central tower of Angkor Wat will happen again, while every year this event attracts the attention of the people and Tourists are very, but at the same time, there are many questions about the secret behind this amazing phenomenon.
Mr. M. Sokrithy explained that the knowledge learned about the sun rising from the top of the central tower of Angkor Wat is not a new discovery, but a study that researchers have conducted in the past. The course explores the relationship between ancient architecture and astronomy to prove that it was not a coincidence or a miracle, but a foregone conclusion of the ancient Khmer scholars who led the construction of Angkor Wat.
To understand this, M. Sokrithy explains that one must first study the shape of the general universe and compare it to the architecture of Angkor Wat.
Ancient Khmer scholars designed the temple of Angkor Wat to replace the compact image of the universe on Earth in physical form, such as the arrangement of the oceans and the surrounding mountains with the four continents in the universe and Mount Sumeru in the center, as well as the journey. The evolution of the universe.
Researchers have taken the latter into account through Indian astronomical algorithms on the age of the universe, which is divided into four successive eras. Age is the love cycle of the universe in relation to birth, evolution, and disappearance. Between each era there is a transition, just born into a new era.
Each epoch is divided into four sub-eras, including:
2. The Tret Age, or Silver Age, has a life span of 1,296,000 years in the human realm, equivalent to 3,600 years in the angelic realm. People living in this age have a longer average life and more happiness.
Indian astronomical algorithms divide time according to the lunar and solar orbits of the moon and the sun. In one orbit of the sun, one year is divided into two journeys of 189 days and 176 days.
Because Angkor Wat is related to the love cycle of the universe, the size and length of the main structures of this temple are related to the age of each era that researchers have discovered in the past.
Mr. M. Sokrithy continued to explain through the results of that research that the scale used by ancient architects and engineers was "hand", but the length of the hand in the Khmer Empire always changed according to the period, that is, in the Angkorian era, the Khmer government used 1 hand. And 0.436 meters at present.
If we deliberately exclude some gaps, which are the tradition of carpenters and fillers, and deduct the remainder of the required integers, we will be able to understand the relationship of the length of the main structures of Angkor Wat to The age of the age of the love cycle of the universe can be summarized as follows:
3. The distance from Ta Reach Prison to the first staircase up to Bakan can be estimated to be the age of Tret Yuk, which is 1,296,000 years.
4. The distance from the front of the dragon to the central tower of Bakan can be estimated to be about the age of Kret Yuk, which is 1,728,000 years.
5. The length of the Bakan floor, which has a total of 365 cubits perpendicular, corresponds to the orbit of the sun at 365 days per year, which the astronomical field divides into two orbits, 189 days and 176 days.
We can also recognize this phenomenon if we stand facing straight when the sun rises straight in front of us, then rises straight in the center of our heads and casts shadows and human bodies. We overlap.
By calculating these astronomical and cosmological rules, the ancient Khmer architects built Angkor Wat to reflect both the universe and the love cycle of the universe, with the central tower of the entire temple acting as the center and the zero point. The orbit of the sun. Between 189 days and 176 days, the sun will reach this point.
According to this rule, only once a year, the sun always rises directly on the top of the central tower of Angkor Wat twice a year regularly. General Knowledge: Who is recognized as having the longest life expectancy and who is living the longest?
(Phnom Penh): The National Election Committee (NEC) has announced that it plans to register more than 300,000 new voters and remove more than 100,000 names from the voter list. This is according to the press release on the posting of the list of polling station locations and the final voter list in 2019 for the examination of the voter list and voter registration in 2020, which was received by Fresh News on the evening of September 21, 2020. .
According to the NEC, following the calendar of review of the voter list and voter registration in 2020, the list of polling station locations and the final voter list in 2019 will be posted in communes across the country on September 21. 2020.
The NEC added that the purpose of posting the final voter list in 2019 is for those who have already registered to check and verify their data. If the information on the voter list is not in accordance with the information on the Khmer Nationality Identity Card, the voter can request a correction with the voter registration team during the voter registration period in the commune.
Voter registration and voter registration will begin in all communes across the country on the same day, October 1 and end on October 19, 2020.
