Cambodia Representative to the United Nations: Cambodia is committed to the promotion and protection of all human rights.
(Geneva, Switzerland): Mr. An Sok Khoeun, Ambassador and Permanent Representative of Cambodia to the United Nations in Geneva, Switzerland, emphasized that Cambodia is committed to the promotion and protection of all human rights. Strongly welcomes the active participation of all stakeholders, including the Office of the United Nations High Commissioner for Human Rights.
Mr. An Sok Khoeun emphasized this during the 45th Session of the Human Rights Council, discussing the current report of the United Nations High Commissioner for Human Rights, Ms. Michael Basilleth, on September 15, 2020. .
In this intervention, Mr. An Sok Khoeun highlighted the strong cooperation of the Royal Government of Cambodia with the United Nations human rights officials to highlight the human rights work in Cambodia, despite the fact that Cambodia is facing the crisis of Kovid 19.
Mr. An Sok Khoeun recalled that last August, senior Cambodian officials from six ministries met with the Special Rapporteur on the situation of human rights in Cambodia, Rona Smith, via video. Cambodia has also agreed to a request for a visit to Cambodia by an independent expert in charge of protection against violence and discrimination scheduled for next year.
The Cambodian representative added that Cambodia respects the value of pluralism, including critical views that comply with the law. Earlier this month, a number of prominent former opposition politicians were reinstated, bringing the total to 12. This proves that the political space is open for opposing views of the government in Cambodia.
In addition, many former members of the opposition also wanted to reclaim their political rights, but they were blocked by their leaders, who publicly declared those who dared to re-apply for political rights. "Traitors."
By intervening on the human rights agenda, Mr. An Sok Khoeun also encouraged the High Commissioner to listen to the government's concerns at all times before concluding on human rights issues in Cambodia. Mr. An Sok Khoeun stressed that meaningful dialogue with the government before making any hasty conclusions will definitely help to promote the common cause of the promotion and protection of human rights.
