Pailin Provincial Authority Inspects Flood Situation in Stung Trang Commune to Rescue People in Time
(Pailin): After heavy rain in the upper part for several days in a row on September 21, 2020, Mr. Phan Chanthul, Governor of Pailin Province, accompanied by Mr. Cheng Nhan and Mr. Hok Sophal, Deputy Governor and leaders Relevant officials and youths of the Provincial Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia inspected the flood situation in Stung Trang commune, Sala Krao district, Pailin province to be ready to provide emergency food to the affected people in time.
On that occasion, Mr. Phan Chanthul urged the people living along the river and the lower part to be very careful when it rains for several days in a row and if any problems occur to report to Local authorities in a timely manner, especially to take care of health and live hygienically to prevent the occurrence of various diseases.
It should be noted that Stung Trang commune, Sala Krao district, Pailin province, is a lowland area that is inundated by floods almost every year when it rains heavily on the upper mountain. Cambodia is intervening to help people in time.
