Spokesman for the General Commission: On September 21, another 573 vehicles were inspected and fined
According to the spokesperson of the General Commissioner, within 144 days of tightening the road traffic law by increasing the fine according to Sub-Decree No. 39, from May 1 to September 21, 2020, the traffic police nationwide inspected And fined a total of 172,650 vehicles, including 127.43 motorcycles and 44,707 vehicles of all types.
Notable offenses for motorbikes are mostly without helmets, offenses, without license plates, drunkenness and using mobile phones. The offenses for cars are mostly speeding, overcrowding, drunk driving and cell phone use.
Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun said that for the past 144 days, the implementation of the new sub-decree to fine vehicles for offenses has been going well. He thanked and commended all the road users for their good obedience to the traffic law so far, especially the traffic police for their dedication and hard work. Tighten traffic with the highest sense of responsibility.
Please note that for September 21, 2020, traffic accidents across Cambodia also occurred 9 times, in which 4 people died, 024 people were injured (09 people were seriously injured).
