The suspect is currently being held in custody at the Meanchey District Police Inspectorate and the case is being processed by the court. Expert: Restrictions on the real estate sector provide good opportunities for legitimate businesses, but illegal businesses face serious challenges (Video inside)
Dr. Kim Heang emphasized that the development in the real estate sector in Cambodia includes the development of the subdivision of the lot, the development of the condominium sector, the development of the Borey sector and the development of recreational areas. Development, opportunities and challenges go hand in hand if entrepreneurs in this field know how to grasp.
Dr. Kim Heang stated that in the field of subdivision from 2013 to 2018, there are many opportunities and challenges are less, but now the subdivision sector is more challenging than opportunities. The reason is that the Ministry of Economy and the Ministry of Land have set a limit for those who want to do business in the field of subdivision.
"Therefore, it is a big challenge for illegal traders in this field, but for those who have a valid legal license, they can only move forward," said Dr. Kim Heang.
The reason is that some relevant ministries have intervened strongly against the builders, because in the past, people used to buy and there was a problem, the builders took the buyer's deposit and refused to build.
In addition, Dr. Kim Heang said that the condominium sector in Cambodia is not a problem because most of the condos are foreign projects are properly licensed and there are very few opportunities. On the other hand, the risk can be said that the problem changes over time, such as during the 19-year Kovid disease, making it impossible for foreigners to come, so the condominium sector is in trouble.
Dr. Kim Heang said that from February to the present, in the first seven months of 2020, foreigners who come to do business in the condominium sector have almost all disappeared, but there is still a local market.
At the same time, Dr. Kim Heang continues to claim that the real estate business in Cambodia in the future, whoever is in the real estate business illegally will fail because the people today have a lot of understanding.
"People can no longer trust those illegal traders, and when the wrong people face serious challenges, then the opportunity will fall to the legitimate traders," he said. More than 80 families in Sala Krao district, Pailin province are being affected by floods, authorities visit and intervene
