(Phnom Penh): In his presentation to the Japanese company Yamato Green Co., Ltd., which is famous for its tourism development, Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, mentioned the rich potential that is conducive to investment in tourism development in Cambodia, especially in the field of tourism. Ecotourism, agro-tourism as well as rural tourism.
The purpose of Yamato Green in this meeting with the Ministry of Tourism is to request the cooperation of the Ministry of Tourism to promote the development of the Green Belt in Cambodia related to tourism, social and economic.
Mr. Nabisima Makatsuheito said that through the green belt development project related to the above tourism sector, Yamato Green Company will make Cambodia's agricultural products "agro-tourism" and national and international tourists can enjoy the food. Exist at each tourist site safely. In addition, tourists can also visit the cultivation and maintenance techniques directly.
It should be noted that Yamato Green has also been successful and very famous in the development of agro-tourism and ecotourism in Battambang and Mondulkiri. Due to this factor, the company has a new development project with the Royal Government of Cambodia, the green belt above.
After many presentations by Mr. Nabisima Makatsuheito, Minister Thong Khon expressed his satisfaction and full welcome, approval and full support for the company's major development projects. This Japanese one.
Mr. Thong Khon also introduced to Mr. Nabisima and the Japanese delegation that Cambodia is a close friend of Japan and always welcomes all Japanese investment, especially in the field of tourism, because Cambodia has a lot of potential, which is a gift for Invest in tourism, especially ecotourism, agro-tourism as well as rural tourism.
In terms of the development of the above three types of tourism, Siem Reap and Kampong Thom are the most favorable for investment in agro-tourism and rural tourism, especially the construction of green belts, Mr. Thong Khon wants the company to consider. Invest in tourism development in these provinces after investing in Battambang and Mondulkiri. In addition, the company should build a model in each province before expanding to other provinces.
He added that in the context of Kovid-19, ecotourism, agro-tourism and rural tourism are being globally recognized and encouraged.
Minister Thong Khon and Mr. Na Bissima agreed to prepare a Memorandum of Understanding between the Ministry of Tourism and Yamato Green Co., Ltd. and to set up a joint working group to make this cooperation a success. Smooth success brings benefits to the people of Cambodia and to companies that strive to invest. Visit the gallery of international events on September 21, 2020 (Photo inside)
