(Phnom Penh): Twenty foreigners, including a woman, were allowed to enter the place of oath to take the oath of allegiance as Cambodian citizens. The swearing-in came after the 20 foreigners had met the criteria set by Cambodian law.
The swearing-in ceremony for Khmer citizenship took place on the afternoon of September 21, 2020 in the Supreme Court of the Kingdom of Cambodia. The Royal Decree is prepared to be sworn in before the Supreme Court to fulfill the legal status of a Cambodian citizen in accordance with the principles and procedures set by the Nationality Law.
Pursuant to Articles 16 and 27 of the Law on the Management of Foreigners, foreigners who have already acquired Khmer nationality through a Royal Decree shall take an oath before the Supreme Court. The Royal Decree granting Khmer nationality must be handed over to the person concerned after taking the oath.
