Her Majesty Queen Norodom Monineath Sihanouk Inaugurates the Samdech Mey Library of the Documentation Institute of the Documentation Center of Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Her Majesty Queen Norodom Monineath Sihanouk, Queen Mother of Cambodia, this morning, September 21, 2020, decided to inaugurate the Samdech Mey Library of the Documentation Institute of the Documentation Center of Cambodia.
The ceremony was also accompanied by two special exhibitions: 1: The relics of His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk, the former King Father of the Khmer nation. 2: Design of the Leaf Institute building of the Documentation Center of Cambodia by a world-class architect, Ms. Zaha Hadid.
The Samdech Mey Library was officially established by the Documentation Center of Cambodia to pay homage to Her Majesty Queen Norodom Monineath Sihanouk, the Queen Mother of Cambodia in the freedom, dignity and happiness that she strives for. Norodom Sihanouk, former King Father, King Father of Cambodia, Cambodia and the Cambodian people.
The Samdech Mey Library holds a collection of more than 3,000 books and 2,800 boxes of documents collected by Ambassador Hollywood. Jeldres spent many years compiling his documents on the royal family and the history of Cambodia. Ambassador Gelredres generously donated this large collection to the Documentation Center of Cambodia in late 2019.
* Exhibition of the relics of King Norodom Sihanouk, the former King Father of the Khmer nation.
This collection of excerpts is taken from the collection of Ambassador Holly Gelredes, collected between 1981 and 2019. Most of the relics originated from the personal collection of King Norodom Sihanouk, the former King Father of Cambodia, which was copied in Beijing between 1996 and 2004, before the relics were found. Sent for preservation in archives in France.
Most of the inscriptions include the period between 1950 and 1991, which shows the various activities of Samdech Preah Borom Ratanakod, the former King Father of the Khmer Nation, including: During his visit to Throughout Cambodia, in the cause of independence, he sometimes had horses as his queen to explain to the Cambodian people why Cambodia needed independence from France.
Some relics show that the period after Cambodia gained independence was a time when Cambodia was peaceful and the activities led by His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk, the former King Father of the Khmer Nation, in building the nation according to Volunteering and other activities with the Cambodian people.
