Samdech Techo Hun Sen Gives Compassion to Children and Mothers to Reunite in Case of Separation for More Than 7 Years
(Phnom Penh): In fact, Ms. So Srey Pov has been having a hard time getting divorced since 2013. The divorce required the parties to lose custody of their dependent daughter, Elis, as determined by the court.
The civil case is a family dispute that has been a final verdict since 2015 but was not implemented successfully by Mr. Duong Dara, the personal assistant of Samdech Techo Prime Minister, so that both parties can agree to implement it voluntarily successfully for the sake of Sok Sopheak Mongkul after the divorce on Sunday morning, September 20, 2020 this morning at the Peace Palace.
Under the highest guidance of Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister Duong Dara led a wise coordination team based on the win-win principle of Samdech Techo, reconciling and reconciling a middle-aged ex-spouse. The parties agree to abide by the Civil Judgment and the minutes of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court voluntarily.
Disillusioned with the deadlock, So Srey Pov, the mother, decided to ask Samdech Techo Prime Minister for mercy for the last time so that she could have the opportunity to meet her beloved daughter, who has been separated since 2015. Come on.
Of course, every citizen is a descendant of both princes. Samdech Lok has always been compassionate to people of all walks of life, no matter what the situation. After receiving a request from So Srey Pov (mother), Samdech Techo assigned Mr. Duong Dara, Samdech's personal assistant, to do this work immediately to check the legal aspect for a reunion between mother and child.
After receiving the highest guidance from Samdech Techo, Mr. Duong Dara invited both parties to mediate and guide the legal aspect until the end of the answer agreed to hand over the daughter named Suong So Elis to the mother named So Srey Pov by the verdict. Voluntarily, both parties agreed to sign a voluntary implementation agreement in front of Mr. Duong Dara.
In the afternoon of the same day, Mr. Duong Dara and his team, including local authorities, went to witness the handover of the daughter at the home of the father, Suong Phisir Narak, in a happy atmosphere.
Mr. Duong Dara explained that divorce is just one way to dissolve a legal marriage, but after the divorce, the parties must consider their children's happiness and do not create a culture of hatred because the child is not at fault and the parties do not Yes, children should not be taken hostage.
