Samdech Techo Hun Sen hopes that the Cambodia-China Free Trade Agreement will make Cambodia a target for US companies (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen met this morning, September 21, 2020. Some of the work involves investing and doing business with the US-ASEAN Business Council via video.
Samdech Techo emphasized that in this situation, the Royal Government of Cambodia has already set out five steps. Both measures help the economic and social sectors, aiming to help balance production and business, as well as ensure the livelihood of the severely affected people.
Samdech Techo said that some US businesses present in Cambodia have also benefited from these measures. Meanwhile, despite the Kovid disease problem, Samdech is proud of the increase in bilateral trade between the two countries, which in the first eight months of 2020 increased by nearly 17% compared to the same period last year. Go.
Samdech Techo informed the US-ASEAN Business Council delegation that although the Kovid 19 pandemic has been causing many difficulties to the social and economic life, the Royal Government of Cambodia has not slowed down the reform work in all areas. Its not.
Samdech Techo said that in order to attract more investors, especially when Kovid-19 disease is relieved, Cambodia is preparing to improve the investment law and new incentive system that is comprehensive and attractive for the electronics industry, assembly, Agro-industry, spare parts, support industry and other industries.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also mentioned the signing of a free trade agreement between Cambodia and China. He expressed hope that the agreement would help attract US investors to Cambodia.
Samdech Techo also told the US-ASEAN Business Council that as a way forward, Cambodia will implement appropriate and timely intervention measures combined with strategic considerations through the introduction of public financial policy. Monetary policy and structural reform measures aim to achieve two priority goals: to maintain economic and social stability and to stimulate economic growth.
In this meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked Mr. Alexander Fleman and all company representatives who came to attend today's meeting. Samdech Techo noted that the meeting was a demonstration of the attention of American companies to Cambodia, as well as the willingness to contribute to the development and improvement of the lives of all Cambodians.
