"International Day of Peace on September 21" is a historic day that the 55th General Assembly of the United Nations and all Member States unanimously adopted, designating September 21 as an annual Day of Peace to mark Stop all hostilities and strengthen the peaceful ideals of all nations and peoples in the world. The International Day of Peace 2020 is held under the theme "Building Peace Together".
Cambodia is known to have suffered the most devastation and national disintegration since the fall of the Angkorian Empire in the 13th century. Because of the conflict, Cambodia's vast territory in the Indochina Peninsula gradually became smaller. At the last stage, the Democratic Kampuchea regime of the Pol Pot genocide made Cambodia almost to ashes because of their genocidal policies.
The lives of the Cambodian people and the Cambodian nation as a whole were restored after the day of liberation on January 7, 1979. Cambodia has been prosperous and re-developed after 1998, after Cambodia completely extinguished the flames of war, ended the buffer zone, became a single country with a single regime and rule after the win-win policy set by Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
In this message, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the founder of peace in Cambodia, emphasized that Cambodia has just lived in peace and full national unity for more than two decades after going through the flames of war, division, suffering and tragedy. Not centuries ago in its history.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodia's bitter experience in the past and the successful implementation of the "win-win policy" in 1998 made the Cambodian people more aware of the value of peace and better understood its importance. Lack of foundations for development is peace and stability.
In this message, Samdech Techo Hun Sen reminded the Cambodian people to remember that peace is the only way to ensure sustainable development and a prosperous and prosperous life. Peace only guarantees the stability and progress of democracy and freedom, and the success of the development process and the strength of democracy and, in turn, ensures the sustainability of peace.
On this International Day of Peace, Samdech Techo Prime Minister also expressed his respect and appreciation to the Cambodian people at all levels who have sacrificed their physical and mental strength to participate in maintaining peace and political stability, promoting national sovereignty, strengthening Democracy, rights, freedoms and the rule of law and national development.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also thanked many friendly countries, development partners and international organizations that have supported the Cambodian people since the National Rescue from the genocidal regime, which is continuing to strengthen and Further expand fruitful relations and cooperation for the cause of peace, democracy and development.
Samdech Techo stressed that everyone needs peace, except for terrorists who want to destroy peace.
On this International Day of Peace, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also reaffirmed his strong commitment to maintaining this peace by adhering to the ownership of the two main priorities, including:
First, maintaining political stability as a basis for situation management
