Legal Awareness: Condemnation List
(Phnom Penh): In general, in the relationships of people in society, knowing the background of an individual is a necessary thing that is used as a basis for evaluating that person before deciding to establish a relationship, judgment and acceptance. Or assign any task, especially to that person's criminal history.
Therefore, in order to know whether a person has committed a crime before or not, it is necessary to have a record of the criminal record of that person. In Cambodia, for example, to document the history of criminal convictions against individuals, we have developed a record book administered by the Ministry of Justice called the Judiciary.
A convicted list is a type of list that is provided for in the Code of Criminal Procedure of the Kingdom of Cambodia and is held by a unit of the Ministry of Justice, which is a special data record of final criminal convictions and other measures related to convictions. Criminal, as well as a number of other measures that are similar to the civil penalties of each citizen who is a prisoner or has committed a previous criminal offense.
The above convictions may be removed from the list of convictions in some cases: * Convictions imposed in absentia when the convictions are considered void at the time of appeal * Convictions are waived by waiver Common penalties * Convictions arising from misrepresentation * Convictions that are considered nonsense by the review procedure.
The list of convicts also receives statements related to foreign-born persons and persons whose identities are not verifiable or suspicious, and in this case a special indication is made in the list of convicts whose identities are not verifiable. Or a dubious identity.
Generally, the information and documents to be recorded in the conviction list are obtained from the court clerk, the director of the prison, and the treasury unit involved in the sentencing decision, the notice of execution, the coercion, the payment of discipline, and the information on the amnesty. And commute the sentences imposed by the King and the decision to expel foreigners.
For the information of the list of convictions related to a legal entity, it must receive the affidavits confirming all kinds of convictions by the criminal court against that legal entity. The Judicial Registry may issue a criminal record, which is an excerpt of all or part of the record contained in the criminal record to any individual.
According to the Code of Criminal Procedure, there are three types of sentencing bulletins: a: The first bulletin of the list of convicts includes all the entities on the list of individual convicts, which can only be issued to the court authorities.
C: Bulletin 3 contains only the sentence of imprisonment without suspension, which declares to any person a felony or misdemeanor. However, convictions that have been rehabilitated do not appear in Bulletin 3. Bulletin 3 shall be issued to the relevant persons in any case, Bulletin 3 shall not be issued to third parties.
The Prakas of the Ministry of Justice also defines any measures necessary for the functioning of the Judiciary Unit. This Prakas specifies the conditions under which the banknotes are created, reviewed and submitted by the registrar, as well as any conditions of issue.
When an individual is convicted of a misdemeanor, the prosecutor must immediately request that the list of convictions be corrected. Rehabilitation eliminates criminal sanctions. However, this sentence is still on the list of convicts, with a conviction that he has been rehabilitated.
In summary, a list of convictions is a record of whether a natural person or legal entity has a history of crime or conviction and penalties, and on the other hand, it is a clean act for a natural person or Legal entities used in their field of work, occupation and business, etc.
Ta Mok Bridge in Anlong Veng District, Oddar Meanchey Province Temporarily Suspended Traffic
(Oddar Meanchey): O Chik Bridge or Ta Mok Bridge in O Chenchean Village, Nglong Veng Commune, Anlong Veng District, Oddar Meanchey Province was closed to traffic on the morning of September 20, 2020 due to the high water flow across the bridge.
Mr. Nhen Kuon, Director of Oddar Meanchey Provincial Department of Water Resources and Meteorology, told Fresh News that the water level at Ochik Bridge or Ta Mok Bridge in Anlong Veng District, Oddar Meanchey Province on September 20, 2020 was 3.95 meters above the precautionary level. With a height of 3.80 meters while the emergency level is 4.20 meters.
He added that due to the high water level crossing the bridge, Ta Mok bridge was temporarily closed to traffic for a short time. He said that for Oddar Meanchey province, there is no flood problem, that is, the water level is high, but only at the Ta Mok bridge, other places are normal.
At the same time, Mr. Nhek Kuon called on people to be careful and always be prepared to avoid any danger, even if the water situation is not threatening. He said that both the authorities and the authorities were ready and at all times to save the people.
The suspect is currently being held at the Sen Sok police station to follow legal procedures.
