Today, there are ten major religions with the highest number of adherents. Of the world's 7.79 billion people by 2020, the ten major religions are: 1. Christianity Christianity is the largest religion in the world. 2,000 years ago in present-day Israel. It has 2.4 billion adherents, or 29 percent of the world's population.
2. Islam Islam is the second most widely practiced religion in the world. Islam originated about 1,400 years ago in present-day Saudi Arabia and has 1.9 billion adherents, or 24 percent of the world's population.
3. Hinduism Hinduism is considered to be one of the oldest religions in the world where no one knows the history of its origins. Hinduism has 1.2 billion adherents, or 15.4 percent of the world's population.
4. Buddhism Buddhism originated about 2,500 years ago in India. It currently has 506 million adherents, or 6 percent of the world's population.
