(Kampong Chhnang): On the evening of September 18, 2020, the Kampong Chhnang Provincial Administration held a procession of gold, silver, and Nimit ships of Chhorn Chhong, Kampong Chhnang city sub-committee, to offer offerings to their ancestors on the banks of the Doeum Po Phsar River. The ancestors had to return to their abode after 15 days of Pchum Ben.
The ceremony was presided over by Mr. Long Chhun Lay, Chairman of the Provincial Council, Mr. Chhour Chandoeun, Governor of Kampong Chhnang Province and Mrs. Chhim Srey Mom, his wife. Also.
The ancestral farewell ceremony is a ceremony that people always hold on the last day of the 15-day Pchum Ben festival, the Cambodian people will never forget this ancestral farewell ceremony.
In this ceremony, the people make a box or cut a banana peel, tie the head and tail to make a boat with offerings such as prahok, salt, rice, sesame seeds, cakes and other offerings in small packages and burn incense candles Connect with the dedication, pray for the happiness that has returned, and turn around to bless the children, wish only happiness, prosperity and business for all families.
The ancestral farewell ceremony of Kampong Chhnang Provincial Administration under the leadership of Mr. Chhour Chandoeun is always held every year without interruption to dedicate the merits to the ancestors who have passed away to receive these achievements. Looking back to bless the leaders, civil servants at all levels and the people to be happy and prosperous for everyone.
