Ms. O Vandin reports on the current situation of influenza throughout the country from 15 August to 18 September
In response to the flu, the working groups of the eight provincial health departments have been active and quick to respond to prevent the spread of the disease and provide 100% cure for the monks and patients. And for 7 provinces. In Kampong Thom province, 15% healed, which will be possible in the near future.
In order to avoid the spread of influenza, Mr. Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health, called on the people, grandfathers, abbots, tachi, grandmother, pagoda committee and all monks across the country to take the following preventive measures:
* Must have good hygiene and living space, especially hand hygiene, by washing frequently according to the guidelines of the Ministry of Health.
Use a mask if necessary, especially when wearing a mask when entering a pagoda to listen to the Dharma or in a crowded place, and when coughing or sneezing, cover the mouth and nose with a scarf or paper towel.
Avoid direct contact with mammals and birds. If touched, wash hands thoroughly with soap and water immediately before touching objects or touching their face.
* Drink warm boiled water and eat well-cooked food, keep food hygienic and store food separately as recommended by the Ministry of Health often.
Avoid places that are very cold, such as air conditioners or walking in the rain.
* If you have a health problem, do not attend any of the ceremonies, stay in a dormitory or stay in a separate place to avoid transmission and seek medical attention at a public hospital near you. .
Spokesman for the General Commission: On September 19, 149 more vehicles were inspected and fined
According to the spokesperson of the General Commissioner, within 142 days of tightening the road traffic law by increasing the fine according to Sub-Decree No. 39, from May 1 to September 19, 2020, the traffic police nationwide inspected And fined a total of 172,029 vehicles, including 127,492 motorcycles and 44,537 vehicles of all types.
