Angry wife asks to go to work at a drinking factory, hanged herself in Krakor district, Pursat province
(Pursat): A man drank alcohol and hanged himself because he was angry with his wife and asked to work in a factory to earn money to support his family. This incident caused a surprise on September 18, 2020 in Po Angkor village, Boeung Kantuot commune, Krakor district, Pursat province.
According to the Krakor District Police report, the victims who hanged themselves were Thuong Theam, a 34-year-old Cambodian man, and Roat Laom, a 34-year-old Cambodian woman with three children. Dependents live in Po Angkor village, Boeung Kantuot commune, Krakor district, Pursat province.
According to the report, before the incident, the victim's wife asked her husband to work in a factory to support the family. Unfortunately, the victim, the husband, thought short of drinking and decided to commit suicide, leaving his three young children to live as orphans.
After the inspection and forensic examination, the police concluded that the victim actually committed suicide and handed over the body to the family to take to the traditional ceremony.
