Cambodia's representative to the UN tells the Human Rights Council that Cambodia is taking effective measures to respond to Kovid 19
(Geneva, Switzerland): Cambodia's Ambassador and Permanent Representative to the United Nations (UN) An Sok Khoeun told the UN Human Rights Council that the Royal Government of Cambodia, led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, has Many effective measures and measures to respond to the 19 epidemics of Kovid in Cambodia as well as the world.
An Sok Khoeun made the remarks at the 45th session of the Human Rights Council in Geneva, Switzerland, on September 19, 2020.
Mr. An Sok Khoeun said at the meeting that Cambodia had effectively controlled 19 Kovids, with a total of 275 cases as of September 15, all of which were import cases. Of the positive cases, there were no deaths and no signs of community infection. In particular, Cambodia has never reached the stage where it is required to close the country.
The Cambodian representative at the United Nations added that in addition to measures to support affected businesses, the Royal Government of Cambodia has launched several rounds of social protection interventions to support the livelihoods of vulnerable groups. The Royal Government's "Cash for Work" program continues to contribute to rural development and support farmers by improving community infrastructure and creating more employment opportunities.
The Royal Government has also launched a cash subsidy program for poor and vulnerable families, including the disabled, pregnant women and children, who have already provided benefits to more than half a million families. More than 60,000 more families will be added to the second phase of the interim program.
Nearly 250,000 employees in the tourism and garment sectors, most of whom are women, whose jobs have been suspended due to HIV 19 also received a monthly stipend from the government during this difficult time. Well.
Mr. Sokhoeun stressed that Cambodia's response to the 19-year-old virus included human rights values and the principle of non-discrimination in order not to abandon any individual.
Mr. An Sok Khoeun claimed that the relevant ministries and authorities of Cambodia are advised to cooperate with the World Health Organization and the World Food Organization, as well as UN agencies and humanitarian agencies to facilitate the above operations. COVID-19 Daily Report: "The number of infected people in the world has exceeded 30 million, more than 950,000 have died, more than 22 million have been cured, 193 countries and territories have more than 100 cases"
