Cambodian police crack down on money laundering case, arrest 4 Nigerians and 1 Cambodian, court issues detention order
(Phnom Penh): A large case of fraud and money laundering in Phnom Penh was investigated by the police and arrested 4 foreigners and a Cambodian woman.
The operation was carried out under the direct command of General Dr. Neth Savoeun, National Police Commissioner, and Lt. Gen. Di Vichea, Deputy Commissioner and Director of the Central Department of Security Police, and Lt. Gen. Sean Sen, Director of the Anti-Commercial Gambling Department.
A report by the Anti-Gambling Crime Department, obtained by Fresh News on September 16, 2020, states that on July 15, 2020, specialized forces received information about fraudulent transactions (Fraud). ) And receive money transfers into an irregular account, with the transaction of withdrawing from a bank account originating from the United States into some bank accounts in Cambodia.
After receiving the above information, the relevant authorities continued to search for information until they broke into the nest of a large group of scammers and money launderers in Phnom Penh on September 11-13, 2020 and arrested a total of suspects. Five people, including four Nigerians and a Cambodian woman, have filed a case to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court for further proceedings.
According to the source, the suspects used pseudo-tricks to persuade people to open bank accounts to receive remittances from abroad and pay them a commission.
Therefore, if people are contacted to open a bank account or help pay from any kind of money transfer service in Cambodia to avoid cheating this group, please be careful not to believe all kinds of temptations or consolation. And report to the nearest authority for timely action.
The five defendants were remanded in custody on the evening of September 17, 2020.
