Aunt Seny, 63, wife of Pich Born (former commune councilor - deceased), living in Prakeab village, Rong Chrey commune, Thmor Kol district, Battambang province, came to meet Mr. Duong Dara at the 53rd Brigade, where the solidarity meal was held. He holds a letter requesting the intervention of Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia, to seek justice.
As a result of the long-running dispute, Aunt Seni lost all her possessions, her husband died and became so poor that she lost her shelter and her children and family no longer trusted her because she had repeatedly lost her case and was facing lawsuits. Other lawsuits.
Due to the stalemate and the hunger for justice, Ming Seny sought justice in all directions and also applied for the intervention of the Dhamma Party, but still did not receive a solution. Hun Sen did as he wished.
Due to his ability to mediate reconciliation, Mr. Duong Dara spent almost three hours, ending more than 20 years of conflict between the two parties, and the two sides agreed to sign a settlement agreement and end the dispute on the 17th of this month. September 2020, which is Pchum Ben Day.
At the same time, Mr. Duong Dara confirmed to all parties to the dispute that: Samdech Techo Hun Sen's win-win principle not only ends the civil war between Cambodia and Cambodia by bringing peace and development to Cambodia. However, the win-win principle of Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen is the wisdom to resolve disputes outside the judiciary in order to find real justice for all parties to the dispute effectively.
Finally, the parties to the settlement of both disputes and Mr. Duong Dara expressed their deepest gratitude to Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen and wished him good health. Abundance and longevity to be the shadow to lead the country to greater prosperity.
