(Phnom Penh): The ASEAN Labor Ministers and the 10 ASEAN Education Ministers, as well as relevant development partners, met through a video system to discuss in detail the issues related to the situation of human resource development and work. Make ASEAN human resources ready to meet current and future labor market needs, especially 21st century skills development and the Industrial Revolution 4.0.
(VOVworld) - The ASEAN Ministerial Summit on Human Resource Development for Changing the World of Work on the 21st Century Skills Education and Training System, organized by Vietnam during the ASEAN rotating chairmanship, will be held in the afternoon. September 16, 2020.
The four main topics that the conference discussed and exchanged experiences were:
1. Partnerships in human resource development 2. Post-epidemic human resource development 3. Private sector leadership in human resource development and 4. Readiness of the education system and Training for 21st Century Skills
At the same time, Mr. Ith Sam Heng also shared recommendations to ASEAN, such as:
2. Promote and accelerate cooperation in the field of labor in arranging mutual recognition of skills between ASEAN Member States.
3. Encourage public-private partnerships to improve the quality of skills for young skilled workers through ASEAN skills competition.
4. Accelerate the study of regional skills needs and establish a common labor market information system for ASEAN.
5. Prepare a book on the work history and skills of migrant workers in ASEAN member states.
6: Continue to cooperate to exchange training programs and study visits of technical teachers and students
7. Share experiences and skills to the people of ASEAN Member States by providing opportunities for skills training to migrant workers working in host countries.
