(Phnom Penh): Mrs. O Vandin, Secretary of State and spokesperson of the Ministry of Health, confirmed to Fresh News about the recent flu situation in monks. She said 120 monks in four provinces had contracted the flu, but so far almost all had been completely cured and only a small number were still receiving treatment.
"According to a total of four provinces (Takeo, Tbong Khmum, Battambang and Banteay Meanchey), there are more than 120 infected monks in the past and recently," said O Vandin. "Almost all of the affected monks have been cured and only a small number are still receiving treatment, but their condition has improved."
