ASEAN Supports Cambodia to Lead ASEAN Tourism Restoration Plan During and After Kovid Crisis
(Phnom Penh): At the 52nd Meeting of the Directors-General of the ASEAN National Tourism Institution on September 15, 2020, via video conferencing, the Ministry of Tourism of Cambodia was supported by ASEAN member countries to lead the planning of tourism rehabilitation. ASEAN during and after the Kovid-19 crisis as a compass to strengthen tourism development in the worst-affected areas.
Mr. Thong Rathasak, Director General of Tourism Product Development and International Cooperation, who chaired the meeting, told Fresh News that in accordance with the spirit of the ASEAN Tourism Ministers' Special Meeting under the chairmanship of the Cambodian Minister of Tourism on April 29, 2020. So far, ASEAN has set out seven strategies to help prevent the spread of Kovid-19, address the impact of the crisis and plan after the crisis.
Mr. Thong Rathsak said that in the future direction, ASEAN member countries have agreed to establish a common ASEAN safety and health measures and this rehabilitation plan to be led by Cambodia.
Senior ASEAN tourism officials also discussed promoting travel between member countries in accordance with health and hygiene rules approved by professional bodies and in line with international norms.
Currently, some ASEAN member countries are planning to travel with countries outside the region through public health mechanisms and Travel Bubble travel, that is, between the goal of recognizing one safe destination to another.
