(Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia, and Ms. Manika Jain, the outgoing Indian Ambassador to Cambodia, have both expressed the same desire to see direct flights between Cambodia and India to help. Let the tourism sector between the two countries grow even more. This is according to Mr. Koy Kuong, spokesman for the Ministry of Foreign Affairs.
The will of both sides was expressed on September 15, 2020 at the Ministry of Foreign Affairs on the occasion that the Head of the Cambodian Embassy allowed the outgoing Indian Ambassador to Cambodia to pay a courtesy call and say goodbye after her. Successfully complete your diplomatic mission in Cambodia.
For the pre-Kovid 19 tourism eruption, the number of Indians visiting Cambodia increased from more than 60,000 in 2018 to 750,000 in 2019. Cambodia and India are both optimistic that if there are direct flights between those countries, the tourism sector will grow even better and also make it easier for businesses of both countries to do business.
At a press conference on the meeting between Cambodian and Indian diplomats in Cambodia at the end of his term, Koy Kuong confirmed to reporters: "This is an initiative that Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon and the Ambassador consider to help boost the sector. "Tourism as well as business between more than two countries."
