(Phnom Penh): Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, said that Cambodia must strive to find solutions to attract new types of investment that provide better jobs and income for the people.
The Minister made this statement at the second meeting of the Working Group of the Tripartite Mechanism Plus to discuss the amendment of the Labor Law on September 15, 2020 at the Ministry of Labor.
This meeting was held in order to continue the discussion on the amendment of the Labor Law to achieve the draft law on the amendment of the Labor Law that is comprehensive and has the support of all stakeholders before proceeding. The way in force to pass this law before the end of 2020.
Based on the results of this workshop, the Working Group on Tripartite Mechanism Plus to Discuss and Amend the Labor Law was established and held its first meeting on July 21, 2020 to review and consult on Preliminary draft of the Law on the Amendment of the Labor Law with the active participation of all members.
Based on these results, the Secretariat of the Legislative and Legal Commission on Labor and Vocational Training prepared the first draft law, which is the subject of today's meeting, and sent it to the International Labor Organization for comment.
In order to push today's meeting to achieve the expected results, the Minister reiterated to the meeting:
2. The abolition of the next day's leave for the Sunday holiday is not contrary to international labor conventions. The amendment aims to boost labor productivity and enhance Cambodia's competitiveness in facilitating investment and national development. Cambodia still has less working hours than any other country in the region.
3. Expanding the scope of the Arbitration Council in resolving individual labor disputes is a contribution to strengthening the effectiveness of labor dispute resolution films in Cambodia by making it a choice for the parties to the dispute to choose a mechanism for resolving labor disputes that respond to their actual situation. This amendment is in line with the universal principle of ensuring that the parties to the dispute receive justice as soon as possible.
After today's meeting, the Ministry of Labor will continue the procedure in force by sending the draft law to the inter-ministerial meeting in order to get the approval of this law as soon as possible to meet the needs of stakeholders. Senior Minister Kun Kim and Family Visit Ben 6 Pagodas in Takhmao City
