The former CNRP was dissolved by the Supreme Court on November 16, 2020, following the arrest of party president Kem Sokha in connection with a conspiracy with foreigners to overthrow Cambodia's legitimate government. With the party convicted, the Supreme Court banned a total of 118 former party leaders from engaging in politics for five years.
However, under the Law Amending the Law on Political Parties, all individuals banned from politics by the courts will be able to re-engage in politics by submitting a letter to the Ministry of Interior requesting the Royal Government to resign. The King issues a Royal Decree granting legal status.
The domestic retail sector grew 0.5 percent in August from a year earlier, while industrial output rose 5.6 percent, the National Bureau of Statistics (NBS) said on Tuesday. In the same month. In the first eight months of 2020, the retail sector contracted by 8.6 percent from the same period in 2019, while industrial output increased by 0.4 percent, the first increase in the year. This.
The Chinese government recently unveiled a new strategic plan aimed at boosting domestic consumption and advancing more key technologies in the country in the face of growing geopolitical tensions and the possibility of an outbreak. The return of the coronavirus remains a concern.
In fact, the gradual easing of restrictions on services such as cinemas has also contributed to boosting Chinese spending. US Investment and Financial Services Bank Morgan Stanley estimates that movie ticket sales in China will return to normal in the fourth quarter of 2020.
In August, the unemployment rate in China fell to 5.6 percent, while the real estate market continued to grow despite the government's tightening of property policy.
Meanwhile, real estate investment rose 3 percent in the first eight months of the year, while state-owned investment fell 3.2 percent during the same period as private company spending fell. Down 2.8 percent, the best result this year.
