(Phnom Penh): Mr. Say Sam Al, Minister of the Environment, sent a message congratulating the World Ozone Day on September 16, 2020 and the 35th anniversary of the establishment of the "Vienna Convention on the Protection of the Ozone Layer" in 1985. 33. Establishment of the "Montreal Protocol on Ozone Depletion" in 1987.
September 16 has been designated by the United Nations Environment Program Ozone Secretariat as the "World Ozone Day" every year since 1995 to commemorate the founding of the Samaritan Festival, as well as to celebrate the achievements and Many joint ventures have been made to protect the ozone layer.
So far, through the joint efforts of many nations around the world, we have almost completely eliminated ozone depleting substances, and we hope that the ozone layer will regenerate in the 2050s.
Since ozone depleting substances have the potential to cause high global warming, mankind's efforts to implement the Montreal Protocol have made significant contributions to reducing global warming. In fact, between 1990 and 2010, the world jointly reduced CO2 emissions to about 135 billion tons.
At the same time, since 2000, the ozone layer has been closed between 1-3% per year, with a complete closure occurring in 2030 at the North Pole and 2050 at the South Pole. With the restoration of the ozone layer, we also hope to prevent overheating through the implementation of the Kigali amendment of the Montreal Protocol.
In this regard, Cambodia is committed to continuing to engage with the international community in the successful implementation of all its obligations to ensure the effectiveness of the reduction and elimination of the use of ozone depleting substances and potentially heating substances. High.
One person was killed and 15 others were injured when a driver of a passenger bus crashed into a tuk-tuk in Siem Reap province.
(Siem Reap): There was a traffic accident caused by a Samsung car driving to hit a tuk-tuk parked in the opposite direction, causing a landslide on September 15, 2020. The incident happened on National Road 6 in Kiettis village, Prey Chrouk commune, Puok district, Siem Reap province.
Siem Reap Provincial Police Commissioner Major General Tit Narong said that the incident was caused by a Samsung car with license plate number 2M-4406 driving from east to west, swerved and hit a recycling tuk-tuk that was parked at the same time. The same direction caused the car to overturn on the south side of the national road and the tuk tuk to fall on the north side.
The accident left one person dead and 15 seriously injured while the driver of the car was asleep when the car was traveling from Sihanoukville.
This is according to the appeal of the National Committee for Road Safety on the prevention of road accidents on the occasion of Kan Ben, Pchum Ben, Khmer tradition, from 16 to 18 September 2020, received by Fresh News Available on September 15, 2020.
At the same time, on the occasion of Kan Ben, Pchum Ben, which has been taking place from September 3 to 18, 2020, people may have traffic activities to their hometown pagodas and excursions. The country is busy and there may be an increase in traffic accidents.
In order to prevent this challenge, Samdech Krala Hos Kheng would like to urge all people to pay attention to traffic safety by consistently implementing the following important measures:
1: For passenger cars or trucks, please do not load people or goods beyond the limit, especially passenger cars must not load people on the roof and do not increase the fare.
2: Check the technical characteristics of your vehicle before traffic.
3: Car drivers and passengers, please wear seat belts properly and regularly.
4: All motorcyclists and passengers must wear helmets properly, whether traveling near or far and at all times. Always remember that "a helmet saves one life."
5. Drivers must reduce their driving speed according to the law and the actual situation, such as town, school, curves, intersections, slopes, narrow roads or slippery roads, etc. The main cause of road accidents is Driving over the speed limit.
6: Before overtaking, the driver must know that the road ahead is free to overtake safely, avoid overtaking with risk, which can cause accidents eventually.
7. Drivers must respect the right of way at the intersection by slowing down when approaching the intersection and must give the right to drivers who drive on the main road and straight ahead.
8: Do not drive under the influence of alcohol or drugs and always remember the slogan "If you drink alcohol, do not drive." Drunkenness can cause the driver to lose consciousness, lose consciousness, be unable to control the vehicle safely, and be prone to road accidents.
9. When driving, adhere to good manners, ethics and mutual understanding to prevent accidents or ease traffic congestion.
Samdech Krala Hos Kheng would like to express his hope and trust in the public vigilance in implementing this call to bring safety and happiness with the family on the occasion of the upcoming Pchum Ben celebration.
