Switzerland commends government measures to curb Kovid-19 outbreak
This statement was made by Mr. Markus Buerli on the occasion of his courtesy call with the Minister of Health, Prof. Mam Bun Heng, to find out more about the health situation of the people in Cambodia at the Ministry of Health this afternoon, September 14, 2020. .
At the same time, he also praised the local health officials for providing good patient care services. He said that while visiting some provinces, such as Kampong Thom, Siem Reap, he saw that the progress of the health sector in Cambodia has improved significantly.
In response, the Minister of Health thanked Switzerland for its support to the health sector, especially the continued support of Kantha Bopha Hospital in Cambodia and the continued training of human resources by health officials to strengthen the provision of medical services to Cambodian children. More improvements.
In addition, the Minister of Health is also strongly committed to working with Switzerland to make Kantha Bopha Hospital in Cambodia more successful.
Please be informed that in the past, Switzerland has helped a lot in helping the health sector, especially in donating about $ 40 million per year to Kantha Bopha Hospital in Cambodia, including other areas.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol Visits and Thanks Phnom Penh Gendarmerie for Security Work
(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, on Monday, September 14, 2020, brought a large number of donations to visit officers and deputies of the Phnom Penh Military Police.
The event was attended by Lt. Gen. Rath Sreang, Deputy Commander of the National Gendarmerie and Commander of the Phnom Penh Municipal Gendarmerie, as well as officers and deputies of the Phnom Penh Municipal Gendarmerie.
In this ceremony, the Senior Minister highlighted the important role of the Gendarmerie in maintaining security and order in the country, especially in Phnom Penh, to provide opportunities for the Royal Government to develop the country according to its plan to achieve a middle-income country. High levels in 2030 and high income countries in 2050.
The Senior Minister also briefed the participants on the transportation infrastructure development policy, with the first step being to integrate internally (connecting the capital to the provincial capital and from one province to another) with two layers of thin rubber (DBST). And in the second step, the Royal Government will strengthen, expand and build new ones in response to economic growth and vehicle growth from year to year.
(Phnom Penh): Russey Keo District Governor Mr. Chea Pisey announced that the Phnom Penh Capital Administration under the leadership of Mr. Khuong Sreng will prepare a drainage system with a diameter of 1 meter and a length of 200 meters to relieve flooding due to flooding. This rainy season, to make it easier for people to travel, as well as to help reduce accidents on National Road 5 (twin roads), Sangkat Kilometer 6.
The official Facebook announcement of the Governor of Russey Keo District and a member of the Secretariat of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, was made when he and Mr. Sam Piseth, Director of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Phnom Penh, led officials to inspect the actual situation of the canal. To release the rain that fell on National Road No. 5 (Twin Road), Sangkat Kilometer 6 on September 14, 2020.
