Minister of Commerce: Continuing treatment of 19 Kovid patients and no deaths is a great success of the Royal Government
(Kampong Cham): Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce and Chairman of the National Task Force for Prey Chhor and Batheay Districts, Kampong Cham Province, considered the treatment of 19 Kovid patients, no deaths because 19 Kovid Infectious diseases are a great achievement for the Royal Government of Cambodia, led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, in the context of the world being plagued by Kovid 19.
The Minister of Commerce said this during the meeting and handed over laptops, antiseptic soap, medical masks and some funds to the administration of Batheay and Prey Chhor districts, referral hospitals and health centers, schools at all levels in Prey Chhor district and Batheay district on September 14, 2020.
In this conversation, the Minister highlighted the hardships of the world, including Cambodia today, due to Kovid 19. However, the Minister highlighted the timely and effective action of the Royal Government led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen to reduce the spread of Kovid 19 disease and not to infect communities like some countries in the world. Mr.
As of September 14, 2020, Cambodia has identified 275 cases of Kovid 19 infection. Of those, 274 have been treated and only one is being treated. What is very encouraging is that the Cambodian medical team has treated the patient 100% twice.
The minister said that in the context of Kovid 19, almost every country is facing an economic crisis, but the most important thing to consider is to save the lives of the people and prevent the disease from spreading to the community. Mr. Pan Sosak told the authorities and officials in Prey Chhor and Batheay districts that this was a great achievement for the Royal Government of Cambodia in the context of the Kovid 19 society.
The Minister of Commerce also highlighted some of the Royal Government of Cambodia's efforts to address the difficulties of Cambodian society and people. In order to solve the challenges of society, the Royal Government of Cambodia has already introduced five measures to help maintain the balance of production and business for both domestic and foreign supply, especially to ensure the stability of the lives of people who are severely affected. .
Due to the current outbreak of Kovid 19, there is no vaccine to prevent the disease and there is no vaccine yet, Mr. Pan Sosak appealed to the authorities at all levels, commune councils, government officials, teachers and doctors at health centers. All to continue to pay attention to the fight against Kovid 19 by striving to promote all preventive measures and participate in the implementation of the guidelines of the Ministry of Health.
