Health Minister tells WHO member countries in Asia and the Pacific that Cambodia manages Kovid 19 well
On that occasion, Mr. Mam Bunheng told the member countries of the World Health Organization in the Asia-Pacific region that the Royal Government of Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen has managed the disease 19 well. This is according to a press release from the Ministry of Health, obtained by Fresh News.
He said that this strategy is an opportunity for Cambodia to strengthen and expand public health services to ensure the provision of fair and equitable services for all Cambodians, that is, no one is left without access to care.
Please note that this meeting of the Minister of Health has three purposes, including:
* 1: Examine the impact of Code-19 on global health coverage goals * 2: Identify and share current health system practices to address the Corridor-19 issue and tap the potential of this crisis to reach Global Health Coverage * 3: Discuss how to invest from the crisis of Code 19 as a basis for achieving global health coverage goals.
