(Svay Rieng): Mr. KER Ratha, Director of Svay Rieng Provincial Health Department and Chairman of Svay Rieng Sangkat Assistance Team, Representative of Dr. Men Sam An, Chairman of the Working Group of the Cambodian People's Party, visited Svay Rieng Province on September 14, 2020. Led a team to visit and bring gifts to a helpless nun who is chronically anemic and paralyzed on both sides is being treated at Svay Rieng Provincial Hospital.
Mr. KER Ratha stated that with the care of Ms. Men Sam An, the people of Svay Rieng province who are in need and helpless, she sent him to visit Mrs. Thong Ny. Address: Bassac village, Bassac commune, Svay Chrum district, Svay Rieng province, who is being treated at this provincial hospital.
He added that on behalf of the working group of the Cambodian People's Party, always pay attention to the general population, especially people who are sick in the referral hospitals in the province, as at this time, the working group visited the sick grandmother. Who is being treated in this provincial hospital, please take care of your health by following the doctor's prescription to get well soon.
Mrs. Thong Ny also thanked Ms. Men Sam An and all the doctors of the provincial hospital for their care, as well as all the people in need of living in Svay Rieng province. .
It should be noted that Mrs. Thong Ny, who is chronically anemic and paralyzed in both legs, was sent to the provincial hospital for treatment and received 8 transfusions, 2 of which were donated by a philanthropist and 6 from a public hospital.
