(Tbong Khmum): A jeep collided with a fully loaded ice truck, causing three people to be seriously injured while the car was almost completely destroyed. This incident happened at more than 12 noon on September 14, 2020, near the primary school in the village of Chiro II, Tbong Khmum district, Tbong Khmum province.
After the incident, the professional police force took the two vehicles and facilitated the traffic and stored them at the Tbong Khmum District Police Inspectorate to wait for the procedure and sent the victims to the hospital. Spokesman for the General Commission: On September 14, another 506 vehicles were inspected and fined
According to the spokesperson of the General Commissioner, within 137 days of tightening the road traffic law by increasing the fine according to Sub-Decree No. 49, from May 1 to September 14, 2020, the traffic police throughout the country inspected And fined a total of 170,127 vehicles, including 126,083 motorcycles and 44,044 vehicles of all types.
Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun said that for the past 137 days, the implementation of the new sub-decree to fine vehicles for offenses has been going well. He thanked and commended all the road users for their good obedience to the traffic law so far, especially the traffic police for their dedication and hard work. Tighten traffic with the highest sense of responsibility.
Please note that for September 14, 2020, traffic accidents across Cambodia also occurred 14 times, in which 8 people died, 20 people were injured (16 seriously injured).
All Christian representatives also expressed their commitment and efforts to implement the prevention and control of Kovid-19 in accordance with the rules of the Ministry of Health to the best of their ability in accordance with the policy of the Royal Government under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen. .
In addition, Cambodian Christians have issued a directive on preventing the spread of Kovid-19 during the reopening of church services from September 12, 2020.
In the spirit of high responsibility, in order to increase the highest level of vigilance, priests, pastors, Christian leaders, and all denominations of the Church should take part in the following preventive and preventive measures:
* First: Follow the instructions of the Ministry of Health
* Third: Prohibit people with various diseases and children from worshiping in church.
* Fourth: It is forbidden to shake hands during salutation, instead of raising your hands in salute and saying Christian greetings and keeping communication safe.
* 5th: Worship meeting at the church and worship place should not exceed 30 minutes
* Sixth: Always adhere to clean hygiene before worship.
* Seventh: Maintain a social gap by allowing worship at about 30% of the members of each location by increasing the number of worship hours as much as possible, and from one worship interval to the next, clean the table. Seats, chairs, other equipment, first allowed to enter next time
* 8th: For the program for children in the church, the head office must increase the vigilance and increase the number of pediatric teachers in each class and each program is responsible according to the number of children
9th: Do not have a gathering to eat together at the church after worship.
