(Phnom Penh): While private schools across the country are preparing to re-apply for school reopening under the guidance of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, Mr. Pech Bolen, President of the Federation of Education Services in Cambodia, issued a message and suggestions. Blessings 10 important points.
Please read the full content of Mr. Pech Bolen below:
Private schools across the country have been preparing to reopen applications under the guidance of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports. In the meantime, as the President of the Education Services Federation of Cambodia, which has more than 100 institutions so far, I have the following suggestions and suggestions:
1: I would like to express my deepest gratitude and appreciation to Samdech Techo Prime Minister for leading the campaign against the spread of Kovid 19 with the highest wisdom and effectiveness in other countries in the world.
2: I would like to thank the Ministry of Economy and Finance for its efforts in considering and launching various economic policies to help prevent, revive and promote business development.
4: We would like to thank Dr. Heng Vanda and the leaders of the Association of Higher Education Institutions of Cambodia for allowing us to recognize and provide cooperation opportunities in partnership in education and training, and especially the opportunity for dialogue with relevant ministries and institutions. .
5: I wish all educational and training institutions, parents, guardians and students to continue to participate in the implementation of measures to prevent the spread and spread of Kovid 19 to maintain the excellence of safety, well-being, economic stability and peace that the Royal Government has built and developed. So far.
6: Parents, guardians, students, staff, teachers and all educational institutions cooperate to understand and sympathize with each other when we reopen the school as instructed by the Ministry of Guardians now.
7: We would like to thank and request the building owners, financial institutions and related partners to continue to understand and provide favors to private educational and training institutions for a while so that all educational and training institutions can afford to organize schools. Re-learn and rebuild stability.
8 - Please all students continue to work hard to learn and continue to participate in safety and hygiene measures to continue to prevent the spread and spread of Kovid 19 disease.
9: Thank you and be grateful to all the staff and teachers who have understood and supported to join all educational and training institutions to overcome this difficult time together.
10: Please continue to contribute to the development of education and training of human resources in Cambodia together, especially to maintain security, well-being, sustainability and economic growth and peace of our beloved Cambodia.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Ou Phannarith, Director of the Department of Security, Information and Communication Technology of the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications, said that the crime of fraud or fraudulent transfer of money through the banking system is still a concern if we do not understand how to use it.
In a weekly interview with Fresh News, Ou Phannarith stated that consumers should not allow anyone to borrow money from a bank account to transfer money, as it could be money with an ambiguous history. Makes us afraid to be victims.
"If we do not know the history of the money transferred to our bank account, we should not allow the bank loan to make money," he said.
In addition, Mr. Ou Phannarith said that we do not respond to requests by e-mail or request to fill out information by phone or ask for information about the phone sent to us. Generally, the bank never does that, if you receive such an email, do not follow it, and if you want to be clear, you should call the bank that you use.
At the same time, the official of the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications would also like to ask people as bank users to understand this technology clearly, what are the security functions? To avoid fraud or transfer of money through the banking system.
