(Phnom Penh): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, said on September 14, 2020 that farmers' rice cultivation in 2020 will increase to 99.09% and the harvest will increase. Up to more than 85%.
Minister Veng Sakhon emphasized that the Royal Government also has a vision to turn Cambodia into a high middle income country by 2030 and a high income country by 2050.
Minister Veng Sakhon added that "in particular, the use of equipment for sowing and planting rice is also on the rise, including planting equipment for irrigating vegetables, fertilizing and harvesting potatoes."
At the same time, Minister Veng Sakhon also said that the Royal Government has ambitions to modernize Cambodia's agricultural sector to be more competitive, environmentally resilient and sustainable.
The Minister of Agriculture stated that this modernization is to turn the Cambodian agricultural sector from a stage of development to a new stage focusing on intensive production.
"That is, relying mainly on the use of new technologies, research and development of mechanization, as well as increasing irrigation capacity to increase productivity, diversify potential crops and markets." This was further confirmed by Minister Veng Sakhon.
Mr. Veng Sakhon added that to achieve this ambition, the Department of Agricultural Engineering of the General Department of Agriculture of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries has been focusing on research and cooperation with the private sector and development partners.
The Department of Agricultural Engineering has gradually introduced a number of agricultural equipment and machinery to the middle-class farming community and farmers in accordance with the geography and land size of resource farmers.
In addition, to respond to the current and future decline in the agricultural workforce. Riverside Park in Kampong Cham City Crash, Authorities Will Rebuild on September 21
(Kampong Cham): The Governor of Kampong Cham Province, Mr. Un Chanda, confirmed that the construction site of the riverside park will start rebuilding on September 21, 2020.
The provincial governor said so on the morning of September 14, 2020, while inspecting the landslide park by the river in Veal Vong commune, Kampong Cham city.
Please be reminded that the riverside park in Kampong Cham City collapsed at around 12 midnight on September 13, 2020, and this landslide did not endanger the lives of the people.
According to Kampong Cham City Hall officials, immediately after the incident, Kampong Cham Provincial Governor Un Chanda ordered officials from the relevant departments in the province to conduct an urgent study to find out the cause of the park's disappearance.
As a result, according to the conclusion of the official that the collapse may be caused by the drainage system from Kampong Cham into the river is a dilapidated sewer system built from the old society and before the incident. Heavy rain in Kampong Cham city as well.
However, after inspecting and receiving information from the research of relevant professional officials, the Governor of Kampong Cham Province decided to re-establish on September 21, 2020 at the riverside park. That collapse. Kampong Thom Constituency Deputies Call on Monks and Pagoda Committees to Transform Pagodas into Religious Tourism Destinations
