(Stung Treng): Nearly 500 families in Sekong and Thmor Keo communes, Siem Pang district, Stung Treng province want to use direct electricity from Electricite du Cambodge (EDC) after the current supplier caused them difficulties and many irregularities that can lead Give them a loss of funds to use.
The request of 443 families was made this morning, September 14, 2020, on the occasion of the authority and professional officials from relevant ministries and institutions to investigate the irregularities in the provision of electricity supply services of Ms. Huy Cheng. In Siem Pang district, Stung Treng province.
As a result of the research, Ms. Huy Cheng's abnormalities were found as follows:
* Cut the reading of the counter number for the June bill for more than 12 days, causing the price of electricity to increase, which is a source of conflict.
* During the problem, the counter was replaced and the cable in the counter box was not notified to the user, making people unhappy and skeptical.
* Service providers do not pay attention to entering the counter ID (ID) correctly and record the reading number of some users incorrectly to issue invoices
* There are delays in providing services such as replacing broken counters, bounce discs (especially some metal boxes are closed and locked) and some clock boxes are not set up properly.
* During the problem, the service provider disconnected electricity in some backyards without notifying the relevant authorities and consumers.
* The service staff lacks clear professional staff and has an inappropriate number in the service and uses inappropriate words.
* Service providers are rarely present in hidden districts to solve user issues in a timely manner
* The service provider charges incorrect connection fee and deposit as determined by the Electricity Authority of Cambodia.
Through this meeting with the people, the authorities and relevant officials promised to solve for the people, while a total of 443 families asked to end Ms. Huy Cheng's license and want to use electricity directly from Electricite du Cambodge.
Kampot Provincial Governor Meets All Kinds of Armed Forces on the Occasion of Pchum Ben
(Kampot): Mr. Chiao Tai, Provincial Governor, on September 14, 2020, led relevant officials to meet with 1202 members of the Armed Forces of all kinds on the occasion of Pchum Ben at Kampot Provincial Hall.
During the meeting, Mr. Chiao Tai paid a courtesy call on Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Samdech Kittipritthbandit, both of whom always consider the well-being of the Armed Forces of all kinds, government officials at all levels and relatives. People in Kampot province as a whole.
At the same time, the provincial governor commended the Armed Forces of all kinds for their active participation in implementing the policy of safe villages and communes in accordance with their respective roles and responsibilities with a high sense of responsibility to prevent and Prevent any problems in Kampot province.
The provincial governor also confirmed that our forces of all kinds have always cooperated to help each other to solve and avoid all traffic jams for all kinds of travelers without fear of fatigue, even in hot weather. Or it rains anyway.
During the ceremony, the provincial governor also provided a total of 1,202 troops from the three types of forces, each of whom received 50,000 Riels, equivalent to 60,100,000 Riels. The budget provided is from the 50% contribution of the provincial administration with the commanders of the three forces.
The Ambassador also recalled Deputy Prime Minister Hor Namhong's contribution to the peace talks in Cambodia. In addition, the Ambassador praised the Deputy Prime Minister for chairing the meeting of the Cambodia-China Intergovernmental Coordinating Committee with Mr. Wang Yi, State Councilor and Minister of Foreign Affairs of the People's Republic of China.
In particular, the Deputy Prime Minister noted that the diplomatic relations between Cambodia and Japan since January 9, 1953, the two sides signed a friendship treaty in 1955 and in 1959, Cambodia and Japan also signed an economic cooperation agreement. And technique. The Deputy Prime Minister also stated that as the Minister of Foreign Affairs for 21 years, he had signed a large number of agreements on Japanese aid to Cambodia.
Deputy Prime Minister Hor Namhong also stated that "To date, our two countries have enjoyed good relations of friendship and cooperation, and the Government of Japan has always provided support and assistance to Cambodia in all areas that have contributed to Cambodia's economic development. All sectors.
Deputy Prime Minister Hor Namhong added that no matter who the new Prime Minister takes office in the near future, the friendly relations and close cooperation between Cambodia and Japan will continue to grow in all fields.
On this occasion, the Deputy Prime Minister thanked the Government of Japan for always providing assistance to Cambodia, such as:
* Grants and loans for the socio-economic development of Cambodia
* Provide scholarships to many Cambodian officials and students to study in Japan
In addition, Deputy Prime Minister Hor Namhong thanked the Japanese government for receiving many internships, with more than 10,000 people currently working in Japan.
Deputy Prime Minister Hor Namhong also called for greater trade between the two countries in line with the economic potential of the two countries and more Japanese investment in Cambodia.
