The decision by the Japanese Ministry of Agriculture was made last weekend, while China and South Korea also banned such imports after Germany announced on Thursday that African swine fever had been eradicated. Found in a dead wild boar near the border between Germany and Poland.
According to the Japanese Ministry of Agriculture, the suspension of pork and hog imports from Germany is aimed at preventing African swine fever from spreading to other countries. Japan imported 40,240 tons of pork from Germany in 2019, accounting for 3.3 percent of the total 1.2 million tons of meat imports.
