Spokesman for the General Commission: On September 13, another 966 vehicles were inspected and fined
According to the spokesperson of the General Commissioner, within 136 days of tightening the road traffic law by increasing the fine according to Sub-Decree No. 49, from May 1 to September 13, 2020, the traffic police throughout the country inspected And fined a total of 169,621 vehicles, including 125,748 motorcycles and 43,873 vehicles of all types.
Notable offenses for motorcycles are mostly helmet offense, offense, no license plate and drunkenness. In particular, the offenses for cars are mostly speeding, over-capacity, no belts, offenses, no license plates, overweight, no driver's license, use the phone and so on.
Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun said that for the past 136 days, the implementation of the new sub-decree to fine vehicles for offenses has been going well. He thanked and commended all the road users for their good obedience to the traffic law so far, especially the traffic police for their dedication and hard work. Tighten traffic with the highest sense of responsibility.
Please note that for September 13, 2020, traffic accidents across Cambodia also occurred 12 times, in which 5 people died, 17 people were injured (10 people were seriously injured).
