The Minister and his delegation also distributed budgets, materials and food to officers, deputies and soldiers, as well as provided scholarships for various technical subjects at the Institute and Technical and Vocational Training Centers of the Ministry of Labor. And vocational training for officers, deputies, soldiers and their families. Legal Awareness: Appeals in Civil Cases
(Phnom Penh): In the Kingdom of Cambodia, the courts are divided into two levels and three levels, namely the Lower Court (Capital / Provincial Court) and the High Court (Court of Appeal, Supreme Court). The class makes decisions by judgment or judgment. The Capital / Provincial Court decides by judgment, while the Court of Appeal and the Supreme Court decide by judgment.
In fact, in the event that the parties are dissatisfied with the decision of the Capital / Provincial Court, the parties may appeal against the judgment issued by the other Capital / Provincial Court in case the parties remain dissatisfied with the decision of the parties. An appeal can also be lodged against the judgment issued by the Court of Appeal. This week's topic will focus on key points in the appeal procedure only.
Therefore, the legal awareness program of FRESH NEWS in collaboration with the Cambodian Lawyers for International Cooperation would like to raise the topic of "Civil Appeals" to the following students:
How to appeal To appeal, the parties must file a complaint to the original court, in which case the appeal must be filed with the Court of Appeal if the appeal is against the final judgment of the Court of Appeal or the appeal must be filed in the court of first instance. Capital / Province for cases where the parties agree in writing not to appeal.
Writing the reasons for the appeal After receiving the appeal of the appellant, the Supreme Court must send a letter of acceptance to the parties, and for the parties to the appeals party must also attach an appeal. . After receiving the letter of appeal, the appellant must file the reasons for the appeal within 30 (thirty) days.
In the case of an appeal made in accordance with the general cause of the appeal as stated above, the appellant shall state in writing the reasons for the violation of the Constitution, the law, the legal norms, or in the case of an appeal Due to the absolute cause of the appeal, the plaintiff must clearly state the facts that point to any point of the absolute cause.
In summary, an appeal is a type of appeal to the Supreme Court that is made against the decision of the Court of Appeal or the Capital / Provincial Court (in cases where the parties have agreed in writing not to appeal).
In addition, an appeal must be made to the Supreme Court based on a specific reason set by law. Alternatively, an appeal may be dismissed as illegal or dismissed for no apparent legal reason.
