(Siem Reap): A suspect who was active in seizing people's bags in Siem Reap City was arrested by the police on September 11, 2020.
Police confirmed that on July 15, 2020, on the street in front of a rented room in Wat Bo village, Sala Kamroeuk commune, Siem Reap city, while the victim, Nim Saren, a 33-year-old female, was locking the door of the house. Suddenly, a suspect on a motorcycle grabbed the victim's bag, which he was carrying on his shoulder, and the victim retrieved his wallet and mobile phone.
The suspect took a backpack with a pink iPod, a music player and some valuables and escaped.
After the incident and after receiving the complaint from the victim, the police force of Sala Kamroeuk Sangkat Administration Post in cooperation with the Criminal Police led by Lieutenant Colonel Nuon Sak Chamroeunrith, Deputy Inspector in charge of Criminal Affairs, arrived at the scene to investigate and Identified the target and the motorcycle that the suspect was riding was a black 2017 Honda Dream with license plate Siem Reap 1Y-6834, but the suspect escaped.
