Cambodian Representative to UN Rejects UNOHCHR Allegations of Arrest of Youths for Social Security
Similarly, Article 31 of the Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia also clearly states that the exercise of the above rights and freedoms must be in accordance with the law. Therefore, the Office of the High Commissioner for Human Rights has the duty to raise public awareness of the obligations described above in its commentary.
The Cambodian representative to the United Nations added that the spokesperson appeared to be unwilling to seek details and verify properly and did not opt for dialogue with the state to assess the human rights situation in Cambodia.
There are many examples of past officials being punished for wrongdoing. In addition, legitimate NGOs and human rights defenders who are performing their duties in accordance with the law have been operating freely and are encouraged to participate in national development. Only organizations and individuals that violate the law are prohibited.
If the rule of law is considered as a restriction on freedom, it is a violation of the rule of law and the principle of equality for all citizens guaranteed in the Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia. Joining any political party or organization that claims to work in the field of the environment or human rights does not guarantee the right to violate the law with impunity.
An offense under the law is an offense and can not be used as an argument for any other cause. Individuals in legal disputes have the full opportunity to attend a fair hearing to present evidence and acquit in the judiciary as part of their right to a fair trial guaranteed by the Cambodian Constitution.
In this statement, the Cambodian representative to the United Nations also emphasized that the Royal Government of Cambodia has been actively participating and cooperating openly with the Office of the High Commissioner for Human Rights for nearly three decades. Come on.
