APSARA Authority: Travel agencies receive training on temple risk management
(Siem Reap): Angkor Wat Travel Agents receive training on temple risk management as this course is organized by the Angkor Tourism Development Department in collaboration with the Department of Temple Conservation in Angkor Park and Preventive Archeology and Angkor Training Center of Angkor Wat. APSARA Authority.
Mr. Lim Srou, Deputy Director of Angkor Tourism Development Department, commented at the opening ceremony of the training course held at the Preah Pan Gallery of Angkor Wat, so that the purpose of this training is to strengthen the additional capacity of travel agents stationed directly in the temple. .
He added that the study was an additional capital for all agencies to be aware of the actual condition of the temple and to compile statistics from each point to the management, as well as to report immediately to the conservationist and repair of the temple.
According to Mr. Lim Sru, the training will be held at some of the major temples in the Angkor resort to ensure that all travel agents receive basic knowledge of each temple to contribute to the better conservation of the temple for now. And into the future.
Mr. M. Sokrithy, Director of the Department of Temple Preservation in Angkor Park and Preventive Archeology, said that the temple is considered a home for all travel agents, so it is necessary to observe everywhere to know the general condition of the temple and this timely knowledge can Professionals are competent enough to repair or preserve.
He added that all temples need maintenance, such as stone maintenance, which is to slow down the erosion of the stone. He explained that every citizen has a duty to protect and preserve the ancestral heritage, and these works are part of the conservation of the temple as well.
