Notice! National Veterans Fund will pay for September for the first 2 weeks and Pchum Ben allowance from 2pm on September 14th
(Phnom Penh): The National Veterans Fund of the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation will pay the first two weeks of September and Pchum Ben allowance to all types of veterans and their families from 2 pm on the 14th. September 2020 through Canadia Bank and ACLEDA Bank in 25 capitals and provinces nationwide.
According to the announcement of the National Veterans Fund received by Fresh News on September 12, 2020, "September Social Security for the first two weeks and Pchum Ben allowance "All types of veterans and families of veterans will be held from 2 pm on September 14, 2020 onwards."
(Preah Sihanouk): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, on September 12, 2020, met with 63 families in Ta Ork village. Thom, Samaki Commune, Prey Nob District, Preah Sihanouk Province.
The ceremony was also attended by the Secretary of State, Undersecretary of State, the delegation of the Royal Government of Cambodia in charge of the Director of Fisheries Administration, Director of the Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, officials and local authorities in large numbers.
The Director of the Provincial Department of Agriculture read out the welcome remarks and briefed the participants on the progress of the agricultural sector throughout the province, noting that there are 1,767 saltwater aquaculture sites and 199 ponds and 163 freshwater ponds. Salt and fresh water are able to supply the market in the province and bring to Phnom Penh.
Taking this opportunity, Minister Veng Sakhon gave a talk, bringing a message from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister, Samdech Kittipritthbandit to the people and wishing all the people and families to meet the Buddha. 4 things should not be forgotten.
Minister Veng Sakhon also briefed the participants on the cultivation of crops (rice, vegetables, chickens, ducks, pigs, fish and frogs) and the overall situation of the country, economic security and important measures related to preventing the spread of Kovid-19 disease. .
Separately, Minister of Agriculture and Irrigation Minister Veng Sakhon said that according to the instructions of Samdech Techo, the Ministry of Fisheries Administration as its staff has worked hard to implement the recommendations of Samdech Techo to ensure food security. In the family and increase the supply by achieving optimal results.
Meanwhile, Minister Veng Sakhon instructed the Department of Fisheries Administration and local authorities to make every effort to promote fish and frog farming, vegetable growing and animal husbandry to increase food production through increased productivity. To expand and strengthen breeding capacity in all forms.
On the other hand, it is necessary to monitor all the activities of the aquaculture farmers who will adopt the young fish today to make the rearing work good.
At the same time, professional officers of the Fisheries Administration must continue to provide additional training on breeding techniques, hatching techniques, feed mixing, maintenance and economic efficiency, and increase activities to distribute fish, frogs and raising tents to families who want to expand their business. More and those who want to start feeding. For today, 63 farmers, each family received 700 catfish, 4 bags of food and 1 plastic tent to raise fish.
In total, the results obtained from the campaign to promote family food production by raising catfish and frogs for almost 2 months in the 11 target provinces were achieved: 580 farming families, of which 207 families received a total of frogs 828,000 frogs and 373 families received a total of 261,100 catfish fry, 58 tons of food, 1,719 packs of vitamins and 580 plastic tents.
From the program, Minister Veng Sakhon also continued to release fish fry in the Prey Nob 2 fishing community in Prek Sangke village, Samaki commune.
According to the community leader, the community covers an area of more than 605 hectares, including 655 hectares of mangrove forest, with more than 1,000 family members covering three villages. Raising oysters in the wild and fishing in the sea.
In the past, the Swedish Cooperative Project has supported the implementation of projects on the restoration and conservation of coastal habitats and fisheries resources (mangrove forests, seagrass, swamps).
Looking at the mangrove forest and fishing activities of community members, Minister Veng Sakhon praised and appreciated the community's efforts to raise fish and shellfish to improve living standards as well as meet market demand in the province to cut Reduce imports.
Taking this opportunity, Mr. Veng Sakhon advised the Fisheries Administration and the Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries to continue to promote more technical work and to participate in planting more seedlings to maintain and protect the mangrove forest for the sustainability of the livelihood of community members. Samdech National Assembly President and Samdech Thom Visoth Vongsa Sao Ty Heng Samrin Celebrate the 10th Kanben Ceremony at Wat Trapeang Pring
