The construction of the ancient temple at Wat Reachbo changed its beautiful new beauty after renovation
(Siem Reap): The project to repair and preserve the ancient temple of Wat Reachbo in Siem Reap, which received full funding from the APSARA Authority, has been successfully completed under the efforts of the technical staff of the APSARA Authority.
The APSARA Authority told Fresh News on September 12 that the project was completed on September 4, 2020, with the aim of contributing to the preservation of Khmer cultural heritage in the field of Buddhism and to help preserve and Revitalize the cultural values of ancient Khmer art.
In this work, the technical team focused on repairing the walls, legs, walls, walls, stairs, tiles, doors, windows and roofs of the church and some other challenges to avoid the risk to make this old church look beautiful again. Again on the territory of Angkor in Siem Reap.
(Phnom Penh): The Joint Police Force brought a mobile test vehicle of the General Department of Consumer Protection, Competition and Anti-Fraud (KPR) to continue inspecting food and packaging products in Central Market, Daun Penh District. Officers found dumplings and rice cakes containing the banned chemical boracic and confiscated them from traders to be destroyed.
According to the official who conducted the operation, the operation took place on September 11, 2020 under the cooperation of the Phnom Penh branch of the CPP and the Phnom Penh Department of Commerce and the Central Market Committee in order to prevent Food safety as well as public health under the direction of Mr. Phan Oun, Director General of the General Department of Consumer Protection, Competition and Anti-Fraud.
As a result, officials found the presence of the banned chemical boracic acid in rice dumplings and rice husks, the official said. Officers then recorded the confiscation of the food and stored it for later incineration according to the procedure, and instructed the owners of the vendors selling dumplings and rice to stop the food containing borax.
At the same time, the official also advised other traders to understand and follow the law on quality control, safety of products and services, as well as the law on consumer protection to avoid affecting the health of people and may face. More legal issues. Ministry of Tourism announces the launch of the second phase of the Skills Development Program (SDP) from 2020-2024 in the Northeast
(Mondulkiri): The Ministry of Tourism has announced the launch of the second phase of the Skills Development Program (SDP) from 2020-2024 in the regional areas of Kratie, Stung Treng, Preah Vihear, Ratanakkiri and Mondulkiri.
This program will work with the Royal Government of Cambodia and the Ministry of Tourism to provide vocational training for young men and women and low-level professionals in the above five provinces to receive decent work and increase additional income. In line with the strategic plan for human resource development in tourism 2017-2025.
Mr. Chak Mengheang said that professional education in tourism is a key factor for young people to seize job opportunities immediately after graduation and may have the opportunity to start other small businesses.
(Kampong Thom): Five wooden houses donated by Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, have been announced for the construction of 5 needy families and widows living in Kor Koh commune, Santuk district, Kampong Thom province.
