(Phnom Penh): The management team of Puthisastra University received a high-level delegation of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports led by Mr. Youk Ngoy, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, and the technical working group visited and signed a Memorandum of Understanding on the opening of Puthisastra University. Back.
The Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports appreciates and appreciates the University's preparation and readiness to implement the Ministry's guidelines in response to hygiene standards as well as health protection measures. In addition, the University of Puthisastra is committed to sharing information and educating about the risks of Kovid 19 infection.
On that occasion, the senior delegation of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports was also pleased with the inspection of the online education system, which allows students of the University of Puthisastra to have the opportunity to continue their studies for nearly 15,000 hours in For the last 6 months.
The University of Puthisastra would also like to thank Mr. Youk Ngoy and the technical team for their valuable time and honor to inspect the campus to prepare for the reopening of the second phase.
The management of the University of Puthisastra is pleased that the University has implemented high safety standards for students as well as faculty staff to prepare for the reopening of the University soon. This university is one of the few universities in Cambodia that will be allowed to reopen.
The University of Puthisastra sincerely hopes and warmly welcomes the students to return to the University in a new way of study with hygiene and safety standards soon and ensures good hygiene to combat any risk from Kovid 19 infection.
