Royal Government Working Group Visits Sandan District, Kampong Thom Province to Organize Public Forum to Solve People's Challenges
(Kampong Thom): The Royal Government Working Group visited Sandan District, Kampong Thom Province, led by Mr. Leang Phaly, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Planning and Chairman of the Royal Government Working Group on Sandan District, organized a public forum to solve problems for people who are facing problems. Some as well as responding to the requests of the people who are currently in need.
On that occasion, Mr. Leang Phaly, Chairman of the Royal Government Working Group in Sandan District, said that the forum was held to help solve some of the remaining challenges for the people well and especially the service. Public: To give people more effective means to give people trust and support the current policy of the Royal Government.
In addition, he called on people to be very careful about Kovid 19, although there are no cases of communicable disease in Cambodia, urging people to be clean and follow the principles of the Ministry of Health. Published in the past.
"Apart from Kovid 19, people also need to be aware of dengue fever and chickenpox, which are caused by mosquito bites, and this type of disease occurs during the rainy season," he said. Please take good care of your health to avoid any disease that can affect the whole family.
After the completion of the public forum, solving some problems for the people, the Royal Government team in Sandan district visited and distributed gifts to 10 poor families in the back of the house, each family received 1 bag of fragrant rice. Equivalent to 25 kg of seeds for growing 5 crops (seaweed, cucumber, rice, nong, cabbage and papaya) with a budget of 20,000 Riels to distribute medicine to 81 people.
Please be reminded that on August 14, 2020, the Royal Government team in Sandan district decided to support the repair of a 23-kilometer road in Sochet commune at a cost of more than 20 million Riels at the request of the people in This commune. The team also inspected the repair of this road to speed up the repair in order for people to travel easily.
About 20 million Riels of the Royal Government's working group in Sandan district, Kampong Thom province has already been handed over to the local authority to repair 23 kilometers of roads in Sochet commune.
It should be noted that in the meeting "Monitoring, supporting and promoting the identification of poor families during the Kovid-19 epidemic" and the opening of a public forum with the distribution of funds and medicines, along with the participation of Kan Ben Eighth, at Wat "Maha Poreuk" called "Wat Boeung Pra" of the Royal Government working group in Sandan district spent a total budget of about 15 million riels.
