Spokesman for the General Commission: On September 11, another 957 vehicles were inspected and fined
According to the spokesperson of the General Commissioner, within 134 days of tightening the road traffic law by increasing the fine according to Sub-Decree No. 49, from May 1 to September 11, 2020, the traffic police nationwide inspected And fined a total of 167,398 vehicles, including 124,082 motorcycles and 43,316 vehicles of all types.
Notable offenses for motorcycles are mostly overtaking, no license plates and drunken driving. In particular, the offenses for cars are mostly speeding, over-capacity, no belts, offenses, no license plates, overweight, no driver's license, use the phone and so on.
Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun said that for the past 134 days, the implementation of the new sub-decree to fine vehicles for offenses has been going well. He thanked and commended all the road users for their good obedience to the traffic law so far, especially the traffic police for their dedication and hard work. Tighten traffic with the highest sense of responsibility.
Please note that for September 11, 2020, traffic accidents across Cambodia also occurred 8 times, in which 1 person died, 12 people were injured (10 people were seriously injured).
