(Rattanakiri): On the morning of September 11, 2020, Major General Yin Chamnan, Ratanakkiri Provincial Police Commissioner, and Deputy Commissioner, Chief of Office, Commander of the 623rd Border Guard Regiment, O'Yadao District Police Inspector, Immigration Police Officer O'Yadao International and Buddhists near and far join the 9th Kanben Blessing Ceremony at Wat Seima Sovankiri, O'Yadao District.
The 9th Kan Ben Ceremony has been held since the afternoon of September 10, 2020, with a meeting of the Commissioner, Deputy Commissioner, Chief of Office, District Inspector of O'Yadao, Buddhists at the foot of the pagoda. Perform a sermon.
On the morning of September 11, 2020, there will be a ceremony to give yaku to the monks, counting the ancestral rites and offerings to the ancestors who have passed away, and to the monks and nuns.
Separately, 4 grandfathers, each received 50,000 Riels and 4 grandmothers received 50,000 Riels each.
Minister of Commerce asks students to study abroad to help promote Cambodia's investment potential
(Phnom Penh): The Minister of Commerce, Mr. Pan Sosak, considered that Cambodian students who have received scholarships to study abroad are not only the ones who have the opportunity to gain knowledge, but also the Cambodian ambassador who can help promote Cambodia to the world. Well.
The Minister told the scholarship students, "All of you must know how to disseminate the achievements and progress of the country to the outside world. "We need to inspire Japanese people and investors to visit and invest more in our country."
In this meeting, Mr. Pan Sosak also instructed all scholarship students to adhere to the national identity and dignified character to be worthy of young men and women representing the country in order to strengthen friendship, solidarity and good cooperation with Japanese students and students from other countries.
The Minister also highlighted another important achievement of the Ministry: the establishment of eight working groups to negotiate the establishment of eight free trade agreements in charge of free trade negotiations with China, the United Kingdom, the Republic of Korea, the European Economic Union (EAEU). ), America, Japan, Mongolia and India. In addition, Cambodia has just reached a free trade agreement with China, which has just been successfully completed and is ready to sign soon.
