Senior Minister Kun Kim Tells Honorary President of Kep Veterans Association to Take Care of Solving Veterans' Difficulties
(Kep): Senior Minister Kun Kim, Vice President and Secretary General of the Cambodian Veterans Association, on Friday afternoon, September 11, 2020, handed over the position of Honorary President of Kep Veterans Association to Mr. Som Piseth, Governor of Kep Province.
The inauguration ceremony of the Honorary President of Kep Veterans Association was also attended by the President of the Provincial Council and provincial officials, including a total of 352 members of the Provincial Veterans Association.
Major General Chhim Khmao, president of the Kep Veterans Association, said that Kep has a total of 315 members of the Veterans Association. In the past, the management of the association in the province has always taken care to solve the problems of the members in a timely manner. To intervene in a timely manner.
Mr. Som Piseth, the new Honorary President of Kep Veterans Association, expressed his commitment to work hard to fulfill his duties well. In particular, make every effort to solve the difficulties of all members of the Veterans Association.
As the beginning of the conversation in this ceremony, Senior Minister Kun Kim, the energetic staff of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia and the President of the Cambodian Veterans Association, brought his deep greetings and memories. Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen to the leadership of the Armed Forces and all members of the Cambodian Veterans in Kep Province.
As the Chief of Staff of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Mr. Kun Kim praised the past development efforts in the province as well as the participation in various activities to help veterans in all forms of the leadership of the Cambodian Veterans Association in Kep. .
In addition, in order to ensure that the veterans in Kep get a better life, Senior Minister Kun Kim instructed the new Honorary President of the Cambodian Veterans Association in Kep to pay special attention to serving the members. Veterans in the province to suit their invaluable merits who have served and sacrificed in the cause of protecting and building peace for the motherland of Cambodia in the past.
The Senior Minister also instructed local authorities at all levels, especially at the commune level, to properly compile the biographical documents of veterans members for basic use when needed and to ensure that they can receive support in accordance with their policies. Royal Government.
