(Stung Treng): The National Bank of Cambodia, in collaboration with the Cambodian Microfinance Association, continues to disseminate financial knowledge and new trends in the banking and microfinance sector in Cambodia to the people by organizing a municipal workshop on " Microfinance in Cambodia ”in Stung Treng City, Stung Treng Province.
The workshop was organized by Mr. Rath Sovannarak, Director General of the National Bank of Cambodia, and was attended by Mr. Nin Sok Sdey, Member of Stung Treng Municipal Board, Mr. Say Kosal, Governor of Stung Treng City, Deputy Chairman and Team Members. Board of Directors of the Microfinance Association, officials of the National Bank of Cambodia, staff of microfinance institutions and local authorities, about 100 people.
The Municipal Workshop on "Microfinance in Cambodia" in Stung Treng City, Stung Treng Province is organized with the aim of disseminating financial knowledge and new trends of the banking and microfinance sector in Cambodia, especially on the measures of the National Bank of Cambodia. Cambodia has set out in the past and in the future to ease the burden on borrowers and protect the interests of the people affected by the Kovid 19 epidemic.
Mr. Rath Sovannarak issued some measures in addition to many measures of the National Bank of Cambodia:
1. Banks and microfinance institutions must continue to pay attention to resolving issues with customers in a gentle and favorable manner in accordance with the spirit of the National Bank of Cambodia's Directive on Credit Restoration for all sectors.
2. Local authorities and banking and microfinance institutions must work closely to prevent activities that intentionally pollute the environment and cause social problems and financial instability in Cambodia.
3: Continue to maintain hygiene and health of themselves and their families to avoid infection with Kovid 19.
The Royal Government is preparing to establish a cashew federation to help the value chain of the whole Cambodian cashew sector (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): The establishment of the Cambodian Cashew Federation has been decided by the Ministry of Commerce, while the technical working group is currently preparing The draft Cambodian Cashew Policy is almost ready, which is scheduled to be submitted to the Joint Working Group (Inter-Ministerial) in early November 2020.
According to the draft plan, the Cambodian Cashew Policy will be approved by Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen in the first quarter of 2021.
Speaking at the ceremony, Mr. Varutsan said that in order to effectively implement the national policy of cashew, which will complete the draft in the future, the active participation of state institutions, partners, NGOs and relevant development partners, as well as Especially the private sector is really indispensable.
The Chairman of the Advisory Group of the Ministry of Commerce also emphasized that after the establishment of the Cambodian Cashew Federation, relevant ministries as well as NGOs have the duty to continue to help the Federation to be strong, transparent and accountable to participate in the implementation of the National Cashew Policy. Good results.
At the same time, Mr. Varuth San said that the draft national policy of cashew set out the vision and objectives for the development of Cambodia's cashew sector in the next 5 years as follows:
1: Utilize Cambodia's competitive advantage in the development of cashew sector.
2: Help change and promote the Cambodian cashew sector, with production based on market demand, increase value-added and processing of various types and levels of cashew products to trade for the country and export, especially to existing markets. Low demand but high price.
3. Produce, process and export directly (do not rely on nose to breathe) to help sustain business by targeting customers.
4: Improve the livelihood and ensure the income of farmers, workers and exporters.
5: Support and make the cashew sector contribute more to the sustainable development of the national economy.
6. Until 2025, Cambodia will be recognized both domestically and internationally as a leading exporter of cashew nuts, competitive, high quality and sustainable, based on high standards of management. Supply chain, food security and social responsibility that comes from thinking and working together.
7. Farmers who produce leading products on yield and quality will be rewarded equally by their labor and investment, with effective service support and better access to information. Market and technology as well as modern machinery to develop Cambodia's cashew sector to grow like other countries.
8. Purchasing and processing products from responsible enterprises, providing reasonable profits with strong connections with producers and buyers through contracts based on effective market prices.
