(Banteay Meanchey): Lieutenant General Hun Manet, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Commander of the Land Forces, presided over the inauguration ceremony of the Infantry Brigade on the morning of September 10, 2020. No. 51, 5th Military Zone, Banteay Meanchey Province.
Lt. Gen. Hun Manet stated that as the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, soldiers at all levels and in all positions have duties and obligations in participating in maintaining the territorial integrity and serving the people. To accomplish this task requires a strong unit, for the most important strong unit, the unit must be a bundle of unity, and the bundle of unity can only depend on the commander and the chief of staff who are the leaders.
General Hun Manet emphasized that in addition to the internal unity, please also submit some leadership principles:
* Maintain absolute loyalty to the nation, religion, the King, and strictly abide by all orders of the Royal Government, the Ministry of National Defense, the General Command and the Army Command.
Strictly abide by the Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia and the general statute and general rules for the soldiers of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, as well as other relevant legal documents.
* Necessary attention must be paid to psychological education and understanding of new situations to promote patriotic conscience. This is something that needs to be done on a regular basis to ensure the stability of the army's commitment to peacekeeping, to avoid believing in mobilization and other deceptive tactics if we are not careful.
* Care must be taken to manage forces well and use human resources effectively.
* Must pay attention, train and actively participate in learning properly and strictly, with respect, perseverance and physical and mental training in all skills.
* Must pay attention to the collection, preparation, maintenance, technical maintenance, weapons, ammunition, ammunition, machinery, machinery, equipment, ensure safety and technical conditions.
* Continue to implement good cooperation with local authorities at all levels, contribute to strengthening security and public order, contribute to building safe villages and communes, as well as good cooperation with friendly parties in maintaining stability along the border and in Geography is responsible.
* Continue to pay close attention to improving the living standards and well-being of the army. Especially in the era of Kovid-19 disease, care must be taken to prevent the spread of the disease in the unit, as well as to help prevent the spread in the community, the army and the people.
