(Phnom Penh): The section of National Road No. 3, about 135 kilometers long, from the Chaom Chao roundabout in Phnom Penh to Kampot City, has been completed more than 80 percent after the construction process for about two years. Currently, although Cambodia is suffering from Kovid 19, the construction of National Road 3 continues as usual, and the construction team has been making the road from the Chaom Chao roundabout to Bek Kous.
While the construction team was working on the road park, some phenomena also appeared: People and monks in some temples on both sides of National Road 3 protested against the construction team not to block the road. The road where they used to cross. On the road from the Choam Chao roundabout to the intersection of about 70 kilometers, there are 17 people protesting to block the road.
Residents have expressed their concern that the roadblocks they used to cross cause them to waste time driving around and worry about traffic accidents while traveling across the road.
On Thursday, September 10, 2020, Mr. Khan Maner, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, led a technical working group to coordinate with the people and explain some technical issues in the construction of this road.
Mr. Khan Maner met directly with the people and tried to explain the technical problems and some of the procedures of the road construction. The Secretary of State stressed that the construction of the road park in the district is very important to reduce congestion and traffic accidents, as well as highlight the beauty of the road.
He said that technically, the construction of the park divides the road to maintain the distance between the road at the point where the main road crosses and the location of the crossing, but to maintain a distance from one space to another from 1.5 kilometers. 2 km outside the town and between 400 m and 700 m in the town.
Mr. Manner also pointed out the risks of improper road construction. He stated that for the road standard, there are 4 lanes like this, if the road is built in a way that leaves the crossing space not in accordance with the technical specifications, it will result in a decrease in driving speed, causing traffic congestion and traffic accidents that cause loss of property, disability or Lose family loved ones and easily fall into the trap of poverty.
Due to the departure of some crossings from gas stations and other businesses, people suspect that there is a conspiracy between road builders and business owners by offering money in exchange for opening crosswalks. Khan Manner denied the allegations.
Mr Khanmaner claimed that there was no corruption or bribery in exchange for paving the way. That is, the opening and closing of the road is done according to the technical specifications. For the opening of the road through some gas stations, unless there are four intersections or major intersections in the province.
After mediation, some residents understood and allowed the construction team to block the road where they were protesting. On September 10, 10 protest streets were closed and the remaining seven will be closed the next day.
The Secretary of State thanked the people for their understanding of National Road 3. Especially those who live along this road related to the disturbances during the construction and also called for cooperation with the Royal Government as well as with the construction company to ensure that the construction is technically good quality and complete the construction. Planned projects.
It should be noted that National Road No. 3 was opened for construction and rehabilitation on May 7, 2018 under the presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
The project to expand and upgrade the quality of National Road No. 3 from the Chaom Chao roundabout in Phnom Penh to Kampot city with a total length of nearly 135 kilometers, passing through Phnom Penh, Kandal, Kampong Speu, Takeo and Kampot. The road rehabilitation project will cost more than 200 million US dollars and is scheduled for completion in 2022.
The project to improve National Road No. 3 is divided into two sections, the first section from Chom Chao roundabout to Bek Kous, Takeo province, with a length of nearly 70 km, to widen the width of the road up to 24.5 meters into 4 lanes (2 lanes) 2 lanes) paved with AC rubber concrete, 9 cm thick, 21 m wide, with a total width of 24.5 m.
Separately, the second section from Bek Kous, Takeo province to Kampot city, with a length of nearly 65 km, was widened to 12 meters in two lanes (1 lane to 1 lane), paved with AC rubber, 7 cm thick and 11 m wide.
This section of National Road No. 3 is a line of Cambodia's potential economic and tourism poles, connecting Phnom Penh to Kampot and connecting to Sihanoukville International Seaport via National Road No. 4 and Koh Kong Province. Cambodia-Thailand via National Road 4 and National Road 48 as well.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, once expressed the expectation that after the completion of the construction, National Road 3 will play an important role in improving the efficiency of travel and transportation of agricultural products and agriculture. Industry of investment companies and people from all over the country to the local market and especially to the international market through the deep sea port easily and quickly.
In addition, National Road No. 3 is also part of the southern corridor along the coast of the Greater Mekong Subregion, connecting the ASEAN Highway network from Thailand to Cambodia and on to Vietnam. Leaders and officials of the National Bank of Cambodia bring suffixes, relics, drinks and food to attend the 8th Ben at Wat Chan Borey Vong
