More than 5 kilos of soybean foam containing chemicals and some defective goods in salads were found by professional officers at Prasot Market, Svay Rieng Province
(Svay Rieng): On the occasion of Pchum Ben, Mr. Pheng Nil, Branch Manager of Consumer Protection, Competition and Fraud Suppression (CPC) on the morning of September 10, 2020, cooperated with the Provincial Department of Commerce to inspect the goods at Prasot Market, Svay Teap District, Svay Rieng Province.
Mr. Pheng Nil said that the CPP team in Svay Rieng province inspected the items on display at the market, including testing 15 samples of foodstuffs and found substances. Chemicals put in 5 kg of bubble beans and some defective goods in Sladak are out of date.
He continued that this season is the Pchum festival season, people need food and salad to give to the monks to ensure the quality and safety of food for the people. Svay Rieng Province.
He added that after identifying the target and inspecting the goods at the market, it was found that 5 kg of chemicals in the bubble, soybeans and lettuce were damaged. No more counterfeit or defective sales.
He said that if the product is damaged beyond the expiration date, it can cause diarrhea, vomiting, kidney damage, stomach upset and dizziness, resulting in decreased strength and poor health can be life-threatening. Also.
