Kandal Provincial Governor Kien Svay Warns of Mastermind Who Incited Citizens to Seize Private Land
(Kandal): Mr. Ou Chheang, Governor of Kien Svay District, issued another legal warning to 3 or 4 ringleaders who incited more than 200 families to seize their private land at Prek Pol Village, Kandal Krom Village, Banteay Dek Commune, Village Prek Takeo, Prek Takeo 2 Village, Chey Udom Village, Chey Udom 2 Village, Chroy Dong Village, Samrong Thom Commune, Kien Svay District, to avoid this problem because it can face legal action because all landowners have filed a complaint gradually.
Speaking to Fresh News reporters in Kandal province on September 10, 2020, the district governor added that the league has issued a preliminary notice to the people to wake up first to wake them up. He succumbed to the machinations of some of the masterminds who used tricks to incite the movement to illegally encroach on other people's private land.
The district governor added that if the case is not withdrawn, the Kien Svay district administration will issue a letter inviting the residents to the district hall to resolve this issue.
(Phnom Penh): Ms. Ing Kantha Phavi, Minister of Women's Affairs, on September 10, 2020, urged stakeholders to implement the Master Plan on "Gender and Climate Change" effectively to help reduce risks.
This push was made on the occasion of Ms. Ing Kantha Phavi's participation in the final workshop of Package C of the Project on Integrating Climate Change Resilience into Development Planning (MCRDP) held at Phnom Penh Hotel this morning. September 10, 2020.
At the same time, there is also the announcement of the official launch of the Master Plan on Gender and Climate Change.
Ms. Ing Kantha Phavi said that seeing the many issues that women face in climate change, the Ministry of Women's Affairs, in collaboration with the Asian Development Bank, as well as other ministries and stakeholders, has developed a master plan on gender and climate change.
The Minister said that the Master Plan aims to increase knowledge on solutions and understand strategic measures for stakeholders to respond to climate change adaptation and resilience, especially in investment projects. In response to climate change in Cambodia.
Ms. Ing Kantha Phavi added that the Steering and Coordinating Committee on Gender and Climate Change led the consultation, reflection and revision of the master plan document with relevant institutions in the fields of agriculture, water resources, rural development, health and public works, including NGOs. Civil society, development partners and technical working groups of relevant ministries and institutions until the master plan document is officially implemented.
In addition, Ms. Ing Kantha Phavi emphasized that this master plan document will be a key document for relevant ministries, civil society organizations and private partners to use in gender mainstreaming in policies, programs and investment projects, climate change adaptation, as well as cuts. Reduce disasters.
Ms. Ing Kantha Phavi also encourages you to implement the Master Plan on Gender and Climate Change effectively to help reduce the risk to the target groups of men, women, children, people with disabilities, indigenous peoples and Vulnerable people caused by climate change in Cambodia.
General Khim Bunsong Brings Donations to Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh to Visit 317 Kulen Disabled Soldiers in Siem Reap
(Siem Reap): On the morning of September 10, 2020, General Khim Bunsong, Secretary of State of the Ministry of National Defense, representing Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense, led a delegation to visit officers, deputies and soldiers on the occasion. Cambodian Buddhists celebrate the traditional Khmer Pchum Ben at the Samdech Techo Hun Sen Kulen 317 Disabled Soldiers Development Center in Siem Reap for 304 families.
In the report of Lt. Gen. Pov Sea, Director of the Center for the Development of Disabled Soldiers, Samdech Techo Hun Sen Kulen 317 Siem Reap confirmed the performance of disabled soldiers in the center and some shortcomings.
Speaking on that occasion, General Khim Bunsong also brought a message from Samdech Prime Minister Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen and Samdech Pichey Sena Tea Banh and Mrs. Samdech always consider the well-being and living conditions of the soldiers. Officers, deputies and soldiers of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces (RCAF) in the Samdech Techo Hun Sen Kulen 317 Disabled Soldiers Development Center, Siem Reap Province.
Especially during the traditional festival season as well as the National Festival of the Royal Government of Cambodia, as well as the delegation of the Ministry of National Defense and the authorities at all levels always visit the disabled soldiers who lost their validity and retired soldiers at the Disabled Soldiers Development Center. As in divisions and units as well.
The General praised the heroism in the spirit of all disabled soldiers who sacrificed their lives to protect the territorial integrity and find peace for the motherland until they became disabled. With the victorious policy of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, national unity, internal unity ended the war in Cambodia completely in 1998, improved the lives of the people and the country developed in all fields.
The Secretary of State also instructed all disabled soldiers to take care of their health and, most importantly, to participate in the prevention of new respiratory infections (COVID-19) caused by the new coronavirus and chickenpox. Regular hygiene in the family is to follow the guidelines of the Ministry of Health by washing hands with soap, alcohol or gel and wearing a mask properly.
The General thanked and commended the Commander, Deputy Commander of the 317 Siem Reap Disabled Officers and Soldiers for maintaining the tradition, morality, character and discipline of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces by never doing anything inappropriate. It is not difficult for the Royal Government to solve that.
In that, General Khim Bunsong handed over 3 million Riels donated by Samdech Pichey Sena Tea Banh to be used in Samdech Techo Hun Sen Kulen 317 Siem Reap Disabled Veterans Development Center and 304 families of disabled soldiers. Noodles, sugar, milk and 30,000 Riels.
Kampong Thom Provincial Administration Continues to Provide Voluntary Options to Citizens Enjoying Nupheap Sothy Economic Land Concession
(Kampong Thom): Kampong Thom Provincial Administration continues to stand by its position on voluntary settlement of land disputes in which people occupy land in economic land concessions that the Royal Government of Cambodia has decided to provide as investment land to "Nupheap Sothy" Company In 2007 to develop land on agro-industrial crops.
Mr. Sok Hay, Deputy Governor of Kampong Thom Province and Chairman of the Land Dispute Coordination Team, went to set up border posts for the people who accepted the principle of voluntary settlement and enjoying the economic land concession of "Nupheap Sothy" Company.
On that occasion, he said that on behalf of the Kampong Thom Provincial Administration, he came down to coordinate for the people based on the principles of cooperation and voluntary agreement of the people whose land is enjoying, such as: potatoes and others are planting. Cashews and so on.
In carrying out this work, the company, together with the provincial authorities, has set a settlement principle based on the company's land allocation to the people in two different conditions, including: First, the principle of 50% equality on the land that the people are enjoying, such as : Potato, rice and Prey Bos and secondly, the company reclaims 40% of the land that people are enjoying (leaving 60% of the land area) on cashew and mango crops.
Mr. Sok Hay continued that the land clearing will prepare all the people who have land in the company to put it together in one place and conduct a lottery to find their land strategically and the people can enjoy this land. Forever, too.
According to Mr. Khakha Bunhim, Deputy Governor of Santuk District, on behalf of the district authority, the company and the people will continue to mediate on the above two principles, which will benefit both the company and the people.
In particular, the people who own the land said that the solution is that they accept the principle voluntarily, without coercion.
It should be noted that "Nupheap Sothy" Company has been investing in this land in Kraya Commune, Santuk District, Kampong Thom Province since 2007, which covers an area of more than 3,000 hectares and now the company has planted more than 900 hectares. Cashew, mango and fragrant coconut. Minister of Information: The media has made a significant contribution to the prevention of Kovid-19
(Central): Mr. Khieu Kanharith, Minister of Information, stated that the media has made an important contribution to the prevention of Kovid-19 infection through public awareness and awareness of anti-Kovid-19 measures. With the Royal Government of Cambodia.
The Minister of Information said this at the inauguration ceremony of the studio, Akp office and meeting hall of Kandal Provincial Information Department on September 10, 2020, with the participation of Mr. Kao Im Ron, Undersecretary of State and Many other senior officials of the Ministry of Information.
