(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, has expressed his ambition to turn Cambodia into a distribution hub in the ASEAN region. The senior minister said that geographically, ASEAN is a central country that is easy to connect, transport and distribute goods.
Seeing the favorable geography of this transportation, the Senior Minister wanted to turn Cambodia into a distribution center. The ministry is currently seeking investment partners to set up the center, and Singaporean investors are showing great interest in the project.
On September 9, 2020, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol led a delegation to discuss the cooperation between Cambodia and Singapore in the development of the Phnom Penh Logistics Center project and to negotiate an agreement with the Deputy Prime Minister and Deputy Minister. Responsible for development and finance of Singapore, Asia Infrastructure and YCH via video.
In his opening remarks, the Senior Minister pointed out that the Phnom Penh Logistics Center plays an important role in driving Cambodia's economic growth to achieve its vision of developing Cambodia into a high-middle-income country by 2030 and High-income countries by 2050.
The Senior Minister continued that in order to achieve this national development plan, the Royal Government has been modernizing the transport infrastructure and planning to establish the Phnom Penh Logistics Center in response to the above vision. In addition, the Ministry as well as the Royal Government want to see Cambodia as a market and logistics center to serve the transportation sector to countries in the region, especially Thailand, Vietnam, Laos and Myanmar.
According to Mr. Sun Chanthol, the Phnom Penh Logistics Center is defined as a strategic plan in both the logistics master plan and the transitional master plan on the connection of multi-modal transport and logistics, which this strategic plan shows the connection between land and rail. Waterways and airways aim to ensure a smooth and efficient transport chain.
The Senior Minister emphasized that Cambodia has been building the Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville Expressway and other infrastructure as the backbone to support the Phnom Penh Logistics Center project.
The Senior Minister expressed his support for the Government of Singapore, Executive Director of Asian Infrastructure and welcomed YCH interested in the Phnom Penh Logistics Center development project, and the Royal Government of Cambodia is ready to help coordinate and resolve the obstruction. Organized as a technical team to coordinate the implementation of this project.
Mr. Sun Chanthol expressed his deep appreciation and gratitude to the Government of Singapore, Asian Infrastructure and YCH for their willingness to study and invest in the logistics sector in Cambodia and requested them to contact the Ministry's Technical Working Group to The team facilitates and resolves issues aimed at implementing the project according to its planned steps and dates with high efficiency.
