(Tbong Khmum): On the morning of September 9, 2020, Mr. Peang Narith, Deputy Governor of Tbong Khmum Province, represented by Dr. Cheam Chansophoan, Governor of Tbong Khmum Province, met with local authorities of Memot District, Choam Kravien Commune, Boeung Kram Community and released 4 species of fish. About 57,000 in Boeung Kram received from the Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries.
Heng Piseth, director of the Tbong Khmum Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, said that 57,000 juveniles in four species, including squid, trout and trout, had been released.
He added that these young fish will increase the fish in the lake for the traditional program of the people in this area and tourists to visit early next year.
Mr. Peang Narith sent a message to visit the whole community and wish you good health and avoid all 19 diseases.
He added that considering the potential of this geography for cultural tourism, Dr. Governor has put out a plan to develop a proper structure to expand the scope, the first step is to dig and expand the lake yard by several square meters. Become a natural cultural tourism destination for all seasons.
Mr. Peang Narith added that Boeung Kram will be a natural cultural tourism resort that can create jobs and additional income for the people in this area. Therefore, we must join together to take care of these fish, not to steal illegal equipment, especially fishing gear, which seriously destroys all kinds of fish resources and keep the surrounding forest well as a shade for tourists.
Please be informed that Boeung Kram has a slope of 30 hectares and 20 small lakes, as well as many kinds of submerged plants, and every year during the month of February, the people here celebrate the fishing Cooking together, which is a tradition from the beginning to the present.
For the past two years, Dr. Cheam Chansophoan has led people to go fishing and distribute cash prizes to big and big fish catchers. In particular, for the coming 2021, according to the plan, Dr. Governor will hold a bigger ceremony by releasing tens of thousands of fish today.
IPA Social Affairs Committee Discusses Improving ASEAN Cultural and Social Community Responding to Kovid 19
On the afternoon of September 9, 2020, Ms. Nin Saphon, Chairperson of the National Assembly Commission of Public Works, Transport, Telecommunication, Post, Industry, Mining, Energy, Trade, Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, led a delegation of IPA Cambodia Social Affairs Committee The ASEAN IPA Inter-Parliamentary Social Affairs Committee of the 41st ASEAN Inter-Parliamentary Assembly, hosted by the National Assembly of Vietnam via video.
The composition of the Cambodian delegation to the meeting on "Improving the role of IPA in supporting the ASEAN Socio-Cultural Community in Response to Kovid-19" includes: Ms. Un Sokunthea, Member of the National Assembly, Mr. Ouk Damri, Member of the National Assembly, Mr. Say Borin, Senator, Ms. Mak Vansitha, Member of the National Assembly, Mr. Prohm Virak, Director General of International Relations, Protocol and Information, and other professional officials.
Ms. Nin Saphon addressed the meeting that 19 cases of Kovid were a threat to the daily life of the ASEAN community, not only in terms of safety and health, but also in the way of life, economy, society and all aspects of life. The world.
She said that for Cambodia, the situation of Kovid 19 is not serious because there is no community infection in the country. All current cases are imported and have zero mortality. This is because Cambodia has put in place strict measures to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 by establishing three battlefields: first, to prevent the occurrence of cases brought into Cambodia; second, to prevent community-based transmission; The third is to provide treatment for the infected.
Moreover, as the world awaits the discovery of the Kovid 19 vaccine, Cambodia calls for the adoption of the vaccine as a universal public commodity that people everywhere can use, as Samdech Techo Hun Sen, head of the Royal Government Cambodia has said, "We hope that when the Kovid 19 vaccine is shown to be effective, it will be used for humanity and as a global commodity."
