Kampot Provincial Administration vows to increase 2.5 million tourists by 2023
(Kampot): The Kampot Provincial Administration has launched a five-year tourism development plan (2019-2023) and is committed to increasing the number of tourists by 2.5 million by 2023. Such commitment in opening a seminar to disseminate tourism development plan in Kampot province on September 9, 2020 at Kampot Provincial Hall under the chairmanship of Mr. Chiao Tay, Governor of Kampot.
The Director of the Kampot Provincial Department of Tourism, Mr. Soy Sinol, stated at the seminar to promote the five-year provincial tourism development plan that the number of tourists in Kampot is increasing every year due to peace, economy, development under the leadership of Samdech Techo And combined with the rich potential of the province as well. In fact, in 2019, there were more than 1.6 million tourists, an increase of 2.17% compared to 2018, which had more than 1.4 million visitors.
In the five-year tourism development plan, relevant officials, especially the provincial administration, will work together to increase the number of tourists to 2.5 million by 2023.
Mr. Chiao Tai said that under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, has brought peace and development in all areas, including tourism, which is considered by the Royal Government as an important economic pole. Active in socio-economic development, create employment opportunities, increase income, improve people's living standards.
According to the provincial governor, the tourism development plan 2019-2023 shows a clear vision for the future of tourism development in Kampot province, focusing on strategic directions, including: development of tourism products, study, marketing, promotion, connectivity and Facilitation of travel, development of infrastructure, fitness development, tourism support, conservation of cultural and natural resources, human resource development, management of negative impacts of tourism.
The development plan also outlines the study of challenges, risks, strengths, opportunities and the development of strategies, measures, action plans, mechanisms for implementation and monitoring.
The provincial governor also set out 12 priority recommendations, including:
1. All relevant parties, departments, units around the provinces, cities and districts must pay attention to implement their competencies mentioned in the plan.
2. Facilitate the construction of an international tourist port to be completed by 2021 on time.
3: Promote the development of Kampot Meas Sen Beach Resort to serve tourists.
4: The provincial administration is studying the possibility of building a new bridge across the Kampong Bay canal in one more place.
5: Together improve the aesthetics of the city to be more attractive, green environment, clean, no garbage or dust.
6: Maintaining the victory of 3 romduol flowers and the ASEAN Clean Tourism City.
7. Encourage companies to invest in tourism.
8. The Department of Tourism should pay more attention to the implementation of the plan by requiring meetings every three months.
9. The Department of Environment and the Department of Land shall co-operate as staff for the Coastal Development Management Committee.
10. Expand tour packages on islands and beaches.
11: The Department of Tourism must study the location to build additional information centers.
12: In the upcoming Kan Ben and Pchum Ben seasons, many tourists will visit Kampot province, so officials and stakeholders, the authorities must encourage all businesses, entertainment providers, tourism service providers to participate in implementing health measures to prevent Kovid. 19.
These 12 recommendations are for all stakeholders, departments and units around the province to pay attention to the implementation of activities that are in their jurisdiction and are stated in this development plan as a priority activity, in line with the annual action plan. Its three-year rolling plan, especially better sanitation management.
