(Battambang): Geographical data for agriculture and water, vegetable cultivation techniques in the modern mobile application was officially launched on September 9, 2020 under the chairmanship of Mr. Chhim Vachira, Representative of the Provincial Governor and Chairman. Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of Battambang, Mr. Bou Sophal, Project Director, Angkor Green Company and farmers from other communities.
Mr. CHHIM Vachira, Director of Battambang Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries in the Department of Specialization, congratulates Angkor Green for collaborating with many other project partners to create this program for the convenience of vegetable growers, collectors , Fertilizer seller, water producer and so on.
He said that the Angkor Salad is integrated with information related to agriculture, the main goal of the Angkor Salad project is to reduce the use of excessive resources on cultivation, including the use of water and fertilizer, while the yield will increase. Acne, especially safe vegetables.
He added that Angkor Salad is an important mobile application that provides many benefits to users such as:
* Farmers receive advice on crop cultivation techniques, use of irrigation systems, proper application of fertilizers according to soil type and area, seasonal crop management (dry and wet), crop control (pests, diseases), implementation. Good Agriculture (GAP) has direct contact with fertilizer sellers, pesticides, vegetable collectors, microfinance institutions, especially direct consultations with agricultural experts from different places.
* Fertilizer sellers receive information on farmers' fertilizer needs, which is important in targeting stocks for farmers, as well as other agricultural technical information.
* Vegetable collector receives information on the farmer's crop, has enough vegetables he needs to study agricultural technical information, is able to pre-determine the demand for the desired vegetable yield, has a direct relationship with the microfinance institution in order to supplement the loan. Cash for its business.
* Microfinance Institutions can directly contact farmers, fertilizer sellers, pesticides, vegetable collectors to provide their cash loan services.
* Government institutions and agricultural experts can share agricultural knowledge, new cultivation techniques and maintenance, new discoveries that are beneficial to farmers. Spokesman for the General Commission: On September 9, another 992 vehicles were inspected and fined
According to the spokesperson of the General Commissioner, within 132 days of tightening the road traffic law by increasing the fine according to Sub-Decree No. 49, from May 1 to September 9, 2020, the traffic police nationwide inspected And fined a total of 165,268 vehicles, including 122585 motorcycles and 42683 vehicles of all types.
Lt. Gen. Chhay Kimkhoeun said that for the past 132 days, the implementation of the new sub-decree to fine the offending vehicles has been going well. He thanked and commended all the road users for their good obedience to the traffic law so far, especially the traffic police for their dedication and hard work. Tighten traffic with the highest sense of responsibility.
Please note that for September 9, 2020, traffic accidents across Cambodia also occurred 10 times, in which 4 people died, 14 people were injured (9 seriously injured).
Speaking to reporters, the US official said that the president will announce on Wednesday this week (US time) plans to withdraw more US troops from Iraq, while plans related to Afghanistan will be announced at The next few days.
By the end of 2011, the United States had withdrawn a large number of its troops from Iraq, leaving only a handful of missions attached to the US Embassy there. But the United States also deployed troops a few years later to support Iraqi forces in the war against ISIS, which launched a major offensive in 2014.
In Afghanistan, the United States has a total of 8,600 troops, in line with a bilateral agreement signed in February 2020 between Washington and the Taliban. Last August, the Pentagon stated that its goal was to reduce the number of US troops to less than 5,000 in Afghanistan as peace talks in Afghanistan progressed.
Under the US-Taliban agreement, all foreign troops must leave Afghanistan between March and June 2021 in exchange for the Taliban's security commitment. Trump has also promised to withdraw all US troops from his homeland in an effort to end what he calls the US endless war.
In a message to North Korean President Received by Fresh News on September 9, 2020, the King of Cambodia congratulated the North Korean state on its success in building a happy country. And peace.
In a message unofficially translated by Fresh News, the King of Cambodia said, "On the occasion of the 72nd anniversary of the founding of the Democratic People's Republic of Korea, I would like to express my warm congratulations, including I wish you success and happiness to His Excellency. "For the Korean people, my friend, I wish you lasting peace and prosperity."
"The efforts of the Democratic People's Republic of Korea under your leadership have helped to accelerate the process of construction, development and well-being of your people," he added.
His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni emphasized that the existing friendly relations and good cooperation between the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Democratic People's Republic of Korea will bring the benefits of new perspectives in the interests of People of both countries.
Please note that North Korea was officially established on September 9, 1948. North Korea has the capital Pyongyang with a total area of 120,540 square kilometers and a water area of 4.48 percent and a population of over 25 million.
National Authority for Combating Drugs and Tbong Khmum Provincial Authority Disseminate Work Results and Cooperate in Suppressing Cross-Border Drug Crimes
(Tbong Khmum): On the morning of September 9, 2020, Lt. Gen. Chey Bopha, Deputy Secretary General of the National Authority for Combating Drugs and Mr. Kun Sophea, Deputy Governor and Chairman of the Secretariat of Tbong Khmum Provincial Drug Control Committee opened the meeting. Disseminate the report of the first half and the direction of the second half of 2020 of the National Authority for Combating Drugs at Tbong Khmum Provincial Hall.
Speaking on the occasion, Mr. Kun Sophea said that based on the Royal Government's plan, the Tbong Khmum Provincial Drug Control Committee has implemented a campaign against illegal drugs to prevent and suppress drug crimes in five measures that have been promoted. Anti-drug operations in all provinces throughout the province have actively implemented the Royal Government of Cambodia's anti-drug campaign plan.
On that occasion, Lt. Gen. Chey Bopha, Deputy Secretary General of the National Authority for Combating Drugs, stated that the process of leading the implementation of the 5th plan to fight against illegal drugs of the Royal Government of Cambodia is to achieve better results and success. To reduce and eliminate all types of drug offenses.
The lieutenant general also instructed the provincial drug control committees at all levels, the authorities, civil servants and the armed forces to continue to pay more attention to the implementation, especially not to be involved, not to be behind, not to be a reference. Relax and do not intervene in all types of drug offenses.
Lt. Gen. Chey Bopha also requested the relevant parties to continue to work together to implement effectively, especially in cooperation with neighboring countries to crack down on cross-border drug crimes, thorough control of chemical compounds, because unscrupulous traders can turn into drug processing. Illegal must continue to educate all targets, especially heavy truck drivers and participate in preventing the spread of Kovid-19, dengue fever and chickenpox.
(Preah Vihear): Two library buildings in Sambo Primary School and another in a quality primary school in Chhep Pei commune, Chhep district, worth $ 50,000, were inaugurated this morning, September 9, 2020. Mr. Sok Santara, Governor of Srok Chep, and the participation of government officials, the Armed Forces, teachers, students and many others.
On that occasion, Mr. Sok Santara sent a message from Senior Minister Meas Sophea, Minister in charge of Special Missions and Chairman of the Royal Government Working Group for Preah Vihear Provincial Assistance, and Mr. Prak Sovann, Governor of Preah Vihear Province, as he always thought. Take care of the well-being and living of the people in our province.
The district governor said that at a time when the world is experiencing a global epidemic of Kovid 19, Cambodia has also been affected by Kovid 19, affecting almost every sector. Especially for the study of students until the suspension of study before the deadline.
At the same time, he urged teachers to consider health and safety issues, mainly in accordance with the guidelines of the Ministry of Health, with students diligently washing their hands and wearing masks.
The guidelines outline general preventive measures to prevent the spread of COVID-19, which must be adopted when schools open to ninth- to twelfth-grade students. Back. In the classroom, sharing of study materials such as textbooks, pens or pencils, as well as water bottles among students is prohibited, and online learning is encouraged.
In addition, the guidelines from the Ministry of Health of India added that the arrangement of seats must be kept at least 2 meters apart, and teachers must ensure that both themselves and students must wear masks together. The school cafeteria is not allowed to operate.
As India prepares to gradually reopen schools, the epidemic of COVID-19 in this densely populated country remains dire, with tens of thousands of cases reported. See every day. India currently has the second highest number of cases in the world. The wife of Oddar Meanchey provincial governor leads the provincial women's association to participate in the 7th Ben at Wat Chey Udom Chongkal in Chongkal district
