Taiwan is currently leading live-fire exercises in the southwestern and eastern coasts, while China is also stepping up military activities by conducting military exercises near Taiwan. Police arrest 6 people, 1 Chinese and 5 Cambodians for extorting money from people in Sihanoukville
(Sihanoukville): Six people, including five Cambodians and a Chinese national, were arrested by Sihanoukville police on September 8, 2020 after impersonating police officers and extorting money from residents. .
After receiving the victims' complaints, under the direction of Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, Provincial Governor, and under the coordination of Mr. Sieng Sok, Provincial Prosecutor, Major General Chuon Narin ordered the Criminal Police Task Force to conduct a thorough investigation. Carefully identified the suspects and arrested a total of six suspects (a Chinese national) in a row at 7:30 pm on September 8, 2020.
In front of the police, the suspects confessed that they actually stopped the search car in the car and extorted $ 2,300 from the victim. Currently, the specialized force is building a case to be sent to proceed with the procedure. Koh Kong Red Cross Branch Holds World First Aid Day for Victims
(Koh Kong): In order to save lives in the event of an accident in the middle of the road or any location encountered in the first aid, the Cambodian Red Cross branch office in Koh Kong province on the morning of September 9, The World First Aid Day 2020 will be organized in the presence of Mr. Samkhit Vien, Deputy Governor of Koh Kong Province.
Also present were Ms. Mom Chanthy, Deputy Director of the Department of Health of the Cambodian Red Cross and the first aid specialist of the headquarters, members of the sub-branch committee of the Royal Khemarak Municipality, three commune chiefs, volunteers, youth, poor youth. Youth Scouts, citizens, as well as government officials in various departments and units.
Ms. Mom Chanthy said that first aid is an important subject that we all need to study to be the foundation for rescuing people in the community who are accidentally injured, such as: suffocation. Fractures and accidents before the doctor arrives or sends the victim to the hospital.
Mr. Samkhit Vien, Deputy Governor, emphasized that the celebration was to celebrate the World First Aid Day in order to educate people on how to rescue victims in their communities properly and safely before The doctor came to the rescue and before sending to the hospital.
The Cambodian Red Cross has educated the first aid to protect children from harm, and the topics covered include: burns (hot water, fire ...), broken bones, drowning, lightning and Choking.
The Cambodian Red Cross has been expanding first aid courses in government institutions and departments upon request and providing free first aid courses to the private sector and non-governmental organizations. The purpose of the Cambodian Red Cross is to have a first aid expert in each family.
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense and Chairman of the National Assistance Team for Siem Reap Province, on the afternoon of September 9, 2020, chaired a meeting to discuss 38 road infrastructure improvement projects. The line in Siem Reap aims to improve people's livelihoods, boost tourism and the national economy after the Kovid-19 crisis.
