At the same time, his professional staff advertised to traders that there is nothing better than breastfeeding alone for up to 6 months and explained to guide traders to understand the laws and technical regulations. Australia, Korea, New Zealand and UNDP continue to provide assistance for mine clearance projects in Cambodia
(Banteay Meanchey): Senior Minister Ly Thuch, First Vice President of the Mines Authority, said on September 9, 2020 that Banteay Meanchey province is highly regarded by the Royal Government of Cambodia and donors for demining.
On behalf of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Senior Minister Ly Thuch expressed his deep gratitude to the Government and people of Australia, the Republic of Korea, New Zealand and UNDP for joining the Royal Government of Cambodia through the Mine Action Project for the fourth phase of humanitarian demining. In Cambodia, to provide safe land and save the lives of local people from the threat of landmines.
At the same time, Senior Minister Ly Thuch also thanked the donors and other great friends of Cambodia, including: the United States, the United Kingdom, Japan, Germany, Switzerland, China, Norway, Canada, Ireland and UNICEF, as well as civil society organizations and philanthropists. Also.
The Senior Minister also praised and appreciated the CMAC operators who have participated and achieved many achievements in clearing landmines to save lives in the past. The Senior Minister confirmed that CMAC is a national operator with high experience and expertise in the field of mine action at both national and international levels.
The Senior Minister and donors met directly with the beneficiaries of the demined land and handed over certificates to five villages that have been cleared of landmine threats. He added that Banteay Meanchey is receiving high attention from the Royal Government of Cambodia and donors on demining.
The Mine Action for Results project was established in 2006 and is a multi-donor project that supports the Royal Government of Cambodia in resolving mine issues and contributing to the achievement of the National Mine Action Strategic Plan 2018-2025. UNDP is responsible for mobilizing resources, including funding and technical advisers, and the Mine Authority is responsible for overseeing project implementation.
Please also note that Banteay Meanchey is one of the provinces with the highest number of mine victims in Cambodia, 223 square kilometers of land cleared and used and the remaining land. 147 square kilometers still threatened by landmines. As of June 2020, Banteay Meanchey province had 8,882 landmine and landmine casualties, accounting for 14% of all accidents nationwide.
Separately, O Bei Choan commune is one of the communes with the most mines in Banteay Meanchey province, with 138 deaths and injuries, 10 females due to 128 mines. Or Bei Choan commune has an area of 17.4 square kilometers that has been cleared of mines and the remaining area is suspected to be 16.5 square kilometers.
