More than 400 Vulnerable Families in Stung Treng Province's Siem Bok District Receive Donations from the Royal Government through the Provincial Department of Social Affairs
(Stung Treng): Seeing the hardships of poor and vulnerable people, on September 9, 2020, Mr. Mom Saroeun, Governor of Stung Treng Province, visited and distributed gifts to poor and vulnerable people. 406 families live in Siem Bok commune, Siem Bok district, Stung Treng province.
The program was also attended by district governors, deputy district governors, the armed forces and departments around the province.
Among the gifts distributed at that time were gifts from Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, provided through the Department of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation of Stung Treng Province, with one family receiving Contains: 25 kg of rice, 1 box of noodles, 1 stick of fish, 1 stick of soy sauce and 1 blanket.
