Deputy Governor of Kampong Thom Province: The elderly are an important mechanism to help develop the society
(Kampong Thom): Mr. Nhek Ban Kheng, Deputy Governor of Kampong Thom Province, said that the elderly are an important mechanism to help develop the society.
Mr. Nhek Ban Kheng stated this at a meeting on September 9, 2020 at the Department of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation in Kampong Thom, organized by the Cambodian Organization for the Elderly. President of the Association of the Elderly, social officials in the districts and partner organizations in the province.
He added that the promotion of the well-being of the elderly has improved and shows the important role of the elderly in society, and the elderly are the ancestors who have created important resources and have a very important role in building families. The community provides a lot of knowledge and experience for the next generation, so the elderly are considered as cultural assets, the elderly are the most precious national heritage.
"The Elderly is a living library that provides education, advice and good experiences for the younger generation," he added. And the elderly are also an important resource to contribute to the development of Cambodia to grow.
Due to the recognition of merits and the important role played by the Royal Government of Cambodia, led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, has always paid close attention to the well-being of the elderly.
The Association of the Elderly is an organization that aims to promote the well-being of the elderly through collective activities that benefit themselves and their communities.
The report of Mr. Leang Sophea, Department of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation of Kampong Thom Province confirmed that the Association of the Elderly in Kampong Thom Province has 81 communes, of which 8 are well-functioning associations with 2090 members, 1358 females.
The Ministry of Labor announces the results of the meeting of the National Minimum Wage Council, stating that all parties are mature and united, the meeting will continue tomorrow
(Phnom Penh): On Wednesday, September 9, 2020, the National Minimum Wage Council resumed its meeting to negotiate the minimum wage in the textile, garment and footwear sector in Cambodia for 2021. This is according to the announcement of the Ministry of Labor, which was received by Fresh News.
After the meeting, the Ministry of Labor claimed that as a result, each party presented the techniques of the seven criteria with maturity, brotherhood and solidarity.
Meanwhile, representatives of the workers 'side and employers' representatives also agreed to continue discussions at the National Minimum Wage Council meeting on September 10, 2020.
It should be noted that the Royal Government of Cambodia has set a policy to increase the minimum wage for garment workers every year since 2013. The minimum wage for workers in 2020 will increase to $ 190 per month, which in 2021 may increase some more.
