International tourists traveling to Cambodia must follow the following eight tips:
1. Follow the measures of the Royal Government of Cambodia: Always follow the measures of the Royal Government of Cambodia if you return from an infected area and check the Royal Government's advice on what to do when you arrive.
2. Seek medical advice: If you feel unwell, consult a specialist by calling 115.
5. Wash your hands: Good hygiene is the key to protection. So make sure you wash your hands regularly with soap and water or alcohol gel. Do not forget to cover your mouth and nose with a tissue or your sleeve when you cough or sneeze.
6. Share positive experiences: Use social media to share your positive travel stories.
7. Calm down: Be alert, but do not panic and wear a mask during your trip in a public place or gathering.
8. Please do not cancel your trip to Cambodia: You may consider delaying or changing your destination in Cambodia. Many airlines and hotels are waiving ticket and booking fees, offering a reservation policy to suit your needs.
