About the WHO Charter states that its primary goal is to "raise the standard of human health as high as possible." The main work of this organization is to fight against various diseases, especially major infectious diseases and to promote the general health of mankind.
As of 2020, the World Health Organization has a total of 194 member countries. The organization has an institution that decides whether a country should become a member or not, which is called the World Health Assembly.
"Countries are allowed to become members once their applications are approved by the World Health Assembly by a majority vote," according to the World Health Organization's website.
The charter of the World Health Organization also states that the purpose of the organization is to "achieve the highest possible level of health for all." The mission of the World Health Organization is to fight diseases, especially major infectious diseases, and to improve the overall health of people around the world.
How many millions of dollars does the WHO spend a year? Is there a clear document on how much the World Health Organization spends each year? However, the total health budget of the World Health Organization for 2018-2019 is approved at $ 4.4 billion.
It should be noted that in 2018, the total expenditure of the World Health Organization is $ 2.3 billion, a decrease of 4% compared to 2017.
According to the World Health Organization's website, which lists the countries that will donate to the organization by 2020, the top 10 countries are:
The United States in 2019 provided more than $ 400 million to the organization. However, in 2020, US President Donald Trump announced a cut in financial aid to the World Health Organization, claiming that it did not have the capacity to protect Americans from coronavirus.
