Mr. Malin said her message did not accuse the authorities of taking legal action as a violation of human rights, but only as a general principle of human rights that the government has an obligation to respect and fulfill to ensure that citizens can exercise their rights. Free and within the framework of the law, which the government has been adhering to and strictly enforced through the mechanism of strict law enforcement in the past.
Jean-Malin emphasized that the arrest of protesters was the only legal way to protect the accused in a democracy, the rule of law, rather than anarchic rallies, putting pressure on the government and the judiciary as independent institutions. To release or drop charges in violation of the Constitution, the principles of democracy, the rule of law and the separation of powers.
