Senior Minister Sun Chanthol: The Armed Forces Contribute to Maintaining Peace, Security and Social Order
(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, expressed his deep gratitude and appreciation to the Cambodian Armed Forces. The Senior Minister said that the Armed Forces has played an important role and contributed to maintaining peace, security and social order.
In gratitude for the sacrifices of the Armed Forces on the eve of Pchum Ben, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol brought some food and money to the border troops and the National Police Bodyguard Command this afternoon. On September 08, 202, it was also brought to the National Gendarmerie. According to the plan, Mr. Sun Chanthol will also bring food to the National Gendarmerie.
On the occasion of bringing gifts to General Sao Sokha, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Commander of the National Gendarmerie, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol emphasized the importance of peace and strong political stability under his leadership. Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
The Senior Minister said that it is this principle of peace that pushes Cambodia to develop and progress from the status of a country left over from the flames of war to a country full of beauty today. Peace has also boosted the Cambodian economy, maintaining an annual economic growth rate of around 7%.
Mr. Sun Chanthol stated that maintaining peace, security and social order is the main condition that we can work together to maintain the existing achievements of Cambodia and continue to promote development and expand new achievements. More. Mr. Sun Chanthol emphasized that all armed forces are important operators in maintaining peace, security and order.
The Minister of Public Works expressed his deep gratitude and thanks to all the Cambodian Armed Forces for sacrificing their happiness and making all kinds of sacrifices for the cause of society. In particular, maintaining the security, order and peace of Cambodia.
Please note that the gifts that the Senior Minister brought to the National Gendarmerie include: 200 cans of soy sauce, 200 cans of fish sauce, 500 cans of Cambodian pure water, 500 boxes of national noodles, 50 boxes of fish, 5 tons of rice and budget. Some. The book on "Building a Sustainable Financial Sector" to be compiled by the National Bank of Cambodia has been handed over to representatives of banking and financial institutions in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): A book on the history and development of the microfinance sector in Cambodia, "Building a Sustainable Financial Sector", to be compiled by the National Bank of Cambodia, is provided to representatives of banking and financial institutions in Cambodia.
The handing over of the History and Development Booklet of Microfinance Sector in Cambodia "Building a Sustainable Financial Sector" to the representatives of the Banking and Financial Institutions was made in the presence of Mr. Rath Sovannarak, Director General of the National Bank of Cambodia. Cambodia on September 08, 2020.
Please be informed that the book on the history and development of the microfinance sector in Cambodia "Building a sustainable financial sector" is a book describing the evolution of the microfinance sector in Cambodia, the purpose and causes of development from one stage to another. Composition of key stakeholders, the importance of microfinance and highlight the vision of the future of Cambodian microfinance in participating in the sustainable economic and social development of Cambodia.
Mr. Rath Sovannarak said that the Cambodian microfinance sector emerged in the 1980s after the fall of the genocidal regime of Pol Pot and continued to grow, especially after the peace of Cambodia. Complete through the win-win policy of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
Kea Boran, President of the Cambodian Microfinance Association, said that this book is an important work that serves as a reference document for the financial sector, focusing on the history and development of the microfinance sector in Cambodia for more than two decades. This book not only serves the interests of Cambodia, but also shares Cambodia's valuable financial experience to other parts of the world, especially to other developing countries.
Ron Bewak Kwa also presented an overview and findings in the book. He said that Cambodian microfinance is among the best microfinance systems in the world, so Cambodian microfinance should be taken care of and respected.
Japan and other Asian countries strengthen cooperation with Cambodia after EU suspends EBA
The Japanese Foreign Minister is the first foreign dignitary to pay an official visit to Cambodia at a time when the world is facing 19 cases of Kovid. The visit was not just to boost bilateral diplomatic ties and reflect solidarity in difficult times, the two sides exchanged views on a number of regional and international issues that serve strategic interests for both sides.
China's economic influence is steadily growing in the region and has now become Southeast Asia's leading trading force. China is the third largest source of investment in the region, having signed a free trade agreement with the Association of Southeast Asian Nations (ASEAN) since 2010 and is known as the largest economy under the agreement. Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership (RCEP)
China has been actively involved in ASEAN diplomatic activities since the early 1990s. China also has long-standing close ties with some countries in the region. For these reasons, prior to his visit to Phnom Penh, the Japanese Foreign Minister visited Laos and Myanmar, two other potential allies of Tokyo, to counter Chinese influence.
Mr Motegi made it clear to his Cambodian counterpart, Foreign Minister Prak Sokhon, that Cambodia was more important than ever to further strengthen the implementation of the "Free and Open Indo-Pacific" initiative, given the international situation. Rapid change is difficult to predict due to Kovid 19. The United States is also concerned about the growing influence of China.
The US policy towards Asia is carefully considered to double the influence of China, which is why the Donald Trump administration focuses on security and diplomacy, namely "rebalancing in Asia." And the deployment of troops in the south.
Cambodia has also expanded its international cultural diplomacy by hosting the Asian Cultural Council (ACC) in 2019 in Siem Reap. The international community highly values Cambodia for the protection, restoration and preservation of Khmer temples, which are priceless World Heritage Sites, including Angkor Wat and Preah Vihear.
