Pailin Provincial Governor Holds a Get-Together with Teachers and Students and Examines the Implementation of Sanitation Standards
Mr. Phan Chanthul said that the Ministry of Education has issued instructions to all educational institutions to pay attention to the implementation of hygiene rules and safety gaps in the classroom to prevent infections such as:
* First, before the opening of the school, both public and private educational institutions also carried out cleaning and disinfection activities in the school environment and in the classroom, preparing hand washing facilities and cleaning the bathroom.
* Second: Classes must be limited to no more than 20 students, ie from 15 to 20 students per class, and there must be an alternate analysis of direct attendance with teachers at the school. Keep distance learning (ONLINE) and for students at school requires a gap.
* Third: There must be a temperature measurement at the gate, spraying alcohol and washing hands before entering the classroom, and must prepare food packaging from home, the Ministry does not allow sales on campus outside the school fence. To reduce gatherings at the grocery store when out on vacation.
