Poipet Military Police Arrested for Stealing Motorbike, Pawn Money, Eating and Drinking
(Banteay Meanchey): A suspect who stole a motorbike, took it as a pawn and took all the money to drink was arrested by Poipet City Military Police led by Colonel Nuon Ninaro on September 7, 2020 in a rented room One place in Kbal Spean 1 village, Sangkat Poipet.
Colonel Nuon Ninaro said that the suspect, Narada alias Toeur, 31, stole the motorcycle of the victim, Chuon Sarith, 29, of Vall village, Kouk Romiet commune, Thmor Puok district, Banteay Meanchey province.
After his arrest, the suspect confessed that he had stolen a blue Honda motorcycle with no license plate, and after the action, he took 4,000 baht (about 500,000 riels) as collateral. And spend time with friends.
Now, after the interrogation, the specialized military force has contacted the motorcycle from the pawn shop to return it to its original owner, while the suspect has built a case to be sent to proceed with the procedure.
Minister of Commerce tells stakeholders to work together to sustain production and increase cassava exports
(Pailin): Cassava is a highly favorable crop for the people in Pailin province, which borders Thailand. The Minister of Commerce, Mr. Pan Sosak, instructed all trade officials and stakeholders in Pailin Province to work closely to maintain production sustainability and increase cassava exports.
The Minister of Commerce made this recommendation during a meeting with the Chamber of Commerce and Cassava Exporters Association in Pailin Province on September 7, 2020. The meeting was also attended by Mr. Phan Chanthul, Governor of Pailin Province, as well as relevant officials in some provinces.
The Minister of Commerce also advised the Exporters Association to contact the director of the provincial Department of Commerce to find a solution from the governor to help solve the problem of cassava products.
The Minister also encouraged all stakeholders to work together to strengthen the development of agro-commercial value chain of cassava products and help increase the quantity and quality of this product in the export market to another level. .
After the meeting, the Minister also visited CP Company and Pailin Longan Fruit Packing Company to learn more about the potential, hygiene standards and production line of the company.
According to the report, Pailin province has nearly 49 hectares of cassava plantations and an output of more than 1 million tons, of which 90% of the total output is exported to Thailand and Vietnam and 10% for domestic processing for export. . The potential point is that Pailin province has 16 warehouses and drying kilns, which can store more than 100,000 tons of dried cassava.
