Ministry of Health Receives 3,000 Kovid-19 Sample Collection Equipment to Strengthen Prevention Measures
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Health received 3,000 sets of Kovid-19 samples to help fight the Kovid-19 global epidemic from NagaWorld Charity Heart, a social work unit of NagaWorld on September 7. 2020.
"The situation of Kovid-19 in Cambodia is well controlled, but we must always be vigilant and follow the guidelines of the Ministry of Health to prevent this deadly disease," said Dr. Youk Sambath, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health.
Ms. Youk Sambath would like to express her deepest gratitude for the continued support of NagaWorld, which has provided many necessary facilities in the past. All of these facilities are critical to strengthening Kovid-19 prevention measures.
The storage tube is a tube used to collect and store samples containing viruses such as the Kovid-19 parasite, which is transmitted to humans through insects and mycoplasma. The tube is a plastic tube with a sealed lid and can be stored for 48 hours at room temperature in the refrigerator.
The sampling device is similar in shape to an earmold, with plastic straps of different sizes and shapes. Coverage-19 storage tubes and equipment enable the Ministry of Health to safely collect and screen for suspected Kovid-19 cases.
He said the devices allow front-line staff of the Ministry of Health to send samples quickly and safely for analysis using modern test machines. We continue to support the Ministry of Health in the fight against Kovid-19 virus.
It should be reminded that NagaWorld with a generous heart donated a total of 40,000 face masks, 4,000 bottles of hand wash gel and 720 liters of hand washing alcohol worth a total of 15,400 US dollars to the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction. National Police, Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports and Phnom Penh Capital Hall. Ms. Men Sam An calls on Buddhists to remain vigilant on Kovid-19
Kan Ben celebration is held from the 1st of Roach to the 15th of Roach, the date of which is considered to be the day of Pchum Ben. On that day, people, men, women, young and old, all over Cambodia came to celebrate at the pagoda with happy, fresh faces, full of faith in Buddhism, believe in sin, believe in karma. All of them have new and luxurious clothes.
Today, in every pagoda all over the country, there are devotees, devotees, and masses who make the atmosphere in the presence of solemnity, rejoicing, the sound of Pin Peat music or traditional music sounding beautiful, cool to the senses and very exciting.
The most important event of the day is the offering of yaku or breakfast, lunch to the monks, along with a large-scale ceremony. Monks, devotees, devotees, dedicate merits to the souls of former ancestors, grandparents, relatives, seven generations, and wish good luck to the descendants.
Mrs. Kittisangha Bandith also prayed for the blessings of the King, Queen Mother, Samdech Mey, Samdech Yeay, Samdech Yeay Tuot, Monineath Sihanouk and blessed all the monks and wished Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Samdech Distinguished Dr. Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, Senate Leaders, National Assembly Leaders, and the people throughout the country, may peace and prosperity be with you forever.
