(Phnom Penh): Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Economy and Finance and Chairman of the National Committee for Tourism Development, chaired an inter-ministerial meeting on September 7, 2020 to review and discuss the draft “Master Plan for Development”. Siem Reap Tourism (2020-2035).
The meeting was attended by Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism and Chairman of the Inter-Ministerial Commission for Study Planning, Siem Reap Tourism Development Master, Dr. Pheung Sakona, Minister of Culture and Fine Arts, Mr. Say Sam Al, Minister of Environment and Mr. and Mrs. Member of the National Committee for Tourism Development.
First, Siem Reap is an interesting and universally recognized international tourist province for the conservation and protection of cultural heritage and natural environment, providing tourism resources and many other attractions.
Second, to ensure the maximum socio-economic benefits of tourism, namely the historical area of Angkor, urban areas with the Siem Reap River, Tonle Sap, Phnom Kulen National Park and rural areas, which are tourist destinations must be linked to development. Local economy and poverty reduction.
Third, Siem Reap must be a quality tourist destination to attract quality tourists to visit again and again, stay longer and spend more, can increase income for local people and build a local economy with an environment.
To achieve the above vision, the "Siem Reap Tourism Development Master Plan (2020-2035)" sets out seven strategic goals, including:
The meeting reviewed and discussed the draft sub-decree on "Implementation of the Siem Reap Tourism Development Master Plan 2020-2035" and decided as follows:
First, support in principle on the "Siem Reap Tourism Development Master Plan 2020-2035" and appreciate the efforts of the team that prepared this plan.
Second, request to edit and reduce the detailed content by highlighting only the main strategic points so that the master plan has a short content but a clear goal in advance.
Third, request the relevant ministries and institutions, which are members of the inter-ministerial commission, to review in detail the relevant sections of their jurisdiction and send those sections to the commission working group to include in the master plan to ensure the effectiveness of Apply.
Fourth, it was decided to reconcile between the "Siem Reap Tourism Development Master Plan 2020-2035" and the "Siem Reap City Infrastructure Development Plan" which the Royal Government has already decided.
Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister and Chairman of the Meeting, also thanked and commended the Inter-Ministerial Commission and relevant ministries and institutions for their good cooperation in preparing this important document, which is the draft of this master plan. The meeting decided to reconvene at the end of October 2020 after the amendment before submitting to the Prime Minister for review and high decision.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol Asks Police to Continue Cooperation in Cracking Down on Illegal Car Processing Sites
(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, during a meeting with General Neth Savoeun, National Police Commissioner General, this morning, September 08, 2020, requested the National Police Force to continue to cooperate with the Department of Public Works. To inspect and crack down on illegal vehicle processing sites.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol emphasized that these illegal car recycling garages are also the cause of traffic accidents and overcrowding, so as to ensure traffic safety and prevent technically incorrect vehicles from driving on the road. Further must be applied from the beginning.
In the meeting, which was attended by many relevant police leaders, General Dr. Neth Savoeun gladly accepted the request and immediately ordered the 25 specialized departments of the Capital-Provinces to cooperate with the Department of Public Works. To inspect and crack down on illegal vehicle processing sites from the ground up.
General Neth Savoeun said, "For this request, the Capital-Provincial Commissioner, in cooperation with the Department of Public Works, should be his staff and shake his hand to do this (illegal car repair garage)." "We agree, under the leadership of Samdech Krala Hom, under the leadership of the Senior Minister, we are determined to remove it from the beginning, which means a place to repair, a place to process vehicles."
The General Commissioner of the National Police has ordered all provincial commissioners that this is not the time to educate the owners of unlicensed locations, but to enforce the law, and if the owners do not, they must do so. Detain the owner of the location to build a case to send to court.
In addition, General Neth Savoeun also requested Senior Minister Sun Chanthol to refer to the Capital-Provincial Public Works Department for specialists to manage and provide technical guidance to the garage location to reduce the risk. The general insists that this work must be a combination of public skills and forces in order to be successful.
It should be informed that Mr. Sun Chanthol, Senior Minister, Minister of Public Works and Transport, also expressed his commitment that the Ministry of Public Works will strengthen cooperation with relevant institutions to restrict garages for processing illegal vehicles and overweight vehicles. The main cause of traffic accidents and premature road damage successfully.
So far, it is observed that public officials and relevant authorities have been working together to carry out this work, and also inspected and closed a number of garages.
"We must work together to increase international cooperation and solidarity for our common benefit," he said.
Kovid 19 made the 41st ASEAN Inter-Parliamentary Assembly this year live on video. Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin praised the National Assembly of Vietnam for the good organization of the 41st General Assembly (AIPA), although AIPA could not meet in person.
The 4th ASEAN Inter-Parliamentary Assembly was held under the theme "Parliamentary Diplomacy to Achieve a Cohesive and Responsible ASEAN Community". Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin said that the following theme is very appropriate and reflects the need to achieve the building of the ASEAN Community with unity, solidarity and centrality to encourage ASEAN to seize opportunities and solve Ongoing challenges effectively.
He stressed that the National Assembly plays an important role in promoting the legitimacy of multilateral institutions, especially the establishment of ASEAN as an institution based on the rule of law and people-centered. "AIPA's spirit of friendship, solidarity and close cooperation has always existed under any circumstances."
The ASEAN Inter-Parliamentary Assembly (AIPA) is the inter-parliamentary body representing the legislatures of the Association of Southeast Asian Nations (ASEAN), which includes Brunei, Cambodia, Indonesia, Laos, Malaysia, Myanmar, Singapore, Thailand, Vietnam and the Philippines.
The ASEAN Inter-Parliamentary Assembly is a gathering of the voices of the people of the ASEAN Community, ASEAN's partners in advancing the goals of a single ASEAN Community. The ASEAN Inter-Parliamentary Assembly is held annually by the member countries in alphabetical order of the names of the countries in Latin letters.
The 41st ASEAN Inter-Parliamentary Assembly will be held from September 8 to 10. After the official opening ceremony, the General Assembly will hold several IPA expert committee meetings, such as the IPA Women's Committee Meeting, the IPA Youth Parliamentary Meeting, the Political Committee Meeting, and the Economic Affairs Committee Meeting. Meetings of the Social Affairs Committee and meetings of the Organizing Committee.
In a keynote address to the General Assembly, Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin stated that the Cambodian Parliament supports ASEAN's efforts to maintain and promote peace, security and stability in the region, the peaceful settlement of disputes based on the principles of international law and diplomatic mechanisms. Use of force.
At the same time, the Cambodian Parliament supports and encourages greater participation of young MPs in important IPA meetings and with ASEAN youth. Young people have played an important role in contributing to the development of the society as well as the process of building a progressive and prosperous ASEAN.
Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin also said that the fight against Kovid 19 requires a lot of money, equipment and manpower, what Cambodia can provide experience is to promote and inspire a culture of sharing, including sharing Public-private institutions to the people, sharing from development partners and NGOs to the people and sharing between the local people. This culture clearly shows the spirit of sharing, solidarity and national unity.
Battambang Provincial Administration, in collaboration with the Alliance of Small and Medium Enterprises Associations, held a workshop on building a successful business
(Battambang): Battambang Provincial Administration cooperated with the Coalition of Small and Medium Enterprises Association of Cambodia, Representative of the President of the Provincial Chamber of Commerce and President of the Coalition of Small and Medium Enterprises Association of Battambang Province to hold a workshop on "Successful Business Building This morning, September 8, 2020.
