Mr. Oknha hopes that the small and medium enterprises present in today's workshop will pay attention to listen to learn more new knowledge from the workshop and after receiving training in the program throughout the day. All small and medium enterprises will gain more new knowledge to strengthen their ability to develop their business even more.
Mr. Ty Tang Po continued that with the initiative of the Royal Government of Cambodia to establish a co-financing project for small and medium enterprises in Cambodia. The co-financing project is worth $ 100 million out of $ 50 million, with the participation of 33 microfinance institutions and another $ 50 million from small and medium enterprise banks. The funding project aims to address the challenges posed by the Kovid 19 crisis.
According to the report, the Cambodian SME sector is the backbone of national economic development, with the need for the head of the Royal Government and all relevant institutions to consider financial, technical and marketing considerations. Provide high quality products with low cost to easily compete in the international market. As a driving force to contribute to the growth of the national economy.
Minister of Public Works Meets Leaders of National Police
(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, met with senior police officers of the National Police General Commission led by General Neth Savoeun, National Police Commissioner General, on the morning of September 08, 2020. The meeting was held at the Ministry of Interior.
Speaking at the meeting, General Dr. Neth Savoeun also informed Senior Minister Sun Chanthol about the success of the four-month campaign to enforce the law on road traffic. The general stated that during the restriction period, there was a decrease in the number of traffic accidents, a decrease in the number of deaths and a decrease in the number of injuries on the roads.
The General Commissioner added that due to the peace factor during the Kan Ben festival, many people have been traveling to the pagodas across the country, and at the same time, officials from the Ministry of Public Works and police are also participating. Together to protect citizens and enforce traffic laws.
After presenting the achievements of the National Police Force, General Dr. Neth Savoeun considered the meeting between the leaders of the Ministry of Public Works and the leadership of the National Police General Commission as a warm gesture to continue to work together to serve the people. Traffic accident.
General Neth Savoeun also thanked Senior Minister Sun Chanthol for always providing material and financial support to the General Commission of the National Police, and the General was determined to continue to work together to implement the policies of the Royal Government under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
At the same time, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol also thanked the National Police Force throughout the country for safeguarding peace, security, order and territorial integrity of Cambodia.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol stated that this peace can create the opportunity for the Ministry of Public Works and Transport to have the opportunity to build infrastructure, and without peace and order, the Ministry has no opportunity to build infrastructure for the people.
In addition, the Senior Minister of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport also highlighted the many progress and achievements that the Ministry has achieved, especially in relation to the reform to become a modern system to keep up with the world's technology.
During the meeting, both Senior Minister Sun Chanthol and General Dr. Neth Savoeun raised their respective challenges and suggestions. The two leaders also accepted all the requests to forward to stakeholders to work together to reduce traffic accidents and reduce the number of deaths due to traffic accidents.
It should be informed that after the meeting, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol also handed over some gifts to the General Commission of the National Police, including speed control equipment and many other food items.
