Ms. Khuon Sodary tells the Women Parliamentary Committee of ASEAN Member States about the impact on women due to Kovid 19
(Phnom Penh): During the video meeting of the Women's Parliamentary Committee (WAIPA) on September 8, 2020, the Honorary Dr. Khuon Sodary, Second Vice President of the National Assembly, stated that 19 cases of Kovid have been severely affected. Women are workers in the textile, garment, footwear and tourism sectors.
The meeting was held under the theme "The role of women MPs in ensuring employment and income for women workers" with the participation of the First Vice President of the National Assembly of Vietnam and the Vice President of the National Assembly of the Philippines and members of the ASEAN Parliament. And a total of 60 technical officers.
The meeting discussed the role of women parliamentarians in promoting gender equality and women's empowerment in ASEAN, especially contributing to women's issues in the field of labor during the Kovid 19 pandemic crisis. Decrease in labor and income of workers.
Ms. Kittisangkhab Dr. Khuon Sodary, Second Vice President of the National Assembly, who led the delegation of the Cambodian Women's Parliament, said that the situation of Cambodian women workers in Cambodia is strongly affected by the epidemic crisis, with small and medium enterprises in Cambodia. 60% are owned or controlled by women. On the other hand, the textile and footwear industry, as well as tourism, accounts for 84% of the female workforce.
She also emphasized that the Royal Government of Cambodia has set out a number of mechanisms in response to this crisis, including:
* Cash program for the poor and vulnerable * Investment in skills development, women entrepreneurs and credit restructuring in priority areas * Provision of financial and technical support, including digital transformation to small enterprises Micro, small and medium enterprises develop modern agriculture and agro-industry, focusing on income generation, especially for rural women.
