General Seng Phally: According to the study, people's awareness of road safety is still limited
(Phnom Penh): General Prof. Dr. Seng Phally, President of the Police Academy of Cambodia, this morning, September 08, 2020, presided over the opening ceremony of a seminar to disseminate the results of a research study on "Effectiveness of Road Traffic Law Enforcement." Land in Phnom Penh.
The workshop was held at the University of Human Resources, Phnom Penh, with the participation of representatives of 14 government agencies and institutions, 1 NGO, Passenger Transport Association and Hun Da Company, as well as a total of about 100 participants.
Lt. Gen. Sen Satya, Director of the Police Science Research Institute of the Police Academy of Cambodia, said that the institute conducted a five-month study on the subject from the end of October 2019 to March 2020 and completed the writing. A final research report that needs to be published in this workshop.
On that occasion, General Prof. Dr. Seng Phally expressed his support and appreciation for the results of this study and stated that this research project has financial support from Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior. The Academy conducts scientific research to identify challenges and constraints and to develop timely and effective measures.
General Seng Phally added that the results of the study found that people's awareness of road safety is not yet widespread and most drivers are not yet involved in obeying the law and restrictions. Complaints about effective enforcement of road traffic laws are still low.
He added that the cooperation of stakeholders is still lacking in strengthening law enforcement, and resources to support the implementation of road safety management work is still lacking, which is the reason for efficiency. The implementation of the road traffic law in Phnom Penh is still limited.
At the same time, General Prof. Dr. Seng Phally added that the purpose and importance of this workshop are as follows:
Disseminate the results of the research on the topic "Effectiveness of law enforcement in Phnom Penh" to stakeholders
* Gather additional comments and input from stakeholders on intervention strategies as suggested in the research report
* Strengthen the relationship and cooperation on research between the Police Science Research Institute of the Police Academy of Cambodia with stakeholders and development partners; and
The results of the research will serve the stakeholders for better road safety management in Phnom Penh. "Bakong Phum Khnom" Tourism Community Development Project is committed to following the authorities' guidelines and contributing to the betterment of local economic development.
