(Pailin): The Minister of Commerce, Mr. Pan Sosak, instructed the officials of the Pailin Provincial Department of Commerce to make efforts to find markets for agricultural products as well as the products of the people in Pailin Province in response to the introduction of policies to promote the cultivation and raising of fish and meat. Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, in the context of the crisis caused by Kovid 19.
Mr. Pan Sosak introduced this during a meeting with officials of the Department of Commerce and Consumer Protection Branch of Competition and Anti-Fraud (PAC) in Pailin Province on September 7, 2020 yesterday. .
During the meeting, the Minister highlighted the Royal Government of Cambodia's efforts to address the social crisis caused by Kovid 19. Among the strategies and solutions to this crisis, Samdech Techo Hun Sen has encouraged the cultivation, promotion of crops and animal husbandry in order to increase the supply to meet local demand, ensure food security and improve people's livelihood.
