(Phnom Penh): Dr. Hang Chuon Naron, Minister of Education, Youth and Sports, on September 7, 2020, the first day of the reopening of the second phase of the school, called on the management, teachers and students. All adhere to the implementation of health safety measures to prevent the transmission of Kovid 19.
He also thanked the management of all public and private educational institutions for joining the Royal Government in the fight against Kovid 19 to ensure the safety of students, educators, parents and the community as a whole. .
"I would like to call on teachers to continue to follow the guidelines of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports in ensuring safety and hygiene standards. In particular, continue to train students to wash their hands often and follow the guidelines of the Royal Government.
Please be informed that according to Mr. Ros Sovacha, the spokesperson of the Ministry of Education, the first day of the process of reopening the school in the second phase went smoothly while the school management implemented the preparation well according to the Ministry's instructions.
According to Mr. Ros Sovacha, when the school reopened, parents prepared food and clean water for their children to take with them to ensure safety.
A spokesman for the Ministry of Education confirmed that public schools with ninth and twelfth grade students across the country will resume classes on September 7 for the second phase. The re-admission of students at all levels is only available in four provincial towns: Kratie, Stung Treng, Ratanakiri and Mondulkiri.
Mr. Ros Sovacha said that the reason why the Ministry decided to allow the four provinces to reopen schools at all levels was because the province had a low risk of contracting Kovid-19. In addition, the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports has continued to examine the possibility of opening public schools in other capitals and provinces on a small scale and alternately.
He added that in addition, about 300 private educational institutions from kindergarten to higher education have been reopening for the second phase from September 7, after the Ministry of Education directly inspected and evaluated. School location on the implementation of health safety measures.
He stressed that both public and private educational institutions have been rehabilitated in accordance with the guidelines and standard operating principles for reopening educational institutions in the context of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports. Samdech Chao Fea Veang Kong Sam Ol Kan Ben at Wat Kolampovan and Wat Peany, Kampong Tralach District, Kampong Chhnang Province
(Kampong Chhnang): Samdech Chao Fea Veang Kong Sam Ol, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister, Ministry of the Royal Palace and Member of Parliament for Kampong Chhnang Constituency, a great Buddhist, fulfilled his generosity during the 5th Kan Ben Ceremony at Wat Kolampoun (called Wat Takol) and Wat Peany In Peany commune, Kampong Tralach district, Kampong Chhnang province, on the morning of the 5th day of the month of Roach, in the year of Chuot Tosak BE 2564, which is on September 7, 2020.
