He also instructed all members to help educate the people to be very careful with their families, especially the elderly, young children when there is wind or rain, do not take shelter under the trees to find a safe place to avoid natural disasters such as lightning. The wind blows, trees fall, houses fall, etc. Be careful of health problems by eating clean, drinking clean, living clean.
Mr. Lang Saro urged parents to encourage their children to study hard, especially to stay away from drugs, to think about road safety, to avoid traffic accidents, to obey traffic laws, to wear helmets while driving, to drive at high speeds. Limit driving, do not overtake and do not drive under the influence of alcohol to protect our lives. In the promotion program, there is a procession by truck and by note.
