She also called on all people to participate in maintaining peace and development and to respect and strictly implement the principles of maintaining social gaps, maintaining good hygiene, along with measures as determined by the Ministry of Health. Extreme caution must be exercised to prevent and prevent the spread of the second wave of Kovid-19 while the world is facing an epidemic.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Kheang Puthy, Chairman of the Board of Directors of the Association of Real Estate Professionals, shared his knowledge on how to buy real estate properly to avoid future disputes that could lead to complications or even court.
1: Must buy real estate with a clear title (hard title). He explained that the title deed is a very important document for real estate buyers who are recognized by professional institutions and recognized by the authorities.
2. Payment must be clearly handed over or received by a lawyer, even if the buyer or seller is a known person, it must be done with confidence.
3: Must visit the real estate location directly to know the location to avoid problems in the future. For example, buying land here, but getting land elsewhere, which causes problems.
4: There must be a clear and accurate demarcation of real estate, so that there will be no uncertainty in the future.
