(Phnom Penh): General Mak Chito, Deputy Secretary General of the General Secretariat of the National Authority for Combating Drugs and Deputy Commissioner General of the National Police, said that the current drug crime is a large and complex drug crime. Need to jointly suppress and prevent.
This statement was made on the occasion of General Mak Chito opening a training course on drug control, drug investigation and money laundering at the National Police General Commission this morning, September 7, 2012. This 2020.
"Drug crime is now a major and complex drug crime, if not controlled, it is a major problem in the regional and global society," said General Mak Chito.
General Mak Chito added that all relevant authorities, especially the Anti-Drug Authority, must work together to crack down on and suppress drug offenses that cross the border into Cambodia in order to contribute more actively.
