According to Major General In Song, Deputy Director of the Department of Anti-Drug Crimes, from the beginning of the campaign from the beginning of 2017 until now, all relevant authorities have made efforts to research, investigate and crack down on drug offenses. The sharpest mind.
The Anti-Drug Department cracked down on 4,391 cases, arrested 7,439 people and seized 1,150 kilograms of drugs to build a case to send to court.
The Anti-Drug Department has cracked down on 180 major cases involving more than 1 kilogram of narcotics, arrested 87 ringleaders, 282 networks with a total of 1,936 substances. Kg.
In addition, 32 properties were frozen as a result of drug offenses. Minister of Commerce: Weekend Market helps promote and market products in the province
(Battambang): The Minister of Commerce, Mr. Pan Sosak, expressed his full satisfaction and support for the establishment of the "Weekend Market", which is an important contribution to help promote and sell products of the people.
On September 6, 2020, Minister Pan Sosak visited the weekend market in Battambang province. This weekend's visit to the market was also attended by Battambang Provincial Governor Nguon Rattanak and other relevant officials. The establishment of this weekend's market supports agro-commercial products grown and raised by farmers and put up for sale at this market.
"The sale of vegetables, chicken and meat at the market this weekend, in addition to providing additional income to farmers, also allows consumers to communicate directly with farmers and buy agricultural products with a clear source," he said. In the future, we want to see all of you become good farmers, successful entrepreneurs, more profitable business, more money. That is the main purpose of our project. ”
The weekend market is one of the main activities of the Small-Scale Market Promotion Project (AMS) and is one of the Ministry of Commerce's priority strategies to increase the value of agro-commercial products in the market. And to increase the income of smallholder farmers at the local level through agribusiness and market linkages within and outside the region.
To date, the AM project has launched a pilot market in 12 provinces. The first market to open is the weekend market in Siem Reap, opening on March 9, 2019 and has been selling well ever since. AM plans to continue to open similar markets in other target provinces and Phnom Penh in the near future.
Mr. Pan Sosak proposed and encouraged the project team of AM and each team of the Provincial Department of Commerce to work hard to help and coordinate to make the weekend market that is selling well and sustainable.
During a visit to the market yesterday weekend, the Minister called on farmers to cultivate agricultural production, including animal husbandry, rice production and other crops to increase supply to meet domestic demand. Both create markets for small farmers, which are opportunities for agriculture and markets.
