Tomorrow, some schools will reopen after 6 months
(Phnom Penh): After being closed for about 6 months due to Kovid 19 disease, some public and private educational institutions will reopen on Monday, September 7, 2020 tomorrow.
Public educational institutions that open their doors tomorrow for 21 capitals and provinces are open only for 9th and 12th grade. The other four provinces with a low risk of contracting Kovid 19 are Kratie, Stung Treng, Ratanakkiri and Mondulkiri.
In addition to public schools, 300 private schools from kindergarten to higher education will also reopen after the Ministry of Education inspects and evaluates the safety of school facilities.
The reopening of schools comes after the condition of 19 Kovid in Cambodia has improved, with almost all infected people being cured and no new cases. However, the reopening of schools still pays close attention to measures to prevent the transmission or transmission of Kovid 19 in the classroom.
The Ministry of Education has instructed all educational institutions to pay attention to the implementation of hygiene rules and safety gaps in the classroom to prevent infection. Prior to the opening of the school, public and private educational institutions also carried out cleaning and disinfection activities in the school environment and in the classroom.
Mr. Hang Chuon Naron, Minister of Education, Youth and Sports, in the previous instructions, instructed the management of educational institutions to follow the standard operating principles (SOP). In particular, strengthen the implementation of measures to prevent and respond to the spread of Kovid 19 disease of the Ministry of Health or can implement beyond the set standards.
According to the Ministry of Education, in order to prevent the spread of Kovid 19, the Ministry has set 20 to 25 students in the classroom (tables, chairs, chairs and teachers) to take turns to ensure safety gaps in the campus. Classrooms should not be below 24 degrees Celsius and have adequate ventilation and lighting.
All gatherings of no more than 50 people, apply temperature measurement to students, teachers and staff (not allowed to enter the campus in case of temperature above 37.5 degrees Celsius), apply masks or masks to students Teachers and staff on campus, set up health rooms and first aid kits, prepare hand sanitizers, alcohol, hand gel.
Design bathrooms and toilets according to the number of students, arrange the yard and entrance without congestion, no sale of food or cafeteria on campus, no student transport service, no sports Which leads to clashes, no entertainment activities or concerts.
Scholars, staff or family members who are foreigners who have entered Cambodia in the last 2 months are required to take the Kovid 19 test before being allowed to study and work in the institution.
Please be reminded that the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports decided to suspend all schools in Cambodia on March 16 to prevent the spread of Kovid 19. During the school closure, the Ministry of Education has introduced a variety of distance learning and online learning mechanisms for students.
