Join to save lives! Cambodian Blood Donation Association Donates Blood to National Blood Transfusion Center
(Phnom Penh): During this year's Kanben Pchum Ben season, the Cambodian Blood Donation Association has mobilized to donate blood to save the lives of people who need blood, especially women giving birth, traffic accidents and other patients who need blood urgently. Save lives.
Mr. Phat Saroeun, President of the Cambodian Blood Donation Association, said that in order to save the lives of people who need blood on the occasion of Pchum Ben, we have gathered nearly 50 people to donate blood at the National Blood Transfusion Center of Cambodia.
Mr. Phat Saroeun said, "The Cambodian Blood Donation Association always donates blood every year during the Pchum Ben season to save victims of other incidents and patients who need blood to save lives immediately. "Apart from the Pchum Ben holiday, it is Valentine's Day, June 14, World Blood Donation Day and other occasions."
The Cambodian Blood Donation Association has been donating blood since 2011, believing that donating blood does not affect our health, especially to help us be healthier and save lives for victims of accidents. Traffic, women giving birth and so on.
"In the future, we will continue to donate blood because it is a gesture to save a large human life to serve the society, especially the humanitarian sector," he said. "So we will increase the dissemination of information to the people."
At the same time, the President of the Blood Donation Association of Cambodia also appealed to all citizens aged 18 years, 60 years, 45 kilograms or more to donate blood at least once a year to save lives. We Cambodians need blood to live.
Please be informed that the President of the National Blood Transfusion Center, Dr. Sok Po, also confirmed in the past that blood can not be produced by any factory or pharmacy or any high-tech institute, blood can be dependent on human donations. The only source we can have enough blood from is humans.
Blood is a precious cell, so only human origin, if we do not have unity, love between our people, which is our national pride, help each other at that time, there can not be enough blood to supply blood.
According to experts, donating blood can not only save the lives of patients and society, but also benefit those who donate. Blood transfusions automatically increase the production of red blood cells in the human body.
In addition, donating blood can reduce the risk of heart disease because all blood transfusions reduce some of the iron in the blood.
