(Kampong Chhnang): Bamboo is a plant that is legally considered a non-timber forest product like rattan, and bamboo has provided a variety of benefits to thousands of palm trees, especially to serve the needs of the people. Our Cambodian farmers in Sre Chamkar district are indispensable from the past to the present.
For construction, such as huts or small houses in Sre Chamkar district, they can also use bamboo as a pillar, as a lizard, as a bed mat, as a locust, for sewing palm leaves, as a roof, as a roof and as other utensils. More according to the needs of our farmers to process for many other uses.
To date, according to research on various documents related to this bamboo plant, confirmed that bamboo can provide benefits to our society is in three parts.
As for the environmental benefits, it is not different from other types of forests, bamboo can create green forest cover, it can contribute to the reduction of climate change, it will be beneficial to participate in the absorption of carbon dioxide and Oxygen emissions for the weather In addition to all these benefits, other environmental benefits include: can protect the filter and can also be planted to withstand the sound of the storm.
In terms of economics, bamboo can provide all the benefits, both stems, leaves and vines, if we know how to process or manage a clear business, we will increase income well, and this bamboo tree is also easy to grow. . The economic benefits of processing this bamboo tree are more than three thousand, which can not be described.
In Cambodia, bamboo is grown and taken away for family use in the provinces, also contributing to the income of the people, such as vines, rattan and other types of wood.
So far, after conducting research in 2014 in our country, the collection of non-timber forest products from bamboo, there are about 321,000 families who benefit from bamboo, while our bamboo can grow in the provinces. There are more than 130,000 hectares, a decrease compared to between the 1950s and 1970s.
As for the bamboo species in Cambodia, we have up to 11 varieties and are currently cooperating with other countries to study other bamboo varieties that grow in the Cardamom Mountains, which have not been clearly named in Khmer. No.
Socially, we can grow bamboo as a garden or grow as a shade for sitting in tourist resorts, moreover, bamboo can also be used in the military, in the past, the history of the Longvek period. They planted wild bamboo trees as a fence to protect the barracks from being easily harassed by the enemy.
He also stated that bamboo has many benefits in terms of environment, economy and society, but is not interested in the Cambodian people, we can earn a lot of money if our people know how to process bamboo. From the benefits of this bamboo tree and also not difficult to grow and maintain.
In the industrial sector, bamboo can also be used to make the most important raw materials, such as processing into writing paper, which is the number one type, and can be used to make plywood, plywood, furniture. In the field of culture, bamboo can be used to make many kinds of musical instruments, such as flute, peronat and many other Khmer musical instruments.
