The ceremony was held at the headquarters of the 105th Border Guard Battalion stationed in Mom Bei area in Choam Ksan district, Preah Vihear province, with the participation of Mr. Ko Subunsoeut, Deputy Governor of Preah Vihear province.
Dr. Steng Sokhom also said that the establishment of sisterhood between ministries and institutions with all border units is a demonstration of the spirit of solidarity and shared culture between the front and rear battles under the common cause. Each is to maintain peace, political stability, public order and potential and sustainable development for today, tomorrow and the long future.
He also announced that he would continue to strengthen ties with the 395th Intervention Battalion under the 4th Army Division and the 105th Border Police Battalion.
Mr. Steng Sokhom also highlighted that "the army is the people's defense. Therefore, we must work together to maintain and implement the people's defense policy consistently. "Because the army is the children of the people and born of the people, so everything must be done in accordance with the interests of the people, to protect the interests of the people is to protect the legitimate government that emerges from the election." .
Mr. Sokhom added, "The army is at the heart of the people's path to democracy, and it is because of this people's defense that we have consistently been successful in thwarting attempts at a color revolution and preventing any aggression from Foreigners as well.
In front of the border guards, Dr. Steng Sokhom also highlighted the heroism of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, who bravely sacrificed to liberate and lead the construction of a proud Cambodia today.
He said, "We are all very proud that under the wise leadership of Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia, our country has achieved significant achievements. A lot. "Especially the peace and national unity that has not been seen in more than 500 years."
Mr. Steng Sokhom said that the win-win policy and the continued implementation of the four-phase rectangular strategy have enabled Cambodia to maintain an average economic growth rate of 7% per year for more than a decade, complete peace. Territorial unity, national unity, political stability, macroeconomic stability, sustainability of state institutions.
He said that the safety, security and good social order throughout the country are a testament to Cambodia's progress, starting from scratch and in the long, flexible and countless difficulties, and received acclaim and admiration. Recognize national and international centers as equals and equals in the journey towards achieving high middle income status by 2030 and becoming high income country by 2050.
