Spokesman for the General Commission: On September 5, another 1,198 vehicles were inspected and fined
According to the spokesperson of the General Commissioner, within 128 days of tightening the road traffic law by increasing the fine according to Sub-Decree No. 49, from May 1 to September 5, 2020, the traffic police throughout the country inspected And fined a total of 161,409 vehicles, including 119722 motorcycles and 41,687 vehicles of all types.
Notable offenses for motorcycles are mostly helmet offense, offense, no license plate and drunkenness. In particular, the offenses for cars are mostly speeding, overcrowding, no belts, offenses, no license plates, overweight, no driver's license, use the phone and so on.
Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun continued that for the past 128 days, the implementation of the new sub-decree to fine the offending vehicles has been going well. He thanked and commended all the road users for their good obedience to the traffic law so far, especially the traffic police for their dedication and hard work. Tighten traffic with the highest sense of responsibility.
Please note that for September 5, 2020, traffic accidents across Cambodia also occurred 6 times, in which 4 people died, 5 people were injured (4 seriously injured).
Ministry of Environment Presents Certificate of Environmental Peace to the First Nikrot One Pagoda in Cambodia for Participating in Environmental Sanitation
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Environment has awarded a certificate of environmental friendliness to Wat Nikrot One (Wat Koul Toteung), the first in the Kingdom of Cambodia to participate in maintaining good environmental hygiene.
The ceremony was presided over by Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Secretary of State and Spokesperson of the Ministry of Environment, on behalf of Mr. Say Sam Al, Minister of Environment, and was attended by leaders and officials of the Ministry of Environment, Ta Chi Yai Chi, on the afternoon of the 5th. September 2020 in the compound of Wat Nikrot One (Wat Koul Toteung) in Sangkat Prek Eang, Khan Chbar Ampov.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra said that Wat Nikrothavorn (Wat Koul Toteung) is really clean environment with a variety of trees that provide shade, a beautiful and quiet place for monks to study the Dharma. On the other hand, participating in protecting and cleaning up the environment is not anyone's obligation, it requires the participation of all to keep Cambodia clean and have a good and green environment.
The Secretary of State added that the pagoda is not only a place of worship, but also plays an important role in participating and promoting to Buddhists to practice environmental peace, as well as to educate people to love the environment and natural resources and to protect and Conservation of wildlife natural resources.
It should be noted that the ceremony of awarding the Certificate of Environmental Peace to Wat Nikrot One, the Ministry of Environment presented the monks with a water filter and two garbage bins. Wat Nikrot One has also already received an incinerator and a dump truck for transporting garbage.
Secretary of State for the Ministry of Environment Net Pheaktra encourages pagoda chiefs and pagoda management committees across the country to participate in environmental friendlies, especially during the Kan Ben and Pchum Ben festivals. Garbage needs to be properly organized and sorted.
Bhikkhu Vachirbanho Kou Sopheap expressed his gratitude to the Ministry of Environment, especially Minister Say Sam Al, for providing the current environmental friendship card, as well as sacrificing his physical and mental strength with officials of the Ministry of Environment to protect the environment and conserve natural resources, forests and animals. The forest is as good as it is today.
Wat Nikrothavorn (Wat Koul Toteung) has always contributed to the maintenance of environmental sanitation in the entire pagoda, as well as the management of environmental sanitation on a regular basis and the planting of trees for shade and provide a holy area for Even Buddhists.
At the same time, Mr. Neth Pheaktra also thanked Coca-Cola for supporting the distribution of waste bins and G Power Group for providing clean water filters. According to Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Coca-Cola has provided 170 bins for schools and pagodas in Phnom Penh, Sihanoukville and Oddar Meanchey.
At the same time, the Ministry of Environment has encouraged environmental friendliness by awarding certificates of environmental friendliness to individuals and legal entities who have participated in environmentally friendly activities, including: sanitation, waste disposal, tree planting, greening. Save water and energy resources, create green technology, etc.
