The keynote address by Samdech Techo, Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, was made via video during the UNIDO "Global Manufacturing and Industry Summit 2020 (GMIS 2020)" held in Geneva, Switzerland on the 5th. This September 2020. The meeting was held under the theme "Restoring Prosperity in a Post-Epidemic World".
Samdech Techo said that economic and social activities in almost all sectors were severely affected. In particular, through measures to prevent the spread of the disease, which are imposed by the governments of each country, such as country closures and travel restrictions.
The head of the Royal Government also said that in this context, global social life is expected to change structure or reach a new normal (New Normal), including: changes in the global economic structure, such as Declining global value chains and global production chains, declining global capital flows due to declining investment demand and declining human flows, declining global productivity and rising social inequality.
In addition, Kovid 19 has seriously affected the development and implementation of industrial and digital economic policies in the context of the fourth industrial revolution of developing countries, especially the least developed ones.
Cambodia is considered to be a country that has put in place better measures to prevent the spread of Kovid 19. To date, Cambodia has identified a total of 274 Kovid 19 cases. Of those, 272 were treated, while only two were being treated and none died.
In addition to expressing interest in the effects caused by Kovid 19, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also shared his experience in preventing and combating Kovid 19, as well as setting out measures to address the problem. Occurs socially and economically during the spread of Kovid 19.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized that the Royal Government has effectively controlled the situation of Kovid 19, so far Cambodia has not been infected as a community and has not reached the closure of the region or the country as a whole.
Samdech Techo added that, in fact, Kovid 19 has brought some serious challenges, especially in the textile, tourism, aviation and service sectors. In this situation, the Royal Government of Cambodia has already set out five rounds of measures to help maintain the balance of production and business for both domestic and foreign supply, especially to ensure the stability of the lives of people who are severely affected.
(Preah Sihanouk): Mr. Say Sam Al, Minister of Environment and Chairman of the Royal Government Working Group visited Preah Sihanouk Province, urged relevant officials to work together to solve the remaining challenges for the people well. In particular, the provision of more effective public services to citizens aims to make people trust and support the policies of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
Mr. Say Sam Al made some key recommendations to Preah Sihanouk Provincial Administration, National Working Group, Departments and Local Officials:
Many leaders of the member countries are allowed to give keynote speeches, share experiences in each country, as a result of crisis resolution and post-crisis manufacturing and industrialization.
The Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen was also given a keynote address at the meeting to share experiences and measures taken by the Royal Government of Cambodia to intervene and manage the socio-economic impact of Kovid. 19 as well as a number of specific policies aimed at restoring production and industry status after the decline and extinction of Kovid-19 in the near future.
