A road donated by philanthropists was built in Po Sen Chey district to facilitate the travel of villagers on the occasion of Pchum Ben
(Phnom Penh): Two philanthropists, Major General Sok Sokunthea, Deputy Director General of the Prison, together with Mr. Taing Kim Srun, spent their own money to help build a road in Trapeang Romchek Village, Sangkat Choam Chao I, Khan Por Sen Chey, Phnom Penh.
Currently, the road, which is more than 1 km long, is badly damaged, has many potholes, and is flooded, muddy, slippery and very difficult to travel.
Seeing this difficulty, the two philanthropists helped to build to facilitate the people, especially grandparents to travel to the festival on the occasion of Pchum Ben, this national tradition easily.
In the morning of September 5, 2020, the construction of this road was started and started to be completed soon, which was presided over by Mr. Hem Darith, Governor of Por Sen Chey District.
Also present were Mr. Choam Chao I, Major General Sok Sokunthea and Mr. Tang Kim Srun, who were philanthropists, as well as village authorities and villagers.
On that occasion, Mr. Hem Darith thanked the two philanthropists who have contributed to the local development of Po Sen Chey district, as now, after seeing the difficulties of the people to travel due to the damaged road. Helped build.
He said that this is a humanitarian gesture that has made it easier for the people in the village to travel on the occasion of Pchum Ben, as well as after Pchum Ben forever.
Lt. Gen. Sok Sokunthea and Taing Kim Srun said that the 1,000-meter-long dirt road will be built by pouring tamarind soil and compacted concrete and it is not yet known how many cars it will cost. No, but about 500 cars.
He said that the two of them helped to build this road is to alleviate the hardships of the people, grandparents traveled to other pagodas during the Pchum Ben festival and also want to participate in the development of Po Sen Chey district. .
