The Royal Government of Cambodia has been encouraging the investment of more plantations to create greenery and create a source of wood for sustainable use, to participate in the preservation of the environment and the conservation of natural resources.
The spokesman for the Ministry of Environment said that the investment in plantations will help reduce the import of processed wood raw materials from abroad and create a sustainable source of wood for use.
According to the same data, processed wood products made in Cambodia are exported to the United States and the European Union. Processing companies welcome the project of planting wood for processing, because if there are more raw materials for processing wood in the country will reduce the import of processed wood from abroad, and the company is ready to buy for processing.
The development of plantations is valuable in supplying wood raw materials for the wood processing industry, while construction in Cambodia has been growing and growing, especially in Phnom Penh and Sihanoukville, where many new building projects Happens.
Currently, due to insufficient domestic production, Cambodia also imports processed wood from abroad. Plantation plantations provide benefits for many people in the process of planting and harvesting as well as processing. As in Vietnam, where they plant plantations, they export to Europe, earning billions of dollars a year and creating a lot of jobs for the people.
In addition, Sing Bay Otec has received the proper permission from the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries to clear all areas of degraded forest within the size of the land used for plantation. Serves in the industrial sector and the company pays royalties and non-timber forest product premiums from clearing land, extension stations and reforestation in its various sub-regions in accordance with the law.
Mr. San Sok Heang said that in the next five years, from 2019 to 2024, Think Bio-Tech plans to plant more than 30 million seedlings to meet the needs of the market. In the wood processing industry that Cambodia is currently in great demand, especially in the construction sector, which is in great need of wood processing to serve the construction of various structures that are growing in Phnom Penh, Sihanoukville and so on.
Ministry of Environment Spokesman: Cambodia has been taking steps on the plantation industry to boost the economy and conserve natural resources.
Dara Chan Beach is getting a lot of attention from customers with unprecedented repurchase terms
(Phnom Penh): Investing in real estate, although very profitable and fast, but also high risk, before deciding to buy a house, condo or any type of property, you need to be very careful and think carefully about the important points.
The key to high reliability at Darachan Beach is the very favorable and low risk investment options, which are rare investment opportunities that you can not overlook.
Dara Chan Beach offers a choice of 6 types of villas and bungalows from 1 bedroom to 3 bedrooms ranging in size from 35 square meters to 302 square meters. The houses in this project can be beautifully designed, which can be used as a permanent residence, a vacation home or for monthly income with a reasonable starting price of only $ 56,320.
Especially for customers who make a reservation or buy a house in the Dara Chan Beach project, now the project owner will provide a buyback guarantee after 2 years and 4 years (from the date of delivery), that is, give you a choice To sell the house back to the project owner at the original price (after 2 years) or 1.2 times the original price (after 4 years).
This means that after use and dissatisfaction, you can resell without losing money and even have a 20% chance of profit after 4 years. This special feature has made the Dara Chan Beach project very attractive to local and international clients, so hurry up so as not to miss this rare opportunity.
Dara Chan Beach is a cultural and ecological paradise along the coast, located in Botum Sakor District, Koh Kong Province. Dara Chan Beach is part of the development of the giant resort city of Darasakor, which covers an area of 360 square kilometers and a beautiful beach of 90 kilometers.
The entire project covers multi-sectoral economic zones, including tourism, air transport, industrial parks, agriculture, culture and health. To date, a 300-kilometer road network has been completed, including six expressways connecting the oceans to the outside world.
Other infrastructure such as ports (20,000 tons), reservoirs, water treatment plants, power plants, five-star hotels, international standard golf clubs and tropical nature resorts are also important parts of the project, and what a wonderful thing. Most notably, Darasakor International Airport, which will be officially opened at the end of 2020.
In terms of the Darachan Beach project, the project has a total development area of 4.5 million square meters, covering an area of 20 square kilometers, which includes private residences, five-star hotels and coastal ecological resorts. Dara Chan Beach has officially started the first phase of development project, which is expected to be completed by 2021.
In this initial phase, the developer is focusing on the construction of private residences covering an area of 170,000 square meters, with a choice of villas and bungalows as described above.
In addition to the benefits of the rental guarantee from the project owner, customers who buy a house in Dara Chan Beach will become a permanent member of Dara Sakor Vacation Resort.
