(Phnom Penh): With the belief that "ghosts die and can be resurrected", former lawmakers and senior officials of the party that was dissolved by the court have started to apply for political rights again.
Son Chhay, a former Phnom Penh constituency lawmaker, and two other former party officials, Tan Kimchhorn and Wasamon, have been reinstated by a royal decree dated September 3, at the request of They asked. This is the resurgence of the second wave of political activism after a lull for a while under the political pressure of the extremist party.
The revival is likely to be large-scale because, according to sources obtained by cafe politicians, former lawmakers and other former CNRP officials are also preparing to run for office. Coming back soon.
At the same time, they are preparing to form a new opposition party that is no longer dependent on Sam Rainsy. By the way, at the moment, Sam Rainsy is left with only his body and a handful of monkeys, all of whom are convicted and have an arrest warrant. And besides, they have been running away from this cowardly party leader.
There are many reasons why former lawmakers and senior former opposition officials have left Sam Rainsy and returned to politics:
Reason 2: In anticipation of the popularity of the government of Prime Minister Hun Sen, the opposition led by Sam Rainsy became weaker and weaker from year to year due to internal divisions and due to The political weakness of Sam Rainsy, which made all his plans fail.
Sam Rainsy's last and most embarrassing defeat was his plan to return home on November 9, 2019. It can be said that this failure caused Sam Rainsy to lose his credit or, in other words, to lose completely. Body.
Reason 3: The expectation of the international community to intervene to resurrect the dead party according to Sam Rainsy's propaganda is gone.
Reason 4: The time for elections at both the local and national levels is approaching. So "waiting for the dead and the resurrected is no different than waiting for the rain to fall in the middle of the month." And if they did, it would be too late.
Do not forget that they have to wait five years for an election. Therefore, the failure to participate in the 2022 commune elections and the upcoming 2023 parliamentary elections equals almost 10 years since the dissolution of the extremist opposition party.
These are the reasons why former lawmakers and high-ranking officials, including former opposition activists, decided to abandon Sam Rainsy and return to politics at will and in his own way.
Continuing political life in a legitimate political arena by re-applying for political rights by freeing oneself from the pressures of painted politics is a wise and full of opportunity. On the contrary, continuing under the political pressure of Sam Rainsy is no different than burning opportunities for yourself in vain, because "ghosts can not be resurrected."
