Mr. Neth Pheaktra: Natural Resource Protected Areas are responsible for conservation by the relevant authorities and take action against all natural resource crimes
(Kratie): Speaking to the media during a visit to Prey Lang area in Kratie province on September 4, 2020, Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Secretary of State and spokesman of the Ministry of Environment confirmed that the Ministry of Environment The relevant authorities continue to implement the measures to protect and conserve the protected areas they manage responsibly and take action on all natural resource crimes that occur.
In the first six months of 2020 alone, from January to June 2020, the Ministry of Environment rangers patrolled 13,804 times and cracked down on crime, according to a senior official of the Ministry of Environment. 3,689 cases, of which 329 cases were sent to court, 2,578 chainsaws were confiscated, and 433 cases were fined.
Despite efforts to protect natural resources from park officials and relevant authorities, Mr. Pheaktra, on behalf of the Ministry of Environment, acknowledges that small-scale natural resource crimes continue to occur. However, the authorities of the Ministry of Environment will continue to cooperate with the relevant authorities to continue to crack down and prevent the number to decrease.
