(Japan): Located in East Asia, Japan is known as one of the countries with the most frequent natural disasters in the world, including 1,500 small earthquakes and volcanic eruptions, hurricanes. Floods and other natural disasters strike the island nation every year.
The islands are located in the subcontinent below the Pacific Ocean and have been active since hundreds of millions of years ago. As the magma in the Earth's crust moves, it causes seismic waves beneath the seabed, and in the ocean floor, there is also a seismic movement that causes giant waves to collide with Japanese islands.
Results of the Cabinet Meeting on September 4
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, this morning, September 4, 2020, chaired a meeting of the Council of Ministers. The meeting reviewed and approved the draft law on securities and the draft law on the organization and functioning of the Non-Banking Financial Services Authority.
During the meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also announced the release of US $ 100 million to US $ 150 million for 38 road construction projects in Siem Reap to help improve Siem Reap city infrastructure, create jobs and improve livelihoods. People boost tourism and national economy after Kovid-19 crisis.
The Prime Minister stressed that the project to improve road infrastructure in Siem Reap will be completed by the end of 2021 and will make tourists more proud of Cambodia's historical and cultural heritage in this wonderful land. Proud of the development of physical infrastructure in Siem Reap.
The Prime Minister also thanked all ministries, institutions and sub-national administrations for their efforts to save money during the Kovid-19 epidemic phase, which saved Cambodia more than 600 million US dollars. In addition to national development.
Samdech Techo stated that Cambodia needs to develop its economy to keep pace with the situation by promoting the implementation of bilateral or multilateral trade agreements and must strive to export the products produced to those markets and continue to negotiate and reach an agreement. Trade agreements with new partners to enhance the economic and political relations of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
The Prime Minister also stressed that in the current phase of the Kovid-19 crisis, Cambodia needs to increase its competitive advantage in boosting food exports, especially rice exports to foreign markets, with the annual rice surplus that Cambodia has achieved.
