(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Health on September 5, 2020 issued a press release on facilitating Muslims to practice their religious activities in mosques and mosques in stages from September 11, 2020. 2020 onwards.
A press release obtained by Fresh News from the Ministry of Health also recommends that worship services in mosques and mosques in which Muslims live in permanent villages be adhered to in accordance with the Ministry of Health's rules:
* Second: Muslims must take the rug from home for personal use.
* Fourth: It is forbidden to shake hands during salutation, instead of raising hands and saying Islamic greetings, and break up immediately after the end of worship for about 20-30 minutes.
* Fifth: Friday worship meeting is a short prayer of no more than 30 minutes.
* Sixth: Social distance must be maintained by allowing worship at about 30% of the capacity of each church location.
The Ministry of Health also stressed that Islamic leaders should start implementing this first step on Friday, September 11, 2020, due to the four-Friday trial, and then start worshiping in Sora, implementing health protection measures. Of the Ministry of Health always.
The Islamic Council must monitor the implementation of this launch as thoroughly as possible. In the event of a problem with suspected Kovid-19 disease, each church leadership should immediately report it to the nearest local authority or health center.
