Mr. Seang Nam thanked Samdech Techo Hun Sen for dropping the road construction budget in Siem Reap
(Phnom Penh): The announcement of the dropping of the national budget between 100 and 150 million US dollars from the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, for the construction and improvement of 38 roads in Siem Reap, is a great congratulations for the people in the province. Siem Reap speaks for itself and for the Cambodian people as a whole.
Duke Seang Nam, Member of Parliament for Siem Reap Province and also a citizen of Siem Reap Province, through Fresh News, expressed his congratulations and happiness for this news. On his own behalf, as well as the people of Siem Reap, Mr. Sieng Nam expressed his deepest gratitude to the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
Mr. Sieng Nam said that Samdech Techo's high decision will promote the development of infrastructure in the province to improve the beauty of Siem Reap. In particular, it has greatly contributed to the potential of tourism and investment business in Siem Reap, better for tourists and people living in Siem Reap.
It should be noted that in the meeting of the Council of Ministers on the morning of September 4, 2020, Samdech Techo Hun Sen announced the reduction of the national budget between 100 to 150 million US dollars to build and improve 38 roads in Siem Reap.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized that the decision to build 38 roads in Siem Reap is not only an improvement of the infrastructure system in Siem Reap, a famous tourist city of Cambodia, but also a contribution. Provide employment to the people during the 19-crisis Kovid crisis as well.
The Prime Minister also expressed the hope that the people of Siem Reap will open up the space to facilitate the construction of these roads, like the people in Sihanoukville. Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that people in Sihanoukville were hungry for the road and cooperated with the authorities without demanding compensation for the impact.
Along with announcing the budget reduction for road construction in Siem Reap, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also stated that although Cambodia suffered from the Kovid 19 crisis, it did not interfere with the infrastructure project.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also thanked all the ministries and institutions that contributed to saving Cambodia more than 600 million dollars to develop the country.
Battambang provincial officials found 147 kilograms of defective goods at a mall in Battambang city
(Battambang): On September 4, 2020, Battambang Provincial Anti-Consumer Protection and Anti-Fraud Branch Officers (Battambang) cooperated with officials from the Department of Commerce and local authorities to inspect the products. A display at an apartment supermarket in Battambang City found 147 kilograms of expired and stored goods for later incineration.
Mr. Branch President confirmed that in order to prevent the sale of defective goods during Pchum Ben and Kan Ben this year, professional officers went to various targets to monitor the sales of vendors just found and confiscated to store branches Discard later.
At the same time, Mr. Hak Sokrin also called on traders to prevent and not sell counterfeit goods or food containing illegal banned chemicals, because it causes harm to the health of consumers and disseminate through education. Directly or by sticker at the point of sale.
ASEAN is accelerating the implementation of new online tourism skills training projects
"ASEAN is accelerating the implementation of the new ASEAN Tourism Skills Training Scheme," he said. Revitalization of the sector is a key priority in the Association of Southeast Asian Nations to ensure that tourism remains a source of revenue for the national economy and a major source of employment.
He argued that in the current context, tourism needs to play an even more urgent role than ever before in bringing the region back to normal, at least by facilitating some necessary business trips and restoring confidence. You travel again.
Please be reminded that the ASEAN Tourism Professionals Agreement (MRA) Conference is held every two years, the first in 2016 in Indonesia and the second in 2018 in Cambodia.
