MOSCOW (Reuters) - Russia's Federal Security Service (FSB) on Friday arrested 13 Russians on suspicion of plotting a massacre with explosives and other weapons. This was released by the Xinhua News Agency on Friday evening, September 4, 2020.
The FSB said in a statement that 11 of the 13 suspects were operating through a secret network. The suspects were arrested at their home and authorities confiscated records of the attack plan and some communication devices. Russian authorities have not yet confirmed the whereabouts of the suspects, while interrogations and investigations are ongoing.
Prey Veng Provincial Governor Meets Representatives of 19 Schools in Prey Veng City
(Prey Veng): Mr. Chea Somethy, Governor of Prey Veng Province and Deputy Provincial Governor and his colleagues on September 4, 2020, met with representatives of 19 schools in Prey Veng City and donated sanitary ware as instructed by the Ministry of Health during When reopening schools in Prey Veng to facilitate the management of hygiene measures.
Mr. Chea Somethy expressed his appreciation, congratulations and appreciation for the efforts to strictly implement the guidelines of the Ministry of Health of Cambodia and would like to continue to work together to develop the education sector in the province, focusing on Improve the quality of education and effective school management during the current reopening of schools.
The provincial governor stressed that teachers must work hard to train more students to improve the quality of education to contribute to the development of the country in all areas, especially to guide students to pay attention. Take care to clean regularly, wash your hands with soap and alcohol to avoid Kovid 19.
Mr. Chea Somethy also donated 50,000 Riels and some hygiene items to the teachers representing 19 schools in Prey Veng City. Siem Reap Governor Releases Letter of Thanks to Samdech Techo Hun Sen for Providing $ 150 Million for Road Construction in Siem Reap
(Siem Reap): Mr. Tea Seiha, Governor of Siem Reap Province, on September 4, 2020, issued a letter of thanks to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, for announcing a decision to provide a budget of $ 150 million for road construction in Siem Reap.
Please be informed that in the meeting of the Council of Ministers on the morning of September 4, 2020, Samdech Techo Hun Sen announced the release of the national budget of 150 million US dollars to build roads in Siem Reap.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen pointed out that there are 38 small and large roads planned to be built in the provincial town. Samdech Techo said that the construction of these roads will improve the living standards of the people and will boost the national economic growth after Kovid 19.
Samdech Techo announced that Samdech will open the construction office directly. The Prime Minister expressed hope that by the end of 2021, Siem Reap, Cambodia's famous tourist city, will have a better infrastructure system.
The Prime Minister thanked all the ministries and institutions for saving and not wasting Cambodia to save more than 600 million dollars to develop the country. Minister Chea Van Det advises students who receive scholarships to study in France to strive to return to help develop digital technology in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Chea Van Det, Minister of Posts and Telecommunications, on September 3, 2020, allowed six Cambodian students who received scholarships to continue their studies in France in 2020 to pay a courtesy call.
The six students will study for a master's degree at a prestigious state university in France in data science, information technology, telecommunications, artificial intelligence and computer language technology.
Speaking at the ceremony, the Minister congratulated the six students who received scholarships to study in France in 2020.
The Minister instructed all students to be well-prepared, to focus on learning well and to do a lot of research, because learning, even learning for life, is not complete.
The Minister expressed his support and look forward to welcoming the winners back to work at the Ministry and the NIPTICT National Institute after graduation to contribute to the development of digital technology in Cambodia.
The Minister also shared with the graduating students his personal experience as a young Cambodian who had gone through the stages of leaving his family and homeland to study abroad for nearly 10 years. Year from Bachelor to Doctor.
It should be noted that the scholarships for the above six winning students were selected through a mechanism organized by the French Embassy and funded partly by the French Government and partly by the Capacity Building, Research and Development (CBRD), Telecommunications and ICT of the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications.
