This baking skill training program is the third generation training which was conducted under the chairmanship of Mr. Pak Sokhom, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Tourism on September 4, 2020 and with the participation of the director of the company, the president of the Cambodian Chefs Association A total of 300 participants.
On that occasion, Mr. Pak Sokhom highly appreciated Dav the Cake Company for its efforts in contributing to the organization of this third generation baking training course, which has actively contributed to the development of human resources in the tourism sector, especially to supply Services in the field of baking.
He added that this baking skill is also a tourism profession recognized by ASEAN within the framework of the implementation of the Mutual Recognition Agreement on ASEAN Tourism Professionals, and in the past, the Ministry of Tourism has started to implement this program. Tourism vocational training schools across the country are also ready.
Mr. Song Teng, President of the Cambodian Chefs Association, expressed his optimism about the baking skills training program and supported the Ministry of Tourism's cooperation with Dav the Cake. The above training program and plan to organize ASEAN level training program as well as baking skills competition.
Secretary of State Pak Sokhom observed the training of the trainees and instructed the trainees to pay attention to study and absorb the knowledge from the trainers to strengthen their capacity and to get job opportunities and establish their own bakery business to day. The future.
For the training program, he also encouraged the implementation of safety measures that have been put in place, especially during training to prevent the transmission of Kovid-19 virus. Cambodia, US vow to continue boosting trade and investment, especially e-commerce (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Cambodia and US vow to continue to boost trade and investment, especially e-commerce Even better.
The commitment was made during a working meeting between Commerce Minister Pan Sosak and US Ambassador to Cambodia W. Patrick Murphy on September 3, 2020. According to the Ministry of Commerce, the meeting focused on strengthening bilateral trade and investment relations between the two countries.
During the meeting, Mr. Pan Sosak mentioned the potential of bilateral trade between Cambodia and the United States, which increased from 3.3 billion US dollars in 2018 to 4.7 billion US dollars in 2019 at an increase rate of 42 Percentage.
The Minister also mentioned the progress of the Royal Government of Cambodia's deepening reforms, both within the institutional and legal framework, which ensures a better business and investment environment in Cambodia.
On this occasion, Minister Pan Sosak also briefed the Ambassador on cooperation within the framework of the Cambodia-US Joint Trade and Investment Council (TIFA).
The Minister also highlighted the entry into force of the e-commerce law and the establishment of relevant sub-decrees and regulations, and requested the US side to continue to encourage its investors to do business and invest in e-commerce. More.
Mr. Pan Sosak and the US Ambassador expressed optimism on the cooperation between the two countries. Especially in the field of trade and investment, and agreed to hold the 6th Cambodia-US Joint Council on Trade and Investment Framework through the upcoming Video Conference on the actual situation.
During the celebration of trade and investment relations between Cambodia and the United States on September 3, the Ambassador confirmed that economic relations are growing with the entry of new US products and investors. Come to the Cambodian market from year to year.
Patrick Muffy said American companies are bringing transparent and high-quality investment with world-class technology and training programs with high standards of work and the environment that promotes economic growth for all.
The US Ambassador also pointed out that trade in thousands of goods between the United States and Cambodia creates more jobs for workers and more options for customers in both countries.
