Nearly 800 public schools in Kampong Thom province are ready to reopen on September 7
(Kampong Thom): Following the instruction of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports on the reopening of the second phase, Mr. Tan Bun Hong, Director of the Department of Education, Youth and Sports of Kampong Thom Province on September 3, 2020 said that next week From September 7, 2020, nearly 800 public schools in the province will reopen.
According to the director of the department, out of 789 public public schools in Kampong Thom province, there are 207 kindergartens, 490 primary schools and 92 secondary schools.
With the re-enrollment, the director of the department instructed all schools to follow the Ministry of Health's guidelines on standard operating principles for reopening schools in the context of Kovid-19 disease. Each school in shifts and groups should not have more than 200 students and must have some equipment ready, such as hand washing facilities, masks, water, alcohol, soap and so on.
The principal said that each school has now cooperated with the relevant professional institutions to clean the classrooms before starting to allow students to re-enter the school and have ready to wash their hands with alcohol. Thermometers, all of which come at the expense of the school, the community, and alumni.
At the same time, the principal appealed to all parents and guardians of students to support their children with food and clean water, because the Ministry of Education does not allow the sale of food in schools.
At the same time, teachers called on parents to help encourage their children to study hard. Responding to the announcement of the Ministry of Education, students are happy to be back in school.
According to the spokesperson of the Ministry of Education, for the ninth and twelfth grade students who will be completing the program, there will be no major vacation and will be ready for the national exam on November 30 for the grade. 9th and 21st December for 12th grade.
It should be reminded that the Royal Government announced the closure of all schools across the country on March 14 due to the Kovid-19 crisis. After Kovid-19's condition improved, the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports issued a series of notifications on the reopening of schools in three phases, including: Phase 1, schools with high safety standards, Phase 2, schools with medium standards. And the third stage, the school has a minimum standard.
