Phnom Penh Capital Administration plans to open the construction site of a new boulevard 30 meters wide and more than 5 kilometers long from Street 1003 to Victory Blvd (in front of Grand Phnom Penh)
(Phnom Penh): In order to reduce traffic congestion in Khan Sen Sok, Khan Russey Keo and Khan Prek Pnov, the Phnom Penh Municipal Administration plans to open the construction site of a new boulevard with a width of 30 meters and a length of more than 5 kilometers, starting from Street 1003. The road turns into Aeon Mall Sen Sok, parallel to the main canal north of Phnom Penh until Victory Blvd. in Russey Keo district connects to Khan Prek Pnov (in front of Grand Phnom Penh).
Mr. Sam Piseth confirmed that if there is no change at the beginning of next week, Mr. Khuong Sreng will preside over the groundbreaking ceremony and the construction will be completed in six months.
Upon completion, this section of the boulevard will reduce traffic congestion in the northern part of Phnom Penh, parallel to the main canal north of Phnom Penh, from Street 1003 (the turn to enter Aeon Mall Sen Sok) to Channa Chhnang Boulevard in Khan Russey Keo.
