Spokesman for the General Commission: On September 4, another 1093 vehicles were inspected and fined
According to the spokesperson of the General Commissioner, within 127 days of tightening the road traffic law by increasing the fine according to Sub-Decree No. 49, from May 1 to September 4, 2020, the traffic police nationwide inspected And fined a total of 160,211 vehicles, including 118,902 motorcycles and 41,309 vehicles of all types.
Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun said that for the past 127 days, the implementation of the new sub-decree to fine vehicles for offenses has been going well. He thanked and commended all the road users for their good obedience to the traffic law so far, especially the traffic police for their dedication and hard work. Tighten traffic with the highest sense of responsibility.
