Large-scale drug trafficking in Banteay Meanchey arrested by military forces
(Banteay Meanchey): The Office of Drug Crimes cooperated with the local police force of Preah Net Preah District to arrest a suspect who was selling large-scale drugs.
The Armed Forces arrested the suspect at 10:35 AM on September 3, 2020 at Chakrey Village, Chob Vary Commune, Pranet Preah District, Banteay Meanchey Province, under the leadership of Colonel Chea Dara, Deputy Commander of the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Gendarmerie. Get a drug job.
According to Mr. Chea Dara, he told Fresh News that before cracking down on the suspects, the military received information from a network of information agencies that the suspects were involved in drug trafficking. After receiving the information, the specialized force of the Office of Drug Crimes investigated and arrested the suspect at the scene and sent him to the Provincial Gendarmerie for further questioning.
Mr. Chea Dara further stated that according to the confession of the suspect, he confessed that he had hired all these drugs to be given to the buyer twice and the day of the payment was given to him twice. That made $ 1,500. Based on the confession and the above evidence, the military concluded that the suspect was indeed involved in drug trafficking.
On the morning of September 4, 2020, at the Provincial Gendarmerie Headquarters, Mr. Ou Rathrey, Governor of Banteay Meanchey Province, Brigadier General Born Bin, Commander of the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Gendarmerie, and the Provincial Prosecutor came to inspect drugs. Suspects and exhibits are currently being prosecuted. Kandal Provincial Gendarmerie Grand Family Foundation is presented to Gendarmerie officers whose families have died and given birth
