(Phnom Penh): A woman who posed as a judge of the Court of Appeal and used the names of some leaders to defraud her of nearly 1 million dollars was arrested by the police force of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police in cooperation with the Preah Vihear Provincial Police. In Kulen district, Preah Vihear province and sent back to Phnom Penh.
Authorities claimed that the woman had deceived the victim into believing that she was a relative, a senior leader waiting to help behind the scenes, and that she had deceived the victim into giving her money to buy land for future use. The suspect, who has now been transferred from Preah Vihear province, arrived at the Phnom Penh Municipal Police's Minor Criminal Division on September 4, 2020 to build a case to be sent to court for legal action.
