(Phnom Penh): Leaders and officials of the General Department of Consumer Protection, Competition and Anti-Fraud (CPC) of the Ministry of Commerce on Friday On September 4, 2020, participated in the swearing-in ceremony to complete the procedure as a judicial police in front of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, presided over by the representatives of the Oath Council and the Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court.
The participants of the swearing-in ceremony were: Mr. Phan Aun, Director General of the General Department of KPRP, Deputy Director General, Mr. and Mrs. Chairman, Deputy Director of the Department, Chief of Deputy Chief of Office, a total of 86 people.
It should be noted that the Law on Consumer Protection was approved and promulgated urgently by Royal Kram No. NS / RKAM / 1119/016 dated November 2, 2019, Article 29, paragraph 1 indicates. That the investigating officer must be trained as a judicial police to examine the offenses stated in this law in accordance with the provisions of the Code of Criminal Procedure.
In accordance with the spirit of Article 29 of this law, 527 officers of the General Department of Consumer Protection, Competition and Fraud Suppression (CPC) of the Ministry of Commerce were appointed as Investigating Officers through Resolution 158 DPM dated May 29, 2020 on the appointment of investigators of the Ministry of Commerce.
Officers of the General Department of the CPP The Ministry of Commerce, a judicial police force, is mandated by the Consumer Protection Law to carry out its work under the scope of this law to define rules and mechanisms to contribute to creating a business environment that protects the rights and interests of consumers. Promote honest business and provide trust between consumers and traders.
