457 Families in Oddar Meanchey Receive Love and Warmth from Samdech Techo
(Oddar Meanchey): On August 2, 2020, Mr. Lim Phea, 41 years old, a paralyzed person with both arms amputated, damaged left eye and damaged one left ear (disabled by demining) traveled from Trapeang Prasat district, Oddar Meanchey province to meet him. Duong Dara, Samdech Techo Prime Minister's personal assistant to tell about the humanitarian project to share land to build houses to help the same disabled people and the poorest people without land to live.
Mr. Lim Phea is happy to give up the land he bought to celebrate helping the same Cambodian people to have a place to live. At the same time, Mr. Lim Phea stated that the possible sharing depends on a peaceful nation under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen. Although not as physically fit as he is, Lim Phea has a heart full of admirable good deeds.
Mr. Lim Phea is married to Tinary, 34, and has seven children. In 2004, Mr. Lim Phea went on a begging adventure in Thailand and Malaysia, saving little by $ 190,000 to buy more than 53 hectares of land in O'Krouch village, Trapeang Prasat commune, Trapeang Prasat district, Oddar Meanchey province. . He intends to donate this land to the disabled as well as to distribute to poor people in a family size of 8m x 18m to build a house.
So far, Mr. Lim Phea has provided land to 457 families. Mr. Lim Phea made it clear that he and his family respect and love Samdech and support the election of the Cambodian People's Party in all terms. On the other hand, all the families he provides land are loyal and supportive of the CPP.
At the same time, the people expressed their deepest gratitude to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister, who always pays attention to the well-being of people living everywhere. Because the well-being of the people is the personal well-being of the two leaders.
A large left-handed Buddha statue found south of Bayon Temple
(Siem Reap): A sandstone Buddha statue on the left was found in the southern forest about 300 meters from Bayon Temple. The sculpture is 0.95 meters long, 0.42 meters wide and 0.24 meters thick.
The conclusion of such a gesture of Samput Mutra village is based on the reason that there are two large Buddha statues around Bayon temple, including Indra Tep and Ngok, all built in large size and from Lots of sandstone and in the same gesture of the White Sea Village.
The area where the sculpture was found is most likely a Buddhist structure, as we also see some boundary stones. However, research and aerial photographs taken by LiDAR technology have also uncovered traces of many settlements in the Angkor Thom area, including those built of sandstone and Buddhist shrines. Late stone at the compound.
At present, the handwriting box of the Intangible Heritage Registration Team of the Department of Temple Preservation in Angkor Park and Preventive Archeology has cooperated with the Angkor Heritage Police and the Temple Preservation Officer to record, hand over, receive and transport. Keep at the Apsara Authority Center for registration and keep waiting for future repairs.
