(Kratie): Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Secretary of State and Spokesperson of the Ministry of Environment, confirmed that the Royal Government of Cambodia has prepared for the ministries and institutions led by the working group led by the Ministry of Environment to study and prepare documents to put 4 natural tourism sites on the list. UNESCO World Natural Heritage.
Mr. Net Pheaktra confirmed this on the evening of September 3, 2020, when he led a group of multi-institutional journalists to cover the Prek Kampi resort located in Sambok commune, Chit Borei district, province. Kratie.
He also said that so far, a team led by the Ministry of Environment has been working to compile some documents and is continuing to study in the Prek Kam area to prepare any documents. Corner, especially in the area along the Mekong River, which is home to dolphins.
Speaking to the media on this occasion, Mr. Neth Pheaktra said that Prek Kampi is a natural tourist resort with a beautiful view of the river and a safe haven for 92 Mekong River dolphins. Today, Prek Kampi is becoming a popular and well-known resort for Kratie province, and is most popular with national and international tourists during the dry season.
He added that Cambodia is one of the three countries in the world with 92 freshwater dolphins, while Cambodia has the largest number of dolphins. The other two countries where freshwater dolphins are present are Indonesia and Burma.
Second: Prek Prosop Wildlife Sanctuary, with a total area of 12,770 hectares, located in Prek Prosop and Sambo districts of Kratie province, which is a natural area of Cambodia with the presence of endangered deer The world, especially this region, has other rare species.
