General knowledge: Brief history and rise of Kim Jong Un
Under Kim Jong Un, North Korea was widely known in the Western media for its frequent coverage of human rights abuses and nuclear weapons tests, including ballistic missiles, without fear of a UN resolution. No nation. What kind of background does Kim Jong Un have?
Childhood and education: Kim Jong Un is the fourth son of Kim Jong Il and Ko Yong Hee. According to North Korean state media, Kim Jong Un was born in the city of Kim Jong Il in Sam Gyeong Province, near the foothills of Pegu Mountain, a historical site considered by North Koreans to be a sacred site.
Some sources claim that Kim Jong Un was born in Changsong, North Pyongyang Province, or Wushan, in Guangdong Province. But what is clear is that Kim Jong Un spent his childhood living in a luxurious house in Pyongyang. Kim started studying at the age of three.
Kim Jong Un returned to North Korea in 2001, and from 2002 to 2007 he received three years of training from officials at the Kim Jong Il Military Academy in Pyongyang and continued his studies for two years. On the research program at the artillery training school.
Rising power: In North Korea, the issue of succession has been raised since 2004, when Kim Jong Un and his brother Kim Jong Un accompanied Kim Jong Il to inspect the base. The military. In 2006, when Kim Jong Un's picture tag was distributed to officials and senior military leaders, it became clear that he would be chosen to succeed his father.
In fact, it was not until 2009 that Kim Jong Il told North Korean military officials and officials that he had chosen Kim Jong Un to succeed him, and since then, Kim Jong Un has always accompanied his father. Always like a visit to China in 2010.
Kim Jong Un became North Korea's top leader on December 30, 2011, following the announcement of Kim Jong Il's death on December 19. Because Kim Jong Un was only 27 years old at the time, some analysts believe that his aunt, Kim Kyun-hee, and his uncle, Zhang Song-tek, who would be the most trusted people in the world, would be influential and in charge of the administration. The country behind him.
But the opposite is true when Kim Jong Un ordered the execution of Zhang Song-tek in 2013 for treason, a major internal purge since Kim Jong-il. Died. In addition, in 2016, Kim Jong Un organized the first Labor Party Congress in more than 40 years to strengthen his unchanging power in North Korea.
The first son, Kim Jong Nam, was arrested by the Japanese for smuggling into the country using a fake passport, and the eldest son also disagreed with his father's leadership. As a result, Kim Jong Nam was not considered a successor.
The second son is Kim Jong Chul, a man of great wisdom and genius in literature and literature. But the next son is considered by his father to be a soft and gentle man who does not deserve to be the third North Korean leader.
As for the third son, Kim Jong Un, he has the same qualities and personality as his father, or in other words, the youngest son has the idea to follow in the footsteps of the Kim family, which is the most suitable heir. Kim Jong Il always said that his youngest son loves power and can defend power, just as he protected his grandfather, Kim Il-sung.
In addition to the above qualities, Kim Jong Un has also been trained to be strong, courageous and fierce from an early age. He can drive a car and drink a lot of alcohol, not easy to get drunk. Not only that, the future North Korean third leader likes to wear military uniforms, which is very different from the eldest son who likes to wear European clothes.
Kim Jong Un took over from his father at the age of 30. Despite his young age, key figures in North Korea all agreed that he should be the supreme leader of the country, the leader of the government, and in particular the leader of a more powerful army. Some countries in the world. Court gives prisoner three days to file a lawsuit against Sar Thavy over land theft in Samrong commune, Prek Pnov district
