This Royal Decree was made on September 3, 2020, following a request from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
On August 27, 2020, Mr. Son Chhay, Mr. Tao Kimchhorn and Mr. Va Samon wrote separate letters to Samdech Krala Horm Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, requesting for political rehabilitation after their arrest. Ban for almost three years.
"Based on the new Article 45 (a duplicate) of the Law on Political Parties, which allows those who are prohibited from political activity to regain their political rights," he said. Therefore, I would like to request Samdech Krala Hom, the Deputy Prime Minister, to review the procedure in order to give me the legal right to do politics again. ”
Son Chhay, along with a total of 118 former CNRP leaders, was sentenced by the Supreme Court to a five-year ban on political activity on November 16, 2017, following a conviction to dissolve the imprisoned CNRP. Involved in conspiracy with foreigners to overthrow the legitimate government that emerged from the election.
The new law on the amendment of Article 45 (duplicate) of the Law on Political Parties, which is the only way to pave the way for politicians to be banned from politics by a court decision to be able to resume their political activities, has been approved by His Majesty the King. His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of Cambodia, issued a Royal Kram on January 2, 2019.
In order to rehabilitate, a politician who has been banned from conducting politics by the court must submit a letter to the Ministry of Interior, and after scrutiny, the Ministry of Interior will submit a letter to the Prime Minister to consider submitting a letter to the King. Re-rice.
