According to the spokesperson of the General Commissioner, within 126 days of tightening the road traffic law by increasing the fine according to Sub-Decree No. 49, from May 1 to September 3, 2020, the traffic police nationwide inspected And fined a total of 159,118 vehicles, including 118,079 motorcycles and 41,039 vehicles of all types.
Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun said that for the past 126 days, the implementation of the new sub-decree to fine vehicles for offenses has been going well. He thanked and commended all the road users for their good obedience to the traffic law so far, especially the traffic police for their dedication and hard work. Tighten traffic with the highest sense of responsibility.
Please note that for September 3, 2020, traffic accidents across Cambodia also occurred 20 times, in which 10 people died, 48 people were injured (22 seriously injured).
