(Phnom Penh): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, on the afternoon of September 3, 2020, received Mr. Markus Buerli, Director of the Swiss Cooperation Office and the Swiss Consulate in Cambodia and his colleagues for a courtesy call and discussion. To strengthen and expand cooperation between the two countries on agriculture in Cambodia.
To begin with, the Minister thanked the Government of Switzerland for its excellent cooperation with Cambodia in all fields, especially in the field of agriculture. RIICE rice insurance in Cambodia since 2012.
Minister Veng Sakhon emphasized that all these technologies and information are very important for professional officers to provide data and information to farmers and in line with the Ministry's agricultural development strategic plan to promote the implementation of agricultural modernization, agricultural mechanization. Climate change resilience farming, updating of zoning maps, especially improving agricultural production chains and value added.
Therefore, the Minister requested the Swiss side to continue to cooperate with the Ministry on the above work and examine the possibility of strengthening the capacity of officials and farmers to build support infrastructure such as irrigation systems to respond to water shortages caused by climate change and promote education. Research and produce foundation seeds to jointly develop this sector to grow to another level.
Mr. Markus Buerli expressed his great pleasure and congratulations to the Royal Government of Cambodia and the Ministry for continuing to develop the agricultural sector effectively by boosting local production, especially during the Kovid-19 virus phase. He also agreed with the Minister's concerns about water shortages and low water levels in the Mekong River, which could affect crop production this year.
Therefore, the Swiss side is in discussions with a development partner operating in Cambodia as well to develop a short-term support project focused on building support infrastructure and irrigation systems for farmers.
On the other hand, considering that the cooperation between the two sides in implementing the RIICE project has achieved good results, the Swiss side will continue to cooperate with the Ministry, with plans to sign an agreement on the implementation of another project, which is a stimulus project. The horticultural production chain is called the Cambodia CHAIN Fruit and Vegetable Project, Phase 3, from January 2021 to December 2022.
During the meeting, the two sides also discussed a number of topics, such as the progress of amendments to the Fisheries Law and the Forestry Law. Deputy Governor of Tbong Khmum Province and Mr. Oknha Neou Kun Hold the First Ben Ceremony at Wat Po Chey Mongkul, also known as Wat Damnak Char
