(Banteay Meanchey): A drunken husband came out from drinking and suddenly quarreled with his wife. At that time, the niece stopped him and they fought.
This incident happened at 8 pm on September 2, 2020 in Kbal Spean 2 village, Sangkat Poipet, Poipet city, Banteay Meanchey province.
Poipet City Military Officer said that before the incident, the suspect, Chin Nary, a 22-year-old female, left work and arrived at a house in Kbal Spean 2 Village, Sangkat Poipet, Poipet City. I do not know where the drunken man came from, he beat his wife and insulted her.
At that time, the niece saw her uncle beating her aunt so much that she stopped him, causing a quarrel, which led to a fight until the suspect took the knife he bought to cut vegetables for people. The victim was seriously injured and died while being treated at the Cambodia-Japan Friendship Hospital in Mongkol Borei.
Colonel Nuon Ninaro Poipet said that after receiving the complaint, he led a search force to the scene and arrested the suspect, Chin Nary, and confiscated a vegetable knife and sent it to a military base. City to conduct inquiries.
After interrogation, the suspect confessed that he had stabbed the victim with a paring knife, causing serious injuries and even death because he saw the victim use violence on his aunt. But every day.
After receiving the confession and having the evidence, the Municipal Armed Forces prepared a case file and sent it to the Provincial Gendarmerie Command for further action.
The suspect was sent by the provincial military to the provincial court to deal with the procedure.
