(Phnom Penh): At a meeting on setting the minimum wage for textiles, garments and footwear for 2021, Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training and Chairman of the National Council for Minimum Wages, set the National Minimum Wage Council. Together, end the wage talks by September 9-10, before the upcoming Pchum Ben festival.
The push was made at a meeting of the National Minimum Wage Council (NEC) of the first and second mandates on setting the minimum wage in the textile, garment and footwear sector for 2021 this morning. September 3, 2020 at the Ministry of Labor.
On that occasion, Mr. Ith Sam Heng said that the discussion on setting the minimum wage in Cambodia was first implemented in 2000 and has been continuously improved through a tripartite mechanism.
The minister said that for 2020, the minimum wage negotiation process went on as usual, but due to the March 2020 outbreak of 19 Kovid in the European Union and the United States, Cambodia's main export markets. And those countries have declared a state of emergency, which has led to a drop in Cambodia's garment and footwear exports.
However, Minister Ith Sam Heng has set the National Minimum Wage Council to jointly end the pre-Pchum Ben wage talks so that workers as well as the parties to the National Minimum Wage Council can calm down. Mind to rest on that upcoming occasion.
The meeting agreed to set September 9-10 as the last meeting time for the minimum wage talks for workers in the textile, garment and footwear sectors.
