Cambodia-Japan meeting to review challenges and requests of Japanese investors, by the end of July this year, Japan invested in Cambodia 2.8 billion US dollars
This bilateral meeting is the 20th meeting organized under the framework of the Agreement between Cambodia and Japan on the liberalization, promotion and protection of investment, signed by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Shinzo Abe. Prime Minister Shinzo Abe of Japan on June 14, 2007. The first bilateral meeting was held in 2009.
The meeting is part of the Investor Care Mechanism, which provides an opportunity for Japanese investors to directly address challenges and suggestions to government representatives to review and find solutions in order to improve the investment and business environment in Cambodia. Cambodia.
The 20th meeting focused on a number of priority issues, including: (1) electricity prices, (2) fiscal obligations, (3) regulations related to the import of vehicles, and (4) the progress of preparations for opening international border crossings. Stung Bot in Poipet City; and (5) Facilitation of customs clearance procedures.
Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea expressed regret over the resignation of Prime Minister Shinzo Abe on August 28, 2020 due to health problems, but he expressed optimism that the new Prime Minister will continue to promote relations and relations. Bilateral cooperation between Cambodia and Japan as a strategic partner to further improve.
He expressed his deep gratitude to the Japanese investors who have always believed in the Royal Government of Cambodia under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, in ensuring peace, political stability, which is necessary to create the environment. Favorable investment.
Taking this opportunity, on behalf of the Royal Government and the people of Cambodia, Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea also thanked the Government and the people of Japan for providing medical equipment to Cambodia to fight and prevent the spread of disease. Kovid-19.
He expressed hope that ANA would resume direct flights between Japan and Cambodia in the near future, which would help boost trade and investment between the two countries.
In response, Mr. Masahiro Mikami praised and thanked the Council for the Development of Cambodia and all relevant ministries and institutions for their past efforts with a high sense of responsibility to facilitate and provide a gentle response. To the concerns and suggestions of Japanese investors, which confirms the high attention of the Royal Government of Cambodia to maintain and provide warmth to all investors.
On behalf of the Head of the Japanese Embassy in Cambodia, he also pledged to provide support in preventing the spread of Kovid-19 in Cambodia and facilitate the return of reciprocal travel between the two countries.
At the end of the meeting, the two sides pledged to continue to work together to resolve the remaining issues, promote the timely provision of information to each other, simplify procedures and speed up the process. Ongoing investment projects are better, ensuring competition and win-win, which contributes to sustainable economic growth.
(Siem Reap): In order to alleviate the boredom of the people as well as the local guests and to contribute to the promotion of national tourism, the Siem Reap Provincial Authority has been discussing with relevant partners to plan the establishment of tourism events. Have fun every weekend at various tourist destinations in your province.
This special plan was presented by the Director of the Siem Reap Provincial Department of Tourism, Mr. Ngov Sengkak, during his presentation at a press conference on the state of tourism during the Kovid 19 crisis organized by the Government Spokesperson's Unit. This morning, September 3, 2020 at the Office of the Council of Ministers.
Mr. Ngov Sengkak said that under the initiative of Mr. Tea Seiha, the Governor of Siem Reap and with the support of the Ministry of Tourism, the Provincial Administration and the Department of Tourism of Siem Reap have been seeking discussions with relevant departments, units and partners to jointly organize Plan to create touring events every weekend or maybe on Fridays, Saturdays and Sundays.
The director of the department said that this plan can be prepared only with the close cooperation of the relevant departments, partner organizations, as well as the private sector in the tourism sector, both in terms of spirit, activities and financial resources.
He added that the organization of daily tours this weekend will help people as well as domestic tourists have more opportunities to visit tourist sites in Siem Reap and will make it easier for Family tourists and group friends as well.
He expressed the expectation that the tourism plan would greatly benefit local people and communities by recovering tourism revenue after being affected by Kovid since the end of 2019.
The director of the Department of Tourism has not forgotten his commitment to adhering to tourism safety measures, as the world as well as Cambodia has not yet recovered from the Kovid crisis, he said. " Provincial Governor and Kampong Chhnang Provincial Prosecutor's Office hold the first Ben at Wat Aranyakaram in Kampong Chhnang City
