(Phnom Penh): Mr. Tith Chantha, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Tourism, said that as of August 2020, Cambodia's tourism sector has lost about 5 billion US dollars due to the effects of Kovid 19 disease.
Mr. Tith Chantha said this on the morning of September 3, 2020, on the occasion of the Government Spokesperson's Unit held a press conference on "The situation of tourism during the outbreak of Kovid 19" at the Council of Ministers.
A senior official at the Ministry of Tourism confirmed: "In the first phase of the impact study, we severely affected both national and international tourists, and we lost about $ 5 billion in tourism revenue."
According to Mr. Tith Chantha, added that each year, the Cambodian tourism sector can earn at least around 5 to 6 billion US dollars received from national and international visitors. For 2020, due to the effects of Kovid 19, international tourists are almost completely lost.
However, due to better control over the spread of Kovid 19 in Cambodia and proper measures, national tourists have been resuming sightseeing activities and gradually resuming tourism services. . This makes the Ministry of Tourism claim that by the end of 2020, Cambodia's tourism sector can earn at least 100 to 500 million US dollars.
