(Phnom Penh): Mr. Tith Chantha, Permanent Secretary of State of the Ministry of Tourism, said this morning, September 3, 2020, during the New Year holidays for the past 5 days, there were about 1.4 million tourists. People traveled all over the country, spending more than $ 100.
At a press conference organized by the Royal Government Spokesperson on "Tourism Situation during the Kovid 19 Outbreak", Mr. Tith Chantha stated that the spending of tourists is a boost to the internal economy. Ideally, foreign tourism is declining almost completely.
Mr. Tith Chantha said, "During the last holiday, domestic tourism activities have pushed everywhere to reach about 1.5 million people, of which 10% are foreigners in Cambodia. "Stimulate the domestic economy, which we initially estimated at about $ 100 million over the past nine days."
The senior official also claimed that the $ 100 million budget is a direct stream of tourist spending on destinations, and that the capital will help boost other relevant sectors of the socio-economy. He added that the figures also encourage more investment in hotels, restaurants, restaurants, local tourism services to reopen.
According to Tith Chantha, during the nine days of holidays (including Saturdays and Sundays), many tourist destinations experience a shortage of supplies, such as accommodation, and if there are more tourist attractions, they may receive more tourists. Even more interior during this holiday.
At the same time, Mr. Tith Chantha said that so far, according to the figures that the Ministry of Tourism has received business services for tourism, 30 percent reopened out of 90 percent closed due to Kovid-19. More than 100,000 workers have returned to work.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol leads Kan Ben officials at a remote pagoda in Siem Reap
(Siem Reap): On Thursday, September 3, 2020, the first day of Kanben, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol led the civil servants of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport to participate in the Kanben ceremony. 1 at Wat Sovankiri, called Wat Peung Bak Rotes, with the participation of leaders, government officials, ministries and about 200 Buddhists at the foot of the pagoda.
Wat Sovankiri has a total of 34 monks and nuns who are waiting for the rain. This pagoda is located in a remote place with a winding path along the hillside and accompanied by beautiful plants and beautiful natural air in O village, Khvav commune, Chi Kreng district, Siem Reap province.
At the same time, the Senior Minister also prayed for the people's journey to be safe, secure and full of smiles, and called on all road users to respect the traffic law consistently and be tolerant. High while driving to avoid traffic accidents and always remember the noble words of Samdech Techo Prime Minister: "Today, tomorrow, please do not have a traffic accident."
Please be informed that Wat Sovankiri is located in O village, Khvav commune, Chi Kreng district, Siem Reap province, about 50 kilometers from Kampong Kdei market, traveling on some rubber roads, some red gravel roads and some dirt roads. From the foot of the mountain to the pagoda, the road is difficult to drive because it is a dirt road. The road bends along the slopes and is accompanied by beautiful vegetation and natural fresh air.
As this pagoda is an attractive natural resort and a sacred place of worship, although the road to the pagoda is a bit difficult to drive, Buddhists come out to bring food, relics and offerings to the monks at the pagoda every day. Absolutely. Minister Vong Soth: All social officials must strengthen their capacity and serve the people
