(Kampong Cham): The Governor of Kampong Cham Province, Mr. Un Chanda and Mr. Lou Kimchhon, Chief of Srey Santhor District Assistance Team, together with relevant officials, this morning, September 3, 2020, organized a public forum to find a solution for Prek Dambok Market traders. Srey Santhor District, Kampong Cham Province.
According to Prek Dambok commune chief Phal Von, after the district authorities reorganized the new shopping area and renovated the Prek Dambok market about two months ago, there was a controversy over the location of more than 100 vendors. Controversial to date. Among them, some traders agreed to accept the new location and some traders refused to accept the new location.
In relation to the above issue, after listening to the opinions of the business community, Mr. Un Chanda assumed that this issue could not be resolved immediately.
He said that in order to solve this problem successfully through win-win politics, he decided to confiscate the remaining 25 stalls and hand them over to the chairman of the market management committee to use for the benefit of Prek Dambok market and set up a joint working group of one province. The deputy governor led a working group to successfully resolve this issue within 30 days.
