Lt. Gen. Thet orders police to be on duty 24 hours a day to solve problems for the people on the occasion of Pchum Ben
(Phnom Penh): Lt. Gen. Thet, Deputy Commissioner General and Phnom Penh Municipal Police Commissioner, on August 3, 2020, ordered the police force to be on duty 24 hours a day to be ready to solve various problems for the people on the occasion. Kan Ben - National Pchum Ben Festival 2020.
The order was issued by Lt. Gen. Thet on the occasion of chairing a meeting to disseminate the plan for the protection of security, public order and social safety during the Kan Ben-Pchum Ben Festival 2020, which was held at the Phnom Penh Municipal Police this morning. This August 3, 2020.
The meeting was also attended by the Deputy Commissioner, the Director of the Office, the Inspector and other relevant officials.
In addition, the Deputy Commissioners and the 14 District Police Inspectors also participated in many opinions related to the planning and organizing of a joint force to organize order to facilitate traffic, especially to protect the safety of leaders and people. Citizens who attend the Kan Ben and Pchum Ben festivals.
During the meeting, Lt. Gen. Thet instructed all authorities to pay high attention to the responsibility of organizing traffic order, especially to ensure the safety and security of the leaders and people during the festival. Kan Ben, Pchum Ben festival.
On the other hand, the commissioner stressed that all officers must perform their duties with proper speech and behavior, dress appropriately as a force, especially always cut their hair short.
Lt. Gen. Thet also stressed that all authorities must be very careful and always ready to prevent and prevent any crime such as theft, burglary or car glass, take the property of the people who brought food to the monks. And to visit various entertainment places in Phnom Penh.
Lt. Gen. Thet further stated that in addition, at all targets, district police inspectorates and administrative police stations must have officers on duty 24 hours a day to be ready to solve problems for the people.
