Banteay Meanchey Provincial Police clarifies the case of a police officer who detained a drug dealer until a weapon exploded and injured a suspect
(Banteay Meanchey): The Banteay Meanchey Provincial Police Commissioner issued a statement on September 2, 2020 regarding the case of a police officer from the Virtual Administration Post of the Poipet City Police Inspectorate who detained a person who used and distributed drugs until a weapon exploded, causing a suspect Injured.
In this explanation, Banteay Meanchey Provincial Police described as follows:
On August 27, 2020 at 23:20, the Nim Administrative Police Force of Poipet City Police Inspectorate patrolled the target area and met 2 suspects riding a motorbike, which was an old subject used and distributed. Drugs and gun violence during 2016, who escaped.
During the patrol, Lieutenant Colonel Pithy Piseth, Deputy Chief of Nimit Administration Post, detained the suspects for questioning and examination, but the two suspects refused to cooperate and even called the other two accomplices on motorcycles. One unit came to intervene and reached to commit violence.
Later, the experts targeted and summoned the three people, 16-year-old Kem Chhayya, 16-year-old Huon Ratha, alias Khouch, and 18-year-old Mab Nith, living in Nimit 1 Village, Nimit Sangkat, Poipet City, Banteay Meanchey Province for questioning. And took a urine test for drugs, the result was positive. Following the advice of the Prosecutor of the Provincial Court, the competent authorities have prepared a case file for procedural action.
Separately, on September 1, 2020, the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Police Commission built a case on the case of Lieutenant Colonel Pithy Piseth sent to the Provincial Court for legal proceedings.
Ministry of Tourism Introduces 7 Capital-Provincial Departments of Tourism to Improve the Quality of Tourism Products on the Occasion of Pchum Ben
(Phnom Penh): In order to contribute to the promotion of tourism services and prevent the spread of Kovid-19 disease, the Ministry of Tourism has issued seven guidelines to the Capital-Provincial Department of Tourism to improve the quality of tourism products on the occasion of Pchum Ben.
First, to promote the consistent implementation of the measures issued by the Ministry of Health and the Tourism Safety Rules of the Ministry of Tourism to prevent the spread of Kovi-19, especially the registration of tourists visiting tourist destinations. Arrangements to control the heating of water, alcohol, disinfection and require tourists to wear masks or krama regularly.
Second, to cooperate with local authorities and authorities at all levels to ensure security, safety, traffic order and parking for tourists better.
Third, to cooperate with the Ministry of Environment, Department of Health and other relevant departments to educate business owners, tourism services and tourists to participate in maintaining a clean environment by eliminating litter and waste, especially to stop throwing paper under the table and be Take all possible steps to ensure the cleanliness of the restaurant, including the restrooms and toilets, and the staff must be in proper uniform.
Fourth, to cooperate with traders and tour operators to improve the quality of tourism products and maintain appropriate prices of products and services. All accommodation, food and other services must be clearly written in the table to inform guests in advance to avoid excessive fees. In case of non-compliance with the posted schedule, the business owner shall be liable before the law in force.
Fifth, to instruct the owners of boats and tourist boats that do business to transport tourists across the sea, rivers, streams and lakes not to overcrowd and to be equipped with the necessary relief equipment.
Sixth, to cooperate with the provincial hall and the media, such as the press, radio and television broadcast spots on tourism safety measures to prevent the spread of Kovid-19 disease, as well as tourism spots and participate in the competition "Clean city, clean resort, good service and hospitality. Good. ”
And (7) to cooperate in the main tourist destinations to raise public awareness to tourists and citizens about the risks and measures to prevent the spread of Kovid-19 disease, as well as to improve the quality of tourism products and services. .
