The Rice Federation said that the decline in exports of dry rice, especially fragrant rice, due to two main factors, including:
1: Climate change has caused a large number of dry season rice planted in May and harvested in late July and August due to drought (dry season in June and August). For farmers to replant, especially rice fields far from water sources, and for rice to be harvested in limited quantities, also pushed the price of rice to increase by about 20% compared to the same period in 2019.
