Community forestry chief and resident of Kep province's Pong Teuk commune accuse the principal of Chamkar Dong High School of encroaching on the community's permanent forest reserve and threatening to shoot him.
(Kep): The head of the forestry community and residents of Chamkar Bei village, Pong Teuk commune, Damnak Chang Eur district, Kep province, accused Long Sophea, principal of Chamkar Dong High School, of threatening to sue and shoot them because they banned the high school principal. To stop the clearing of forest land in the permanent forest reserve in Neak Ta Chhor community.
Nak Yut, head of the Neak Ta Chhor community forest in the Kep City Forestry Administration's permanent forest reserve, said that in the past, Long Sophea had threatened to sue him because he had reported to professional institutions and authorities in Damnak Chang Eur district. Clear forest land in the community to take ownership of the land.
The head of the community forestry said that in the past, Damnak Chang Eur district authorities and forest officials had banned the high school principal from clearing the forest land, but recently, the high school principal has been clearing the community forest land. Increasingly.
Svay Sok Kheang, a plantation worker in Chamkar Bei village, said he was also threatened with shooting by the principal of Chamkar Dong High School when he went to film forest clearing in the state's permanent reserve.
She added that the land that Long Sophea is clearing is actually in the community forest. She added that she had assigned cadastral and forestry administration officials to verify the plots of land if it was found that the high school principal was encroaching on the land in the state's permanent forest reserve. The case is sent to court for legal action.
