The National Co-Prosecutor informed that Kaing Guek Eav alias Duch had passed away based on the report of the relevant officials and the investigation into the cause of death of Kaing Guek Eav alias Duch is the responsibility of the National Authority.
Kaing Guek Eav alias Duch was born on November 17, 1942 in Pov Veay village, Peam Bang commune, Srong Stong province, Kampong Thom province, Khmer nationality. He was arrested and detained on 10 May 1999 and transferred to the Extraordinary Chambers in the Courts of Cambodia (ECCC) on 30 July 2007. .
On July 31, 2007, he was placed under scrutiny for crimes against humanity, grave breaches of the Geneva Conventions of August 12, 1949, and torture and murder under the Code. Criminal 1956.
On 30 March 2009, the Trial Chamber held a 72-day hearing for Kaing Guek Eav alias Duch, a cross-examination of evidence, witnesses and Civil Parties.
On July 26, 2010, the verdict was announced that Kaing Guek Eav alias Duch had been in charge of S-21 for more than three years, resulting in the deaths of more than 12,272 victims.
The Trial Chamber's verdict was appealed by Civil Party Co-Prosecutors Kaing Guek Eav alias Duch to the Supreme Court Chamber. On February 3, 2012, the Supreme Court Chamber sentenced Kaing Guek Eav alias Duch to life in prison.
Kaing Guek Eav alias Duch was sent to Kandal Provincial Prison on 6 June 2013 to serve his sentence following the decision of the Supreme Court Chamber.
