On the morning of September 2, 2020, Kaing Guek Eav alias Duch, former chief of Tuol Sleng prison during the Khmer Rouge regime, died at the Khmer-Soviet Friendship Hospital at 00:51, according to a spokesman for the Kandal Provincial Prosecutor's Office. Skip minutes into the night on September 2, 2020.
Kaing Guek Eav alias Duch was born on November 17, 1942 in Pov Veay village, Peam Bang commune, Stong district, Kampong Thom province, Khmer nationality. He was arrested and detained on 10 May 1999 and transferred to the Extraordinary Chambers in the Courts of Cambodia (ECCC) on 30 July 2007. Crimes against humanity carry a life sentence.
As of September 2, 2020, Kaing Guek Eav alias Duch was detained at Kandal Provincial Prison for 7 years, 2 months and 25 days. While serving his sentence at Kandal Provincial Prison, Kaing Guek Eav alias Duch, a 78-year-old man, was in poor health and suffering from chronic health problems.
Kaing Guek Eav alias Duch has been sent to four outpatient hospitals for treatment, including:
* First time: October 20, 2018, sent to Victory Referral Hospital, Kandal Province, with extreme fatigue, Victory Referral Doctor sent to Khmer-Soviet Friendship Hospital on October 21, 2018 and sent Prison unit on November 13, 2018.
* Second time: On November 20, 2018, he was sent to Victory Referral Hospital in Kandal Province and sent to Khmer-Soviet Friendship Hospital with kidney pain (obstruction) and sent back to the prison unit on the 17th. December 2018.
* Third time: On May 4, 2019, he was sent to the Khmer-Soviet Friendship Hospital with swollen feet after being examined and sent back to the prison unit.
* 4th time: On August 31, 2020, he was sent to Victory Referral Hospital in Kandal Province and transferred to Khmer-Soviet Friendship Hospital. He was very tired and died at 00:51. Midnight enters on September 2, 2020.
