The ASEAN Inter-Parliamentary Assembly (AIPA) is an inter-parliamentary body representing the legislatures of the Association of Southeast Asian Nations (ASEAN), which includes Brunei, Cambodia, Indonesia, Laos, Malaysia, Myanmar, Singapore, Thailand, Vietnam and the Philippines.
The ASEAN Inter-Parliamentary Assembly is a gathering of the voices of the people of the ASEAN Community, ASEAN's partners in advancing the goal of a single ASEAN Community.
The ASEAN Inter-Parliamentary Assembly is held annually by the member countries in alphabetical order of the names of the countries in the Latin alphabet.
