The ministry said that by monitoring the continuous evolution and change of the weather conditions, it was observed that Cambodia was affected by the valleys of the low pressure system that stretched across northern Thailand, central Laos and Vietnam. Such a situation makes:
The ministry also called for caution against thunderstorms and strong winds in some parts of the central lowlands.
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of September 1, 2020, the National Election Committee (NEC) held a meeting with stakeholders regarding the commencement of the work of reviewing the voter list and voter registration 2020 at the NEC office. NEC under the high presidency of Mr. Sik Bun Hok, Chairman of the NEC.
Taking the opportunity to meet with stakeholders for two years after the 2018 National Assembly election, today the President of the NEC has the opportunity once again to present the vision of Electoral leadership and reform.
He said this in a meeting with stakeholders on the review of the voter list and voter registration on September 1, 2020 at the NEC.
The meeting was held with the active participation of stakeholders, including:
1: Representatives of 16 political parties 2: Representatives of 21 NGOs 3: Representatives of 9 journalists 4: Representatives of 5 ministries - institutions
Under the chairmanship of the NEC Chairman, on this occasion, four non-profit organizations and representatives of political parties such as the Khmer Patriotic Party, the Khmer Will Party, the Local Democrat Party and the Cambodian People's Party raised some suggestions and questions. Related:
Responding to the first point of the representative of the political party, Mr. Sik Bun Hok said that the NEC always advises election officials to serve all voters without discrimination, and on behalf of the President himself never considered any Khmer. Also an enemy. Good, correct and progressive opinions, we must accept and we respect each other's opinions, not only that opinion is destructive, exaggerated, distorted is not acceptable.
Regarding the third question above, regarding the issue of foreigners holding Khmer nationality identity cards or voting cards, Mr. Kheang Sokunthea, Director of the Khmer Nationality Identity Card Department of the General Department of Identification of the Ministry of Interior, stated that if a foreigner who is a Khmer nationality, he has The right to hold a Khmer identity card has the right to manage real estate and has the same rights as a typical Khmer.
Before having a Cambodian identity card, you need to have documents such as birth certificate, family book or residence book. Therefore, if any party finds or suspects that a foreigner is using a Cambodian identity card, please contact him at his personal telephone number 012 258 858 and he welcomes suggestions from all parties regarding his work. Or provide Khmer identity card to citizens.
Mr. Tep Nytha, Secretary General of the NEC, responded to the fourth question on the application for registration of political party agents that the NEC only changed the date of the voter list and voter registration. The legal framework related to the registration of our political party agents remains the same, so the party's letter of transfer to the lower levels is still valid.
