(Oddar Meanchey): Seven Cambodian citizens were sent back to the Cambodian authorities by the Thai authorities through the Choam International border crossing in Anlong Veng district on September 1, 2020, after being detained for many years. Year in Thailand for illegal border crossing.
According to the police report, among the seven Cambodian citizens who were deported by the Thai authorities were living in Kampong Speu, Oddar Meanchey and Preah Vihear provinces.
After being instructed to stop illegal cross-border activities and having a Kovid-19 heat scan, they were allowed to return to their respective homes. Switzerland vows to continue training tourism skills for Cambodians for another 4 years
(Phnom Penh): Cambodia's tourism sector is even more hopeful as the Swiss Cooperation Office informed the Ministry of Tourism that the Swiss government will continue to support tourism professional development projects for Cambodians living in the southern provinces. Legs and northeast for another 4 years.
From 2022-2025, the Swiss government will launch a new major development project that will follow a number of countries in the ASEAN region, including Cambodia. The project will be implemented in many areas such as tourism, employment and vocational training.
In connection with this new development project 2022-2025, Switzerland will continue to help develop tourism skills for Cambodians in the northern and northeastern provinces such as Kratie, Stung Treng, Preah Vihear, Ratanakkiri and Mondulkiri.
