Senior Minister Osman Hassan asks Australia to help develop and invest in halal sector in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Osman Hassan, Senior Minister in charge of Special Missions, requested that Australia continue to provide various assistance to Cambodia, especially to develop and invest in the halal sector, such as raising cattle, goats and sheep in Cambodia, by requesting to mobilize experts and Investors come to study investing in this sector.
Senior Minister Osman Hassan said that the investment will be very profitable, while Cambodia has the potential and favorable, as well as tax preferences from many rich countries.
During the meeting, the Senior Minister also informed about the economic and political situation as well as the situation of the Cambodian Muslim community under the leadership of Samdech Techo Prime Minister, who paid close attention to the Cambodian Muslim community in Cambodia has received many benefits. In general, the Royal Government of Cambodia has given equal rights and freedoms to all people without discrimination on the basis of race, which is what has made Cambodia harmonious.
At the same time, Senior Minister Osman Hassan also expressed the hope that the relationship between Cambodia and Australia will be stronger in all areas. In particular, hope that Cambodia will receive more scholarships for students to study in Australia, Australia is also famous for its education.
In response, the Australian Ambassador thanked and said that the Royal Government of Australia has been providing charitable assistance in three main areas: health, social affairs and the economy. In fact, in the field of health, Australia has helped in the fight against Kovid 19 by providing 10 ambulances and many medicines.
In the field of social affairs, Australia has partnered with the Ministry of Planning as well as other relevant ministries to search for the truly poor in order to receive assistance, while the Royal Government of Cambodia has provided support to the poor in During the 19 epidemics of Kovid.
He also claimed that Australia, in particular, had invested heavily in helping the Cambodian economy recover during the 19 19th period. Australia has also focused on the agricultural sector, promising to do what it can to help improve the sector, as Cambodia has a lot of potential to support the economy after being affected by Kovid. 19.
Please be reminded that Cambodia and Australia established official diplomatic relations on January 15, 1952. On September 24, 1993, Australia reopened its embassy in Phnom Penh.
