Sixteen families affected by typhoon in Ochrov district receive donations from Red Cross branch in Banteay Meanchey province
(Banteay Meanchey): Mr. Oum Rath, Chairman of Banteay Meanchey Provincial Red Cross Branch Committee, in the afternoon of August 31, 2020, led a working group to visit 16 families affected by the typhoon on August 29, 2020. Damage to houses in Samrong commune, Ochrov district, Banteay Meanchey province.
On that occasion, Mr. Oum Rath brought a message to visit and mourn the property of the 16 families of the victims from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross. In the past, both Samdech always thought about the well-being of the people everywhere and without letting anyone die of starvation.
Please note that humanitarian donations distributed to people affected by the typhoon, each family received 25 kg of rice, 1 box of 10 cans of fish, including cooking oil, soy sauce, blankets, mosquito nets, sarongs and some money.
Battambang Provincial Administration: Battambang Cloth Market will reopen tomorrow after a fire
(Battambang): On September 1, 2020, Mr. Nop Dara, Deputy Governor, Representative of Mr. Nguon Rattanak, Governor of Battambang Province and the three forces of the garbage collection company, including professional officers, continued to inspect and organize the sales area as well as order. Cleaning and cleaning as well as repairing as a solution for aunts and uncles who are traders affected by the fire in Battambang Central Market on August 30, 2020.
On this occasion, Mr. Nop Dara also met with the traders of Battambang cloth market, he shared his regret and claimed that the market will be reopened tomorrow.
At the same time, he also brought a greeting from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng to the brothers and sisters on this occasion.
Mr. Nop Dara also donated money to all the forces involved in organizing the market.
Please note that 33 out of 335 stalls in Battambang cloth market were completely engulfed by fire.
The fire broke out at 6 pm on August 30, 2020, immediately Battambang provincial leaders led a joint inspection force at the scene, while seven fire trucks, including cars from the police. 3 units, 1 unit in Sangke district, 1 unit in Thmor Koul district, 1 unit in Ek Phnom district and 1 unit in Banan district, 29 vehicles use water.
Nat Market or Central Market of Battambang Province was built in 1937 during the reign of King Sisowath Monivong. Apart from being an important commercial area, the cloth market is also considered to be one of the most valuable heritage buildings of Battambang province. 2020
A statement of thanks from Mr. Buerli Markus was made during a working meeting with Senior Minister Ly Thuch, First Vice President of the Mine Authority on Cooperation and Partnership in the field of mine action in Cambodia on September 1, 2020. This.
On that occasion, Mr. Buerli Markus stated that the Swiss Government appreciates the partnership and good cooperation with the Royal Government of Cambodia in the work of clearing humanitarian mines in Cambodia and will continue to support until Cambodia is demined by 2025 and continue. Help after 2025.
He also praised the work of clearing mines and explosive remnants of war, which has contributed significantly to the development of almost all sectors of the country, such as agriculture, infrastructure, health, education, gender and poverty reduction.
In this meeting, Senior Minister Ly Thuch informed Mr. Buerli Markus about the efforts of the Royal Government of Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, set out a clear vision and strategic plan that Samdech Techo wants to see Cambodia end the threat. Due to anti-personnel mines known to be complete by 2025 and reduce the risk of landmines to a minimum.
On behalf of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Senior Minister Ly Thuch expressed his deep gratitude to the Swiss government and people for their contribution to Cambodia's development, including humanitarian demining since 2013. He added that participating in supporting demining is helping to reduce poverty in Cambodia.
