According to Inspector Yi Vanda, the victim, Hok Kry Sok Leang, a 36-year-old female, lived in the village where the incident took place and worked at home. As for the suspect, his name is Soy Chansith, male, 29 years old, Khmer, address is Phum Sangkat, Occupation is not real.
The source said that at the time of the incident, the suspect had been drinking alcohol and had thrown stones and bricks at the walls of the victim's house and fence without knowing the reason. The Doeum Mean police force then detained the suspect and sent the evidence to the Takhmao City Police Inspectorate for processing.
The villagers were very happy with this arrest because he always walked around the village for no reason and he was good enough to have no drugs, but only when he was drunk he knew he was pulling a lump. Stones and bricks were thrown all over their houses throughout the village.
Sources confirmed that the suspect had been imprisoned five times for throwing stones at the walls and fences of his house.
