The use of this new technology does not interfere with traffic congestion and affect infrastructure because it drills up to 8 meters deep, and this is also the fourth phase of flood protection and drainage system project in Phnom Penh. Also.
It should be noted that the fourth phase of the flood prevention and improvement project in Phnom Penh with a total of 30 million US dollars, a grant from the Government of Japan through the Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA).
The project will implement the following works, including:
1: Install a sewerage network in Tuol Kork district with a length of 8.2 km 2: Install a sewerage network in Daun Penh district with a length of 4.4 km 3: Build an underground water reservoir and build a pumping station in the front garden Council for the Development of Cambodia CDC4: Install automatic mechanical bar to collect garbage in front of the drainage road at Chaktomuk Water Pumping Station, Preah Konlong 1, Preah Konlong 2 and Old Market 5: Provide 2 mobile pumping trucks.
