Kaing Guek Eav alias Duch was sent to the Khmer-Soviet Friendship Hospital for emergency treatment.
(Phnom Penh): Kaing Guek Eav, alias Duch, former director of Tuol Sleng Prison during the Khmer Rouge era, was sent to the Khmer-Soviet Friendship Hospital on the night of August 31, 2020.
This is according to Mr. Kim Santepheap, Secretary of State and spokesman for the Ministry of Justice, who received information from the Kandal Provincial Prosecutor to confirm to Fresh News on the morning of September 1, 2020.
The source said that before being sent to the rescue, Kaing Guek Eav alias Duch was very tired as he got older.
Kaing Guek Eav alias Duch, 78, was born in Pov Veay village, Peam Bang commune, Stong district, Kampong Thom province. He was arrested in 1999 and remanded in custody at the military tribunal until his transfer to the Khmer Rouge tribunal on 31 July 2007. Duch served as Deputy Secretary, then Secretary of the S-21 Committee (the Department of Peace, commonly known as Tuol Sleng Prison) during the Khmer Rouge regime.
