(Oddar Meanchey): As of August 1, 2020, Thailand has deported seven Cambodians back through O'Smach International Airport in O'Smach Sangkat, Samrong City, after serving many years in the territory. Thailand on charges of illegal border crossing.
According to Oddar Meanchey provincial officials, as of August 2020, Thai authorities in Surin province have deported seven Cambodians after being convicted in Thailand of illegally crossing the border. Cutting rosewood.
Separately, at 02:21 on August 30, 2020, Thai authorities sent a Cambodian prisoner named Oeun Koeun, 42 years old, living in Cheung Phnom village, Trapeang Prey commune, Anlong Veng district, after returning to prison in the province. Surin for 2.4 years for illegally crossing the border to cut rosewood.
After undergoing a heat scan for Kovid 19 and washing his body with alcohol, authorities instructed him to stop illegal immigration and return to his home.
Cambodian Entrepreneurs and National Institute of Entrepreneurship and Innovation Find Winners of National Entrepreneurship Award 2020
(Phnom Penh): The National Entrepreneur Awards 2020, co-organized by Cambodian Entrepreneurs and the National Institute of Entrepreneurship and Innovation, successfully concluded the finals with 15 candidates representing 15 companies from 5 regions in Cambodia. Come and present your business model to win this national entrepreneurial award.
After a full day of competition, the three winners were found, with the first place going to Ms. Chen Sopheap, the founder of KTK Khmer Textile Enterprise, Phnom Penh, and the second place to Miss Thong Thida, the founder. Thong Enterprise Salt Production Enterprise, Kampot Province and the third place went to Mr. Chhim Chanchhaya, the owner of Hang Mach Farm, Takeo Province.
The Ministry of Economy and Finance, through Cambodian Entrepreneurs, has partnered with the National Institute of Entrepreneurship and Innovation and SATHAPANA Bank to organize the National Entrepreneurship Competition 2020 in order to promote entrepreneurship in Cambodia and expand public-private partnerships. .
The National Entrepreneurship Awards 2020 has been running for the past three months, with the elimination from the regional level to the capital level. The Organizing Committee received a total of 181 applications for the program and selected only 75 eligible entrepreneurs to participate in the five regional qualifiers: Kandal, Siem Reap, Battambang. Svay Rieng and Kampot.
Separately, only 15 outstanding candidates were ranked to compete in the finals in Phnom Penh.
Dr. Chheang Vann Monin, Executive Director of Khmer Entrepreneurship, said at the award ceremony for the National Entrepreneur of 2020 that there are three main reasons that motivate the celebration of this program that cooperation between Cambodian entrepreneurs and the National Institute. Entrepreneurship and innovation in organizing this competition is based on three main reasons:
Reason 1: Mr. Vongsey Visoth, Permanent Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and Chairman of the Board of Governors of the Entrepreneurship Development Fund directly advised Cambodian entrepreneurs to find potential partners to create a competitive environment that promotes Elevation of entrepreneurial culture.
Reason 2: The initiative of this program also responds to the policy of the Ministry of Economy and Finance in private sector development, as well as the recommendation of the Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth, Minister of Economy and Finance, who wants to have entrepreneurial competition. A national level to inspire and motivate every entrepreneur to be brave and have the opportunity to present their business.
Reason 3: At the same time, the National Institute of Entrepreneurship and Innovation also received a sub-decree of Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia to organize a national entrepreneurship competition to create participation from large enterprises. Small and medium enterprises and start-ups in all areas of Cambodia.
He said that looking at these three reasons, there is a common goal of Cambodian entrepreneurs and the National Institute of Entrepreneurship and Innovation has organized a competition for the National Entrepreneurship Award 2020.
He added that the participation of all candidates from the regional qualifiers to the last round reflects the spirit of competition, perseverance and innovation that entrepreneurs should adhere to and also respond to the strategic goals of the Rectangle. 4 which the Royal Government has prepared. Such competition also provides an opportunity for every entrepreneur to explore the various business models of partners and more markets.
(Kratie): Police in Kratie City, Kratie Province, in cooperation with Chit Borei District Police and Provincial Criminal Investigation Force under the command of Major General Lon Sophat, Provincial Police Commissioner, on the evening of August 30, 2020, arrested one of the suspects. Two people at Thmor Bang resort in Banteay village, Koulab commune, Chit Borey district, Kratie province.
According to the Kratie City Police report, the suspect, named Dieng Van, male, 38 years old, resides in Thmey Village, Pong Ro Commune, Samaki Meanchey District, Kampong Chhnang Province in connection with the theft on August 30 in a rented room in Daun Chram Village, Kratie Sangkat. Kratie City.
According to the report, prior to the incident on August 30, at 5:00 AM, Huot Da rode the motorbike to prepare goods for his wife to sell at Kratie Market. When he returned, he took the motorbike In front of the counter and leave the keys for his wife to ride to pick up goods at the market, and he rode a motorcycle trailer to work until 7 am, his system came out to pick up the motorcycle only to find out that the motorcycle is missing.
Immediately after receiving the information, Kratie City Police, in cooperation with Chit Borei and provincial police, conducted a series of investigations and arrested the suspect while he was trying to escape from the police. At the detention point above, another accomplice escaped.
During the operation, the police confiscated two motorcycles, one suspect's belongings, one victim's motorcycle and one motorcycle lock device. The suspects and exhibits are currently being detained and temporarily kept at the provincial police commission to complete the procedure.
