Spokesman for the General Commission: On August 30, another 950 vehicles were inspected and fined
According to the spokesperson of the General Commissioner, within 122 days of tightening the road traffic law by increasing the fine according to Sub-Decree No. 49, from May 1 to August 30, 2020, the traffic police nationwide inspected And fined a total of 155,400 vehicles, including 115,267 motorcycles and 40,133 vehicles of all types.
Lt. Gen. Chhay Kimkhoeun continued that for the past 122 days, the implementation of the new sub-decree to fine the offending vehicles has been going well. He thanked and commended all the road users for their good obedience to the traffic law so far, especially the traffic police for their dedication and hard work. Tighten traffic with the highest sense of responsibility.
Please note that for August 30, 2020, traffic accidents across Cambodia also occurred 8 times, in which 4 people died, 8 people were injured (6 seriously injured).
The fire broke out at Phsar Thom, Battambang province at around 6 pm today. After the fire, Mr. Nguon Ratanak led the operational force to intervene to put out the fire.
After more than two hours of emergency operations, the fire was completely extinguished. Mr. Nguon Rattanak said that the fire started from an electric smoke in the market stalls. The provincial governor said about 50 stalls were on fire.
The provincial governor said authorities had not yet been able to sum up the extent of the damage caused by the fire. According to Nguon Ratanak, the firefighting operation consumed about 30 vehicles.
Although the fire has been extinguished, the provincial governor and relevant authorities have not yet withdrawn from the scene, but must continue to maintain security as well as the remaining property in the market not to be lost.
Please note that Battambang Central Market is one of the oldest markets in Battambang, left over from the French colonial period.
