General knowledge: Behind Tasaklo's funny laughter is full of countless sadness.
(Foreign): When it comes to Western comedy, everyone knows Tasaklo, a popular comedian who used his talent to make people laugh, but in real life. His was not as pleasant and peaceful as what he showed in front of the audience.
Want to know behind the scenes how the real life of the comedian Saklou encountered some tragedy and how he overcame the karma punishment, please continue to know with his biography as follows:
As a child, Charlie was a weakling, and when Charlie cried, his mother would comfort him by letting his son watch the action outside the window and let Charlie rehearse it. A funny face. Hannah always comforted and taught her children, so much so that it became a habit of Charlie and Sidney and part of their childhood sense of humor.
A few years later, Charlie and Sydney's mother were taken from the hospital, and they were reunited, but only for a short time, after Sydney left home to become a pilot. Also as an actor on stage. Charlie, who was closest to his brother, later followed in his brother's footsteps.
At the same time, Charlie's mother fell ill again and was sent back to the hospital for another seven years, until Charlie was 16 years old.
In Europe, he received a warm welcome from many fans and later brought his mother back to the United States for treatment. He then started working on some feature films.
In 1928, Charlie received an Oscar for his work as a director, actor and producer. But that fame turned into shocking news because his beloved mother passed away that year. For Charlie, despite the pain, he continued to work.
In the wake of World War II, the US government required Charlie to donate a fortune, but he also objected, and he spoke openly about his views. The U.S. government ordered him to be closely monitored on suspicion of treason, especially when Charlie claimed he was British and refused to accept American citizenship.
In 1953, Charlie left the United States to visit Britain, but when he wanted to return to the United States, he was not allowed to return. He also brought his family to Switzerland and lived there for a long time. A year later, Charlie received the World Peace Council Award. He then started producing new films.
Charlie is getting older and his film production is slowing down. Charlie began re-editing his old films and incorporating music into them.
In 1977, Charlie was left in bed with his last breath and died that year. Millions of fans mourn the death of the world's most famous comedian.
His humor comes from his miserable life, which leads to the words, "In order to make a real request, you must know how to turn your pain into a joke." "Come."
Please be informed that at present, the video of Charlie's movie has been attracting a lot of viewers on this modern social network, while many movies are making the audience laugh out loud even though he no longer hears admiration. For him again. 19 Intergovernmental Commission for the Prevention of Kovid Disease Meeting to Facilitate Cross-Border Travel between Japan and Cambodia
