General knowledge! The secret behind the red sun that appears on the Japanese flag?
These are histories related to the name of Japan, with the Japanese believing that their country or their kingdom is the land of the rising sun, or even the homeland of the sun. This is why the Japanese people have been highlighting the rising sun on the emperor's flag as well as the flag of their military leaders since ancient times.
After Japan declared defeat in World War II, the victorious allies of the United States, Britain, the French Republic, and the Soviet Union forced Japan to change its constitution from a military dictatorship to a military dictatorship. Monarchy depends on the Constitution on May 3, 1947.
