NEW YORK (Reuters) - Positive attitudes toward the United States and the United Kingdom on the United States and the United Kingdom have eroded in response to the COVID-19 pandemic, according to a survey released on Thursday. This is according to a release by Xinhua on Saturday, August 29, 2020.
According to the poll, only 46 percent of Britons and 47 percent of Americans think their government has made a good contribution to the fight against COVID-19. The United States ranks the weakest, with only 18 percent saying their country is now united in the fight after the outbreak.
The figures come from the Pew Research Center, which interviewed 14,276 adults by phone from June 10 to August 3.
