Cambodian Political Choices and Foreign Relations
(Phnom Penh): Currently, the world situation is changing rapidly, complicated, difficult to predict and full of dangers. The world has entered an era of new political geography, which is in a difficult transition towards a polar system where new / old characters are competing for roles in world and regional affairs.
Cambodia is a small country between two big countries and has a very dependent economy with external actors as well as a poor internal political bubble. Therefore, political organization and foreign relations are very important for Cambodia in terms of politics, security, strategy, economy and socio-culture.
In the face of this situation, Cambodia must adhere to the fundamental principles of its foreign policy, as stipulated in Article 53 of the 1993 Constitution, which states that "the Kingdom of Cambodia always adheres to the policy of permanent neutrality and non-alignment." "The Kingdom of Cambodia coexists peacefully with its neighbors and all other countries in the world."
But Cambodia must be smart in implementing its foreign policy, a policy that can take advantage of rich countries and superpowers as much as possible, regardless of whether they are liberal or communist, because the great Powers also choose this way, that is, for the benefit of the nation and its people. Money is colorless and odorless, communist or liberal.
If we look at Cambodia's foreign relations, we should divide them into four forms: first: Cambodia's relations with neighboring countries, second: Cambodia's relations with regional powers, and third: Cambodia's relations with other countries. Both inside and outside the region, fourth: Cambodia's relations with three major powers, including Russia, the United States and China.
In this scenario, Cambodia needs to have good brotherly relations with neighboring countries, including: Laos, Thailand and Vietnam for political, security, economic and socio-cultural reasons. Cambodia can not take any neighboring country as an enemy, but Cambodia must not bow to any neighboring country. Cambodia must have equal and equal relations with all countries. Whichever country invades Cambodia, we must respond in their language.
As for the United States, the United States is now like a Borei Spat state that is increasingly worried about losing its position as the world's number one power, with a blink of an eye on the skyrocketing growth and rapid growth of the United States. China, the new superpower, resembled the city of Athens in the ancient Greek Sydney scenario.
Therefore, Cambodia's relationship with the United States is complex and difficult to estimate. In the future, the United States will not take Cambodia as a strategic partner. Overall, in its view, the United States considers Cambodia to be a married woman, or at least an engaged woman. In fact, Cambodia is not a virgin, a widow or a married woman, and whatever, Cambodia is a country that adheres to a colorful foreign policy.
In this sense, Cambodia can not take the United States as an enemy, Cambodia needs to strengthen its relationship with the United States. We need to know that the United States, the world's number one power, has many allies and many partners, so the United States has a salty edge in regional and global affairs.
Xi Jinping also began a project to turn "China into a military power" in the Asia-Pacific. He strengthened the navy, deployed ships, formed military islands in the South and East China Seas to control shipping routes (water and air), demanded submarine oil and gas exploration rights and fishing rights. Finally, China has become increasingly assertive in political geography, from climate change to trade disputes.
China's rise in Asia and growing worldwide is a major geopolitical turmoil that the United States is facing. Historical experience has shown that the integration of emerging powers into the international system is not an easy task.
In this regard, China, which is a comprehensive strategic cooperation partner of Cambodia and a country that has a free trade agreement with Cambodia, good relations with China, Cambodia really enjoys great political, security, strategic and economic benefits. . But Cambodia should also balance its relations with the European Union and Western European countries.
We need to know that China, despite its large economy, rapid development and many partners, does not have many allies, and China is partly at odds with the South China Sea states in ASEAN. India, Japan, South Korea, and China are becoming allies of the United States.
If we talk about the European Union and the countries in Western Europe, these are the traditional strategic allies of the United States, although now the two allies have some differences on some scenarios, but under certain circumstances they cling. Immediately and support each other. The European Union has always followed the United States, and the United States has always supported the European Union.
In conclusion, in its political choices and foreign relations, Cambodia must uphold the fundamental principles of foreign policy set out in the Constitution, but must be smart policies in order to maximize the benefits for our nation.
