Source: CNA (Saturday, August 29, 2020) Banteay Meanchey Provincial Armed Forces arrested a suspect in connection with a drug trafficking case in Serei Sophorn
(Banteay Meanchey): A suspect who was selling drugs was cracked down by the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Armed Forces at a corner near the Saing Tela garage in Prey Russey village, Preah Ponlea commune, Serey Sophorn city.
The operation took place on August 28, 2020, led by Lieutenant Colonel Chea Dara, Deputy Commander of the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Armed Forces, in charge of drug offenses. The police confiscated 14 packages of methamphetamine (ice) and some other materials.
Colonel Chea Dara said that the suspect was named Pith Sanh, 32 years old, living in Preah Ponlea village, Sangkat Preah Ponlea, Serey Sophorn city, Banteay Meanchey province. After the arrest, the suspect was sent to the Provincial Gendarmerie Command for questioning. The suspect admitted that he had actually sold drugs.
Based on the confession and the evidence, the suspect and the exhibits were sent to the provincial court by the competent authorities of the Provincial Office of Narcotics and Military Police to handle the case.
