An ambitious beekeeper wants Pailin to be the largest honey producer in Cambodia, the Minister of Agriculture supports this idea!
On August 29, 2020, Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, Deputy Governor and colleagues visited Dr. Kuy Theavy's beekeeping farm in Suon Ampov Keut village, Pailin commune, Pailin city, Pailin province. .
Dr. Kuy Theavy described the biological characteristics of bees and honey production. Pailin is a province with high potential for honey production because it has a lot of tamarind and cassava plantations, which are a source of pollen for bees to collect sugar.
He said that in one hectare of Ta Nen plantation, one bee can be placed, and in one container, it can hold 10 lobsters in a month.
In the future, Dr. wants Pailin to be the largest honey-producing province in Cambodia due to the potential of tamarind and cassava crops, especially low investment capital and low income.
Dr. called on plantation owners to raise bees to take advantage of honey and increase tannin production as bees are breeding agents.
He also mentioned that due to the unsustainable water supply to Ta Nen and other fruit trees, the flowering plants in this season are a problem for honey production in the dry season.
After learning something about the biological characteristics of bees and honey production, Minister Veng Sakhon praised and appreciated the knowledge and past research results of the team that led to the success today.
Understanding the benefits of honey and the role of bees in assisting in the field of crop breeding, Minister Veng Sakhon suggested that efforts should be made to expand this production further and to study regional products (GI) for Pailin province to make customers recognize this product more, including packaging.
