Minister of Agriculture instructs professional officers to vaccinate people's livestock across the country to avoid infectious diseases
(Pailin): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, on August 29, 2020, instructed the professional officers to vaccinate people across the country to avoid infectious diseases.
This instruction was made on the occasion of Minister Veng Sakhon leading a team to vaccinate livestock in Tumnup village, Stung Trang commune, Sala Krao district, Pailin province this morning, August 29, 2020.
Minister Veng Sakhon instructed the department and professional officers to make every effort to implement all plans to ensure that people's livestock receive vaccines to prevent the spread of infectious diseases that affect cattle production, including the family economy.
He said that we must encourage our farmers to raise cows in the barn or in the right farm to ensure good health and high income, stop letting cattle roam the open field, which is an opportunity to easily get sick and destroy crops.
Livestock need to be vaccinated against all kinds of infectious diseases, so Minister Veng Sakhon took this opportunity to advise owners of chickens, ducks, pigs, cattle, sheep and goats, as well as families and companies across the country to be vaccinated. Regularly and regularly to ensure that pets are healthy for humans to eat.
