Samdech Techo Hun Sen Establishes Inter-Ministerial Working Group to Study and Solve Unexploded Ordnance Disposal Case in Shipwreck in Kampong Cham Province
(Phnom Penh): The Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Chacho Hun Sen on August 28, 2020, decided to set up an inter-ministerial working group to study and solve the case of unexploded ordnance found in a ship that sank in the river in the village. Veal, Meanchey commune, Srey Santhor district, Kampong Cham province.
According to the decision of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, obtained by Fresh News, this working group is composed of 17 people, with General Neang Phat, Permanent Secretary of the Ministry of National Defense as the Chairman, and General Neth Savoeun, General Commissioner of the National Police. As Deputy Chairman, General Sem Sovanny, Director General of the National Center for Peacekeeping Forces and Demining and Unexploded Ordnance, as the Vice-Chairman and 14 other members.
According to the same decision said:
* The task force is responsible for conducting research on the history of shipwrecks as well as other evidence to determine the exact location of the shipwreck, the type of ship and the type of unexploded ordnance contained in the ship for basic targeting purposes. Balloons or markers are at risk areas where entry and exit is prohibited.
Coordinate requests for naval forces and water border police to co-operate in the protection of the above risk areas in order to prevent people from entering and leaving through the sand dredging and navigation business in that area.
Disseminate widely to the public about the above-mentioned risk areas to prevent any eventual danger by unexploded ordnance.
* Study and determine technical conditions to organize operations to retrieve unexploded ordnance from the sunken ship. * Perform other duties as necessary.
In addition, in carrying out its work, the working group must report and request regular suggestions from Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior.
Please be reminded that at the above point of shipwreck, on November 05, 2019, the police force of Srey Santhor District Police Inspectorate joined with a group of divers to inspect the sand dredging site, which pumped 3 types of ammunition: AK57 ammunition 3 kg, 16 60 mm bullets and 1 80 mm bullet.
