Announcing the new Director of Preah Sihanouk Provincial Department of Economy, Mr. Chey Vimeanrith, Deputy Director of Phnom Penh Department of Economy, replacing Mr. Sun Thong, who has retired.
(Preah Sihanouk): The Ministry of Economy and Finance has announced the appointment of Mr. Chey Vimean Rith, Deputy Director of the Department of Economy and Finance of Phnom Penh, to the position of Director of the Preah Sihanouk Provincial Department of Economy and Finance, replacing Mr. Sun Thong. Retire.
On the occasion of the announcement of the new position on the afternoon of August 28, 2020, Mr. Chey Vimean Rith expressed his strong commitment in front of all the leaders in Sihanoukville 6 points:
1: Coordinate the management of the economic and financial sector with specialized departments, units and sub-national administration.
2: Disseminate and guide the implementation of the policy of the Ministry of Economy and Finance to specialized departments, units and sub-national administrations, including: Public Financial Management Reform Program, Public Administration Reform, Decentralization and Reconstruction and Reform. Salary system in line with the policy and strategy of the fourth phase of the Royal Government.
3. Manage, control and promote all types of non-tax revenue collection of specialized departments, units and sub-national administrations as much as possible.
4: Strengthen and increase the efficiency of state property management.
5: Participate in organizing, managing, monitoring and evaluating the implementation of revenue-expenditure of specialized departments, units and sub-national administrations.
6: Strengthen friendship and internal unity for the efficiency of daily work and harmony in the department.
Dr. Chhorn Sopheap, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy, Deputy Prime Minister Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Minister of Economy and Finance, stated that the reform work is a priority for the Royal Government to lead Cambodia to achieve a high middle-income country this year. 2030.
He instructed Mr. Chey Vimeanrith, the new director of the department, to strive to perform his duties well, be gentle, thorough, transparent, efficient and responsible and to cooperate with all departments in accordance with the policy of financial management reform. Public objects of the Ministry of Economy and Finance for the better.
Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, Governor of Sihanoukville Province, said that in order to be able to build local development, we need to have a budget and that budget must be managed transparently to make our achievements as big as we want.
Obey traffic rules, drive carefully every second! One killed, one injured in road accident nationwide on August 28
(Phnom Penh): According to the report of the General Commission of the National Police, on August 28, 2020, there was one traffic accident across the country, resulting in one death and one minor injury.
The Ministry of Health requested the governors of the 25 capitals and provinces to deploy patrols at Chattalysak centers throughout the country to strengthen security and order for the people.
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Health on August 28, 2020, issued a letter requesting the governors of the 25 capitals and provinces to have security forces patrolling all the centers in Cambodia to increase security and order. More people, although these days, Cambodia has no new cases of Kovid-19 infection.
The proposed additional action is to ensure the 14-day management of citizens and foreigners who are undergoing a four-day internship at Level 1, Level 2 and at a hotel designated by an inter-sectoral team, including the health sector. And the competent authority.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen posted two commemorative photos with Samdech Kittipritthbandit 33 years ago when he went out to negotiate for the first time in France
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on the night of August 28, 2020, posted two commemorative photos with Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, 33 years ago, during the signing ceremony. Joint proclamation with Samdech Preah Norodom Sihanouk on December 4, 1987 in France.
Samdech Techo, the head of the Royal Government, also confirmed that these two photos were the time when Samdech went out to negotiate for the first time in France.
Victims of electric shock caused paralysis in both arms, deeply grateful for the kindness of Samdech Kittiprittbandit
(Phnom Penh): With great sympathy, on Friday, August 28, 2020, Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, assigned Ms. Men Neary Sopheak, First Deputy Secretary General, to meet with Mr. Ong. Khean, 41, is the biological father of 19-year-old Vorn Khao, who was injured by an electric shock while working as a construction worker in Saang district, Kandal province.
Due to the seriousness of the situation, the doctors decided to amputate both arms to the forearm to save the life of the victim, who is currently being treated at Preah Kosomak Hospital.
Vorn Khao, the eldest son and the mainstay in the family, was born in Prasna Thom village, Sena Reach Udom commune, Preah Sdach district, Prey Veng province, who struggled to support himself and his family while he had three younger siblings. A farmer with one arm and a mother who just gave birth to a one-month-old baby.
On that occasion, the First Deputy Secretary-General conveyed the remarks of Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, who sent a message of visit, sympathy and encouragement to the victims to take good care of their health, follow the doctor's instructions and work hard. For life to go on.
At the same time, she called on all people to be careful and protect themselves from electricity by learning to have clear skills and have enough equipment to protect themselves while performing work related to electricity.
At the same time, Mr. Ung Kheang expressed his deepest gratitude to Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, a humanitarian mother who always considers the suffering of all people without any discrimination.
In a statement issued by Fresh News on August 28, the General Department of Taxation confirmed that so far, the General Department of Taxation has observed that some property owners have not yet fulfilled their tax declaration obligations.
The General Department of Taxation emphasizes that for failing to file a tax return on time, property owners will be punished according to the law in force.
At the same time, the General Department of Taxation sincerely hopes that all property owners will pay attention and come to fulfill their tax obligations on time.
(Foreign): Below are some pictures of the international situation selected for Friday, August 28, 2020.
Kun Kim Delivers Food to 500 Families Affected by Kovid 19 in Oddar Meanchey Province
(Oddar Meanchey): Senior Minister Kun Kim, First Vice President of the National Committee for Disaster Management, met with 500 Covid-19 vulnerable families in Oddar Meanchey province.
In this ceremony, the Senior Minister brought greetings from Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit to the people in Oddar Meanchey province. The Senior Minister said that both Samdech always remember and care about the well-being of the people and always guide him and his team to help Oddar Meanchey to meet and solve all the difficulties for the people in Oddar Meanchey.
Senior Minister Kun Kim urged people to follow the Ministry of Health's guidelines on Covid-19 prevention measures to keep themselves, their families and communities free of the Kovid 19 virus. In addition to preventing Kovid 19, the Senior Minister also instructed the people to work hard to grow crops, vegetables and raise livestock to solve the problem of lack of livelihood.
Mr. Kun Kim also called on the authorities and all people to work together to prevent the use and trafficking of drugs for the future of the people.
(Phnom Penh): The European Union (EU) decided on August 12, 2020 to withdraw the Cambodian preferential tariff system under the "Everything But Arms (EBA)" program, with a tariff on Cambodian goods. 20 percent. The Royal Government of Cambodia does not object to this decision, but some Cambodian historians and social analysts have expressed regret over the decision.
Historians and social analysts see the EU decision as a gesture to please the former opposition party, ignoring the kindness as well as many good deeds of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
In a roundtable discussion organized by the Royal Academy of Cambodia on Cambodia's challenges to the world on the morning of August 28, 2020, Mr. Diep Sophal, a researcher and historian of Cambodia, said that about 20% tax on Cambodian goods from The European Union does not seriously affect the Cambodian economy. But for the historian, it hurts the EU more than for this decision.
Mr. Diep Sophal said that the decision of the European Union was made at the request of officials of the former CNRP, the opposition party in Cambodia. Mr. Sophal described the former CNRP as a criminal who committed illegal acts to overthrow the legitimate Royal Government of Cambodia in 2013.
Mr. Diep Sophal considers the actions of Samdech Techo Hun Sen as a great humanitarian act for humanity.
In 2018, Cambodia exported more than 6 billion dollars to the European Union. Of the more than $ 6 billion from the sale of goods to the EU, Cambodia gains about $ 600 million from tax evasion. The EU decision will bring Cambodian goods as part of a total of about 40 items of clothing, footwear and personal belongings that Cambodia is currently exporting to be taxed.
This decision will bring Cambodia's export value to more than $ 1 billion of the current total export value of about $ 6,000 will be taxed more than $ 100 million.
Dr. Kin Phea, President of the Cambodian Institute of International Relations of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, noted that the EU decision did not seem to weigh on the EU's standard of respect for human rights measures.
Mr. Kin Phea said that the European Union raised the issue of human rights in Cambodia, but did not see the issue of human rights in Vietnam and joined hands to sign a free trade agreement with Vietnam with the lowest human rights conditions.
(Phnom Penh): The Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia organized the launch of its membership card system and its own app on the evening of August 28, 2020 to provide various benefits and convenience for members to communicate as well as Maintain closeness as a family Only one.
According to the press release, this membership card is the first membership card of the organization / association that has both an identity card and a card that can be used to pay for expenses.
