Spokesman for the General Commission: On August 28, another 1,361 vehicles were inspected and fined
According to the spokesperson of the General Commissioner, within 120 days of tightening the road traffic law by increasing the fine according to Sub-Decree No. 49, from May 1 to August 28, 2020, the traffic police throughout the country inspected And fined a total of 153,265 vehicles, including 113,663 motorcycles and 39,602 vehicles of all types.
Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun said that for the past 120 days, the implementation of the new sub-decree to fine vehicles for offenses has been going well. He thanked and commended all the road users for their good obedience to the traffic law so far, especially the traffic police for their dedication and hard work. Tighten traffic with the highest sense of responsibility.
Please note that for August 28, 2020, traffic accidents across Cambodia also occurred once, in which one person died.
Russia retaliates by expelling Norwegian diplomat for "spying"
The Russian government on Friday expelled a Norwegian diplomat from the country for alleged involvement in intelligence activities. This is according to a source from the Norwegian Ministry of Foreign Affairs quoted by Reuters on Friday evening, August 28, 2020.
"The Russian Foreign Ministry has informed our Embassy in Moscow that one of our diplomats is no longer welcome in Russia," the Norwegian Foreign Ministry said in a statement. . "This is a completely baseless decision because our diplomats have not violated any law."
Moscow's decision was seen as retaliation against the Norwegian government, which expelled a Russian diplomat in early August on similar charges of espionage. . Russia, however, has denied the allegations and called them baseless.
(Phnom Penh): In a forum on economic challenges and the challenge of influence of the great power of the Royal Academy of Cambodia on August 28, 2020, Dr. Kin Phea, President of the Institute of International Relations of Cambodia, raised nine points that Cambodia must walk How to prepare, what should be the position and attitude to respond to the problems that are happening in the regional framework, the global framework, as well as the framework of domestic politics.
The nine ideas include:
* First: Maintaining political stability
Mr. Kin Phea said that maintaining political stability is the most important thing because it is an indispensable precondition for Cambodia. "Without peace, do not talk about development, do not talk about human rights, do not talk about democracy, do not talk about justice, do not talk about the rule of law, it is impossible," he said.
Dr. reminded that the lesson that we have seen and learned is the history of Cambodia through after the coup of 1970 to the 1990s. He considers that the most painful historical lesson due to political instability.
* Second: Consistent implementation of foreign policy as in the Constitution
Mr. Kin Phea said that the consistent implementation of Cambodia's foreign policy as defined in the Constitution, permanent neutrality, non-alignment is the right thing to do. But smart foreign policy, a policy that takes advantage of rich countries from superpowers as much as possible, is even better.
Dr. added that in Cambodia, we do not discriminate whether Mr. Serey or communist, but all. At the same time, money does not smell free, it does not smell communist, it is not trending. So what is in the national interest, we must pull for our national interest.
He said China today has become an important engine of the regional and global economy. We can say that the world without China would be overthrown. So Cambodia always welcomes Chinese and American investment without discrimination as long as they come to invest.
* Third: Strengthening Cambodia's foreign relations with foreigners
Mr. Kin Phea said that Cambodia's foreign relations should focus on three main areas. The first is with neighboring countries, the second with intermediate powers in the region and the third with non-regional powers.
Foreign affairs with regional superpowers: Mr. Kin Phea also said that maintaining power with regional superpowers means making Cambodia a strategic partner with them, such as India, Japan and Korea. Etc. for political, strategic and economic reasons.
Balancing foreign affairs with non-regional powers: Kin Phea said that with non-regional powers, we also need to balance our relations to diversify our diplomacy and diversify our markets.
* Fourth: Strengthen relations with three great powers: Russia, US and China
Kin Phea suggested that relations with Russia, the United States and China must be focused on taking advantage of each other as much as possible.
Mr. Kin Phea said that strengthening national unity is more important than the political and civil society needs to unite and unleash the power of wisdom to contribute to nation-building. He said some people could not shout at their country and call themselves patriots.
